{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Pain is the foremost complication of chronic pancreatitis (CP), affecting about 70% of patients. However, the pathophysiological understanding and management of CP-related pain is complex, likely as patients have diverse \"pain phenotypes\" responding differently to treatment. This study aims to develop a bedside test panel to identify distinct pain phenotypes, investigate the temporal evolution, and determine whether they can be used to predict treatment response. METHOD: The INPAIN study is an international, multi-center, observational, longitudinal cohort study comprised of 4 sub-studies. The studies will prospectively enroll 400 CP patients (50 without pain and 350 with pain) and 50 control subjects, conducting biannual observations for four years. The test panel is comprised of comprehensive subjective and objective assessment parameters. Statistical analysis strategies differ across the sub-studies. A model to predict treatment efficacy will be developed using various machine learning techniques, including an artificial intelligence approach, with internal cross-validation. Trajectories in pain parameters will be characterized by graphical analysis and mixed effect models. DISCUSSION: The INPAIN study aims to comprehensively understand pain in CP through a test panel developed for routine clinical use. This tool has the potential to personalize treatments, improve clinical practice, enhance patient care, improve quality of life, and minimize treatment side effects.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Hagn-Meincke, Rasmus","Dugic, Ana","Agarwal, Ankit","Phillips, Anna Evans","Waage, Anna","Yadav, Dhiraj","Pillai, Divya","Vivian, Elaina","de-Madaria, Enrique","Niazi, Imran Khan","Easler, Jeffrey","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","McNabb-Baltar, Julia","Kuhlmann, Louise","Faghih, Mahya","Montiel, Maria Belen Garay","Cook, Mathias Ellgaard","Unnisa, Misbah","Tarnasky, Paul","Hegyi, Peter","Garg, Pramod","Nedergaard, Rasmus Bach","Edwards, Robert","Talukdar, Rupjyoti","Farheen, Shagufta","Olesen, Søren Schou","Jagannath, Soumya","Schmidt, Suzette","Singh, Vikesh","Hajnády, Zoltán","Drewes, Asbjørn Mohr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-757017"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["International Pancreatic Pain Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Drewes, Asbjørn Mohr"],"country":["Hungary","India","New Zealand","Norway","Spain","United States"],"glorg":["Alicante University General Hospital","All Global Affiliations","All India Institute of Medical Sciences, New Delhi","Asian Institute of Gastroenterology India","Brigham and Women’s Hospital","Heidelberg University","Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis","Johns Hopkins University","Methodist Health System, Texas","New Zealand College of Chiropractic","Oslo University Hospital","Semmelweis University","University of Pittsburgh"],"keyword":["Chronic pancreatitis","Pain","Prediction model"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"individualized pain treatment in chronic pancreatitis inpain an international multicenter investigator initiated prospective cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85204190431&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: Professor Asbj\\u00F8rn Mohr Drewes initiated this research project. Researchers behind this study declare no conflicts of interest. This study is economically supported by the INPAIN study sponsored by Aalborg University Hospital (\\u201CForskningsKUBE\\u201D). This grant will be used to cover expenses related to equipment and salary for study personnel. Various funds will be applied to cover any additional financial expenses."],"id":"S01-000.00-757017","identifier":[{"id":"39259852","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85204190431","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8e485df7-a6d0-4974-b2d0-63c43b5ae089"],"keyword":["Bedside test panel","Chronic Pancreatitis","Pain","Prediction model","Trajectories in pain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-04835DCDC1EF69A413FB340A370ECB01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-01-01","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Gastroenterology and Hepatology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"heidelberg university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"all india institute of medical sciences new delhi","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"All India Institute of Medical Sciences, New Delhi","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of pittsburgh","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Pittsburgh","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"no","key":"oslo university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"methodist health system texas","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":