","key":"zanonimarcmpau","last":"Zanoni Marc","name":"Zanoni Marc, M.","rank":1131,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"zennarompau","last":"Zennaro","name":"Zennaro, M.","rank":1132,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"F. M.","key":"zerbifmpau","last":"Zerbi","name":"Zerbi, F. M.","rank":1133,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"I. A.","key":"zinchenkoiapau","last":"Zinchenko","name":"Zinchenko, I. A.","rank":1134,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"zoubianjpau","last":"Zoubian","name":"Zoubian, J.","rank":1135,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"zuccaepau","last":"Zucca","name":"Zucca, E.","rank":1136,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"zumalacarreguimpau","last":"Zumalacarregui","name":"Zumalacarregui, M.","rank":1137,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1051/0004-6361/202450810","issn":["00046361","14320746"],"issn_org":["00046361"],"journal":"Astronomy & Astrophysics","paperid":"A1","publisher":"EDP Sciences","status":"p","title":"Astronomy & Astrophysics","title_org":"Astronomy and Astrophysics","volume":"697"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004926577"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e438652b-7c19-41f9-b96d-dd98fc08c379","ku-6f8be101-ec61-4b1e-a802-6ea468411780"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Euclid: I. Overview of the Euclid mission","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.83-813945","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Building on transaction cost economics and the literature on capabilities, we provide a new, integrative lens on core firms in ecosystems. Specifically, we characterize ecosystems with core firms as a hybrid governance structure and describe the externally-oriented capabilities of core firms as means to reduce ecosystem-level transaction costs. The starting point for our analysis is the identification of three adaptation problems that stem from limitations to modularity in ecosystems (interoperability, customization, and availability), and we argue that each is associated with observable characteristics of the technology prevalent in an ecosystem. Thus, the core firm's externally-oriented capabilities are geared towards solving the respective adaptation problems. We further distinguish between governance capabilities, which serve to influence other ecosystem participants in ways that mitigate the above-mentioned adaptation problems, and problem-focused capabilities, which are targeted at making sure that adaptation problems are solved or do not arise in the first place. Overall, our focus on adaptation problems and transaction costs allows us to provide a theoretically unified view on core firms in ecosystems while simultaneously showing how their capabilities systematically differ in different types of ecosystems.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schmidt, Jens","Foss, Nicolai J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-710024"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Foss, Nicolai J."],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Core firms","Ecosystems","Governance","Limitations to modularity","Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modularity adaptation problems and the governance and problem solving capabilities of core firms in ecosystems","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-710024","identifier":[{"id":"85177215925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-25bf7cdb-547a-4a93-9ade-225a4cbc5937"],"keyword":["Core firms","Ecosystems","Governance","Limitations to modularity","Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D73E28C73C369A97768566858020BBA4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai J.","key":"fosspau","last":"Foss","locid":"7f0ced62-e3e8-4d60-ac5d-48a57edef7ca","name":"Foss, Nicolai J.","orcid":"0000-0003-2049-8347","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/01492063231215023","issn":["01492063","15571211"],"issn_org":["01492063"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Management","pages":"1484-1513","publisher":"SAGE Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Management","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001657260","2-s2.0-85177215925"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-25bf7cdb-547a-4a93-9ade-225a4cbc5937"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Modularity, Adaptation Problems, and the Governance and Problem-solving Capabilities of Core Firms in Ecosystems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-710024","year":"2025","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This study explores the use of generative AI (GenAI) and research integrity assessments of use cases by researchers, including PhD students, at Danish universities. Conducted through a survey sent to all Danish researchers from January to February 2024, the study received 2534 responses and evaluated 32 GenAI use cases across five research phases: idea generation, research design, data collection, data analysis, and writing/reporting. Respondents reported on their own and colleagues' GenAI usage. They also assessed whether the practices in the use cases were considered good research practice. Through an explorative factor analysis, we identified three clusters of perception: \"GenAI as a work horse\", \"GenAI as a language assistant only\", and \"GenAI as a research accelerator\". The findings further show varied opinions on GenAI's research integrity implications. Language editing and data analysis were generally viewed positively, whereas experiment design and peer review tasks faced more criticism. Controversial areas included image creation/modification and synthetic data, with comments highlighting the need for critical and reflexive use of GenAI. Usage differed by main research area, with technical and quantitative sciences reporting slightly higher usage and more positive assessments. Junior researchers used GenAI more than senior colleagues, while no significant gender differences were observed. The study underscores the need for adaptable, discipline-specific guidelines for GenAI use in research, developed collaboratively with experts to align with diverse research practices and minimize ethical and practical misalignment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Andersen, Jens Peter","Degn, Lise","Fishberg, Rachel","Graversen, Ebbe Krogh","Horbach, Serge Pascal Johannes M","Kalpazidou Schmidt, Evanthia","Schneider, Jesper Wiborg","Sørensen, Mads P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786982"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Jens Peter"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Radboud University Nijmegen"],"keyword":["Generative Artificial Intelligence GenAI","Research integrity","Research practice","Research process","Use cases"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generative artificial intelligence genai in the research process a survey of researchers practices and perceptions","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techsoc.2025.102813","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-786982","identifier":[{"id":"85214793683","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-33a7aeac-d7a1-4d09-a25d-b637dcc837a9"],"keyword":["Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI)","Research integrity","Research practice","Research process","use cases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB5F7A02B76FB4D8D2F58BCEDB1BAF15"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techsoc.2025.102813","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science - Danish Centre for Studies in Research and Research Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Peter","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b1e70d8a-0883-480d-8c07-5a7775417377","name":"Andersen, Jens Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2444-6210","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise","key":"degnpau","last":"Degn","locid":"7c40c5f0-8571-476e-b8a6-6041c38e5e77","name":"Degn, Lise","orcid":"0000-0001-6571-9743","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rachel","key":"fishbergpau","last":"Fishberg","locid":"85c23222-c3c2-4915-8c7b-62b2e0f861cf","name":"Fishberg, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0002-4386-2933","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ebbe Krogh","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","locid":"7ad5f98b-e0b1-48c6-a8f3-a9c413ea584f","name":"Graversen, Ebbe Krogh","orcid":"0000-0003-4009-2678","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Serge Pascal Johannes M","key":"horbachpau","last":"Horbach","name":"Horbach, Serge Pascal Johannes M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Evanthia","key":"kalpazidouschmidtpau","last":"Kalpazidou Schmidt","locid":"30cd8ce5-47fe-495b-a57f-03e9c5e5eae6","name":"Kalpazidou Schmidt, Evanthia","orcid":"0000-0002-3204-0803","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Wiborg","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"8fcbf953-b83f-4fe7-b698-d4aec218e1f5","name":"Schneider, Jesper Wiborg","orcid":"0000-0001-5556-0919","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads P.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fa411f34-079c-444b-afc9-a1ad05e462e3","name":"Sørensen, Mads P.","orcid":"0000-0003-2455-2515","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.techsoc.2025.102813","issn":["0160791X","18793274"],"issn_org":["0160791X"],"issue":"June 2025","journal":"Techn