m impacts of wind energy developments: Key research challenges and opportunities","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798516","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Insecure adult attachment patterns have recently been associated with an increased risk of developing persistent post-concussion symptoms (PCS) and poorer treatment outcomes, highlighting the potential of attachment-informed treatment protocols for persistent PCS. A key requirement for such approaches is that attachment patterns remain relatively stable during the post-injury illness course, allowing them to serve as reliable indicators for guiding initial care and treatment planning. This study aimed to assess the stability of self-reported attachment anxiety and attachment avoidance in individuals aged 15–30 years, from three (T1) to nine (T2) months after a concussion, corresponding to the period when treatment for PCS typically becomes relevant. This study is a methodological follow-up of a larger clinical cohort study comprising 3080 individuals aged 15–30 years who were diagnosed with a concussion. Attachment dimensions were measured using the Experiences in Close Relationships-Relationship Structures Questionnaire at three (T1) and nine (T2) months post-injury. Both mean-level and individual changes were examined, taking relevant covariates such as sex, age, level of PCS, post-traumatic stress disorder symptoms, and social support into account. At T1, 958 respondents were included (39%), with 416 also responding at T2 (43%). Mean-level changes were minimal (attachment anxiety: β = −0.07 (95% confidence interval [CI]: −0.22; 0.08)), attachment avoidance: β = 0.00 (95% CI: −0.11; 0.11). Larger individual changes that could not be explained by measurement error were observed in 12% of participants. No association was found with any of the covariates. Self-reported attachment patterns appear to remain stable in most young people with a concussion from 3 to 9 months post-injury. The findings strengthen confidence in conducting research to investigate whether attachment-informed treatment approaches can improve healthcare for these patients.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Tuborgh, Astrid","Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","Elklit, Ask","Hunter, Jon","Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","Ørnbøl, Eva","Schröder, Andreas","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Thastum, Mille","Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-813736"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tuborgh, Astrid"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Toronto"],"keyword":["Attachment anxiety","Attachment avoidance","Experiences in close relationships relationship structure questionnaire","Post concussion symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"is self report of attachment patterns in young people stable from three to nine months after a concussion","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sjop.13094","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-813736","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12235073","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39979129","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85218695568","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-95a13f9a-ce83-4f90-b8f0-6ec73b13d2c3","sdu-9df95499-6bb7-4d8b-bcaa-fef759ab8354"],"keyword":["Experiences in Close Relationships-Relationship Structure Questionnaire","attachment anxiety","attachment avoidance","post-concussion symptoms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F4940779E0DB1ADAA3BEDDA0C365B6EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sjop.13094","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/292910006/Is_Self_Report_of_Attachment_Patterns_in_Young_People_Stable_From_Three_to.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Psychiatric Hospital for Children and Adolescents"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, Clinical Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, The National Center of Psychotraumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"tuborghpau","last":"Tuborgh","locid":"f019f6a6-ef3a-403d-b9f8-60d62215cafc","name":"Tuborgh, Astrid","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne Wulff","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"1de9ffe9-dbf8-4bbd-8708-35bce0da950f","name":"Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ask","key":"elklitpau","last":"Elklit","locid":"d90151d4-a374-4c6d-b7ff-42a930c5a468","name":"Elklit, Ask","orcid":"0000-0002-8469-7372","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"hunterpau","last":"Hunter","name":"Hunter, Jon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Søndergaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f77754dc-4ec3-47ff-8227-808446a30644","name":"Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"ørnbølpau","last":"Ørnbøl","locid":"e781e74a-aaa8-439f-ae9f-274a3abb6dae","name":"Ørnbøl, Eva","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"schröderpau","last":"Schröder","locid":"200c6dd9-43cd-41da-8c27-ce8adb073e24","name":"Schröder, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mille Møller","key":"thastumpau","last":"Thastum","locid":"c3813500-c313-4961-a854-ad2dba72d7d9","name":"Thastum, Mille","name_org":"Thastum, Mille Møller","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erhard Trillingsgaard","key":"næssschmidtpau","last":"Næss-Schmidt","locid":"c1a1a6b6-deb0-4e07-8cc0-f7d3beeaca85","name":"Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2539-0362","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Ulrikka","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","locid":"1e308742-df61-47da-83ce-53d8a7c774c3","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","orcid":"0000-0002-7426-0353","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39979129"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sjop.13094","issn":["00365564","14679450"],"issn_org":["00365564"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Psychology","pages":"459-472","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Psychology","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218695568"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-95a13f9a-ce83-4f90-b8f0-6ec73b13d2c3","sdu-9df95499-6bb7-4d8b-bcaa-fef759ab8354"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Is Self-Report of Attachment Patterns in Young People Stable From Three to Nine Months After a Concussion?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-813736","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Cardiac implantable electronic devices (CIEDs) can be implanted epicardially or transvenously in children. Both techniques involve procedure-specific complications, and evidence for the choice of technique in children of different ages is scarce. Objectives: The purpose of this study was to characterize a complete national pediatric cohort with de novo CIED implantation and compare the risks and causes of reintervention between transvenous and epicardial CIED recipients. Methods: This retrospective nationwide cohort study included all Danish children aged ≤15 years receiving a CIED from 1977 to 2021. Outcomes included time to first reintervention stratified by age and implantation technique. Reintervention was due to either battery depletion or lead or generator complication. Results: A total of 376 children received an epicardial (n = 131 [35%]) or transvenous (n = 245 [65%]) CIED with median [interquartile range] follow-up of 14 [6–21] years. Median age was 6 [1–11] years. For epicardial recipients, complication-driven reintervention was equal across age groups (P = .10), whereas among transvenous recipients the risk was significantly lower with increasing age (P <.001). Age-specific risk analyses revealed different risks for children aged <1 year, 1–8 years, and 9–15 years (P interaction <.001). For children <1 year, a complication-driven reintervention was more frequent for transvenous vs epicardial recipients (P <.001), whereas in children aged 9–15 years, the opposite was observed (P = .02). Conclusion: Transvenous implantation in children <1 year and epicardial implantation in children 9–15 years was associated with higher risk of CIED-related complication leading to reintervention, whereas for children aged 1–8 years, the complication risk was similar between implantation techniques.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Thuraiaiyah, Jani","Jensen, Annette Schophuus","De Backer, Ole","Lim, Chee Woon","Idorn, Lars","Jakobsen, Frederikke Noerregaard","Joergensen, Troels Hoejsgaard","Schmidt, Michael Rahbek","Smerup, Morten","Johansen, Jens Brock","Riahi, Sam","Sondergaard, Lars","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Philbert, Berit Thornvig","Jons, Christian"],"cuid":["S03-099.91-822235"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thuraiaiyah, Jani"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Laboratories","Abbott Structural Heart","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Cardiac implantable electronic device complication","Congenital heart disease","Epicardial cardiac implantable electronic device implantation","Pacemaker therapy","Pediatric cardiology","Transvenous cardiac implantable electronic device implantation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"device related complications in a national pediatric cardiac implantable electronic device cohort stratified after age and implantation technique","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105003467561","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.91-822235","identifier":[{"id":"40157438","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003467561","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0f35c18d-6328-4c12-acdf-4ae7ec3783bb","au-780977f8-8fc6-45cf-b9f6-057179151f55","sdu-d67cf159-6266-46ca-8772-a2bd62bd41ed"],"keyword":["Cardiac implantable electronic device complication","Congenital heart disease","Epicardial cardiac implantable electronic device implantation","Pacemaker therapy","Pediatric cardiology","Transvenous cardiac implantable electronic device implantation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D36701C7E1AA69467AE706F2D00B0903"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Cardiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-H