ions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-19c13491-bcfe-4322-ac7b-ef3b0553b97b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Skeletal muscle characteristics and submaximal work capacity in veteran football players and age-matched untrained controls","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-801721","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Low systolic blood pressure (SBP) is a key criterion for diagnosing cardiogenic shock (CS) caused by a reduction in stroke volume and cardiac output (CO). The temporal interaction between changes in pressure and flow has not been well described in the development of CS. In a large animal model, we assessed the temporal relationships of SBP, CO, and blood flow in the carotid artery during induction of CS. Methods: Fifteen adult Danish landrace pigs (median weight 71 kg) underwent CS induction by stepwise injection of polyvinyl alcohol microspheres into the left main coronary artery every 3 min to induce microvascular obstruction. After each injection, CO, SBP, and mixed venous saturation (SvO2) were recorded simultaneously from a ventricle sheath in the carotid artery and a pulmonary artery catheter in the right internal jugular vein. A Doppler flow probe measured blood flow in the left carotid artery. CS was defined as a ≥ 50% reduction in CO or SvO2 from baseline, or absolute SvO2 < 30%. Results: CS occurred after a mean of 8 (range 5 to 19) boluses of microspheres. SBP declined from 99 (± 15) mmHg to 74 (± 6) mmHg, equal to 74 (± 13)% of the baseline value. CO was reduced to 5.8 (± 0.7) L/min to 2.2 (± 1.3) L/min, equal to 38 (± 23)% and SvO2 from 63 (± 7)% to 37 (± 7)%, equal to 60 (± 13)% of baseline values. The decrease in CO was due to a reduction to 43 (± 26)% in stroke volume, as heart rate remained unchanged. The carotid artery blood flow was reduced from 285 (± 50) mL/min to 155 (± 56) mL/min, equal to 54% of baseline values. The decline in SvO2 and CO preceded a reduction in SBP, and after 25% of emboli were given, CO decreased by 24% while SBP was unchanged. Conclusion: In a porcine model of ischemic myocardial injury, the decrease in blood flow and stroke volume preceded a decline in SBP, suggesting pressure preservation occurs in the presence of hypoperfusion.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Svanekjaer, Laura","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Frederiksen, Peter H.","Linde, Louise","Gregers, Emilie","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Schmidt, Henrik","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Ravn, Hanne Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-831307"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Svanekjaer, Laura"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Arterial blood pressure","Cardiac Output","Cardiogenic shock","Hypoperfusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of changes in arterial blood pressure and cardiac output during cardiogenic shock development in a porcine model","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-025-00802-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-831307","identifier":[{"id":"105014915344","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12401854","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40889089","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-99c6c123-241b-4b77-aae6-6fc0de41d621"],"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Arterial blood pressure","Cardiac output","Cardiogenic shock","Hypoperfusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A2597EA45DFD594B8C24319AC41E8882"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/296110677/s40635-025-00802-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40635-025-00802-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"svanekjaerpau","last":"Svanekjaer","name":"Svanekjaer, Laura","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe K.P.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9c1f7b9d-9e43-45ec-aa4d-310cdce6686a","name":"Larsen, Jeppe P.","name_org":"Larsen, Jeppe K.P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter H.","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"85d6facd-93bf-44ee-a117-269fb26a52be","name":"Frederiksen, Peter H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-7980","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","locid":"4fc23628-00d4-466a-9e6e-269e23160481","name":"Linde, Louise","orcid":"0000-0002-7757-2571","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie","key":"gregerspau","last":"Gregers","name":"Grege