{"abstract":"Diabetic retinopathy (DR) is the most common complication in patients with diabetes, and screening for sight-threatening end-stages is indicated to avoid severe visual loss. Screening of DR is nationally implemented in Denmark according to evidence-based national guidelines, which includes the use of individualised screening intervals. Treatment is indicated for proliferative DR and diabetic macular oedema, and treatment modalities include retinal laser therapy, intravitreal angiostatic therapy, and vitrectomy. In this review, we summarise the current guidelines for screening and treatment of DR in Denmark.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Grauslund, Jakob","Andersen, Nis","Andresen, Jens","Bek, Toke","Brandi, Sara","Hajari, Javad","Knudsen, Søren Tang","Laugesen, Caroline Schmidt","Lind, Majbrit","Nielsen, Mette Slot","Schielke, Katja Christina","Subhi, Yousif"],"cuid":["S02-093.65-793093"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Grauslund, Jakob"],"keyword":["Denmark","Diabetic Retinopathy diagnosis","Humans","Macular Edema therapy","Mass Screening","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Vitrectomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Danske Øjenlægers Organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diabetisk retinopati","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V04240246","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.65-793093","ide