ll,"first":"Desalegn","key":"wanadesalegnpau","last":"Wana","name":"Wana, Desalegn","rank":63,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"53","corresponding":null,"first":"Hua Feng","key":"wanghuafengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hua Feng","rank":64,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"54","corresponding":null,"first":"Timothy","key":"whitfeldtimothypau","last":"Whitfeld","name":"Whitfeld, Timothy","rank":65,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"55","corresponding":null,"first":"Georg","key":"zizkageorgpau","last":"Zizka","name":"Zizka, Georg","rank":66,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 56","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesco Maria","key":"sabatinifrancescomariapau","last":"Sabatini","name":"Sabatini, Francesco Maria","rank":67,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"bruelheidehelgepau","last":"Bruelheide","name":"Bruelheide, Helge","rank":68,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39627407"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41559-024-02589-0","issn":["2397334X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","pages":"237-248","paperid":"e12976","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Nature Ecology & Evolution","title_org":"Nature Ecology and Evolution","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211487038"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f6dc5a09-1647-46e7-8b66-a66e328367d6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Global decoupling of functional and phylogenetic diversity in plant communities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-774075","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Characteristics of device-related thrombus (DRT) may differ between types of left atrial appendage occlusion devices, and the association of different DRT characteristics to clinical outcomes is largely unknown. Objectives: The incidence, characteristics, and clinical outcomes through 5 years of high- and low-risk DRTs were assessed in the Amulet IDE trial (AMPLATZER Amulet Left Atrial Appendage Occluder [LAAO] Investigational Device Exemption [IDE] Trial). Methods: An independent core laboratory analyzed all available images at the required 45-day and 12-month visits, and clinical events were reported through 5 years’ post–left atrial appendage occlusion. Results: Of the 1,788 patients with a successful device implant, DRT was observed in 3.3% (30 of 903) and 4.5% (40 of 885) of Amulet and Watchman 2.5 device patients throughout 12 months, respectively (P = 0.192). DRTs were successfully classified as high risk if pedunculated, mobile, >3 mm in thickness, or without continuation onto the left atrial wall. A significantly higher incidence of high-risk DRTs was observed on the Watchman 2.5 device (4.0% [35 of 885]) compared with the Amulet occluder (2.2% [20 of 903]) (P = 0.030). Most low-risk DRTs resolved (12 of 15), whereas high-risk DRTs remained mostly unresolved (34 of 55). Through 5 years, all clinical outcome rates were numerically higher in the high-risk DRT group compared with the low-risk DRT or no-DRT group; significance was observed in the composite of stroke, systemic embolism, or cardiovascular death (30.4% vs 19.9%; HR: 1.74; 95% CI: 1.03-2.92; P = 0.037) and cardiovascular death (26.4% vs 14.5%, HR: 2.09; 95% CI: 1.20-3.66; P = 0.009). Conclusions: High-risk DRTs were observed in a higher number of Watchman 2.5 device patients compared with Amulet occluder patients. The composite of stroke, systemic embolism, or cardiovascular death occurred more often in patients with high-risk DRTs compared with those with low-risk DRTs or no DRTs.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Schmidt, Boris","Windecker, Stephan","Shah, Neeraj","Gray, William","Ellis, Christopher R","Koulogiannis, Konstantinos","Anderson, Jordan A","Gage, Ryan","Lakkireddy, Dhanunjaya"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807741"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Structural Heart","All Global Affiliations","Cardioangiologisches Centrum am Bethanien Krankenhaus, Frankfurt, Germany.","HCA Midwest Health","University of Bern","Vanderbilt University"],"keyword":["Amulet","Atrial fibrillation","Device related thrombus","Left atrial appendage occlusion","Stroke","Watchman"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization and clinical outcomes of high risk device related thrombus in the amulet ide trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105002315786","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-807741","identifier":[{"id":"40208159","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105002315786","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e85f15b6-776d-4218-a6b1-f93665eed5a8"],"keyword":["Amulet","Watchman","atrial fibrillation","device-related thrombus","left atrial appendage occlusion","stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-854EA3C8BF726F686D419092370AD0B8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"cardioangiologisches centrum am bethanien krankenhaus frankfurt germany","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Cardioangiologisches Centrum am Bethanien Krankenhaus, Frankfurt, Germany.","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"vanderbilt university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Vanderbilt University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"abbott structural heart","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Abbott Structural Heart","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"hca midwest health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"HCA Midwest Health","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Boris","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Boris","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"windeckerpau","last":"Windecker","name":"Windecker, Stephan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Neeraj","key":"shahpau","last":"Shah","name":"Shah, Neeraj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"graypau","last":"Gray","name":"Gray, William","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher R","key":"ellispau","last":"Ellis","name":"Ellis, Christopher R","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Konstantinos","key":"koulogiannispau","last":"Koulogiannis","name":"Koulogiannis, Konstantinos","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordan A","key":"andersonpau","last":"Anderson","name":"Anderson, Jordan A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ryan","key":"gagepau","last":"Gage","name":"Gage, Ryan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Dhanunjaya","key":"lakkireddypau","last":"Lakkireddy","name":"Lakkireddy, Dhanunjaya","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40208159"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jacep.2025.02.016","issn":["2405500X"],"issue":"7","journal":"JACC: Clinical Electrophysiology","pages":"1543-1554","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Clinical Electrophysiology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002315786"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e85f15b6-776d-4218-a6b1-f93665eed5a8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Characterization and Clinical Outcomes of High-Risk Device-Related Thrombus in the Amulet IDE Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-807741","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The microbiota in individual habitats differ in both relative composition and absolute abundance. While sequencing approaches determine the relative abundances of taxa and genes, they do not provide information on their absolute abundances. Here, we developed a machine-learning approach to predict fecal microbial loads (microbial cells per gram) solely from relative abundance data. Applying our prediction model to a large-scale metagenomic dataset (n = 34,539), we demonstrated that microbial load is the major determinant of gut microbiome variation and is associated with numerous host factors, including age, diet, and medication. We further found that for several diseases, changes in microbial load, rather than the disease condition itself, more strongly explained alterations in patients’ gut microbiome. Adjusting for this effect substantially reduced the statistical significance of the majority of disease-associated species. Our analysis reveals that the fecal microbial load is a major confounder in microbiome studies, highlighting its importance for understanding microbiome variation in health and disease.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Nishijima, Suguru","Stankevic, Evelina","Aasmets, Oliver","Schmidt, Thomas S.B.","Nagata, Naoyoshi","Keller, Marisa Isabell","Ferretti, Pamela","Juel, Helene Bæk","Fullam, Anthony","Robbani, Shahriyar Mahdi","Schudoma, Christian","Hansen, Johanne Kragh","Holm, Louise Aas","Israelsen, Mads","Schierwagen, Robert","Torp, Nikolaj","Telzerow, Anja","Hercog, Rajna","Kandels, Stefanie","Hazenbrink, Diënty H.M.","Arumugam, Manimozhiyan","Bendtsen, Flemming","Brøns, Charlotte","Fonvig, Cilius Esmann","Holm, Jens-Christian","Nielsen, Trine","Pedersen, Julie Steen","Thiele, Maja Sofie","Trebicka, Jonel","Org, Elin","Krag, Aleksander","Hansen, Torben","Kuhn, Michael","Bork, Peer"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-785494"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corpau":["GALAXY and MicrobLiver consortia"],"corresponding_author":["Bork, Peer"],"country":["Estonia","Germany","Japan","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Foundation for Study of Chronic Liver Failure","European Foundation for the Study of Chronic Liver Failure","European Molecular Biology Laboratory","Julius-Maximilian University of Würzburg","Max Delbrück Center for Molecular Medicine in the Helmholtz Association","Max-Delbrück-Center for Molecular Medicine (MDC), Berlin-Buch, Germany, Germany.","Tokyo Medical University","University of Münster","University of Tartu","University of Würzburg"],"keyword":["Gut microbiome","Machine learning","Microbial load","Shotgun metagenomics","absolute abundance","disease associations"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fecal microbial load is a major determinant of gut microbiome variation and a confounder for disease associations","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2024.10.022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-785494","identifier":[{"id":"39541968","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85210741911","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b27646f8-736e-4c98-b4a0-66d69108bcea","sdu-73b01cb0-b75f-476c-903b-2d31696c08ed"],"keyword":["absolute abundance","disease associations","gut microbiome","machine learning","microbial load","shotgun metagenomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"no