ast":"Krag","locid":"0064696b-9c65-4990-ab96-3635d5a20e4b","name":"Krag, Aleksander","orcid":"0000-0002-9598-4932","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"kuhnmichaelpau","last":"Kuhn","name":"Kuhn, Michael","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 14 15 16 17","first":"Peer","key":"borkpeerpau","last":"Bork","name":"Bork, Peer","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39541968"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2024.10.022","issn":["00928674","10974172"],"issn_org":["00928674"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cell","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Cell","volume":"188"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210741911"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b27646f8-736e-4c98-b4a0-66d69108bcea","sdu-73b01cb0-b75f-476c-903b-2d31696c08ed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Fecal microbial load is a major determinant of gut microbiome variation and a confounder for disease associations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785494","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: This study investigated the association between the plasma marine n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids (n-3 PUFAs) eicosapentaenoic acid and docosahexaenoic acid and cardiovascular (CV) events and all-cause mortality in patients treated with hemodialysis. METHODS: Prospective multicenter cohort study with 5 years of follow-up. Primary outcome was CV events and secondary outcomes were all-cause mortality and each component of CV events. The sum of plasma eicosapentaenoic acid and docosahexaenoic acid was expressed as marine n-3 PUFAs in weight percentage (wt%). The population was divided into tertiles according to plasma n-3 PUFA levels: lower tertile <5.06 wt%, middle tertile 5.06-6.52 wt%, and upper tertile >6.52 wt%. RESULTS: In total, 336 patients were included. Median follow-up was 5.05 (5.02-5.07) years. Generally, the lower tertile was associated with a higher risk of CV events. Unadjusted, the middle tertile was associated with a 36% lower risk of CV events [hazard ratio (HR) 0.64 (95% confidence interval (CI) 0.43-0.96)], and the upper tertile was associated with a 34% lower risk of CV events [HR 0.66 (95% CI 0.44-0.98)]. After adjusting for confounders, the middle tertile was associated with a lower risk of CV events [HR 0.60 (95% CI 0.40-0.92)], peripheral arterial disease [HR 0.44 (95% CI 0.22-0.88)], and all-cause mortality [HR 0.61 (95% CI 0.42-0.86)]. A restricted cubic spline showed that the CV risk was higher in patients with levels below the median of 5.7 wt%, indicating a potential threshold effect. CONCLUSION: Low plasma marine n-3 PUFA levels were associated with a higher risk of CV events, peripheral arterial disease, and all-cause mortality in patients treated with hemodialysis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liboriussen, Caroline Hundborg","Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Jensen, Jens Dam","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Glerup, Rie Io","Svensson, My"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-803811"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Liboriussen, Caroline Hundborg"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular events","Fish Oils","Hemodialysis","Mortality","N 3 polyunsaturated fatty acids","n 3 PUFAs"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low plasma marine n 000000000003 polyunsaturated fatty acids are associated with increased risk of cardiovascular events in patients treated with maintenance hemodialysis","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=105001413502&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Support: This work was supported by The Danish Kidney Association, Danish Society of Nephrology, North Denmark Region, Karen Elise Jensen Foundation, Hertha Christensen Foundation, Helen and Ejnar Bj\\u00F8rnow Foundation, Medical specialist Heinrich Kopp's Grant, Lundbeck Foundation, Spar Nord Foundation, and Obel Family Foundation. The funders did not influence study design; data collection, analysis, or interpretation; writing of the report; or the decision to submit the report for publication. Support: This work was supported by The Danish Kidney Society , The Danish Society of Nephrology , The North Denmark Region , Karen Elise Jensen\\u2019s Foundation , The Hertha Christensen Foundation , The Helen and Ejnar Bj\\u00F8rnow Foundation , Medical specialist Heinrich Kopp\\u2019s Grant , Lundbeck Foundation , The Spar Nord Foundation , and The Obel Family Foundation . The funders did not influence study design; data collection, analysis, or interpretation; writing of the report; or the decision to submit the report for publication."],"id":"S02-100.00-803811","identifier":[{"id":"105001413502","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40020764","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-be2b59a7-99b2-4e1f-ab78-fb202d30946e","au-20427435-dbd7-43bc-b5a1-2c7bfe9a1767"],"keyword":["cardiovascular events","fish oils","hemodialysis","mortality","n-3 PUFAs","n-3-polyunsaturated fatty acids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C6CDF4F2DFDE9FB2F2ACC82D69EAF3D7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nephrology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central and West Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health