search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-67ade775-a40e-42ad-92d4-0c5db04d3388"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Low carbon solution for short-span bridges : Soil-steel composite bridges versus concrete bridges","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-742876","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Powerpoints til musikterapeuter der underviser i ledelse af demenskor. Materialet introducerer kursister til viden om demens, indsigt i brugen af sang for demensramte, teori og forskning i sang og demens, etablering og ledelse af demenskor eller demensvenlige kor. Undervisningen støttes af erfaringsudveksling og praktiske øvelser.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ridder, Hanne Mette Ochsner","Jensen, Hugo","Anderson-Ingstrup, Jens","Christensen, Karen Bjørnskov","Schmidt, Maria Gjerulff","Hestbæk, Trine","Skov, Ursula"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752018"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Marienlund, Center for Socialpsykiatri, Kolding Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ledelse af demenskor","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://sangenshus.dk/demenskor/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752018","ids":["aau-197ebc0f-b881-4a59-b067-e1163c758e19"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-740B7E2D08F54E5B8565AA95D7D1CDBD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Art, Aesthetics & Health","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Music Therapy - CEDOMUS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Marienlund, Center for Socialpsykiatri, Kolding Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Mette Ochsner","key":"ridderoth","last":"Ridder","locid":"adbb45d2-f9ea-4070-a748-bffd83e2a062","name":"Ridder, Hanne Mette Ochsner","orcid":"0000-0002-3204-5997","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hugo","key":"jensenoth","last":"Jensen","locid":"15af7a61-8851-425b-b54c-86d1546d1d19","name":"Jensen, Hugo","rank":2,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"andersoningstrupoth","last":"Anderson-Ingstrup","locid":"39edb70f-be2b-40ea-89f9-bcfeec873d3f","name":"Anderson-Ingstrup, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-5709-3664","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen Bjørnskov","key":"christensenoth","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Karen Bjørnskov","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Gjerulff","key":"schmidtoth","last":"Schmidt","locid":"4dedecd2-1575-4db2-928b-f8fd0f3ab0e6","name":"Schmidt, Maria Gjerulff","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"hestbækoth","last":"Hestbæk","name":"Hestbæk, Trine","rank":6,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ursula","key":"skovoth","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Ursula","rank":7,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-197ebc0f-b881-4a59-b067-e1163c758e19"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Ledelse af demenskor","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752018","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The multiplicity of possible different and possibly interacting processes contributing or governing deterioration processes in bridges requires systems representations way beyond the deterministic approach where the focus is on few processes and corresponding models. A Probabilistic Digital Twin (PDT), supported by Structural Health Monitoring (SHM) and big data from observations and monitoring, can provide a novel contribution to support integrity management with knowledge improved over time. This paper explores the preliminary analyses for the future full development of the PDT as part of the Bridgitise Project. An approach to build the PDT of a bridge will be developed using FEM modelling of the deterioration effects. The simulated structural responses under deterioration progressing in time will be used to develop a PDT model that will then be utilized as a representation of the best available knowledge and applied to generate simulations of very significant numbers of structural performance scenarios over time.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Darò, P.","La Mazza, D.","Basone, F.","Mancini, G.","Limongelli, M. P.","Faber, Michael Havbro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752282"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, IABMAS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan","Sacertis Ingegneria S.r.l."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"probabilistic digital twin for continuous bridge performance modeling","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-409","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752282","identifier":[{"id":"85200319188","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8f7dc0ec-6f5e-4c2c-b90e-69fa1bc3caa5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-320ABFBE1EAC406FAFD032DF7C4B7C99"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-409","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/752018323/10.1201_9781003483755-409_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"sacertis ingegneria s r l","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sacertis Ingegneria S.r.l.","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Danish Centre for Risk and Safety Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Structures, Geotechnics and Risk","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Risk, Resilience, Safety, and Sustainability of Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"daròpau","last":"Darò","name":"Darò, P.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"lamazzapau","last":"La Mazza","name":"La Mazza, D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"basonepau","last":"Basone","name":"Basone, F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"mancinipau","last":"Mancini","name":"Mancini, G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. P.","key":"limongellipau","last":"Limongelli","name":"Limongelli, M. P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M. H.","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"304dde84-c558-4302-a230-e375d61f0c1e","name":"Faber, Michael Havbro","name_org":"Faber, M. H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3761-0737","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Sandager","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens Sandager","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan M.","key":"frangopolpedh","last":"Frangopol","name":"Frangopol, Dan M.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003483755-409","eisbn":["9781003483755"],"isbn":["9781032770406","9781032775609"],"pages":"3457-3464","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, 24-28 june 2024, Copenhagen, Denmark","title":"Bridge Maintenance, Safety, Management, Digitalization and Sustainability"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200319188"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8f7dc0ec-6f5e-4c2c-b90e-69fa1bc3caa5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Probabilistic digital twin for continuous bridge performance modeling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752282","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The decisions about placing an ICD in a child are more difficult than in an adult due to longer expected lifespan and the complication risk. Young patients gain the most years from ICDs, despite higher risk of device-related complications. The secondary prevention ICD indication is clear, and device is implanted regardless of potential complications. For primary prevention, risk of sudden cardiac death and complications need to be evaluated. We aimed to compare outcomes for primary and secondary prevention ICDs. METHODS AND RESULTS: Retrospective nationwide cohort study including paediatric patients identified from the Danish ICD registry with ICD implanted at an age ≤ 15 from 1982-21. Demographics, complications (composite of device-related infections or lead-failure requiring re-operation, mortality because of arrhythmia, or unknown cause), and mortality were retrieved from medical charts. Endpoint was appropriate therapy (shock or anti-tachycardia pacing for ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation). Of 72 receiving an ICD, the majority had channelopathies (n = 34) or structural heart diseases (n = 28). ICDs were implanted in 23 patients for primary prevention and 49 for secondary prevention, at median ages of 13.8 and 11.6 years (P-value 0.01), respectively. Median follow-up was 9.0 (interquartile ranges: 4.7-13.5) years. The 10-year cumulative incidence of first appropriate therapy was 70%, with complication and inappropriate therapy rates at 41% and 15%, respectively. No difference was observed between prevention groups for all outcomes. Six patients died during follow-up. CONCLUSION: In children, two-thirds are secondary prevention ICDs. Children have higher appropriate therapy and complication rates than adults, while the inappropriate therapy rate was low.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Thuraiaiyah, Jani","Philbert, Berit Thornvig","Jensen, Annette Schophuus","Xing, Lucas Yixi","Joergensen, Troels Hoejsgaard","Lim, Chee Woon","Jakobsen, Frederikke Noerregaard","Bække, Pernille Steen","Schmidt, Michael Rahbek","Idorn, Lars","Holdgaard Smerup, Morten","Johansen, Jens Brock","Riahi, Sam","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","De Backer, Ole","Sondergaard, Lars","Jons, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762447"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Thuraiaiyah, Jani"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Laboratories","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Age Factors","Appropriate therapy","Arrhythmias Cardiac therapy","Child","Child Preschool","Congenital heart disease","Death Sudden Cardiac prevention control","Defibrillators Implantable","Denmark epidemiology","Electric Countershock instrumentation","Female","Humans","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Male","Paediatric cardiology","Primary prevention","Registries","Retrospective Studies","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Secondary Prevention methods","Sudden cardiac death","Tachycardia Ventricular therapy","Time Factors","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"implantable cardioverter defibrillator therapy in paediatric patients for primary vs secondary prevention","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euae245","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-762447","identifier":[{"id":"85205335271","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39345160","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11440178","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-b45e8d50-bf18-4702-b370-a64215f15084"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Age