tersen, Anne Suhr","orcid":"0000-0002-2621-4360","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lonny","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"ab6bde17-94c0-482d-bb34-495daa518640","name":"Stokholm, Lonny","orcid":"0000-0002-9727-6649","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","dansk oftalmologisk selskab","organization of danish ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8d6b9352-1174-4cea-ab6e-2fbbc6ad990c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diabetic retinopathy as an independent marker of cardiovascular disease in type 1 diabetes: results from a nationwide longitudinal matched case-cohort study.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-766162","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Information technology (IT) projects often fail. Postmortem analysis is not general practice in IT project management. This is a missed opportunity for IT project management because postmortem analysis is a proven source of practice improvements and preventive actions in other domains. In this article, the root causes of failure of a major IT project are identified by postmortem analysis, a well-established method for investigating accidents and failure ex post facto to improve practice and performance. The root causes of failure identified are: a) inadequate planning, b) novelty of a technology to the organization, and c) inappropriate software development method and process. The postmortem offers insights into risks and challenges that IT projects still face today. Significantly, the postmortem analysis shows how a different approach to project planning could have prevented the failure and termination of the project. This article also demonstrates how systematic IT project postmortem analysis can be conducted based on leading theory of process tracing and causal modeling in combination with the literature on IT project failure. The demonstration of this approach to IT project postmortems is new and original.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Schmidt, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776419"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Information technology","Process tracing","Project failure","Project management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an it project postmortem identifying root causes and eliminating rival explanations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107628214/An_IT_Project_Postmortem.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776419","identifier":[{"id":"85212413805","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-81dd829c-05a4-4e7f-a4ef-56e96d22cf2c"],"keyword":["Information technology","Process tracing","Project failure","Project management","Project postmortem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-90938CC44D8DE19A8C849DA13EF9CF93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107628214/An_IT_Project_Postmortem.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"e0edf6ca-5a14-41d8-81cc-77fd67f03ee5","name":"Schmidt, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-2500-0467","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15228053"],"journal":"Journal of Information Technology Case and Application Research","pages":"1-47","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Journal of Information Technology Case and Application Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212413805"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-81dd829c-05a4-4e7f-a4ef-56e96d22cf2c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An IT project postmortem : Identifying root causes and eliminating rival explanations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776419","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Novel Fiber Reinforcement Polymers (FRP) systems hold significant potential for future strengthening of existing structures; however, such systems may also add complexity to the structural assessment. Material properties and structural interaction can cause response deviation compared to conventional structures, affecting both SLS and ULS. The latter can be influenced significantly, as new and extended number of failure modes and complex interfacial interaction must be considered. A novel ductile prestressing Carbon Fiber Reinforcement Poly-mer (CFRP) strengthening system was designed to limit failure modes and provide a tailored ductile response. The paper describes some historical results, including several steps to provide such improvements. These are supplemented by recent indicational performance, fatigue-and temperature anchor test results additionally included. The anchor system seems excellent for controlling the strengthening utilization, response, and ductility. The system resisted the fatigue exposure in all tests. Exposure of the anchored CFRP prestressing system to cycles from 90°C to 8°C for 12 hours at each temperature limit did not seem to affect the anchorage resistance and stability, where only small temperature-generated deformations were measured.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Christensen, Christian Overgaard","Goltermann, P."],"cuid":["S02-085.19-755789"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, IABMAS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anchored response tailored prestressed cfrp strengthening preliminary long term and temperature investigations","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-468","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-085.19-755789","identifier":[{"id":"85200396379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-389bf361-2c98-4f14-bc44-c1e1d02fd49c","dtu-aae7e642-38fe-4e00-84ef-e1ffbee0a017"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F637CBC399EB1E0F49680B0BD3218A1E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/740057795/Anchored_response_tailored_prestressed_CFRP_strengthening_preliminary_long-term_and_temperature_investigations.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/372602601/Anchored_response_tailored_prestressed_CFRP_strengthening_preliminary_long-term_and_temperature_investigations.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-468","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Structures, Geotechnics and Risk","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Sustainable Structures, Materials and Construction Research Group"],"