{"abstract":"Plastic pollution is a pressing environmental challenge, necessitating the development of biodegradable alternatives like polyhydroxybutyrate (PHB). This study focuses on optimizing PHB production by Neobacillus niacini GS1, a bacterium isolated from a municipal dumping site. By utilizing agricultural residues such as corn flour, wheat bran, and peptone as substrates, we aimed to establish an eco-friendly method for biopolymer production, contributing to sustainable agricultural residue management and bioplastic innovation. The bacterium was identified using morphological, biochemical, and molecular techniques. The optimization process involved adjusting variables such as inoculum age, inoculum size, incubation time, agitation rate, incubation temperature, pH of the medium, carbon sources, and nitrogen sources. Response surface methodology (RSM) was employed to identify optimal conditions, with the highest PHB yield of 61.1% achieved under specific conditions: 37 °C, pH 7, and an agitation rate of 150 rpm. These findings underscore the potential of Neobacillus niacini GS1 in converting agro-industrial residues into valuable biopolymers, promoting sustainable bioplastic production, and advancing agricultural residue valorization efforts through the use of eco-friendly materials.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Shrimali, Gaurav","Gangawane, Ajit","Rami, Esha","Shah, Hardik","Thummar, Kashyap","Sahoo, Dipak Kumar","Patel, Ashish","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-792243"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Shrimali, Gaurav"],"country":["India","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ganpat University","Gujarat Technological University","Hemchandracharya North Gujarat University","Iowa State University","Parul University","Swaminarayan University"],"keyword":["Biodegradable plastics","Response surface methodology RSM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized polyhydroxybutyrate production by neobacillus niacini gs000000000001 utilizing corn flour wheat bran and peptone a sustainable approach","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomass4040064","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-792243","identifier":[{"id":"85213514841","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e8b33076-fb40-4554-9b44-a40f29380eef"],"keyword":["Neobacillus niacini GS1","agricultural residual","biodegradable plastics","biopolymer production","polyhydroxybutyrate (PHB)","response surface methodology (RSM)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-353BE53ABFD4B4689469E505A7C096B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomass4040064","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/280605269/Optimized_Polyhydroxybutyrate_Production_by_Neobacillus_niacini_GS1_Utilizing_Corn_Flour_Wheat_Bran_and_Peptone_A_Sustainable_Approach.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"gujarat technological university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Gujarat Technological University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"parul university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Parul University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"swaminarayan university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Swaminarayan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"in","key":"ganpat university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Ganpat University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"iowa state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Iowa State University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"in","key":"hemchandracharya north gujarat university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Hemchandracharya North Gujarat University","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gaurav","key":"shrimalipau","last":"Shrimali","name":"Shrimali, Gaurav","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ajit","key":"gangawanepau","last":"Gangawane","name":"Gangawane, Ajit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Esha","key":"ramipau","last":"Rami","name":"Rami, Esha","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hardik","key":"shahpau","last":"Shah","name":"Shah, Hardik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kashyap","key":"thummarpau","last":"Thummar","name":"Thummar, Kashyap","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Dipak Kumar","key":"sahoopau","last":"Sahoo","name":"Sahoo, Dipak Kumar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashish","key":"patelpau","last":"Patel","name":"Patel, Ashish","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/biomass4040064","issn":["26738783"],"issue":"4","journal":"Biomass","pages":"116