, Laura","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter-Martin","key":"kraruppau","last":"Krarup","name":"Krarup, Peter-Martin","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","name":"Pfeiffer, Per","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"qvortruppau","last":"Qvortrup","name":"Qvortrup, Camilla","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39692004"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/sla.0000000000006611","issn":["00034932","15281140"],"issn_org":["00034932"],"journal":"Annals of Surgery","paperid":"10.1097/SLA.0000000000006611","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"e","title":"Annals of Surgery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212944416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["aau-f4826155-7b8b-42aa-aeeb-f44a539e4ead","au-e038ae03-ffe3-4334-b2cf-e479248056cc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Neoadjuvant Pembrolizumab in Stage I-III Deficient Mismatch Repair Colon Cancer: A Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.84-784965","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Opioids used to manage severe pain in acute pancreatitis (AP) might exacerbate the disease through effects on gastrointestinal and immune functions. Methylnaltrexone, a peripherally acting µ-opioid receptor antagonist, may counteract these effects without changing analgesia. METHODS: This double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial included adult patients with AP and systemic inflammatory response syndrome at 4 Danish centers. Patients were randomized to receive 5 days of continuous intravenous methylnaltrexone (0.15 mg/kg/d) or placebo added to the standard of care. The primary end point was the Pancreatitis Activity Scoring System score after 48 hours of treatment. Main secondary outcomes included pain scores, opioid use, disease severity, and mortality. RESULTS: In total, 105 patients (54% men) were randomized to methylnaltrexone (n = 51) or placebo (n = 54). After 48 hours, the Pancreatitis Activity Scoring System score was 134.3 points in the methylnaltrexone group and 130.5 points in the placebo group (difference 3.8, 95% confidence interval [CI] -40.1 to 47.6; P = 0.87). At 48 hours, we found no differences between the groups in pain severity (0.0, 95% CI -0.8 to 0.9; P = 0.94), pain interference (-0.3, 95% CI -1.4 to 0.8; P = 0.55), and morphine equivalent doses (6.5 mg, 95% CI -2.1 to 15.2; P = 0.14). Methylnaltrexone also did not affect the risk of severe disease (8%, 95% CI -11 to 28; P = 0.38) and mortality (6%, 95% CI -1 to 12; P = 0.11). The medication was well tolerated. DISCUSSION: Methylnaltrexone treatment did not achieve superiority over placebo for reducing the severity of AP.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Knoph, Cecilie Siggaard","Cook, Mathias Ellgaard","Novovic, Srdan","Hansen, Mark Berner","Mortensen, Michael Bau","Nielsen, Liv Bjerre Juul","Høgsberg, Irene Maria","Salomon, Celina","Neergaard, Celine Emilie Lindqvist","Aajwad, Aseel Jabbar","Pandanaboyana, Sanjay","Schmidt Sørensen, Lone","Thorlacius-Ussing, Ole","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Olesen, Søren Schou","Drewes, Asbjørn Mohr"],"cuid":["S03-099.23-766730"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Drewes, Asbjørn Mohr"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Freeman Hospital","Newcastle upon Tyne Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Adult","Aged","Analgesics Opioid therapeutic use","Double Blind Method","Female","Humans","Male","Methylnaltrexone","Middle Aged","Naltrexone analogs derivatives","Narcotic Antagonists therapeutic use","Opioids","Pain Measurement","Pancreatitis","Pancreatitis drug therapy","Severity","Severity of Illness Index","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no effect of methylnaltrexone on acute pancreatitis severity a multicenter randomized controlled trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14309/ajg.0000000000002904","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.23-766730","identifier":[{"id":"85208514904","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38916223","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11524628","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-647ac330-8892-4a9d-bb99-436276bf17d1","ku-3f6fda42-4a08-4f58-8003-d6a13a8fae0c","sdu-8994d5a9-5e14-46b0-a35b-3a7e5e862ac3"],"keyword":["Acute Disease","Adult","Aged","Analgesics, Opioid/therapeutic use","Double-Blind Method","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Naltrexone/analogs & derivatives","Narcotic An