alth","status":"p","title":"The American Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208514904"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-647ac330-8892-4a9d-bb99-436276bf17d1","ku-3f6fda42-4a08-4f58-8003-d6a13a8fae0c","sdu-8994d5a9-5e14-46b0-a35b-3a7e5e862ac3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"No Effect of Methylnaltrexone on Acute Pancreatitis Severity: A Multicenter Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.23-766730","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Context Current guidelines for exercise-related glucose management focus on reducing bolus and/or basal insulin doses and considering carbohydrate intake. Yet far less attention has been paid to the potential role of other macronutrients alongside carbohydrates on glucose dynamics around exercise. Objective To investigate the effects of a low-carbohydrate-high-protein (LCHP) compared with a high-carbohydrate-low-protein (HCLP) pre-exercise meal on the metabolic, hormonal, and physiological responses to exercise in adults with insulin pump–treated type 1 diabetes. Methods Fourteen adults (11 women, 3 men) with insulin pump–treated type 1 diabetes (median [range] HbA1c of 50 [43-59] mmol/mol (6.7% [6.1%-7.5%]), age of 49 [25-65] years, and body mass index of 24.0 [19.3-27.1] kg/m2) completed an unblinded, 2-arm, randomized, crossover study. Participants ingested isocaloric meals that were either LCHP (carbohydrate 21%, protein 52%, fat 27%) or HCLP (carbohydrate 52%, protein 21%, fat 27%) 90 minutes prior to undertaking 45 minutes of cycling at moderate intensity. Meal insulin bolus was dosed according to meal carbohydrate content but reduced by 25%. Basal insulin rates were reduced by 35% from meal ingestion to end of exercise. Results Around exercise the coefficient of variability was lower during LCHP (LCHP: 14.5 ± 5.3 vs HCLP: 24.9 ± 7.7%, P = .001). Over exercise, LCHP was associated with a lesser drop (LCHP: Δ−1.49 ± 1.89 vs HCLP: Δ−3.78 ± 1.95 mmol/L, P = .001). Mean insulin concentration was 30% lower during exercise for LCHP compared with HCLP (LCHP: 25.5 ± 11.0 vs HCLP: 36.5 ± 15.9 mU/L, P < .001). Conclusion Ingesting a LCHP pre-exercise meal lowered plasma glucose variability around exercise and diminished the drop in plasma glucose over exercise.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kristensen, Kasper B.","Ranjan, Ajenthen G.","Mccarthy, Olivia M.","Holst, Jens Juul","Bracken, Richard M.","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Schmidt, Signe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720640"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swansea University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of a low carbohydrate high protein pre exercise meal in type 000000000001 diabetes a randomized crossover trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385583167/Effects_of_a_Low_Carbohydrate_High_Protein.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720640","identifier":[{"id":"85181177680","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37463489","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6fc79931-29ab-4970-aa9c-37ee53da11d5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-954EC4B6A4718F8CE907246B8034E50F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385583167/Effects_of_a_Low_Carbohydrate_High_Protein.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"swansea university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swansea University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper B.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Kasper B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ajenthen G.","key":"ranjanpau","last":"Ranjan","name":"Ranjan, Ajenthen G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olivia M.","key":"mccarthypau","last":"Mccarthy","name":"Mccarthy, Olivia M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Richard M.","key":"brackenpau","last":"Bracken","name":"Bracken, Richard M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Signe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37463489"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgad427","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"208-216","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181177680"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6fc79931-29ab-4970-aa9c-37ee53da11d5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of a Low-Carbohydrate-High-Protein Pre-Exercise Meal in Type 1 Diabetes—a Randomized Crossover Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720640","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Hay-Schmidt, Anders","Høeg, Jens Thorvald"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739850"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"obituary claus nielsen march 000000000028th 000000001938 january 000000000018th 000000002024","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-739850","ids":["ku-ce4bf8ec-6c31-40b0-b568-e609989a8416"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7FDF1B80D10F1CF2D17DF5C92C42D027"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Odontology, Section 03 - Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"hayschmidtpau","last":"Hay-Schmidt","locid":"f0f495a2-fe48-4cdf-8f27-ea207182bda8","name":"Hay-Schmidt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9984-7014","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens T.","key":"hoegpau","last":"Hoeg","locid":"3d3d3a77-d688-427f-b3d1-605ff0969ecc","name":"Høeg, Jens Thorvald","name_org":"Hoeg, Jens T.","orcid":"0000-0002-3596-1691","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00435-024-00656-5","issn":["0720213X","1432234X"],"issn_org":["03406725"],"journal":"Zoomorphology","pages":"1-3","status":"p","title":"Zoomorphology","volume":"143"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ce4bf8ec-6c31-40b0-b568-e609989a8416"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Obituary: Claus Nielsen (March 28th, 1938–January 18th, 2024)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739850","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Circular economy is the central strategy in the EU chosen to decrease today’s overconsumption of raw materials extracted from nature. Due to the vast amounts of raw materials used in the building and construction sector, it is pointed out as a key sector. At the end of life of structures, reuse of whole components is rated over recovery of materials for pro-duction of new components. The cases found in literature that relate bridge engineering and reuse are limited to a case on reuse of cut out concrete blocks in a pedestrian bridge. Related to buildings, there is more literature on reuse (though less than 100), so reuse is still very far from being mainstream. Learnings from reuse of the structural elements in buildings could inspire reuse in relation to bridges, however, there are no cases of reuse to the full strength potential. The barriers towards implementation of circular principles are several and can are categorized as: economic, sociological, political, organizational, technological, and environmental. The potential risks associated with structural safety when reusing elements need to be overcome by the development of methodologies for strength estimations and durability assessment","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ottosen, Lisbeth M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-746416"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"innovations in buildings and bridge engineering associated with circular economy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-746416","identifier":[{"id":"85200420503","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-317cdb9f-6590-4bc9-8ee2-40ce5c74c507"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A67BC8CE8C8D116A817BB1A3BCF84599"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/364702517/Ottosen2024_Bridge_Maintenance_Safety_Management_Digitalization_and_Sustainability_First_Edition.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Materials & Durability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L. M.","key":"ottosenpau","last":"Ottosen","locid":"653cfe69-d98d-42ec-b241-5409bbfc951c","name":"Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","name_org":"Ottosen, L. M.","orcid":"0000-0001-7756-382X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Sandager","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens Sandager","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan M.","key":"frangopolpedh","last":"Frangopol","name":"Frangopol, Dan M.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003483755-8","isbn":["9781032770406"],"pages":"85-92","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management","title":"Bridge Maintenance, Safety, Management, Digitalization and Sustainability"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200420503"],"sdg":["12. Responsible Consumption and Production","8. Decent Work and Economic Growth","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-317cdb9f-6590-4bc9-8ee2-40ce5c74c507"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Innovations in buildings and bridge engineering associated with circular economy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-746416","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Cardiovascular (CV) disease is the leading cause of death in patients with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) receiving hemodialysis (HD). The two major marine n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids (n-3 PUFAs) eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) and docosahexaenoic acid (DHA) may have cardioprotective effects. This study aimed to investigate the predictive value of plasma n-3 PUFAs on CV events and all-cause mortality in patients with ESRD receiving HD.A validated prospective multicenter cohort study of 336 patients with ESRD receiving HD with 5 years of follow-up was conducted. Blood samples were collected at baseline and analyzed for the plasma levels of EPA and DHA expressed as a weight percentage (wt%) of total plasma fatty acids. The primary outcome was CV events defined as acute myocardial infarction, unstable angina pectoris, stroke, transient ischemic attack, peripheral artery disease (PAD), or cardiovascular mortality. The secondary outcomes were all-cause mortality and each individual component of CV events. The sum of EPA and DHA (EPA+DHA) was used in all analyses and expressed as n-3 PUFAs in wt%. The population was divided into three groups according to n-3 PUFA tertiles. Kaplan-Meier curves and multivariable Cox regressions adjusted for relevant confounders were used to analyze the association between plasma n-3 PUFA levels and study outcomes.Median follow-up time was 5.05 years (IQR, 5.02-5.07). Mean age was 65 ± 15 years and plasma n-3 PUFA levels ranged from 2.1 to 16.8 wt%, with a median of 5.7 wt% (IQR, 4.72-6.96 wt%). During follow-up 60% of the cohort died, 17% died of CV disease, and 42% had a CV event. Figure 1 shows the unadjusted associations between the plasma n-3 PUFA tertiles and the risk of CV events. A n-3 PUFA level between 5.06-6.52 wt% was associated with a 36% lower risk of CV events [unadjusted HR 0.64 (95% CI 0.43-0.96)]. Additionally, a n-3 PUFA level above 6.52 wt% was associated with a 34% lower risk of CV events [unadjusted HR 0.66 (95% CI 0.44-0.98)], both in comparison to levels below 5.06 wt%. After adjusting for relevant confounders, as shown in Figure 2, n-3 PUFA levels between 5.06 to 6.52 wt% were associated with a significantly lower risk of CV events [adjusted HR 0.60 (95% CI 0.40-0.92)], PAD [adjusted HR 0.44 (95% CI 0.22-0.88)], and all-cause mortality [adjusted HR 0.61 (95% CI 0.42-0.86)], when compared to levels below 5.06 wt%.In this study of patients with ESRD receiving HD, a low plasma level of n-3 PUFA was associated with a higher risk of CV events, peripheral artery disease, and all-cause mortality.Figure 1:Kaplan-Meier curves illustrating the absolute risk of cardiovascular (CV) events according to n-3 PUFA tertiles. CV events were defined as acute myocardial infarction, unstable angina pectoris, stroke, transient ischemic attack, peripheral artery disease, or cardiovascular mortality. Years on the X-axis and absolute risk of CV events on the Y-axis. The number of patients alive during follow-up is illustrated below the figure. N-3 PUFA n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acid.Figure 2:Event rates and multivariable Cox regressions examining the associations between n-3 PUFA tertiles and cardiovascular outcomes. Adjusted for age, sex, diabetes mellitus, smoking status, and a history of previous cardiovascular disease. N-3 PUFA n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acid, HR hazard ratio, CI confidence interval. *Cardiovascular events include acute myocardial infarction, unstable angina pectoris, stroke, transient ischemic attack, peripheral artery disease, and cardiovascular mortality.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liboriussen, Caroline Hundborg","Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Jensen, Jens Dam","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Glerup, Rie Io","Svensson, My"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752051"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-26","place":"Stockholm, se","start":"2024-05-23","title":"61th ERA Congress","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"marine n 000000000003 polyunsaturated fatty acids and cardiovascular events in patients with end stage renal disease receiving hemodialysis","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-752051","ids":["aau-261f7c02-1f56-4e29-a3a6-e37a98cfbc4d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8D916566630662F3F8FEBF20CB2A94F5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nephrology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central and West Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline Hundborg","key":"liboriussenpau","last":"Liboriussen","locid":"c3a31b77-ac83-417d-825f-ec3539d64516","name":"Liboriussen, Caroline Hundborg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","name_org":"Nygaard, Louis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Dam","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5925bf6b-6811-4844-a49d-d3eac405cc90","name":"Jensen, Jens Dam","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Berg","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"3eff6ccc-90b4-48ee-b121-8df4865f0342","name":"Schmidt, Erik Berg","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-5666","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rie","key":"gleruppau","last":"Glerup","locid":"44949bea-9f63-484e-a74c-16bc7330bc40","name":"Glerup, Rie Io","name_org":"Glerup, Rie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"My","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"0ed91c60-a2c2-44d5-b7f5-c17fb1318c47","name":"Svensson, My","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ndt/gfae069.871","issn":["09310509","14602385"],"issn_org":["09310509"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","title_org":"Nephrology, Dialysis, Transplantation","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-261f7c02-1f56-4e29-a3a6-e37a98cfbc4d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Marine n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids and cardiovascular events in patients with end-stage renal disease receiving hemodialysis","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752051","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Danish Road Directorate has developed a guideline for proof loading of road bridges. The guideline ensures that proof load tests are planned and executed in a consistent manner and that test results may be used to update the load-carrying capacity of the considered bridge. The guideline describes how proof load tests may be planned, executed, and interpreted to demonstrate that the considered bridge can withstand a given load with sufficient reliability. One of the primary hypotheses is that many bridges have a load-carrying capacity that may be larger than the one determined by traditional computational analysis. This is mainly because the computational models, that are used to determine the load carrying capacity, of a given bridge does not predict the actual response of the considered bridge with sufficient accuracy. Most models are inherently conservative and underestimates the actual load carrying capacity of the considered bridge. Load testing is a cost-effective method to demonstrate that a given bridge has a sufficient load carrying capacity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Engelund, S.","Sørensen, John Dalsgaard","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","von Scholten, C.","Bang, R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752498"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, IABMAS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Vejdirektoratet"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a guideline for proof loading of bridges","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-37","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752498","identifier":[{"id":"85200361045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-eb708dcf-8f7a-435d-bbe7-9b976465ac00"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-751451B4FDEE672B994F62C6D0174362"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-37","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/752005999/10.1201_9781003483755-37_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Danish Centre for Risk and Safety Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Structures, Geotechnics and Risk","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Risk, Resilience, Safety, and Sustainability of Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Vejdirektoratet"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"engelundpau","last":"Engelund","name":"Engelund, S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. D.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"6fe22c77-cd3d-4e06-9337-3f870be8f135","name":"Sørensen, John Dalsgaard","name_org":"Sørensen, J. D.","orcid":"0000-0001-6987-6877","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. W.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"c6a9ee27-7ba7-4074-8f67-1a082d871faa","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","name_org":"Schmidt, J. W.","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"vonscholtenpau","last":"von Scholten","name":"von Scholten, C.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","name":"Bang, R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Sandager","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens Sandager","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan M.","key":"frangopolpedh","last":"Frangopol","name":"Frangopol, Dan M.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003483755-37","eisbn":["9781003483755"],"isbn":["9781032770406","9781032775609"],"pages":"350-357","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, 24-28 june 2024, Copenhagen, Denmark","title":"Bridge Maintenance, Safety, Management, Digitalization and Sustainability"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200361045"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-eb708dcf-8f7a-435d-bbe7-9b976465ac00"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Development of a guideline for proof loading of bridges","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752498","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Veno-arterial extracorporeal membrane oxygenation (VA-ECMO) with profound left ventricular (LV) failure is associated with inadequate LV emptying. To unload the LV, VA-ECMO can be combined with Impella CP (ECMELLA). We hypothesized that ECMELLA improves cardiac energetics compared with VA-ECMO in a porcine model of cardiogenic shock (CS). METHODS AND RESULTS: Land-race pigs (weight 70 kg) were instrumented, including a LV conductance catheter and a carotid artery Doppler flow probe. CS was induced with embolization in the left main coronary artery. CS was defined as reduction of ≥50% in cardiac output or mixed oxygen saturation (SvO 2) or a SvO 2 < 30%. At CS VA-ECMO was initiated and embolization was continued until arterial pulse pressure was <10 mmHg. At this point, Impella CP was placed in the ECMELLA arm. Support was maintained for 4 h. CS was induced in 15 pigs (VA-ECMO n = 7, ECMELLA n = 8). At time of CS MAP was <45 mmHg in both groups, with no difference at 4 h (VA-ECMO 64 mmHg ± 11 vs. ECMELLA 55 mmHg ± 21, P = 0.08). Carotid blood flow and arterial lactate increased from CS and was similar in VA-ECMO and ECMELLA [239 mL/min ± 97 vs. 213 mL/min ± 133 (P = 0.6) and 5.2 ± 3.3 vs. 4.2 ± 2.9 mmol/ (P = 0.5)]. Pressure-volume area (PVA) was significantly higher with VA-ECMO compared with ECMELLA (9567 ± 1733 vs. 6921 ± 5036 mmHg × mL/min × 10 -3, P = 0.014). Total diureses was found to be lower in VA-ECMO compared with ECMELLA [248 mL (179-930) vs. 506 mL (418-2190); P = 0.005]. CONCLUSIONS: In a porcine model of CS, we found lower PVA, with the ECMELLA configuration compared with VA-ECMO, indicating better cardiac energetics without compromising systemic perfusion.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Peter H.","Linde, Louise","Gregers, Emilie","Udesen, Nanna Louise Junker","Helgestad, Ole Kristian Lerche","Banke, Ann","Dahl, Jordi Sanchez","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Larsen, Jeppe P.","Schmidt, Henrik","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-755487"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Frederiksen, Peter H."],"keyword":["Animals","Cardiogenic shock","Disease Models Animal","ECMELLA","Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation methods","Heart Assist Devices","Hemodynamics physiology","Impella","Pressure volume loops","Shock Cardiogenic therapy","Swine","VA ECMO"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"haemodynamic implications of va ecmo vs va ecmo plus impella cp for cardiogenic shock in a large animal model","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ehf2.14780","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-755487","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11287291","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85191153245","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38649295","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-9ec5f08b-0cef-46dd-b3ad-a784ad27067f"],"keyword":["Animals","Cardiogenic shock","Disease Models, Animal","ECMELLA","Extracorporeal Membrane Oxygenation/methods","Heart-Assist Devices","Hemodynamics/physiology","Impella","Pressure-volume loops","Shock, Cardiogenic/therapy","Swine","VA-ECMO"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F05684D599459DF0B9CD099883CB6F33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/268641892/ESC_Heart_Failure_-_2024_-_Frederiksen_-_Haemodynamic_implications_of_VA_ECMO_vs_VA_ECMO_plus_Impella_CP_for_cardiogenic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/1