f Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","private practice ølsemaglevej"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b541ba10-d828-4066-a572-44606a355a1c","ku-9d1945fe-0b09-4195-93f8-cd839304b846","nfa-1ed6a668-cf82-4f8c-8fa8-6a85a426195c","sdu-3711c9b5-23ce-412e-ba33-e4a257373b36"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Meta-analysis of ACE inhibitor–induced angioedema identifies novel risk locus","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-091.21-767798","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: We provide an overview of nationwide environmental data available for Denmark and its linkage potentials to individual-level records with the aim of promoting research on the potential impact of the local surrounding environment on human health. BACKGROUND: Researchers in Denmark have unique opportunities for conducting large population-based studies treating the entire Danish population as one big, open and dynamic cohort based on nationally complete population and health registries. So far, most research in this area has utilised individual- and family-level information to study the clustering of disease in families, comorbidities, risk of, and prognosis after, disease onset, and social gradients in disease risk. Linking environmental data in time and space to individuals enables novel possibilities for studying the health effects of the social, built and physical environment. METHODS: We describe the possible linkage between individuals and their local surrounding environment to establish the exposome - that is, the total environmental exposure of an individual over their life course. CONCLUSIONS: The currently available nationwide longitudinal environmental data in Denmark constitutes a valuable and globally rare asset that can help explore the impact of the exposome on human health.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Horsdal, Henriette Thisted","Pedersen, Marianne Giørtz","Schullehner, Jörg","Østergaard, Cecilie Schmidt","McGrath, John J","Agerbo, Esben","Timmermann, Allan","Closter, Ane Marie","Brandt, Jørgen","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Frohn, Lise Marie","Geels, Camilla","Ketzel, Matthias","Khan, Jibran","Ørby, Pia Viuf","Olsen, Yulia","Levin, Gregor","Svenning, Jens Christian","Engemann, Kristine","Gyldenkærne, Steen","Hansen, Birgitte","Hertel, Ole","Sabel, Clive E","Erikstrup, Christian","Sigsgaard, Torben","Pedersen, Carsten Bøcker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-675269"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Greenland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","University of Queensland","University of Surrey"],"keyword":["Environment","Exposome","Health","Population","Registers"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perspectives on environment and health research in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/14034948231178076","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-675269","identifier":[{"id":"37278162","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11308320","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85162962548","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-865d4caf-4b8e-4a51-b748-b1c36608570a"],"keyword":["Environment","exposome","health","population","registers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6981B28623E09079C646E111F591D4A4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/375816481/horsdal-et-al-2023-perspectives-on-environment-and-health-research-in-denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/14034948231178076","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - National Centre for Register-based Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country"