{"abstract":"Proof load testing is increasingly used to assess existing road bridges. The load configuration of a proof load test is however an open research question and approaches vary in the literature. To the author’s knowledge, a comprehensive comparison of different load configuration approaches is not available in the literature. As part of a Danish bridge testing project a literature study has been carried out regarding proof load configurations. This paper presents part of this study with an emphasis on comparison between the Danish approach and approaches using the Eurocodes LM1. A brief state-of-the-art is presented. Following this, proof load configurations calculated from Danish codes and guidelines are compared with LM1 approaches. The results indicate numerous benefits of a bridge classification system like the Danish. The research may inspire a common European bridge classification system, ultimately paving the way for better utilization of bridges through proof loading.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Damsgaard, K. D.S.","Engelund, S.","Sørensen, John Dalsgaard","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Christensen, Christian Overgaard","von Scholten, C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752096"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, IABMAS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Vejdirektoratet"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COWI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COWI","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparative study of proof load configurations related to bridge classification","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-34","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752096","identifier":[{"id":"85200332878","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3e1b11fe-4d83-4e7d-825d-9fe139ae1295"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F10DBF14E11DA03F31590B4AD458342"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/740056452/A_comparative_study_of_proof_load_configurations_related_to_bridge_classification.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-34","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cowi","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COWI","l3nl":"COWI A/S","l3nn":"COWI","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"COWI","namevar":["COWI A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COWI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Danish Centre for Risk and Safety Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Structures, Geotechnics and Risk","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Risk, Resilience, Safety, and Sustainability of Systems Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Vejdirektoratet"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K. D.S.","key":"damsgaardpau","last":"Damsgaard","name":"Damsgaard, K. D.S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"engelundpau","last":"Engelund","name":"Engelund, S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. D.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"6fe22c77-cd3d-4e06-9337-3f870be8f135","name":"Sørensen, John Dalsgaard","name_org":"Sørensen, J. D.","orcid":"0000-0001-6987-6877","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. W.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"c6a9ee27-7ba7-4074-8f67-1a082d871faa","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","name_org":"Schmidt, J. W.","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C. O.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"60cf4289-69b1-4285-b6ff-528bc3ffaf67","name":"Christensen, Christian Overgaard","name_org":"Christensen, C. O.","orcid":"0000-0002-6334-9280","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"vonscholtenpau","last":"von Scholten","name":"von Scholten, C.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Sandager","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens Sandager","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan M.","key":"frangopolpedh","last":"Frangopol","name":"Frangopol, Dan M.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003483755-34","eisbn":["9781003483755"],"isbn":["9781032770406","9781032775609"],"pages":"323-331","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, 24-28 june 2024, Copenhagen, Denmark","title":"Bridge Maintenance, Safety, Management, Digitalization and Sustainability"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200332878"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","COWI A/S","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3e1b11fe-4d83-4e7d-825d-9fe139ae1295"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A comparative study of proof load configurations related to bridge classification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752096","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"When performing vibration tests on bridges, engineers face the challenge of extracting the global dynamic properties of these structures from the vibration responses measured at several degrees of freedom. In this paper, the new subspace-based poly-Reference Complex Frequency (SpCF) technique is applied to the vibration measurements of a large span bridge. The advantage of the SpCF with regard to other modal or system identification techniques is that it provides robust estimates for the modal properties, which leads to very clear stabilization diagrams. In order to assess the performance of the new SpCF, its estimates for the modal properties of the aforementioned bridge are compared to those of the poly-reference Least Squares Complex Frequency (pLSCF, also known by its commercial name polymax), which is deemed as a standard technique in experimental and operational modal analysis.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Amador, Sandro","Gaile, L.","Brincker, R.","Ventura, C. E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759307"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Latvia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Riga Technical University","University of British Columbia"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust modal identification of a large span bridge with the new spcf technique","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-181","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759307","identifier":[{"id":"85200318158","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d9f6931e-9104-4299-9147-d7b8470a5a57"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9623094319FB58BD505511906F1EF7B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-181","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering and Structural Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"lv","key":"riga technical university","loc":["Latvia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Riga Technical University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Brincker Monitoring ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S. D. R.","key":"amadorpau","last":"Amador","locid":"3e53da0b-d147-43c5-8eea-c9214bae8d48","name":"Amador, Sandro","name_org":"Amador, S. D. R.","orcid":"0000-0003-3045-2916","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"gailepau","last":"Gaile","name":"Gaile, L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"brinckerpau","last":"Brincker","name":"Brincker, R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"C. E.","key":"venturapau","last":"Ventura","name":"Ventura, C. E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"sandagerjensenpedh","last":"Sandager Jensen","name":"Sandager Jensen, Jens","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan","key":"mfrangopolpedh","last":"M. Frangopol","name":"M. Frangopol, Dan","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"wittrupschmidtpedh","last":"Wittrup Schmidt","name":"Wittrup Schmidt, Jacob","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003483755-181","isbn":["9781032770406"],"pages":"1547-1555","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management","title":"Bridge Maintenance, Safety, Management, Digitalization and Sustainability"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200318158"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","brincker monitoring aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d9f6931e-9104-4299-9147-d7b8470a5a57"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Robust modal identification of a large-span bridge with the new SpCF technique","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759307","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose of Review: In the presented review, we have summarized and highlighted recent developments in the use of lignin peroxidase (LiP) to remove a variety of pollutants from water matrices. The high redox potential of LiP is underlined by its excellent catalytic functionalities in the elimination of pharmaceuticals, phenolics, dyes, polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs), endocrine-disrupting chemicals (EDCs), and other miscellaneous pollutants. LiP-based computational frameworks for theoretical bioremediation of multiple pollutants have also been discussed, which have prompted a rise in scientific interest. Recent Findings: According to current studies, both free and immobilized LiPs are biocatalysts capable of efficient pollutant degradation and LMW transformation. Some immobilized LiP preparations demonstrated excellent recyclability, enabling its reusability in multiple catalytic cycles. Additionally, computational degradability makes it easier to comprehend the mechanisms underlying the degradation of recalcitrant pollutants. Summary: The capacity of LiP to cleave C–C and C–O–C bonds has led to its widespread application as a biocatalyst. Its outstanding potential to catalyze oxidative cleavage has been effectively used in the remediation of pollutants without needing mediators. Nevertheless, we brought attention to the current LiP system in pollutants remediation and computational framework, which has generated a significant rise in scientific interest.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Singh, Anil Kumar","Fernandez-Lafuente, Roberto","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Boczkaj, Grzegorz","Bilal, Muhammad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-761110"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bilal, Muhammad"],"country":["India","Poland","Spain"],"glorg":["Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR)","All Global Affiliations","CSIR-Indian Institute of Toxicology Research","Campus of International Excellence UAM+CSIC","Gdańsk University of Technology"],"keyword":["Antibiotics degradation","Bioremediation","Environmental Pollutants","Environmental biotechnology","Wastewater treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biocatalytic functionalities of lignin peroxidase based systems in lignin depolymerization and pollutants removal from environmental matrices","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40726-024-00310-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-761110","identifier":[{"id":"85191723543","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-a32d98da-280a-4cf4-bbd4-7371eb13b633"],"keyword":["Antibiotics degradation","Bioremediation","Environmental biotechnology","Environmental pollutants","Redox reaction","Wastewater treatment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2182B4399EE330AAE8969AD3A4DCBF78"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/269164148/Biocatalytic_Functionalities_of_Lignin_Peroxidase-Based_Systems_in_Lignin_Depolymerization_and_Pollutants_Removal_from_Environmental_Matrices.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40726-024-00310-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"csir indian institute of toxicology research","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"CSIR-Indian Institute of Toxicology Research","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"academy of scientific and innovative research","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"campus of international excellence uam csic","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Campus of International Excellence UAM+CSIC","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"pl","key":"gdańsk university of technology","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Gdańsk University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anil Kumar","key":"singhpau","last":"Singh","name":"Singh, Anil Kumar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Roberto","key":"fernandezlafuentepau","last":"Fernandez-Lafuente","name":"Fernandez-Lafuente, Roberto","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Grzegorz","key":"boczkajpau","last":"Boczkaj","name":"Boczkaj, Grzegorz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Muhammad","key":"bilalpau","last":"Bilal","name":"Bilal, Muhammad","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40726-024-00310-0","issn":["21986592"],"issue":"3","journal":"Current Pollution Reports","pages":"345-361","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Current Pollution Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191723543"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a32d98da-280a-4cf4-bbd4-7371eb13b633"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Biocatalytic Functionalities of Lignin Peroxidase-Based Systems in Lignin Depolymerization and Pollutants Removal from Environmental Matrices","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-761110","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy (ICP) is one of the most common hepatic disorders during pregnancy, and the etiology is thought to be multifactorial including both environmental and hormonal contributions. In twin pregnancies, the fetal and placental mass is generally greater than in singleton pregnancies, and is, theoretically, likely to have a greater influence upon the maternal hepatic metabolism compared to singleton pregnancy. The aim of this study was to compare ICP in twin and singleton pregnancies according to ICP characteristics, time of diagnosis, serum bile acid levels, pharmacological treatment, and pregnancy outcomes. Material and Methods: This case control study was undertaken at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, from 2012 to 2019. The study comprised 51 women with twin pregnancies and ICP. These women were matched with 153 women with twin pregnancies without ICP and 153 women with singleton pregnancies with ICP, respectively. Three controls were matched per case, and data obtained from medical records and Danish obstetrical databases were compared. Results: We found a significantly lower gestational age at ICP diagnosis in twin pregnancies (227 vs. 242 days for singleton pregnancies; p = 0.002). Bile acids reached significantly higher maximum blood levels in twin pregnancies (32.9 vs. 22.2 μmol/L; p = 0.012), and at a lower gestational age (gestational age maximum bile acids: 235 vs. 250 days; p < 0.001). No difference in pharmacological treatment was observed between the groups. Twin pregnancies with and without ICP had comparable pregnancy outcomes; however, ICP pregnancies had a higher incidence of gestational diabetes mellitus (15.7% vs. 5.2%; p = 0.03). In repeat pregnancies, ICP was diagnosed earlier in the twin pregnancy (p = 0.006). Conclusions: Compared to singleton pregnancies, twin pregnant women with ICP have an earlier diagnosis of ICP, and levels of bile acids are higher. Compared to twin pregnancies without ICP, the pregnancy outcomes are comparable.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Axelsen, Silja Maigaard","Schmidt, Maria Cathrine","Kampmann, Ulla","Grønbæk, Henning","Fuglsang, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762891"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Axelsen, Silja Maigaard"],"keyword":["Intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy","Liver","Obstetrics","Pregnancy Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of twin pregnancy in intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy a case control study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aogs.14928","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-762891","identifier":[{"id":"85199793512","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11426215","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39058263","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-33414f08-5c96-4d90-8805-1c8bc56f5ebc"],"keyword":["Gemelli","intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy","liver","obstetrics","pregnancy outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6942DD6DA3EF4360E6669FC2985A377C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aogs.14928","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Silja Maigaard","key":"axelsenpau","last":"Axelsen","name":"Axelsen, Silja Maigaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Cathrine","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"35d5dfba-0d1e-45f2-9eb3-d07643dad3eb","name":"Schmidt, Maria Cathrine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulla","key":"kampmannpau","last":"Kampmann","locid":"26c25195-6d9d-4899-9737-e1c0b09bec29","name":"Kampmann, Ulla","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"32aaf9c5-5cf0-4e7b-86d8-a534fa4a9ae9","name":"Grønbæk, Henning","orcid":"0000-0001-8998-7910","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"fuglsangpau","last":"Fuglsang","locid":"cdc88d13-8dab-4cc1-80e3-b9d85b484e90","name":"Fuglsang, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-1986","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39058263"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aogs.14928","issn":["00016349"],"issue":"10","journal":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","pages":"1994-2001","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","volume":"103"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199793512"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-33414f08-5c96-4d90-8805-1c8bc56f5ebc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effect of twin pregnancy in intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy : A case control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-762891","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Open Databases Integration for Materials Design (OPTIMADE) application programming interface (API) empowers users with holistic access to a growing federation of databases, enhancing the accessibility and discoverability of materials and chemical data. Since the first release of the OPTIMADE specification (v1.0), the API has undergone significant development, leading to the v1.2 release, and has underpinned multiple scientific studies. In this work, we highlight the latest features of the API format, accompanying software tools, and provide an update on the implementation of OPTIMADE in contributing materials databases. We end by providing several use cases that demonstrate the utility of the OPTIMADE API in materials research that continue to drive its ongoing development.","author_count":59,"contributors":["Evans, Matthew L.","Bergsma, Johan","Merkys, Andrius","Andersen, Casper W.","Andersson, Oskar B.","Beltrán, Daniel","Blokhin, Evgeny","Boland, Tara M.","Castañeda Balderas, Rubén","Choudhary, Kamal","Díaz Díaz, Alberto","Domínguez García, Rodrigo","Eckert, Hagen","Eimre, Kristjan","Fuentes Montero, María Elena","Krajewski, Adam M.","Mortensen, Jens Jørgen","Nápoles Duarte, José Manuel","Pietryga, Jacob","Qi, Ji","Trejo Carrillo, Felipe de Jesús","Vaitkus, Antanas","Yu, Jusong","Zettel, Adam","de Castro, Pedro Baptista","Carlsson, Johan","Cerqueira, Tiago F.T.","Divilov, Simon","Hajiyani, Hamidreza","Hanke, Felix","Jose, Kevin","Oses, Corey","Riebesell, Janosh","Schmidt, Jonathan","Winston, Donald","Xie, Christen","Yang, Xiaoyu","Bonella, Sara","Botti, Silvana","Curtarolo, Stefano","Draxl, Claudia","Fuentes Cobas, Luis Edmundo","Hospital, Adam","Liu, Zi Kui","Marques, Miguel A.L.","Marzari, Nicola","Morris, Andrew J.","Ong, Shyue Ping","Orozco, Modesto","Persson, Kristin A.","Thygesen, Kristian Sommer","Wolverton, Chris","Scheidgen, Markus","Toher, Cormac","Conduit, Gareth J.","Pizzi, Giovanni","Gražulis, Saulius","Rignanese, Gian Marco","Armien