Wastewater Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171977052"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-754df80d-8551-4a35-95cb-c0816fc50a32"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Environmental and toxicological implications of chitosan nanostructures","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-802351","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Heparin-induced thrombocytopenia (HIT) is a life-threatening condition that requires urgent diagnostic clarification. However, knowledge of the diagnostic utility of the recommended diagnostic tests is limited in clinical practice. Objective: To evaluate the current diagnostic practice for managing the suspicion of HIT. Design, Setting, and Participants: This prospective diagnostic study was conducted from January 2018 to May 2021 among consecutive patients with suspected HIT from 11 study centers in Switzerland, Germany, and the United States. Detailed clinical data and laboratory information were recorded. Platelet factor 4/heparin antibodies were quantified using an automated chemiluminescent immunoassay (CLIA). A washed-platelet heparin-induced platelet activation (HIPA) test was used as a reference standard to define HIT. Exposures: Suspicion of HIT. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was the diagnostic accuracy of the 4Ts score, the CLIA, and the recommended algorithm serially combining both tests. Results: Of 1448 patients included between 2018 and 2021, 1318 were available for the current analysis (median [IQR] age, 67 [57-75] years; 849 [64.6%] male). HIPA was positive in 111 patients (prevalence, 8.4%). The most frequent setting was intensive care unit (487 [37.0%]) or cardiovascular surgery (434 [33.0%]). The 4Ts score was low risk in 625 patients (46.8%). By 2 × 2 table, the numbers of patients with false-negative results were 10 (9.0%; 4Ts score), 5 (4.5%; CLIA), and 15 (13.5%; recommended diagnostic algorithm). The numbers of patients with false-positive results were 592 (49.0%; 4Ts score), 73 (6.0%; CLIA), and 50 (4.1%; recommended diagnostic algorithm), respectively. Conclusions and Relevance: In this diagnostic study of patients suspected of having HIT, when the recommended diagnostic algorithm was used in clinical practice, antibody testing was required in half the patients. A substantial number of patients were, however, still misclassified, which could lead to delayed diagnosis or overtreatment. Development of improved diagnostic algorithms for HIT diagnosis should be pursued.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Larsen, Emil List","Nilius, Henning","Studt, Jan Dirk","Tsakiris, Dimitrios A.","Greinacher, Andreas","Mendez, Adriana","Schmidt, Adrian","Wuillemin, Walter A.","Gerber, Bernhard","Vishnu, Prakash","Graf, Lukas","Kremer Hovinga, Johanna A.","Goetze, Jens P.","Bakchoul, Tamam","Nagler, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810401"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cantonal Hospital Aarau","Cantonal Hospital St. Gallen","Municipal Hospital Zurich Triemli","Oncology Institute of Southern Switzerland","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital Zürich","University of Basel","University of Bern","University of Greifswald","University of Tübingen","University of Washington"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accuracy of diagnosing heparin induced thrombocytopenia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.3786","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-810401","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10966416","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85189059943","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38530310","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9189c00d-b030-45ff-ab6e-53658ebf29b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48B7F5851BC028B4A12A90023AF5C789"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/448286976/larsen_2024_oi_240165_1710778707.79012.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2024.3786","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"university hospital bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital Bern","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"university hospital zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"university of basel","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Basel","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"university of greifswald","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Greifswald","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ch","key":"cantonal hospital aarau","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Cantonal Hospital Aarau","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"ch","key":"municipal hospital zurich triemli","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Municipal Hospital Zurich Triemli","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"ch","key":"oncology institute of southern switzerland","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Oncology Institute of Southern Switzerland","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"