,"DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","organization of danish ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c59c8842-ea75-4698-93d0-cd1bd9e7b6c8","ku-60f7e971-7714-4117-80d4-c5b872b92f3a","sdu-06ccc7fe-91d0-49d5-9f68-0ab70503a526"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diabetic Retinopathy Predicts Risk of Alzheimer's Disease : A Danish Registry-Based Nationwide Cohort Study","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-095.27-803819","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To evaluate the five-year incidence of diabetic retinopathy (DR) and associated risk markers in patients with type 1 diabetes in the national Danish DR-screening programme. Methods: Based on national data, we included all 16 999 patients with type 1 diabetes in the Danish Registry of Diabetic Retinopathy, who attended the national screening programme in the period 2013–2018. According to the worse eye at first screening, DR was classified (levels 0–4) and linked with various national health registries to retrieve information on diabetes duration, systemic comorbidity, and medication. Results: At first screening, median age and duration of diabetes were 45.0 and 16.7 years, and 57.5% were males. The prevalence and five-year incidences for DR and progression to proliferative DR (PDR) were 44.2%, 8.9% and 2.0%, respectively. In multivariable Cox models, the incidence endpoints were associated with duration of diabetes (hazard ratio [HR] 1.76, 95% confidence interval [CI] 1.63–1.89, and HR 2.04, 95% CI 1.73–2.40 per 10 years), moderately low Charlson Comorbidity Index score (HR 1.27, 95% CI 1.10–1.47, and HR 2.80, 95% CI 2.23–3.51), and use of blood pressure lowering medication (HR 1.20, 95% CI 1.05–1.36, and HR 1.98, 95% CI 1.53–2.57). Conclusion: In a study of all patients with type 1 diabetes from the Danish DR-screening programme, we identified duration of diabetes, systemic disease and use of anti-hypertensive treatment as consistent risk markers for incident and progressive DR.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Stokholm, Lonny","Pedersen, Frederik Nørregaard","Andersen, Nis","Andresen, Jens","Bek, Toke","Dinesen, Sebastian","Hajari, Javad","Heegaard, Steffen","Højlund, Kurt","Laugesen, Caroline Schmidt","Kawasaki, Ryo","Möller, Sören","Schielke, Katja Christina","Subhi, Yousif","Thykjær, Anne Suhr","Grauslund, Jakob"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-761559"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grauslund, Jakob"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Osaka University","The University of Osaka","University of Osaka"],"keyword":["Adult","Denmark epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 complications","Diabetic Retinopathy epidemiology","Diabetic retinopathy","Disease Progression","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Incidence","Male","Mass Screening methods","Middle Aged","Prevalence","Registries","Registry based","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Risk factor","Screening","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"presence and development of diabetic retinopathy in 000000000016 000000000999 patients with type 000000000001 diabetes in the danish registry of diabetic retinopathy","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aos.16707","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-761559","identifier":[{"id":"85193570908","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38761021","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-1a0cdee8-0574-4410-b96c-cb787112aebf","au-046719ff-6f15-4415-a419-0d9311899a88","sdu-cec68e3e-88de-4c9d-9128-ce50e6de2749"],"keyword":["Adult","Denmark/epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 1/complications","Diabetic Retinopathy/epidemiology","Disease Progression","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Male","Mass Screening/methods","Middle Aged","Registries","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","diabetic retinopathy","incidence","prevalence","re