{"abstract":"Promoting brown adipose tissue (BAT) activity innovatively targets obesity and metabolic disease. While thermogenic activation of BAT is well understood, the rheostatic regulation of BAT to avoid excessive energy dissipation remains ill-defined. Here, we demonstrate that adenylyl cyclase 3 (AC3) is key for BAT function. We identified a cold-inducible promoter that generates a 5′ truncated AC3 mRNA isoform (Adcy3-at), whose expression is driven by a cold-induced, truncated isoform of PPARGC1A (PPARGC1A-AT). Male mice lacking Adcy3-at display increased energy expenditure and are resistant to obesity and ensuing metabolic imbalances. Mouse and human AC3-AT are retained in the endoplasmic reticulum, unable to translocate to the plasma membrane and lack enzymatic activity. AC3-AT interacts with AC3 and sequesters it in the endoplasmic reticulum, reducing the pool of adenylyl cyclases available for G-protein-mediated cAMP synthesis. Thus, AC3-AT acts as a cold-induced rheostat in BAT, limiting adverse consequences of cAMP activity during chronic BAT activation.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Khani, Sajjad","Topel, Hande","Kardinal, Ronja","Tavanez, Ana Rita","Josephrajan, Ajeetha","Larsen, Bjørk Ditlev","Gaudry, Michael James","Leyendecker, Philipp","Egedal, Nadia Meincke","Güller, Aylin Seren","Stanic, Natasa","Ruppert, Philip M.M.","Gaziano, Isabella","Hansmeier, Nils Rouven","Schmidt, Elena","Klemm, Paul","Vagliano, Lara Marie","Stahl, Rainer","Duthie, Fraser","Krause, Jens Henning","Bici, Ana","Engelhard, Christoph Andreas","Gohlke, Sabrina","Frommolt, Peter","Gnad, Thorsten","Rada-Iglesias, Alvaro","Pradas-Juni, Marta","Schulz, Tim Julius","Wunderlich, Frank Thomas","Pfeifer, Alexander","Bartelt, Alexander","Jastroch, Martin","Wachten, Dagmar","Kornfeld, Jan Wilhelm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-750843"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kornfeld, Jan Wilhelm"],"country":["Germany","Spain","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Molecular Biosciences, The Wenner-Gren Institute","German Center for Diabetes Research","German Institute of Human Nutrition","Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health","Institute of Human Genetics, Helmholtz Zentrum München","Ludwig-Maximilian University of Munich","Max Planck Institute for Metabolism Research","Partner Site Hamburg/Kiel/Lübeck","University Hospital Bonn","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University of Bonn","University of Cantabria","University of Cologne"],"keyword":["Adipose Tissue Brown metabolism","Animals","Cold Temperature","Cyclic AMP metabolism","Energy Metabolism","Humans","Male","Mice","Mice Knockout","Thermogenesis genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cold induced expression of a truncated adenylyl cyclase 000000000003 acts as rheostat to brown fat function","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42255-024-01033-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-750843","identifier":[{"id":"85191850631","type":"scopus"},{"id":"105003740274","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40186076","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11971047","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"PMC12021646","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38684889","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b2d9c83e-f6e8-4550-a2eb-78f4a0f41506"],"keyword":["Adenylyl Cyclases/metabolism","Adipose Tissue, Brown/metabolism","Animals","Cold Temperature","Cyclic AMP/metabolism","Energy Metabolism","Humans","Male","Mice","Mice, Knockout","Thermogenesis/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-