193452745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d9625b0c-547f-4c19-be69-d5360b8e8806"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Overview of T and D-T results in JET with ITER-like wall","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776144","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: This article compares metabolic, pancreatic, and gut-derived hormone responses to isomaltulose ingestion, before versus during submaximal sustained exercise, in adults with type 1 diabetes (T1D) using automated insulin delivery systems. Methods: In a randomized, cross-over trial, eight participants with T1D being treated with automated insulin pumps (five females, age: 47 ± 16 years, BMI: 27.5 ± 3.8 kg·m2, diabetes duration: 23 ± 11 years, HbA1c: 8.3 ± 0.9 [67.5 ± 9.5]% [mmol/mol]) attended the laboratory on two separate occasions and consumed an isocaloric amount of isomaltulose as either (1) a single serving (0.75g CHO·kg−1 BM) with a 25% reduction in bolus insulin 90 min before 45 min of cycling (PEC) or (2) three separate isocaloric servings (0.25g CHO·kg−1 BM each) without bolus insulin during exercise (DEC). Plasma glucose (PG), gut incretins (GLP-1 and GIP), pancreatic glucagon, exogenous insulin, and whole-body fuel oxidation rates were determined. Data were treated via a two-way repeated measures ANOVA, with p ≤ 0.05 accepted as significant. Results: PG concentrations throughout exercise were higher and less variable with DEC compared to PEC. The exercise-induced change in PG was directionally divergent between trials (PEC: ∆ − 3.2 ± 1.2 mmol/L vs. DEC: ∆ + 1.7 ± 1.5 mmol/L, p < 0.001), changing at a rate of −0.07 ± 0.03 mmol/L/min with PEC and +0.04 ± 0.03 mmol/L/min with DEC (p < 0.001 between conditions). Throughout the exercise period, GLP-1, GIP, glucagon, and total insulin concentrations were lower with DEC (all p ≤ 0.02). The oxidation rates of carbohydrates were lower (p = 0.009) and of lipids were greater (p = 0.014) with DEC compared to PEC. Conclusions: The consumption of smaller servings of isomaltulose during, rather than as a single isocaloric serving before, submaximal sustained exercise provided (i) a better glycemic protective effect, (ii) a lesser push on pancreatic and gut-mediated glucoregulatory hormones, and (iii) a lower reliance on whole-body carbohydrate oxidation. Such information serves to remind us of the potential importance of nutrition for modulating the metabolic fate of an acute bout of exercise and may help inform best practice guidelines for exercise management in the T1D-sphere.","author_count":9,"contributors":["McCarthy, Olivia M.","Christensen, Merete Bechmann","Tawfik, Sandra","Kristensen, Kasper Birch","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Schmidt, Signe","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Bracken, Richard M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-791019"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swansea University"],"keyword":["Automated insulin delivery systems","Exercise","Glucose","Incretin hormones","Nutrition","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metabolic and hormonal responses to isomaltulose ingestion before or during sustained submaximal exercise in adults with type 000000000001 diabetes using automated insulin delivery systems","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu16234098","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-791019","identifier":[{"id":"85212688297","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11643935","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39683492","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ce7f59c1-824d-4e7a-b4de-cd2f160449b9"],"keyword":["automated insulin delivery systems","exercise","glucose","incretin hormones","nutrition","type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CB48024D600157C976C659E850B1B6E1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/nu16234098","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/419710012/nutrients_16_04098.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"swansea university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swansea University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Olivia M.","key":"mccarthypau","last":"McCarthy","name":"McCarthy, Olivia M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Merete Bechmann","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Merete Bechmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sandra","key":"tawfikpau","last":"Tawfik","name":"Tawfik, Sandra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kasper Birch","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Kasper Birch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Signe","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Signe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Richard M.","key":"brackenpau","last":"Bracken","name":"Bracken, Richard M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39683492"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/nu16234098","issn":["20726643"],"issue":"23","journal":"Nutrients","paperid":"4098","status":"p","title":"Nutrients","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212688297"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ce7f59c1-824d-4e7a-b4de-cd2f160449b9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Metabolic and Hormonal Responses to Isomaltulose Ingestion Before or During Sustained Submaximal Exercise in Adults with Type 1 Diabetes Using Automated Insulin Delivery Systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-791019","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Fatigue cracks in steel bridges can lead to catastrophic failure and cause significant risks to public safety. These cracks can grow, propagate, reduce the structure maximum design capaci-ty, and ultimately lead to a sudden failure. Fatigue cracks in steel bridges are primarily induced by the cyclic loading from constant traffic loads over time. Therefore, monitoring fatigue on steel bridges is essential to ensure structural safety. Operational modal analysis (OMA) is a non-destructive testing technique that can be used to monitor fatigue-induced damage through changes in modal parameters. When the fatigue crack grows, the stiffness of the beam will re-duce. This study implements OMA on a simply supported steel beam with changing stiffness. The natural frequencies and mode shapes of the beam are obtained through OMA, and com-bined with a model to predict the stress/strains at any point of the structure. The case study shows how maximum stresses and the natural frequencies that are affected by the crack growth are varying due to changes in stiffness. The result demonstrates that by combining OMA with fatigue assessment, the risk of fatigue failure in steel bridges can be significantly reduced.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Du, Guangli","Brincker, Rune","Diord Rescinho Amador, Sandro","Alibrandi, Umberto"],"cuid":["S02-092.38-761576"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-24","title":"12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, IABMAS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oma driven structural assessment to prevent fatigue induced failure in steel bridges","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-200","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.38-761576","identifier":[{"id":"85200363438","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-47ab4546-9662-4c40-9885-d716408730ec","dtu-ffbd1575-32f4-4732-9ac5-8e37c9c9aba1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-560A0367A60FEBAF9BE932784B0904C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376178435/OMA-driven_structural_assessment_to_prevent_fatigue-induced_failure_in_steel_bridges_24_10_02_14_42_19.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003483755-200","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/752008459/10.1201_9781003483755-200_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Building Physics Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Building Technology, Management and Indoor Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Brincker Monitoring ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, Structural Engineering and Structural Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Guangli","key":"dupau","last":"Du","locid":"f037da1d-4dc6-4899-93ab-2561170f8bd5","name":"Du, Guangli","orcid":"0000-0001-6399-3546","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"brinckerpau","last":"Brincker","name":"Brincker, Rune","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sandro","key":"amadorpau","last":"Amador","locid":"3e53da0b-d147-43c5-8eea-c9214bae8d48","name":"Amador, Sandro","orcid":"0000-0003-3045-2916","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Umberto","key":"alibrandipau","last":"Alibrandi","name":"Alibrandi, Umberto","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Sandager","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens Sandager","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"sandagerjensenpedh","last":"Sandager Jensen","name":"Sandager Jensen, Jens","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan M.","key":"frangopolpedh","last":"Frangopol","name":"Frangopol, Dan M.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan","key":"mfrangopolpedh","last":"M. Frangopol","name":"M. Frangopol, Dan","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"wittrupschmidtpedh","last":"Wittrup Schmidt","name":"Wittrup Schmidt, Jacob","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/9781003483755-200","edition":"1st","eisbn":["9781003483755"],"isbn":["9781032770406","9781032775609"],"pages":"1712-1718","place":"London","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on Bridge Maintenance, Safety and Management, 24-28 june 2024, Copenhagen, Denmark","title":"Bridge Maintenance, Safety, Management, Digitalization and Sustainability"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200363438"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","brincker monitoring aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-47ab4546-9662-4c40-9885-d716408730ec","dtu-ffbd1575-32f4-4732-9ac5-8e37c9c9aba1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"OMA-driven structural assessment to prevent fatigue-induced failure in steel bridges","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.38-761576","year":"2024","yearsub":"202