{"abstract":"Increased plasma levels of glucagon (hyperglucagone-mia) promote diabetes development but are also ob-served in patients with metabolic dysfunction–associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD). This may reflect hepatic glucagon resistance toward amino acid catabolism. A clinical test for measuring glucagon resistance has not been validated. We evaluated our glucagon sensitivity (GLUSENTIC) test, which consists of 2 study days: a glu-cagon injection and measurements of plasma amino acids and an infusion of mixed amino acids and subse-quent calculation of the GLUSENTIC index (primary out-come measure) from measurements of glucagon and amino acids. To distinguish glucagon-dependent from insulin-dependent actions on amino acid metabolism, we also studied patients with type 1 diabetes (T1D). The d-decline in total amino acids was 49% lower in MASLD fol-lowing exogenous glucagon (P = 0.01), and the calculated GLUSENTIC index was 34% lower in MASLD (P < 0.0001) but not T1D (P > 0.99). In contrast, glucagon-induced glucose increments were similar in control participants and participants with MASLD (P = 0.41). The GLUSENTIC test and index may be used to measure glucagon resistance in individuals with obesity and MASLD.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Kjeldsen, Sasha A.S.","Richter, Michael M.","Jensen, Nicole J.","Nilsson, Malin S.D.","Heinz, Niklas","Nybing, Janus D.","Linden, Frederik H.","Høgh-Schmidt, Erik","Boesen, Mikael P.","Andersen, Thomas L.","Johannesen, Helle H.","Trammell, Samuel A.J.","Grevengoed, Trisha J.","Madsbad, Sten","Vilstrup, Hendrik","Schiødt, Frank Vinholt","Møller, Andreas","Rashu, Elias B.","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Schmidt, Signe","Gluud, Lise L.","Haugaard, Steen B.","Holst, Jens J.","Rungby, Jørgen","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J."],"cuid":["S02-097.90-761763"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J."],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glucagon resistance in individuals with obesity and hepatic steatosis can be measured using the glusentic test and index","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2337/db23-0858","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.90-761763","identifier":[{"id":"38976454","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85204745648","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-706700df-51f6-47f0-8c95-36c2ca7ad399","ku-61dbda18-802a-46d0-80b4-be64508486c7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4167F9E8E684D1D7C281F5C2644C5575"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2337/db23-0858","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Mann Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus universit