tus":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","title_org":"Acta Ophthamologica","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85185126717"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","organization of danish ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-737ec6a7-8486-4f25-9680-d17c1b05775d","au-a310922f-d9cc-4252-9de3-3333e6c17382","sdu-ff79f097-bf87-43e4-83d5-e993963a56a0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diabetic retinopathy as an independent marker of cardiovascular disease in type 1 diabetes: Results from a nationwide longitudinal matched case-cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.09-755837","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"background The effects of temporary mechanical circulatory support with a microaxial flow pump on mortality among patients with ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) complicated by cardiogenic shock remains unclear. METHODS In an international, multicenter, randomized trial, we assigned patients with STEMI and cardiogenic shock to receive a microaxial flow pump (Impella CP) plus standard care or standard care alone. The primary end point was death from any cause at 180 days. A composite safety end point was severe bleeding, limb ischemia, hemolysis, device failure, or worsening aortic regurgitation. RESULTS A total of 360 patients underwent randomization, of whom 355 were included in the final analysis (179 in the microaxial-flow-pump group and 176 in the standard-care group). The median age of the patients was 67 years, and 79.2% were men. Death from any cause occurred in 82 of 179 patients (45.8%) in the microaxial-flow-pump group and in 103 of 176 patients (58.5%) in the standard-care group (hazard ratio, 0.74; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.55 to 0.99; P=0.04). A composite safety end-point event occurred in 43 patients (24.0%) in the microaxial-flow-pump group and in 11 (6.2%) in the standard-care group (relative risk, 4.74; 95% CI, 2.36 to 9.55). Renal-replacement therapy was administered to 75 patients (41.9%) in the microaxial-flow-pump group and to 47 patients (26.7%) in the standard-care group (relative risk, 1.98; 95% CI, 1.27 to 3.09). CONCLUSIONS The routine use of a microaxial flow pump with standard care in the treatment of patients with STEMI-related cardiogenic shock led to a lower risk of death from any cause at 180 days than standard care alone. The incidence of a composite of adverse events was higher with the use of the microaxial flow pump. (Funded by the Danish Heart Foundation and Abiomed; DanGer Shock ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT01633502.)","author_count":36,"contributors":["Møller, J. E.","Engstrøm, Thomas","Jensen, L. O.","Eiskjær, H.","Mangner, N.","Polzin, A.","Schulze, P. C.","Skurk, C.","Nordbeck, P.","Clemmensen, P.","Panoulas, V.","Zimmer, S.","Schäfer, A.","Werner, N.","Frydland, M.","Holmvang, Lene","Kjærgaard, J.","Sørensen, R.","Lønborg, J.","Lindholm, M. G.","Udesen, N. L.J.","Junker, A.","Schmidt, H.","Terkelsen, C. J.","Christensen, S.","Christiansen, E. H.","Linke, A.","Woitek, F. J.","Westenfeld, R.","Möbius-Winkler, S.","Wachtell, K.","Ravn, H. B.","Lassen, J. F.","Boesgaard, S.","Gerke, O.","Hassager, Christian"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-735085"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["DanGer Shock investigators","for the DanGer Shock Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Deutsches Herzzentrum Berlin","Dresden University of Technology","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","Hannover Medical School","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Royal Brompton and Harefield NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospital Bonn","University of Bonn","University of Würzburg"],"keyword":["Aged","Assisted Circulation adverse effects","Female","Heart Assist Devices adverse effects","Humans","Incidence","Male","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction complications","Shock Cardiogenic etiology","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Heart Center Dresden"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microaxial flow pump or standard care in infarct related cardiogenic shock","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405062097/Microaxial_Flow.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.97-735085","identifier":[{"id":"85190971602","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38587239","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-070e109f-890b-4745-8846-d4655c5aeb3e","ku-14aacb21-bd01-45d6-8740-8b2eedaa7d5f","sdu-1a9c22b4-345a-4ca6-80d4-ba562d27025d"],"keyword":["Aged","Assisted Circulation/adverse effects","Female","Heart-Assist Devices/adverse effects","Humans","Incidence","Male","ST Elevation Myocardial Infarction/complications","Shock, Cardiogenic/etiology","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3A39EF4A54757D226EB9E9E2D08BE9B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405062097/Microaxial_Flow.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","