{"abstract":"Insects provide key pollination services in most terrestrial biomes, but this service depends on a multistep interaction between insect and plant. An insect needs to visit a flower, receive pollen from the anthers, move to another conspecific flower, and finally deposit the pollen on a receptive stigma. Each of these steps may be affected by climate change, and focusing on only one of them (e.g., flower visitation) may miss important signals of change in service provision. In this study, we combine data on visitation, pollen transport, and single-visit pollen deposition to estimate functional outcomes in the high Arctic plant-pollinator network of Zackenberg, Northeast Greenland, a model system for global warming–associated impacts in pollination services. Over two decades of rapid climate warming, we sampled the network repeatedly: in 1996, 1997, 2010, 2011, and 2016. Although the flowering plant and insect communities and their interactions varied substantially between years, as expected based on highly variable Arctic weather, there was no detectable directional change in either the structure of flower-visitor networks or estimated pollen deposition. For flower-visitor networks compiled over a single week, species phenologies caused major within-year variation in network structure despite consistency across years. Weekly networks for the middle of the flowering season emerged as especially important because most pollination service can be expected to be provided by these large, highly nested networks. Our findings suggest that pollination ecosystem service in the high Arctic is remarkably resilient. This resilience may reflect the plasticity of Arctic biota as an adaptation to extreme and unpredictable weather. However, most pollination service was contributed by relatively few fly taxa (Diptera: Spilogona sanctipauli and Drymeia segnis [Muscidae] and species of Rhamphomyia [Empididae]). If these key pollinators are negatively affected by climate change, network structure and the pollination service that depends on it would be seriously compromised.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Cirtwill, Alyssa R.","Kaartinen, Riikka","Rasmussen, Claus","Redr, Deanne","Wirta, Helena","Olesen, Jens M.","Tiusanen, Mikko","Ballantyne, Gavin","Cunnold, Helen","Stone, Graham N.","Schmidt, Niels Martin","Roslin, Tomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137231"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cirtwill, Alyssa R."],"country":["Finland","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Edinburgh Napier University","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","University of Bath","University of Edinburgh","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["Diptera","Dryas","Phenology","pollen deposition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stable pollination service in a generalist high arctic community despite the warming climate","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ecm.1551","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137231","identifier":[{"id":"37035419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85139000349","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10078371","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-0dc7368d-3b32-433c-9db4-63b47f17da67"],"keyword":["Dryas","diptera","flower visitor","phenology","pollen deposition","pollen transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4057A43E9DEF87403F7E072664AA4B9D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ecm.1551","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/419147517/Ecological_Monographs_-_2022_-_Cirtwill_-_Stable_pollination_service_in_a_generalist_high_Arctic_community_despite_the.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Agricultural biodiversity, Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"swedish university of agricultural sciences","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"edinburgh napier university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Edinburgh Napier University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of bath","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bath","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alyssa R.","key":"cirtwillpau","last":"Cirtwill","name":"Cirtwill, Alyssa R.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Riikka","key":"kaartinenpau","last":"Kaartinen","name":"Kaartinen, Riikka","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"24ea7809-dde1-44f9-ac17-63b508b998f7","name":"Rasmussen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0003-1529-6548","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Deanne","key":"redrpau","last":"Redr","name":"Redr, Deanne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena","key":"wirtapau","last":"Wirta","name":"Wirta, Helena","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens M.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"5beee907-781b-4998-8f99-97083ea86835","name":"Olesen, Jens M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1998-1083","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikko","key":"tiusanenpau","last":"Tiusanen","name":"Tiusanen, Mikko","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Gavin","key":"ballantynepau","last":"Ballantyne","name":"Ballantyne, Gavin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Helen","key":"cunnoldpau","last":"Cunnold","name":"Cunnold, Helen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham N.","key":"stonepau","last":"Stone","name":"Stone, Graham N.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b91704ca-e126-4c35-af20-95b2269d230a","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-6218","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomas","key":"roslinpau","last":"Roslin","name":"Roslin, Tomas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37035419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ecm.1551","issn":["00129615","15577015"],"issn_org":["00129615"],"issue":"1","journal":"Ecological Monographs","paperid":"e1551","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Ecological Monographs","volume":"93"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139000349"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0dc7368d-3b32-433c-9db4-63b47f17da67"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Stable pollination service in a generalist high Arctic community despite the warming climate","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-137231","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Gaze-Hand Alignment has recently been proposed for multimodal selection in 3D. The technique takes advantage of gaze for target pre-selection, as it naturally precedes manual input. Selection is then completed when manual input aligns with gaze on the target, without need for an additional click method. In this work we evaluate two alignment techniques, Gaze&Finger and Gaze&Handray, combining gaze with image plane pointing versus raycasting, in comparison with hands-only baselines and Gaze&Pinch as established multimodal technique. We used Fitts' Law study design with targets presented at different depths in the visual scene, to assess effect of parallax on performance. The alignment techniques outperformed their respective hands-only baselines. Gaze&Finger is efficient when targets are close to the image plane but less performant with increasing target depth due to parallax.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Wagner, Uta","Lystbæk, Mathias Nørhede","Manakhov, Pavel","Grønbæk, Jens Emil","Pfeuffer, Ken","Gellersen, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-188460"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lancaster University"],"keyword":["Augmented reality","Eye tracking","Gaze interaction","Mid air gestures","Pointing","menu selection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fitts law study of gaze hand alignment for selection in 000000000003d user interfaces","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/312128746/Fitts_Law_Uta.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-188460","identifier":[{"id":"85160021052","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-67899d47-0952-45ee-96fe-9bc057daa4b7"],"keyword":["augmented reality","eye-tracking","gaze interaction","menu selection","mid-air gestures","pointing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B0F46C320DC2EABCA1C7FC84E26F8208"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/312128746/Fitts_Law_Uta.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"lancaster university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lancaster University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uta","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","locid":"56e69a64-6fd3-4b7d-8416-6bbcc8f8b57e","name":"Wagner, Uta","orcid":"0000-0002-7885-5610","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias Nørhede","key":"lystbækpau","last":"Lystbæk","locid":"9ece74ae-b780-4dc5-bc29-ddc50af3b16f","name":"Lystbæk, Mathias Nørhede","orcid":"0000-0001-6624-3732","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pavel","key":"manakhovpau","last":"Manakhov","locid":"f06a8956-8c2c-4c78-8c95-78c4585892a5","name":"Manakhov, Pavel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Emil","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"cb34ed1e-a18d-4b6d-8f80-1cace0ea64c2","name":"Grønbæk, Jens Emil","orcid":"0000-0002-9566-7195","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ken","key":"pfeufferpau","last":"Pfeuffer","locid":"4dc1fbee-ac94-4f49-9063-b11114272d54","name":"Pfeuffer, Ken","orcid":"0000-0002-5870-1120","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"gellersenpau","last":"Gellersen","locid":"2c2abbff-0da0-44ed-a3cc-9cb48661d9c9","name":"Gellersen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-2233-2121","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Albrecht","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Albrecht","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kaisa","key":"väänänenpedh","last":"Väänänen","name":"Väänänen, Kaisa","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tesh","key":"goyalpedh","last":"Goyal","name":"Goyal, Tesh","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per Ola","key":"kristenssonpedh","last":"Kristensson","name":"Kristensson, Per Ola","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anicia","key":"peterspedh","last":"Peters","name":"Peters, Anicia","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefanie","key":"muellerpedh","last":"Mueller","name":"Mueller, Stefanie","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Julie","key":"rwilliamsonpedh","last":"R. Williamson","name":"R. Williamson, Julie","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Max","key":"lwilsonpedh","last":"L. Wilson","name":"L. Wilson, Max","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3544548.3581423","eisbn":["9781450394215"],"place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2023 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","title":"CHI '23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160021052"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-67899d47-0952-45ee-96fe-9bc057daa4b7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Fitts’ Law Study of Gaze-Hand Alignment for Selection in 3D User Interfaces","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-188460","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The aim of this study was to investigate glucose tolerance, glucagon response, and beta cell function during a 1-year maintenance period with either exercise, the glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist liraglutide, or the combination after diet-induced weight loss. METHODS: In this randomized placebo-controlled trial, adults with obesity (BMI: 32-43 kg/m 2 ) without diabetes underwent an 8-week low-calorie diet (800 kcal/d) and were randomized to 52 weeks of aerobic exercise, liraglutide 3.0 mg/d, exercise and liraglutide combined, or placebo. Change in glucose and glucagon response to a 3-hour mixed meal test and disposition index, as a measure of beta cell function, were measured. RESULTS: A total of 195 participants were randomized. After 1 year of treatment, the combination group had decreased postprandial glucose response by -9% (95% CI: -14% to -3%; p = 0.002), improved beta cell function by 49% (95% CI: 16% to 93%; p = 0.002), and decreased glucagon response by -18% (95% CI: -34% to -3%; p = 0.024) compared with placebo. Compared with placebo, liraglutide alone improved postprandial glucose response by -7% (95% CI: -12% to -1%; p = 0.018), but not beta cell function or glucagon. Exercise alone had similar postprandial glucose response, beta cell function, and glucagon response as placebo. CONCLUSIONS: Only the combination of exercise and liraglutide improved glucose tolerance, beta cell function, and glucagon responses after weight loss.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","Juhl, Christian Rimer","Janus, Charlotte","Lundgren, Julie Rehné","Martinussen, Christoffer","Wiingaard, Christoffer","Knudsen, Cecilie","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Stallknecht, Bente","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Torekov, Signe Sørensen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524309"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 drug therapy","Double Blind Method","Exercise","Glucagon","Glucose","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents therapeutic use","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weight loss maintenance with exercise and liraglutide improves glucose tolerance glucagon response and beta cell function","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/oby.23715","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524309","identifier":[{"id":"85150531142","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000953769800013","type":"wos"},{"id":"36942420","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-db1ee20c-8f6a-42cb-8368-8225094dc13d"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/drug therapy","Double-Blind Method","Exercise","Glucagon","Glucose","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents/therapeutic use","Liraglutide/pharmacology","Weight Loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BAD5060E8F8F7AD51FB92392792F8BA6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/oby.23715","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341020333/Obesity_2023_Jensen_Weight_loss_maintenance_with_exercise_and_liraglutide_improves_glucose_tolerance_glucagon.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Simon B K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9edd5734-2279-4744-b174-f70c08e9ad82","name":"Jensen, Simon Birk Kjær","name_org":"Jensen, Simon B K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian R.","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"18d8e8fd-21c1-4352-a747-6c0cc9087510","name":"Juhl, Christian Rimer","name_org":"Juhl, Christian R.","orcid":"0000-0003-3024-4017","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"januspau","last":"Janus","locid":"43d27a16-cbc2-4b44-9ebc-858d3083ec5a","name":"Janus, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-5111-7047","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie R","key":"lundgrenpau","last":"Lundgren","locid":"88bf4b27-fa5b-4090-a986-cb00acedd3b0","name":"Lundgren, Julie Rehné","name_org":"Lundgren, Julie R","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"martinussenpau","last":"Martinussen","locid":"4f245fbb-67ec-4135-a359-b0f73db977a3","name":"Martinussen, Christoffer","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"wiingaardpau","last":"Wiingaard","name":"Wiingaard, Christoffer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Cecilie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ruth","key":"frikkeschmidtpau","last":"Frikke-Schmidt","locid":"bce2c3b4-6e08-46c7-96c6-7e385b0ec8b3","name":"Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente M","key":"stallknechtpau","last":"Stallknecht","locid":"eddf86eb-44d6-44ca-985b-79a29dd3cec7","name":"Stallknecht, Bente","name_org":"Stallknecht, Bente M","orcid":"0000-0003-3117-0451","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe S.","key":"torekovpau","last":"Torekov","locid":"c1d71a61-ee09-4c29-ae48-7520707a73be","name":"Torekov, Signe Sørensen","name_org":"Torekov, Signe S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-0252","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36942420"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/oby.23715","issn":["19307381","1930739X"],"issn_org":["19307381"],"issue":"4","journal":"Obesity","pages":"977-989","status":"p","title":"Obesity","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150531142"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-db1ee20c-8f6a-42cb-8368-8225094dc13d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Weight loss maintenance with exercise and liraglutide improves glucose tolerance, glucagon response, and beta cell function","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-524309","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Disposal of carbon-rich wastes, such as food waste, is one of the several environmental concerns raised nowadays. Conversion of organic residues by dark fermentation produces short-chain (C1–C6) carboxylic acids, which are valuable chemical building blocks. The objective of this study was to optimize the operational parameters and perform comparative studies of cyclic and batch mode dark fermentation for carboxylic acid production from food waste. A maximum yield of short-chain carboxylic acids (SCCAs) 0.21 ± 0.012 g-SCCAs/g-TS in 50 g-TS/L was obtained in the cyclic mode as compared with the 0.13 ± 0.011 g-SCCAs/g-TS in the batch mode. The results showed that the use of the cyclic mode increased the carboxylic acid yield from 54 (batch mode) to 88%.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ashraf, Muhammad Tahir","Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo","Ahmad, Ashfaq","Hai, Abdul","AlBlooshi, Hanifa Taher","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Banat, Fawzi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635018"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Ahmad, Ashfaq","Banat, Fawzi"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University"],"keyword":["Anaerobic","Carboxylic acids","Dark fermentation","Food waste"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced short chain carboxylic acids yield in dark fermentation by cyclic product removal","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85145434937","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635018","identifier":[{"id":"85145434937","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d7a3c34a-48be-4ca0-b652-423922dff980"],"keyword":["Anaerobic","Carboxylic acids","Cyclic mode","Dark fermentation","Food waste"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47C3D7FCBB76E7770DB647447C4EE56D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Muhammad Tahir","key":"ashrafpau","last":"Ashraf","locid":"c15b128f-8f64-4d40-9e4f-79bdd23143a7","name":"Ashraf, Muhammad Tahir","orcid":"0000-0003-3101-3421","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","locid":"840da3ca-81a6-461d-a027-5716b944217e","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo","name_org":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","orcid":"0000-0002-2418-441X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashfaq","key":"ahmadpau","last":"Ahmad","name":"Ahmad, Ashfaq","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Abdul","key":"haipau","last":"Hai","name":"Hai, Abdul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanifa Taher","key":"alblooshipau","last":"AlBlooshi","name":"AlBlooshi, Hanifa Taher","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fawzi","key":"banatpau","last":"Banat","name":"Banat, Fawzi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13399-020-01010-7","issn":["21906815","21906823"],"issn_org":["21906815"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biomass Conversion and Biorefinery","pages":"51-59","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Biomass Conversion and Biorefinery","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85145434937"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d7a3c34a-48be-4ca0-b652-423922dff980"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Enhanced short-chain carboxylic acids yield in dark fermentation by cyclic product removal","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-635018","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Transcatheter closure of patent foramen ovale (PFO) is the recommended stroke prevention treatment in patients ≤60 years with cryptogenic ischemic stroke and PFO. Atrial fibrillation or flutter (AF) is a known potential procedure-related complication, but long-term risk of developing AF remains unknown. This paper studied the long-term risk of developing AF following PFO closure. METHODS AND RESULTS: A Danish nationwide cohort study was conducted. During 2008-2020, this study identified a PFO closure cohort, a PFO diagnosis cohort without PFO closure, and a general population comparison cohort matched 10:1 to the PFO closure cohort on age and sex. The outcome was first-time AF diagnosis. Risk of AF and multivariable-adjusted hazard ratio (HR) of the association between PFO closure or PFO diagnosis and AF were calculated. A total of 817 patients with PFO closure, 1224 with PFO diagnosis, and 8170 matched individuals were identified. The 5 year risk of AF was 7.8% [95% confidence interval (CI): 5.5-10] in the PFO closure cohort, 3.1% (95% CI: 2.0-4.2) in the PFO diagnosis cohort, and 1.2% (95% CI: 0.8-1.6) in the matched cohort. The HR of AF comparing PFO closure with PFO diagnosis was 2.3 (95% CI: 1.3-4.0) within the first 3 months and 0.7 (95% CI: 0.3-1.7) thereafter. The HR of AF comparing PFO closure with the matched cohort was 51 (95% CI: 21-125) within the first 3 months and 2.5 (95% CI: 1.2-5.0) thereafter. CONCLUSION: Patent foramen ovale closure was not associated with any substantial increased long-term risk of developing AF beyond the well-known procedure-related short-term risk.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Skibsted, Christian Valdemar","Korsholm, Kasper","Pedersen, Lars","Bonnesen, Kasper","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Schmidt, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-675789"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Skibsted, Christian Valdemar"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Cryptogenic stroke","Device closure","Epidemiology","Patent foramen ovale","Stroke prevention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term risk of atrial fibrillation or flutter after transcatheter patent foramen ovale closure a nationwide danish study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85169771218","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-675789","identifier":[{"id":"85169771218","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37279491","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d55fe671-87de-4733-be58-bd7f9b8cde01"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Cryptogenic stroke","Device closure","Epidemiology","Patent foramen ovale","Stroke prevention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B76FB5FB9C796A1901F7C7D1A29822D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Valdemar","key":"skibstedpau","last":"Skibsted","locid":"d64d1c08-defa-4461-91dc-538b83b7d71f","name":"Skibsted, Christian Valdemar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"bonnesenpau","last":"Bonnesen","locid":"08f71580-e725-41b2-9592-48981f741350","name":"Bonnesen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8626-2372","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37279491"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehad305","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"36","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"3469-3477","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169771218"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d55fe671-87de-4733-be58-bd7f9b8cde01"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Long-term risk of atrial fibrillation or flutter after transcatheter patent foramen ovale closure : a nationwide Danish study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-675789","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Non-communicable diseases (NCDs), including coronary heart disease, stroke, hypertension, type 2 diabetes, dementia, depression and cancers, are on the rise worldwide and are often associated with a lack of physical activity (PA). Globally, the levels of PA among individuals are below WHO recommendations. A lack of PA can increase morbidity and mortality, worsen the quality of life and increase the economic burden on individuals and society. In response to this trend, numerous organisations came together under one umbrella in Hamburg, Germany, in April 2021 and signed the 'Hamburg Declaration'. This represented an international commitment to take all necessary actions to increase PA and improve the health of individuals to entire communities. Individuals and organisations are working together as the 'Global Alliance for the Promotion of Physical Activity' to drive long-term individual and population-wide behaviour change by collaborating with all stakeholders in the community: active hospitals, physical activity specialists, community services and healthcare providers, all achieving sustainable health goals for their patients/clients. The 'Hamburg Declaration' calls on national and international policymakers to take concrete action to promote daily PA and exercise at a population level and in healthcare settings.","author_count":113,"contributors":["Steinacker, Jürgen M","van Mechelen, Willem","Bloch, Wilhelm","Börjesson, Mats","Casasco, Maurizio","Wolfarth, Bernd","Knoke, Carolin","Papadopoulou, Theodora","Wendt, Janine","Al Tunaiji, Hashel","Andresen, Dietrich","Andrieieva, Olena","Bachl, Norbert","Badtieva, Victoriya","Beucher, Friedhelm J","Blauwet, Cheri A","Casajus Mallen, Jose-Antonio","Chang, Ju-Ho","Clénin, German","Constantini, Naama","Constantinou, Demitri","Di Luigi, Luigi","Declercq, Lukas","Doutreleau, Stephane","Drozdovska, Svitlana","Duclos, Martine","Ermolao, Andrea","Fischbach, Thomas","Fischer, Anastasia N","Fossati, Chiara","Franchel