{"abstract":"Turn-taking is one of the biggest interactivity challenges in multiparty remote meetings. One contributing factor is that current videoconferencing tools lack support for proxemic cues; ie, spatial cues that humans use to enact their social relations and intentions. While more recent tools provide support for proxemic metaphors, they often focus on approach and leave-taking rather than turntaking. In this paper, we present OpenMic, a videoconferencing system that utilizes proxemic metaphors for conversational floor management by providing 1) a Virtual Floor that serves as a fixedfeature space for users to be aware of others’ intention to talk, and 2) Malleable Mirrors, which are video and screen feeds that can be continuously moved and resized for conversational floor transitions. Our exploratory user study found that these system features can aid the conversational flow in multiparty video meetings. With this work, we show potential for embedding proxemic metaphors to support conversational floor management in videoconferencing systems.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hu, Erzhen","Grønbæk, Jens Emil","Houck, Austin","Heo, Seongkook"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-240502"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Virginia"],"keyword":["Proxemics","Turn taking","Video conferencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"openmic utilizing proxemic metaphors for conversational floor transitions in multiparty video meetings","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544548.3581013","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-240502","identifier":[{"id":"85160021404","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c2d85614-a9a3-4d92-9598-6de9187c34c3"],"keyword":["multiparty video meeting","non-verbal cues","proxemics","turn-taking","video conferencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-92D1973136D404BFDA42735ADBBC0E82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://erzhenh.com/pdfs/OpenMic_CHI2023_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3544548.3581013","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of virginia","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Virginia","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erzhen","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Erzhen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Emil","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"cb34ed1e-a18d-4b6d-8f80-1cace0ea64c2","name":"Grønbæk, Jens Emil","orcid":"0000-0002-9566-7195","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Austin","key":"houckpau","last":"Houck","name":"Houck, Austin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Seongkook","key":"heopau","last":"Heo","name":"Heo, Seongkook","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Albrecht","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Albrecht","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kaisa","key":"väänänenpedh","last":"Väänänen","name":"Väänänen, Kaisa","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tesh","key":"goyalpedh","last":"Goyal","name":"Goyal, Tesh","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per Ola","key":"kristenssonpedh","last":"Kristensson","name":"Kristensson, Per Ola","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anicia","key":"peterspedh","last":"Peters","name":"Peters, Anicia","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefanie","key":"muellerpedh","last":"Mueller","name":"Mueller, Stefanie","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Julie","key":"rwilliamsonpedh","last":"R. Williamson","name":"R. Williamson, Julie","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Max","key":"lwilsonpedh","last":"L. Wilson","name":"L. Wilson, Max","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3544548.3581013","eisbn":["9781450394215"],"place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2023 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","title":"CHI'23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160021404"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c2d85614-a9a3-4d92-9598-6de9187c34c3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"OpenMic : Utilizing Proxemic Metaphors for Conversational Floor Transitions in Multiparty Video Meetings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-240502","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Device-related thrombus (DRT) following left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO) can lead to adverse clinical outcomes. DRT rates and outcomes from randomized trials are limited. OBJECTIVES: This analysis investigated the incidence, predictors, and clinical outcomes of DRT following LAAO in the Amulet IDE (AMPLATZER Amulet LAA Occluder Trial) trial. METHODS: Successful implants occurred in 903 patients with an Amulet occluder (dual occlusive mechanism device) and 885 patients with a Watchman device (single occlusive mechanism device). These patients were then followed through 18 months and DRT was assessed by transesophageal echocardiography. RESULTS: The overall incidence of DRT was 3.9% (n = 70) with 3.4% (n = 30) in dual occlusive mechanism device patients and 4.8% (n = 40) in single occlusive mechanism device patients. Most DRTs (n = 19 of 31) were identified early (≤45 days) on the dual occlusive mechanism device, whereas most of the DRTs (n = 31 of 42) were identified late (>45 days) on the single occlusive mechanism device. Strong predictors of DRT included atrial fibrillation at time of procedure (HR: 2.44; 95% CI: 1.42-4.22; P < 0.01), female sex (HR: 1.65; 95% CI: 1.01-2.71; P = 0.04), and older age (HR: 1.04; 95% CI: 1.01-1.08; P = 0.02). There were no stroke events following DRT in the dual occlusive mechanism device group and 3 stroke events following DRT in the single occlusive mechanism device group. Patients with DRT were at a greater risk for cardiovascular mortality compared with non-DRT patients (8.7% vs 3.9%; HR: 2.33; 95% CI: 1.01-5.39; P = 0.04). CONCLUSIONS: Incidence of DRT following LAAO was low. Early DRTs are seen with the dual occlusive mechanism device and late DRTs are seen with the single occlusive mechanism device. Increased cardiovascular mortality risk in patients with DRT should be further investigated. (AMPLATZER Amulet LAA Occluder Trial; NCT02879448).","author_count":15,"contributors":["Schmidt, Boris","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Ellis, Christopher R","Thaler, David","Sabir, Sajjad A","Gambhir, Alok","Landmesser, Ulf","Shah, Neeraj","Gray, William","Swarup, Vijendra","Lim, D Scott","Koulogiannis, Konstantinos","Anderson, Jordan A","Gage, Ryan","Lakkireddy, Dhanunjaya"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-252838"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schmidt, Boris"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Structural Heart","All Global Affiliations","Cardioangiologisches Centrum Bethanien","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Cooper University Health Care","HCA Midwest Health","Tufts University","University of Virginia"],"keyword":["Atrial Appendage","Atrial Fibrillation epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Stroke epidemiology","Thrombosis epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence predictors and clinical outcomes of device related thrombus in the amulet ide trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacep.2022.07.014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-252838","identifier":[{"id":"85146131609","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36697204","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d84cd444-0a6b-4196-aeb4-bcd6af261a50"],"keyword":["Atrial Appendage","Atrial Fibrillation/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Stroke/epidemiology","Thrombosis/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C8B082A0876EED151AB6AEA30D7C6377"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jacep.2022.07.014","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"d