{"abstract":"Background: The Amulet (Abbott) left atrial appendage occluder investigational device exemption trial is the largest randomized trial evaluating the safety and effectiveness of the Amulet left atrial appendage occluder compared with the Watchman 2.5 device (Boston Scientific) through 5 years. Objectives: This analysis evaluated the device effect on 3-year outcomes in the Amulet investigational device exemption trial. Methods: The medication regimen and key clinical outcomes were reported through 3 years including: 1) the composite of ischemic stroke or systemic embolism (SE); 2) the composite of all strokes, SE, or cardiovascular (CV) death; 3) major bleeding; and 4) all-cause death and CV death. Results: A total of 1,878 patients at 108 sites were randomized. A significantly higher percentage of patients were free of oral anticoagulation usage at 3 years with Amulet (96.2%) vs Watchman (92.5%) (P < 0.01). Clinical outcomes were comparable for the composite of ischemic stroke or SE (5.0% vs 4.6%; P = 0.69); the composite of all strokes, SE, or CV death (11.1% vs 12.7%; P = 0.31); major bleeding (16.1% vs 14.7%; P = 0.46); all-cause death (14.6% vs 17.9%; P = 0.08); and CV death (6.6% vs 8.5%; P = 0.14) for Amulet and Watchman, respectively. Through 3 years, device factors (device-related thrombus or peridevice leak ≥3 mm) preceded ischemic stroke events and CV deaths more frequently in Watchman compared with Amulet patients. Conclusions: The Amulet occluder demonstrated continued safety and effectiveness with over 96% free of oral anticoagulation usage through 3 years in a high-risk population compared to the Watchman device.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Lakkireddy, Dhanunjaya","Thaler, David","Ellis, Christopher R","Swarup, Vijendra","Gambhir, Alok","Hermiller, James","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Worthley, Stephen","Nair, Devi","Schmidt, Boris","Horton, Rodney","Gupta, Nigel","Anderson, Jordan A","Gage, Ryan","Alkhouli, Mohamad","Windecker, Stephan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-682161"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Germany","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Structural Heart","All Global Affiliations","Cardioangiologisches Centrum Bethanien","HCA Midwest Health","Macquarie University","Mayo Clinic Rochester, MN","Private medical Practice - USA","St. David's Medical Center","St. Vincent Medical Group","Tufts University","University of Bern","Vanderbilt University","Westmead Hospital"],"keyword":["Amulet","Atrial fibrillation","Left atrial appendage occlusion","Stroke","Watchman"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000003 year outcomes from the amplatzer amulet left atrial appendage occluder randomized controlled trial amulet ide","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85166968806","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-682161","identifier":[{"id":"85166968806","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37587599","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0848cba3-10fc-4840-b614-9dae894ef97a"],"keyword":["Watchman","amulet","atrial fibrillation","left atrial appendage occlusion","stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E1890C08F6ECD0E9836C4B5DD6626AAD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"hca midwest health","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"HCA Midwest Health","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"tufts university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Tufts University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us"