uhr Thykjær, Anne","name_org":"Thykjaer, Anne Suhr","orcid":"0000-0002-2621-4360","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lonny","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"ab6bde17-94c0-482d-bb34-495daa518640","name":"Stokholm, Lonny","orcid":"0000-0002-9727-6649","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36189965"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.15264","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"207-214","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139262253"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","organization of danish ophthalmologists","organization of danish practicing ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bd0918a2-5826-4087-9e16-75b6010e4453","au-7eb66c54-57a0-460e-a2f3-ce0df759d05f","ku-c68381f8-238d-4556-84b7-cfd6fbd6bcc3","sdu-cebb0593-c65f-4698-90cb-0183af69f56d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Presence and development of diabetic retinopathy in 153 238 patients with type 2 diabetes in the Danish Registry of Diabetic Retinopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.43-009119","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To map which factors have been considered, explored, and found to influence physical activity (PA) promotion by oncology physicians and nurses (OPN). METHODS: A scoping review of empirical studies was conducted using Arksey and O'Malley's framework and the PRISMA-ScR guideline. The quality of the studies was evaluated using the QATSDD tool. RESULTS: Twenty-nine publications were included. The methodological quality of the studies was low to moderate. Studies have shown a positive attitude towards PA and recommending PA. PA knowledge seems to influence PA promotion by OPNs to some extent. Structural barriers for PA promotion are the most endorsed barriers but to what extent they influence PA promotion is unclear. The demographic and professional characteristics of OPNs and their PA behavior do not seem to influence PA promotion to a greater extent. Patients' PA interest, health characteristics, and medical conditions are additional factors. Their implications for PA promotion are not fully elucidated. CONCLUSIONS: The varied results across the studies, together with the methodological limitations of the studies, make it unclear to what extent the explored factors influence PA promotion by OPNs. PRACTICE IMPLICATIONS: More research into what influences OPNs' engagement in PA promotion is warranted to support clinical PA promotion.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schmidt, M. L.K.","Østergren, Peter Busch","Kvorning Ternov, Klara","Sønksen, Jens","Midtgaard, Julie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-482052"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Nurses","Physical activity promotion","Physicians","Scoping review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"factors related to promotion of physical activity in clinical oncology practice a scoping review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-482052","identifier":[{"id":"36502560","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85144596246","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-94577495-0d18-46a3-8aff-979bd415d625"],"keyword":["Nurses","Patients living with and beyond cancer","Physical activity promotion","Physicians","Scoping review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6965C0C1645DF288CBB2E67F20779E6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Urology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"M. L.K.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, M. L.K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"P.","key":"østergrenpau","last":"Østergren","locid":"27fc1e9b-5aa1-46e7-b217-73fb0c5e80e7","name":"Østergren, Peter Busch","name_org":"Østergren, P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"K.","key":"kvorningternovpau","last":"Kvorning Ternov","locid":"1675b7c7-291e-47ed-a10a-c9e85dff010f","name":"Kvorning Ternov, Klara","name_org":"Kvorning Ternov, K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J.","key":"sønksenpau","last":"Sønksen","locid":"feaefc17-e926-4892-9f0a-983e08461edf","name":"Sønksen, Jens","name_org":"Sønksen, J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"J.","key":"midtgaardpau","last":"Midtgaard","locid":"9f64fbe5-60e9-49c3-bb06-7ec73d018a77","name":"Midtgaard, Julie","name_org":"Midtgaard, J.","orcid":"0000-0003-2381-2127","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36502560"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.pec.2022.107582","issn":["07383991","18735134"],"issn_org":["07383991"],"journal":"Patient Education and Counseling","pages":"107582","status":"p","title":"Patient Education and Counseling","volume":"107"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144596246"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-94577495-0d18-46a3-8aff-979bd415d625"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Factors related to promotion of physical activity in clinical oncology practice : A scoping review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482052","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Lignin modifying enzymes (LMEs) have gained widespread recognition in depolymerization of lignin polymers by oxidative cleavage. LMEs are a robust class of biocatalysts that include lignin peroxidase (LiP), manganese peroxidase (MnP), versatile peroxidase (VP), laccase (LAC), and dye-decolorizing peroxidase (DyP). Members of the LMEs family act on phenolic, non-phenolic substrates and have been widely researched for valorization of lignin, oxidative cleavage of xenobiotics and phenolics. LMEs implementation in the biotechnological and industrial sectors has sparked significant attention, although its potential future applications remain underexploited. To understand the mechanism of LMEs in sustainable pollution mitigation, several studies have been undertaken to assess the feasibility of LMEs in correlating to diverse pollutants for binding and intermolecular interactions at the molecular level. However, further investigation is required to fully comprehend the underlying mechanism. In this review we presented the key structural and functional features of LMEs, including the computational aspects, as well as the advanced applications in biotechnology and industrial research. Furthermore, concluding remarks and a look ahead, the use of LMEs coupled with computational framework, built upon artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML), has been emphasized as a recent milestone in environmental research.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Singh, Anil Kumar","Iqbal, Hafiz M.N.","Cardullo, Nunzio","Muccilli, Vera","Fernández-Lucas, Jesús","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Jesionowski, Teofil","Bilal, Muhammad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-680603"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, South","Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bilal, Muhammad"],"country":["Colombia","India","Italy","Mexico","Poland","Spain"],"glorg":["Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR)","All Global Affiliations","CSIR-Indian Institute of Toxicology Research","European University of Madrid","Gdańsk University of Technology","Monterrey Institute of Technology and Higher Education","Universidad de la Costa","University of Catania"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Biotechnology","Catalytic mechanisms","Computational framework","Depolymerization","Environmental Pollutants","Laccase","Lignin modifying enzymes","Peroxidases metabolism","Phenols"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Politechnika Poznanska"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structural insights biocatalytic characteristics and application prospects of lignin modifying enzymes for sustainable biotechnology","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijbiomac.2023.124968","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["AKS would thank the Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR), India, Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR)-An Institute of National Importance, and CSIR -Indian Institute of Toxicology Research Lucknow, India. The research leading to these results has received funding from the Norwegian Financial Mechanism 2014–2021 under the Project number 2020/37/K/ST8/03805 . AKS would thank the Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR), India, Academy of Scientific and Innovative Research (AcSIR)-An Institute of National Importance, and CSIR-Indian Institute of Toxicology Research Lucknow, India. The research leading to these results has received funding from the Norwegian Financial Mechanism 2014–2021 under the Project number 2020/37/K/ST8/03805."],"id":"S01-000.00-680603","identifier":[{"id":"37217044","type":"pmid"},{"