{"abstract":"We analyze how innovators facilitate and shape the formation of innovation ecosystems around a systemic innovation. We argue that the ability to engage in cognitive leadership--the ability to influence others' beliefs, in particular owners of complementary assets, in order to achieve coordination and cooperation--is central to the development of nascent innovation ecosystems. Our approach shifts the unit of analysis from the innovation and the underlying (eco)system to the beliefs about the innovation, the ecosystem (including interdependencies) and the different players. Our model is built on three elements: beliefs as targets for successful cognitive leadership, the mechanisms by which innovators can influence others' beliefs, and the enablers as underlying skills for cognitive leadership. We discuss implications of our analysis for our understanding of the formation of innovation ecosystems and the emergence of ecosystem leadership and also highlight managerial implications.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Foss, Nicolai J.","Schmidt, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-292390"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-09","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2022-08-05","title":"The Academy of Management Annual Meeting 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["AOM Seattle 2022","AOM annual meeting proceedings 2022"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cognitive leadership systemic innovation and the formation of innovation ecosystems","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-292390","ids":["cbs-b331eef2-a77d-489c-a4ef-d9341b1f5a10"],"keyword":["AOM annual meeting proceedings 2022","AOM seattle 2022"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-33C843C0B63DF6C67AAEAF19F9F1A420"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai J.","key":"fosspau","last":"Foss","locid":"7f0ced62-e3e8-4d60-ac5d-48a57edef7ca","name":"Foss, Nicolai J.","orcid":"0000-0003-2049-8347","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sonja","key":"tanejapedh","last":"Taneja","name":"Taneja, Sonja","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5465/ambpp.2022.10312abstract","issn":["00650668"],"pages":"117","place":"Briarcliff Manor, NY","publisher":"Academy of Management","series":"Academy of Management Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Eighty-second Annual Meeting of the Academy of Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-b331eef2-a77d-489c-a4ef-d9341b1f5a10"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Cognitive Leadership, Systemic Innovation, and the Formation of Innovation Ecosystems","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-292390","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The coagulation system is not fully developed at birth and matures during the first months of infancy, complicating clinical decision making within hemostasis. This study evaluates coagulation parameters at birth and two months after birth, and tests whether cord blood can be used as a proxy for neonatal venous blood measurements. The Copenhagen Baby Heart Study (CBHS) and the COMPARE study comprise 13,237 cord blood samples and 444 parallel neonatal venous blood samples, with a two month follow-up in 362 children. Because coagulation parameters differed according to gestational age (GA), all analyses were stratified by GA. For neonatal venous blood, reference intervals for activated partial thromboplastin time (APTT) and prothrombin time (PT) were 28-43 s and 33-61% for GA 37-39 and 24-38 s and 30-65% for GA 40-42. Reference intervals for international normalized ratio (INR) and thrombocyte count were 1.1-1.7 and 194-409 × 109/L for GA 37-39 and 1.2-1.8 and 188-433 × 109/L for GA 40-42. Correlation coefficients between umbilical cord and neonatal venous blood for APTT, PT, INR, and thrombocyte count were 0.68, 0.72, 0.69, and 0.77 respectively, and the distributions of the parameters did not differ between the two types of blood (all p-values>0.05). This study describes new GA dependent reference intervals for common coagulation parameters in newborns and suggests that cord blood may serve as a proxy for neonatal venous blood for these traits. Such data will likely improve clinical decision making within hemostasis among newborn and infant children.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nielsen, Sofie Taageby","Strandkjær, Nina","Juul Rasmussen, Ida","Hansen, Malene Kongsgaard","Lytsen, Rikke Mohr","Kamstrup, Pia R.","Rode, Line","Goetze, Jens P.","Iversen, Kasper","Bundgaard, Henning","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-467795"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coagulation","Cord blood","Hemostasis","Neonatology","Reference intervals"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coagulation parameters in the newborn and infant the copenhagen baby heart and compare studies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/396648265/Coagulation_parameters_in_the_newborn_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-467795","identifier":[{"id":"85119398122","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34752018","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7c1c2105-3d40-4a01-9b2c-f75a60b77855"],"keyword":["coagulation","cord blood","hemostasis","neonatology","reference intervals"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7262B483444CF738FB496AE879D5465A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/396648265/Coagulation_parameters_in_the_newborn_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sofie Taageby","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Sofie Taageby","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"strandkjærpau","last":"Strandkjær","name":"Strandkjær, Nina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida","key":"juulrasmussenpau","last":"Juul Rasmussen","name":"Juul Rasmussen, Ida","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malene Kongsgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Malene Kongsgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke Mohr","key":"lytsenpau","last":"Lytsen","name":"Lytsen, Rikke Mohr","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia R.","key":"kamstruppau","last":"Kamstrup","name":"Kamstrup, Pia R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"rodepau","last":"Rode","name":"Rode, Line","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens P.","key":"goetzepau","last":"Goetze","locid":"980bceaf-dbf3-4f7a-a8d7-0a8e81b638b2","name":"Goetze, Jens P.","orcid":"0000-0001-6356-3829","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henning","key":"bundgaardpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"254c7f8d-79dd-4a5d-870f-3ed78cb56464","name":"Bundgaard, Henning","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ruth","key":"frikkeschmidtpau","last":"Frikke-Schmidt","locid":"bce2c3b4-6e08-46c7-96c6-7e385b0ec8b3","name":"Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34752018"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/cclm-2021-0967","issn":["14346621","14374331"],"issn_org":["14346621"],"issue":"2","journal":"Clinical Chemistry and Laboratory Medicine","pages":"261-270","status":"p","title":"Clinical Chemistry and Laboratory Medicine","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119398122"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7c1c2105-3d40-4a01-9b2c-f75a60b77855"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coagulation parameters in the newborn and infant : The Copenhagen Baby Heart and COMPARE studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-467795","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: 20-40% of people with inflammatory arthritis (IA) do not tolerate or do not have sufficient effect of their medication and experience substantial impact of their disease. They need rehabilitation to develop or restore functioning and become able to live an independent and meaningful life (1). Rehabilitation and the organisation of health and social care services are characterised by a high degree of complexity and many different professionals working across different departments, primary and secondary sectors. Objectives: To investigate how health and social care professionals across different departments, levels and sectors work to achieve coherent rehabilitation pathways for people with IA Methods: In total, 26 professionals across primary and secondary health and social care participated in semi-structured interviews. These professionals were all pointed out by people with IA because they had made a significant difference to achieve coherent rehabilitation pathways for them. In addition, participant observations and informal interviews with the healthcare professionals were conducted during the rehabilitation stay. Formula stories (2) and institutional ethnography (3) guided the interpretation of data. In the findings, the term people is changed to users to underline their interactions with the professionals. Results: The analysis derived three themes: 1) Interactions with users: the professional's interactions with users were predominantly characterized by the ideal of focusing on the individual human being with respect for individual’s norms, values and wishes. However, this ideal was challenged when their professional knowledge contradicted the user's norms, values and wishes. 2) Dependent interactions between professionals: expresses dependency of collaboration between professionals both internally within the same department or organization but also across organizations and sectors. Dependency on information about the user to carry out examinations, deliver care or treatment or dependency on referrals to legitimize the efforts the professionals considered necessary for the user. 3) The significance of organisation within institutional frameworks for the professionals’ work: the professionals experienced that they were not always able to meet the users demand for care due to organizational requirements for efficiency, economic cost reductions and documentation. These issues led to lack of time to prepare, implement, and follow up on communication with users and other professional partners. Conclusion: The professionals want to meet the individual with a person-centred approach but sometimes they find it difficult to combine this with their own professional knowledge and values. The professionals are dependent on collaboration with other professionals across departments and sectors. This study shows that the institutional and organizational framework can hinder rather than promote the professionals' intentions to create coherent rehabilitation. References: 1. Hjortbak BR et al. Udfordringer til rehabilitering i Danmark [Challenges in rehabilitation in Denmark]. 2011. 2. Loseke DR. The Empirical Analysis of Formula Stories. In: Holstein J, et al (ed): Varieties of Narrative Analysis. SAGE; 2012. 3. Smith DE. Institutional ethnography. AltaMira Press; 2005.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Feddersen, Helle","Søndergaard, Jens","Schmidt, Bettina Munksgaard","Andersen, Lena","Primdahl, Jette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-654753"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-04","place":"København","start":"2022-06-01","title":"EULAR European Congress of Rheumatology","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Patient Forskningspartner"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCS"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health and social care professionals work to achieve coherent rehabilitation pathways for people with inflammatory arthritis a qualitative interview and observational study","src":["ucsyd"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCS"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://congress.eular.org/myUploadData/files/eular_2022_abstracts_final_lowres.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-654753","ids":["ucsyd-f478ef7f-e3a4-4b3f-88da-8669aa31ccf1"],"keyword":["disease, health science and nursing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-75BC2C547BCF3D979A20AC3DC13EF228"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://congress.eular.org/myUploadData/files/eular_2022_abstracts_final_lowres.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"uc syd university college south denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCS","l3nl":"UC SYD, University College South Denmark","l3nn":"UC SYD University College South Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UC SYD University College South Denmark","namevar":["UC SYD, Pædagogik og skole, Forskning, Forskningsprogrammet for sundhedsfaglig praksis","UC SYD, Samfund og sundhed, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":