ure Targets in Comatose Survivors of Cardiac Arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.68-045694","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Data on Device-related Thrombus (DRT) after left atrial appendage closure (LAAC) remain scarce. This study aimed to investigate risk factors for DRT from centers reporting to the EUROC-DRT registry. Methods: We included 537 patients (112 with DRT and 425 without DRT) who had undergone LAAC between 12/2008 and 04/2019. Baseline and implantation characteristics, anti-thrombotic treatment and clinical outcomes were compared between both groups in uni- and multivariate analyses. Additional propensity-score matching (PSM) was conducted to focus on the role of implantation characteristics. Results: Patients with DRT showed higher rates of previous stroke/transient ischemic attack (TIA) (49.1% vs. 34.7%, p < 0.01), spontaneous echocardiographic contrast (SEC) (44.9% vs. 27.7%, p < 0.01) and lower left atrial appendage (LAA) peak emptying velocity (35.4 ± 18.5 vs. 42.4 ± 18.0 cm/s, p = 0.02). Occluders implanted in DRT patients were larger (25.5 ± 3.8 vs. 24.6 ± 3.5 mm, p = 0.03) and implanted deeper in the LAA (mean depth: 7.6 ± 4.7 vs. 5.7 ± 4.7 mm, p < 0.01). Coverage of the appendage ostium was achieved less often in DRT patients (69.5% vs. 81.5%, p < 0.01), while DRT patients were less frequently on oral anticoagulation (7.1% vs. 16.7%, p < 0.01). Multivariate analysis identified age, prior stroke/TIA and SEC as independent risk factors for DRT. After PSM, implantation depth was found to be predictive. Rates of stroke/TIA were higher in DRT patients (13.5% vs. 3.8%, Hazard Ratio: 4.21 [95%-confidence interval: 1.88–9.49], p < 0.01). Conclusions: DRT after LAAC is associated with adverse outcome and appears to be of multifactorial origin, depending on patient characteristics, anticoagulation regimen and device position. Graphical abstract: [Figure not available: see fulltext.].","author_count":48,"contributors":["Vij, Vivian","Piayda, Kerstin","Nelles, Dominik","Gloekler, Steffen","Galea, Roberto","Fürholz, Monika","Meier, Bernhard","Valgimigli, Marco","O'Hara, Gilles","Arzamendi, Dabit","Agudelo, Victor","Asmarats, Lluis","Freixa, Xavier","Flores-Umanzor, Eduardo","De Backer, Ole","Sondergaard, Lars","Nombela-Franco, Luis","McInerney, Angela","Korsholm, Kasper","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Afzal, Shazia","Zeus, Tobias","Operhalski, Felix","Schmidt, Boris","Montalescot, Gilles","Guedeney, Paul","Iriart, Xavier","Miton, Noelie","Saw, Jacqueline","Gilhofer, Thomas","Fauchier, Laurent","Veliqi, Egzon","Meincke, Felix","Petri, Nils","Nordbeck, Peter","Ognerubov, Dmitrii","Merkulov, Evgeny","Cruz-González, Ignacio","Gonzalez-Ferreiro, Rocio","Bhatt, Deepak L","Laricchia, Alessandra","Mangieri, Antonio","Omran, Heyder","Schrickel, Jan Wilko","Rodes-Cabau, Josep","Sievert, Horst","Nickenig, Georg","Sedaghat, Alexander"],"cuid":["S02-099.76-017903"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","France","Germany","Italy","Russia","Spain","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Asklepios Klinik St. Georg","Autonomous University of Barcelona","CHU de Bordeaux","CardioVascular Center Frankfurt CVC","CardioVasculäres Centrum Frankfurt","Cardioangiologisches Centrum am Bethanien Krankenhaus, Frankfurt, Germany.","Cardiocentro Ticino Foundation","Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Tours","Harvard University","Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf","Hospital Clinic de Barcelona","Hospital Clínico San Carlos de Madrid","Hospital Clínico Universitario de Salamanca","Hospital of Santa Creu i Sant Pau","Humanitas University","IRCCS Istituto Clinico Humanitas - Rozzano (Milano)","Laval University","Marienkrankenhaus","Markus-Krankenhaus Frankfurt","Respiratory Diseases, Humanitas University, Italy.","Russian Academy of Sciences","Sorbonne University","Sorbonne Université","St. Marien Hospital","Universidad de Salamanca","Universite Borde