{"abstract":"Systemic administration of beta-hydroxybutyrate (BHB) decreases whole-body protein oxidation and muscle protein breakdown in humans. We aimed to determine any direct effect of BHB on skeletal muscle protein turnover when administered locally in the femoral artery. Paired design with each subject being investigated on one single occasion with one leg being infused with BHB and the opposing leg acting as a control. We studied 10 healthy male volunteers once with bilateral femoral vein and artery catheters. One artery was perfused with saline (Placebo) and one with sodium-BHB. Labelled phenylalanine and palmitate were used to assess local leg fluxes. Femoral vein concentrations of BHB were significantly higher in the intervention leg (3.4 (3.2, 3.6) mM) compared with the placebo-controlled leg (1.9 (1.8, 2.1) mM) with a peak difference of 1.4 (1.1, 1.7) mM, p < 0.0005. Net loss of phenylalanine for BHB vs Placebo -6.7(-10.8, -2.7) nmol/min vs -8.7(-13.8, -3.7) nmol/min, p = 0.52. Palmitate flux and arterio-venous difference of glucose did not differ between legs. Under these experimental conditions, we failed to observe the direct effects of BHB on skeletal muscle protein turnover. This may relate to a combination of high concentrations of BHB (close to 2 mM) imposed systemically by spillover leading to high BHB concentrations in the saline-infused leg and a lack of major differences in concentration gradients between the two sides-implying that observations were made on the upper part of the dose-response curve for BHB and the relatively small number of subjects studied.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Thomsen, Henrik Holm","Olesen, Jonas Franck","Aagaard, Rasmus","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Voss, Thomas Schmidt","Svart, Mads","Johannsen, Mogens","Jessen, Niels","Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","Rittig, Nikolaj","Bach, Ermina","Møller, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-256917"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thomsen, Henrik Holm"],"keyword":["Amino acid","Beta hydroxybutyrate","Breakdown","Glucose","Insulin","Ketone bodies","Ketosis","Resistance exercise","amino acid tracer","ketone body"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating effects of sodium beta hydroxybutyrate on metabolism in placebo controlled bilaterally infused human leg with focus on skeletal muscle protein dynamics","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.15399","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-256917","identifier":[{"id":"000842006600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9391664","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85136848182","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35986508","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-df7bc4d8-e18b-4321-a326-af41e5d6ede8"],"keyword":["AMINO-ACID","BREAKDOWN","GLUCOSE","INSULIN","KETONE-BODY","RESISTANCE EXERCISE","amino acid tracer","beta-hydroxybutyrate","ketone bodies","ketosis","perfused leg"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1789A601AED9D9E8536FFE2E774AC1B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9391664/pdf/PHY2-10-e15399.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14814/phy2.15399","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Endocrinology and Internal Medicine","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afdeling, Viborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Holm","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"8a62ba63-8721-464e-b09f-c97db8bb4ad9","name":"Thomsen, Henrik Holm","orcid":"0000-0003-0522-0320","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Franck","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"b5ecb345-3bc0-4b45-824d-4e715e08fcdb","name":"Olesen, Jonas Franck","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","locid":"a9b7b871-50e5-4a51-8a5d-56fa812d8704","name":"Aagaard, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent Roni Ranghoj","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"896f4a21-d29c-4ad9-b0ef-4e7f8616c234","name":"Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","name_org":"Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghoj","orcid":"0000-0001-9228-3869","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Schmidt","key":"vosspau","last":"Voss","locid":"cec29a7a-aafc-4df3-9431-0e5895d745d2","name":"Voss, Thomas Schmidt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Vandsted","key":"svartpau","last":"Svart","locid":"a8b24d1c-a84f-4d6c-ad15-b8affc06c72d","name":"Svart, Mads","name_org":"Svart, Mads Vandsted","orcid":"0000-0002-9574-0612","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","locid":"75805917-240a-47fb-8c5f-ef88bb000b43","name":"Johannsen, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-2548-7025","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"f0d20e5e-d5b5-44da-980e-3e052af18b46","name":"Jessen, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5613-7274","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Otto L.","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","locid":"303ebe86-6861-4b19-b4d7-6bda0526b27e","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde","name_org":"Jorgensen, Jens Otto L.","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-1526","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nikolaj","key":"rittigpau","last":"Rittig","locid":"7a9d4a8a-626a-4c30-bf6e-b466d53df686","name":"Rittig, Nikolaj","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ermina","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","locid":"0fde522d-8d9a-4c30-be84-67f4fa728558","name":"Bach, Ermina","orcid":"0000-0002-7649-5658","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"2e0d8e2a-2da1-4d55-b2da-0a25c0375b1e","name":"Møller, Niels","name_org":"Moller, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5627-7322","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35986508"],"pub":{"doi":"10.14814/phy2.15399","issn":["2051817X"],"issue":"16","journal":"Physiological Reports","paperid":"e15399","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Physiological Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136848182"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-df7bc4d8-e18b-4321-a326-af41e5d6ede8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Investigating effects of sodium beta-hydroxybutyrate on metabolism in placebo-controlled, bilaterally infused human leg with focus on skeletal muscle protein dynamics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-256917","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"When thinking about and communicating their views about the future (e.g., whether a novel business model is scalable) strategists use theories and what-if beliefs (e.g., under which conditions the business model is scalable) as a way to simplify a complex space of possibilities. In this paper we propose a formal framework to examine how a strategist (e.g., a founder) can get others (e.g., an investor) to agree on his view of the future by communicating parts of his theory (e.g., convince him that the business model is scalable). Because his theory may be in conflict with others' theories getting them to agree may require them to give up beliefs. We use our framework to derive formal results about the difficulty to get agreement. Our framework builds on established assumptions about forward-looking reasoning, augmented with the assumption that strategists give up weakest premises of their theories first when faced with contradictions. Our results provide insights on how strategists can create “cognitive buy-in” on their views from others and thus shape organizations and markets to tap into new opportunities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ehrig, Timo","Schmidt, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-280102"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-09","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2022-08-05","title":"The Academy of Management Annual Meeting 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Best paper"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"getting others to agree on a view of the future","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-280102","identifier":[{"id":"85176591348","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-31d21b8b-6571-4e52-8ee5-2e9e8b0a69e8"],"keyword":["Best paper"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-4-76204453DAB2D8CBC4C589622D619BE9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Timo","key":"ehrigpau","last":"Ehrig","locid":"cca2661b-d9ba-419c-952e-397c9dc771af","name":"Ehrig, Timo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sonja","key":"tanejapedh","last":"Taneja","name":"Taneja, Sonja","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5465/ambpp.2022.224","issn":["00650668"],"place":"Briarcliff Manor, NY","publisher":"Academy of Management","series":"Academy of Management Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Eighty-second Annual Meeting of the Academy of Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85176591348","2-s2.0-85188076823","2-s2.0-85208721110"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-31d21b8b-6571-4e52-8ee5-2e9e8b0a69e8"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Getting Others to Agree on a View of the Future","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-280102","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The appropriate oxygenation target for mechanical ventilation in comatose survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest is unknown. METHODS: In this randomized trial with a 2-by-2 factorial design, we randomly assigned comatose adults with out-of-hospital cardiac arrest in a 1:1 ratio to either a restrictive oxygen target of a partial pressure of arterial oxygen (Pao2) of 9 to 10 kPa (68 to 75 mm Hg) or a liberal oxygen target of a Pao2 of 13 to 14 kPa (98 to 105 mm Hg); patients were also assigned to one of two blood-pressure targets (reported separately). The primary outcome was a composite of death from any cause or hospital discharge with severe disability or coma (Cerebral Performance Category [CPC] of 3 or 4; categories range from 1 to 5, with higher values indicating more severe disability), whichever occurred first within 90 days after randomization. Secondary outcomes were neuron-specific enolase levels at 48 hours, death from any cause, the score on the Montreal Cognitive Assessment (ranging from 0 to 30, with higher scores indicating better cognitive ability), the score on the modified Rankin scale (ranging from 0 to 6, with higher scores indicating greater disability), and the CPC at 90 days. RESULTS: A total of 789 patients underwent randomization. A primary-outcome event occurred in 126 of 394 patients (32.0%) in the restrictive-target group and in 134 of 395 patients (33.9%) in the liberal-target group (hazard ratio, 0.95; 95% confidence interval, 0.75 to 1.21; P = 0.69). At 90 days, death had occurred in 113 patients (28.7%) in the restrictive-target group and in 123 (31.1%) in the liberal-target group. On the CPC, the median category was 1 in the two groups; on the modified Rankin scale, the median score was 2 in the restrictive-target group and 1 in the liberal-target group; and on the Montreal Cognitive Assessment, the median score was 27 in the two groups. At 48 hours, the median neuron-specific enolase level was 17 μg per liter in the restrictive-target group and 18 μg per liter in the liberal-target group. The incidence of adverse events was similar in the two groups. CONCLUSIONS: Targeting of a restrictive or liberal oxygenation strategy in comatose patients after resuscitation for cardiac arrest resulted in a similar incidence of death or severe disability or coma. (Funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation; BOX ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT03141099.).","author_count":30,"contributors":["Schmidt, Henrik","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Hassager, Christian","Mølstrøm, Simon","Grand, Johannes","Borregaard, Britt","Roelsgaard Obling, Laust E.","Venø, Søren","Sarkisian, Laura","Mamaev, Dmitry","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Nyholm, Benjamin","Høfsten, Dan E.","Josiassen, Jakob","Thomsen, Jakob H.","Thune, Jens J.","Lindholm, Matias G.","Stengaard Meyer, Martin A.","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Sørensen, Marc","Frydland, Martin","Beske, Rasmus P.","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Wiberg, Sebastian","Boesgaard, Søren","Lind Jørgensen, Vibeke","Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"cuid":["S02-098.38-047545"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Møller, Jacob Eifer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oxygen targets in comatose survivors of cardiac arrest","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa2208686","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.38-047545","identifier":[{"id":"36027567","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85140415254","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f8e6b4c7-39a3-44d2-9e0b-f8b85a9a44ea","sdu-dedef7f3-8fb6-4143-b2e5-0e2378081f0e