Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-496f3220-056c-4060-9f6c-85a36257cfb0","ku-fbc4a8cc-a79d-4b62-a0d6-814ef2060a8f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Biomarkers of Clot Activation and Degradation and Risk of Future Major Cardiovascular Events in Acute Exacerbation of COPD : A Cohort Sub-Study in a Randomized Trial Population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.43-018001","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patient satisfaction is the most critical outcome in gynecomastia treatment. However, patient satisfaction may be affected by the patient's decision-making trait, such as exhaustively searching for the best outcome or being content with an outcome that satisfies a preconceived requirement. Objective: To assess whether patient's decision-making characteristic affect their satisfaction with gynecomastia treatment. Methods: This was a cross-sectional study including patients treated for gynecomastia between January 2009 and December 2019 at two tertiary hospitals in Denmark. Alive patients were sent the BODY-Q: Chest module, the SF-36 questionnaire, and the Maximizer/Satisficer decision-making survey. Patients were classified as Maximizers if they scored more than 40 points on the Maximizer/Satisficer survey. Percentage score differences (PDs) in quality of life scales were calculated between Maximizers and Satisficers. Results: In total, 192 gynecomastia patients were included in this study and classified as Maximizers (n = 152) or Satisficers (n = 40). Maximizers were younger and more had gynecomastia following abuse of anabolic steroids than Satisficers (p < 0.05). With respect to bodily satisfaction, Maximizers showed significantly worse satisfaction with nipples (PDs: − 12.98%), psychological function (PDs: − 13.68%) and social function (PDs: − 8.77%, p < 0.05). In addition, Maximizers had significantly worse emotional role functioning (− 11.03%), vitality (PDs: − 11.72%) and mental health (PDs: − 10.00%, p < 0.05). Conclusion: Patients exhibiting maximizing-type decision-making characteristics have worse satisfaction with gynecomastia treatment and poorer psychosocial health. This information may facilitate patient counseling and alignment of treatment expectations. Level of evidence IV: This journal requires that authors assign a level of evidence to each article. For a full description of these Evidence-Based Medicine ratings, please refer to the Table of Contents or the online Instructions to Authors www.springer.com/00266.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","Cho, Bu Youn","Hansen, Frederik Christopher Gulmark","Schmidt, Volker Jürgen","Sørensen, Jens Ahm","Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045266"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf"],"keyword":["BODY Q","Cross Sectional Studies","Decision making","Glandular excision","Gynecomastia","Humans","Liposuction","Male","Patient Satisfaction","Quality of Life","Retrospective Studies","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patients decision making characteristics affects gynecomastia treatment satisfaction a multicenter study using the body q chest module","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85118139288","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-045266","identifier":[{"id":"34704122","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85118139288","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-acdc656c-3382-44b4-9ca2-448c52132a85","sdu-067349f4-4100-4a30-8f2d-10d4a9d3189e"],"keyword":["BODY-Q","Cross-Sectional Studies","Decision-making","Glandular excision","Gynecomastia","Gynecomastia/psychology","Humans","Liposuction","Male","Patient Satisfaction","Quality of life","Retrospective Studies","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D722DD87AC97C47E5215AB45012E10CB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Plastic Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Plastic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Gustaf","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"aebe7465-c8a9-452a-9b45-6259e674c2ee","name":"Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","orcid":"0000-0002-8755-3446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bu Youn","key":"chopau","last":"Cho","name":"Cho, Bu Youn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Gulmark","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"25d105b1-fa78-4c30-96f3-caed7b784dec","name":"Hansen, Frederik Christopher Gulmark","name_org":"Hansen, Frederik Gulmark","orcid":"0000-0002-4588-8053","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Volker Jürgen","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"42a7c6c8-5c08-4c7a-99b2-20df4cde63f5","name":"Schmidt, Volker J","name_org":"Schmidt, Volker Jürgen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Navid Mohamadpour","key":"toyserkanipau","last":"Toyserkani","name":"Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34704122"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00266-021-02633-5","issn":["0364216X","14325241"],"issn_org":["0364216X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Aesthetic Plastic Surgery","pages":"1053-1062","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Aesthetic Plastic Surgery","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118139288"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-acdc656c-3382-44b4-9ca2-448c52132a85","sdu-067349f4-4100-4a30-8f2d-10d4a9d3189e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patients Decision-Making Characteristics Affects Gynecomastia Treatment Satisfaction : A Multicenter Study Using the BODY-Q Chest Module","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045266","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this prospective nationwide multicenter study from Denmark, myopericarditis after Pfizer-BioNTech mRNA COVID-19 vaccination was identified in 13 males and 2 females between May 15 and September 15, 2021, among 133,477 vaccinated males and 127,857 vaccinated females 12-17 years of age, equaling 97 males and 16 females per million. In conclusion, the incidence of myopericarditis after COVID-19 vaccination among males appears higher than reports from the United States.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Nygaard, Ulrikka","Holm, Mette","Bohnstedt, Cathrine","Chai, Qing","Schmidt, Lisbeth Samsø","Hartling, Ulla Birgitte","Petersen, Jens Jakob Herrche","Thaarup, Jesper","Bjerre, Jesper","Vejlstrup, Niels Grove","Juul, Klaus","Stensballe, Lone Graff"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-002302"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Nygaard, Ulrikka"],"keyword":["2021","Adolescent","Adolescents","BNT162 Vaccine adverse effects","Child","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Male","Myocarditis chemically induced","Prospective Studies","mRNA COVID 19 vaccine","myopericarditis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Regionshosp Nordjylland, Dept Paediat & Adolescent Med"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"population based incidence of myopericarditis after covid 000000000019 vaccination in danish adolescents","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/INF.0000000000003389","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was funded by a COVID-19 grant from the National Ministry of Higher Education and Science (grant no. 0237-00004B)."],"id":"S04-100.00-002302","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8658061","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000728786600011","type":"wos"},{"id":"34889875","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122024310","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2db4b734-09c0-44c6-854e-075b9af6fb30","au-ae9ac912-acc4-4724-9cf5-18f364cde151","ku-824cebbe-92a0-4838-b9c3-9dfbde25431c","sdu-bb687a71-2d41-476f-9fc1-4d3337f008c0"],"keyword":["2021","Adolescent","BNT162 Vaccine/adverse effects","Child","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Incidence","Male","Myocarditis/chemically induced","Pericarditis/chemically induced","Prospective Studies","adolescents","adolescents Accepted for publication October 10","mRNA COVID-19 vaccine","myopericarditis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-8381BA9E70333B7F573B04E0309DF262"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/INF.0000000000003389","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8658061/pdf/inf-41-e25.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359087118/Population_based_Incidence_of_Myopericarditis.26_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical S