%20and%20observational%20study&view=1&item=2022OP0296-HPR","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Danish Hospital for Rheumatic Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"uc syd university college south denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCS","l3nl":"UC SYD, University College South Denmark","l3nn":"UC SYD University College South Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UC SYD University College South Denmark","namevar":["University College Syddanmark"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCS","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Sygehus Sønderjylland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"feddersenpau","last":"Feddersen","locid":"6c418665-f120-421f-a856-72cbff84143d","name":"Feddersen, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-3818-5843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"munksgaardschmidtpau","last":"Munksgaard Schmidt","name":"Munksgaard Schmidt, Bettina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lena","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"primdahloth","last":"Primdahl","locid":"e7f33410-2d7a-4869-b5e9-ed886ba48c94","name":"Primdahl, Jette","orcid":"0000-0002-1049-4150","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/annrheumdis-2022-eular.2726","issn":["00034967","14682060"],"issn_org":["00034967"],"issue":"suppl. 1","journal":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","pages":"197","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","UC SYD, University College South Denmark","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-612381d6-fbb1-416b-b96d-61c6b9f71d24"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"OP0296-HPR Health and social care professionals’ work to achieve coherent rehabilitation pathways for people with Inflammatory Arthritis : A qualitative interview and observational study","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-600985","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Food resources are limited in arid countries such as the United Arab Emirates (UAE); the salinity of the groundwater, together with a lack of natural fresh water sources and arable land, force the country to import most of its food. However, seaweed could play an important role in providing a locally available food resource, as it does not require fresh water and arable land to grow. The traditional use of several seaweed species as food sources has been documented in Asia and the Americas, where their nutritional composition has been well reported. Although the UAE’s aquatic environment is quite harsh due to high water salinity (over 40 g/L) and high surface water temperatures (over 35 °C), its native seaweed species could play a role as a food source in this arid region, thereby bolstering the country’s level of food security. To evaluate its potential in this context, fresh samples of the native Ulva intestinalis seaweed were collected in the shallow waters of Abu Dhabi Emirate, UAE. These samples were calculated to contain 34.38 ± 0.24 kcal, with a biomass composition of 5.185 ± 0.04% carbohydrate, 3.32 ± 0.14% protein, and 0.04 ± 0.01% fat (by dry matter). Of all the minerals present in the biomass, potassium had the highest concentration (7947 ± 319.5 ppm), followed by magnesium (3075.9 ± 1357 ppm) and sodium (756.3 ± 478 ppm). The water-soluble vitamins B1, B2, B3, B6, and C were below the detection limit in the samples. The rich concentration of essential minerals such as potassium, magnesium, iron and zinc in Ulva intestinalis makes it a promising novel food source. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first experimental study to examine the feasibility of using seaweed that is native to the UAE as a nutritional and sustainable food source in order to address the challenge of food security currently being faced by the country.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Farzanah, Rashed Husain","Clausen, Mathias P.","Arnspang, Eva C.","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635692"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo"],"keyword":["Food security","Minerals","Nutritional composition","Seaweed"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of united arab emirates native seaweed ulva intestinalis as a food source study of nutritional and mineral compositions","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/phycology2010008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635692","identifier":[{"id":"85181910104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-da2999a5-e67c-448f-8e46-10fa40f7a327"],"keyword":["Ulva intestinalis","edible algae","food security","minerals","nutritional composition","seaweed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E3C5F86EEB3EF8383EF96B14B2A757FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/200457976/Feasibility_of_United_Arab_Emirates_Native_Seaweed_Ulva_intestinalis_as_a_Food_Source_Study_of_Nutritional_andMineral_Compositions.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/phycology2010008","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT), SDU Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rashed Husain","key":"farzanahpau","last":"Farzanah","locid":"65f978cd-0958-4a8c-b6a0-981b925d4bb1","name":"Farzanah, Rashed Husain","orcid":"0000-0002-5142-3842","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias Porsmose","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"dad6e7b1-6013-461d-b9a6-367b146f5d86","name":"Clausen, Mathias P.","name_org":"Clausen, Mathias Porsmose","orcid":"0000-0003-1196-6241","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva C.","key":"arnspangpau","last":"Arnspang","locid":"400511b0-9aec-496e-abc0-9b44c1abb4ed","name":"Arnspang, Eva C.","orcid":"0000-0002-3095-4070","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","locid":"840da3ca-81a6-461d-a027-5716b944217e","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo","name_org":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","orcid":"0000-0002-2418-441X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/phycology2010008","issn":["26739410"],"issue":"1","journal":"Phycology","pages":"120-131","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Phycology","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181910104"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-da2999a5-e67c-448f-8e46-10fa40f7a327"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Feasibility of United Arab Emirates Native Seaweed Ulva intestinalis as a Food Source : Study of Nutritional and Mineral Compositions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-635692","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Schmidt, Jette Reuss","Dolin, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-650041"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Uddannelse professioner og erhverv"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"refleksioner over naturfaglig dannelse og kompetence på baggrund af forskerseminar","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/mona/article/view/133866","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-650041","ids":["ucn-01be442d-61ab-4ce2-a892-fd13018534ce"],"keyword":["Uddannelse, professioner og erhverv"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3AC4BC49BF8ADE0C61E29888F627AEB1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Læreruddannelsen Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette Reuss","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"64019928-723e-46f1-9050-f238ee04efd6","name":"Schmidt, J