ur","key":"toyserkanipau","last":"Toyserkani","locid":"1fe54f0a-4c69-467e-8d39-62f685e36625","name":"Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35037080"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00266-021-02710-9","issn":["0364216X","14325241"],"issn_org":["0364216X"],"issue":"Suppl 1","journal":"Aesthetic Plastic Surgery","pages":"52-53","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Aesthetic Plastic Surgery","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123067226"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fc0aa504-cd8d-4f4f-bab4-70c043bfa632","sdu-06310ead-18b9-40c5-b722-f5d96ac0816e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Invited Response on: Patients Decision-Making Characteristics Affects Gynecomastia Treatment Satisfaction: A Multicenter Study Using the BODY-Q Chest Module","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.59-047632","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Bin/amphiphysin/Rvs (BAR) domains are positively charged crescent-shaped modules that mediate curvature of negatively charged lipid membranes during remodeling processes. The BAR domain proteins PICK1, ICA69, and the arfaptins have recently been demonstrated to coordinate the budding and formation of immature secretory granules (ISGs) at the trans- Golgi network. Here, we identify 4 coding variants in the PICK1 gene from a whole-exome screening of Danish patients with diabetes that each involve a change in positively charged residues in the PICK1 BAR domain. All 4 coding variants failed to rescue insulin content in INS-1E cells upon knock down of endogenous PICK1. Moreover, 2 variants showed dominantnegative properties. In vitro assays addressing BAR domain function suggested that the coding variants compromised BAR domain function but increased the capacity to cause fission of liposomes. Live confocal microscopy and super-resolution microscopy further revealed that PICK1 resides transiently on ISGs before egress via vesicular budding events. Interestingly, this egress of PICK1 was accelerated in the coding variants. We propose that PICK1 assists in or complements the removal of excess membrane and generic membrane trafficking proteins, and possibly also insulin, from ISGs during the maturation process; and that the coding variants may cause premature budding, possibly explaining their dominant-negative function.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Andersen, Rita Chan","Schmidt, Jan Hendrik","Rombach, Joscha","Lycas, Matthew D.","Christensen, Nikolaj Riis","Lund, Viktor Karlovich","Stapleton, Donnie S.","Pedersen, Signe Schultz","Olsen, Mathias A.","Stoklund, Mikkel","Noes-Holt, Gith","Nielsen, Tommas T.E.","Keller, Mark P.","Jansen, Anna M.","Herlo, Rasmus","Pietropaolo, Massimo","Simonsen, Jens B.","Kjaerulff, Ole","Holst, Birgitte","Attie, Alan D.","Gether, Ulrik","Madsen, Kenneth Lindegaard"],"cuid":["S02-095.21-037549"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gether, Ulrik","Madsen, Kenneth L."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","University of Wisconsin-Madison"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coding variants identified in patients with diabetes alter pick000000000001 bar domain function in insulin granule biogenesis","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI144904","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.21-037549","identifier":[{"id":"85125553878","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8884907","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35077398","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-dc9e2d24-b701-490c-be00-008637b49845","ku-15505749-3dc8-4b40-8529-19c5197cfa59"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D4092EFE4332DC33363C55D8F298E18A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/299902551/Coding.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/302225050/144904.2_20220224174833_covered_e0fd13ba177f913fd3156f593ead4cfd.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI144904","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3n