{"abstract":"Hvordan udvikler man de arbejdsmarkeder i Danmark, som ligger udenfor de store bycentre som København, Århus, Odense og Aalborg? Kan udflytning af statslige arbejdspladser være en del af løsningen herpå?","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schmidt, Torben Dall","Jensen, Peter Sandholt","Sørensen, Jens Fyhn Lykke","Svendsen, Gunnar Lind Haase"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-643452"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interviews","Landdistriktspolitik","Regional udvikling","Regionaløkonomi","Spørgeskemaundersøgelse","Udflytning af statslige arbejdspladser"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udflytning af statslige arbejdspladser hvordan påvirkes beskæftigelsen på det lokale arbejdsmarked","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sdu.dk/-/media/files/om_sdu/institutter/miljo/sebe/clf/clf_rapporter/udflytning_af_statslige_arbejdspladser_clf+rapport77.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-643452","ids":["sdu-f57b423b-23ec-4c36-9bb3-255d8f7eba2b"],"keyword":["Effekter på det private erhvervsliv","Interviews","Land-by balance","Landdistriktspolitik","Lokal sammenhængskraft","Regional udvikling","Regional økonomi","Registerdata-analyse","Sikkerhedsstyrelsen i Esbjerg","Skattestyrelsen i Ringkøbing","Spørgeskemaundersøgelse","Statslige styrelser","Syntetisk kontrol metode","Udflytning af statslige arbejdspladser"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F1E9F24DFB9EFEB030079CF6732A63C0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sdu.dk/-/media/files/om_sdu/institutter/miljo/sebe/clf/clf_rapporter/udflytning_af_statslige_arbejdspladser_clf+rapport77.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Dall","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"ec808865-a087-40bc-95b4-443ffae4b2e1","name":"Schmidt, Torben Dall","orcid":"0000-0002-7662-1669","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Sandholt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"44639fdc-5ba6-4f73-b353-e2b4e4578c73","name":"Jensen, Peter Sandholt","orcid":"0000-0003-1905-6859","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Fyhn Lykke","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"86a1d89b-e801-4de5-9599-811c496d9de2","name":"Sørensen, Jens Fyhn Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-1227-1783","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gunnar Lind Haase","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"f78945d9-87ac-45c0-a96f-1fe38464ef58","name":"Svendsen, Gunnar Lind Haase","orcid":"0000-0003-2989-2842","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"77","pages":"116","place":"Esbjerg","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet","repno":"CLF Rapport, No. 77","series":"CLF Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f57b423b-23ec-4c36-9bb3-255d8f7eba2b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Udflytning af statslige arbejdspladser : Hvordan påvirkes beskæftigelsen på det lokale arbejdsmarked?","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-643452","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The global warming and energy requirement have accentuated the need to convert atmospheric CO2 into fuels through a highly efficient photoelectrochemical cell (PEC) process. Typically, CO2 reduction at the cathode is accompanied by water oxidation at the anode to produce O2, which is not of significant value. Herein, we report the design of paired PEC to reduce CO2 to CH3OH and the oxidation of furfural (FF) to 2-furoic acid (2-FA) and 5-hydroxyfuroic acid (5-HFA). The paired PEC electrolyzer was constructed with Au/α-Fe2O3/RGO and Ru/RGO/Pt based asymmetric electrodes. The photocathode-driven PEC CO2 conversion test showed a high CH3OH yield of 63 μmol L−1 cm−2 at 21.5 % quantum efficiency with a Faradaic efficiency of 91 % at -0.6 V under visible light. The anodic furfural oxidation test demonstrated a higher FF conversion (82 %) with higher yields of 2-FA and 5-HFA. This study showed the potential of the paired PEC process to produce valuable products at both electrodes.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bharath, G.","Rambabu, K.","Hai, Abdul","Ponpandian, N.","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Dionysiou, Dionysios D.","Abu Haija, Mohammad","Banat, Fawzi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-645334"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bharath, G."],"country":["India","United Arab Emirates","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bharathiar University","Khalifa University","University of Cincinnati"],"keyword":["Methanol","Photocathode"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dual functional paired photoelectrocatalytic system for the photocathodic reduction of co sub 000000000002 sub to fuels and the anodic oxidation of furfural to value added chemicals","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85110636463","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We would like to thank the Khalifa University of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi , for supporting this study through an internal grant CIRA-2018-27 and CIRA-2020-085 . D. D. Dionysiou also acknowledges support from the University of Cincinnati through the Herman Schneider Professorship in the College of Engineering and Applied Sciences."],"id":"S01-000.00-645334","identifier":[{"id":"85110636463","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-fc205238-9499-4bfa-b568-f164368c5a0a"],"keyword":["Electro-oxidation of furfural","Methanol","Photocathode","Photoelectrocatalytic CO reduction","Sustainable liquid fuel production"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-412AC8FA04C3F2EEDBCD91C5059B5C19"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"bharathiar university","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Bharathiar University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of cincinnati","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Cincinnati","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"bharathpau","last":"Bharath","name":"Bharath, G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"rambabupau","last":"Rambabu","name":"Rambabu, K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Abdul","key":"haipau","last":"Hai","name":"Hai, Abdul","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"N.","key":"ponpandianpau","last":"Ponpandian","name":"Ponpandian, N.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dionysios D.","key":"dionysioupau","last":"Dionysiou","name":"Dionysiou, Dionysios D.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"abuhaijapau","last":"Abu Haija","name":"Abu Haija, Mohammad","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fawzi","key":"banatpau","last":"Banat","name":"Banat, Fawzi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apcatb.2021.120520","issn":["09263373","18733883"],"issn_org":["09263373"],"journal":"Applied Catalysis B: Environmental","paperid":"120520","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Catalysis B: Environmental","volume":"298"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85110636463"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fc205238-9499-4bfa-b568-f164368c5a0a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Dual-functional paired photoelectrocatalytic system for the photocathodic reduction of CO<sub>2</sub> to fuels and the anodic oxidation of furfural to value-added chemicals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-645334","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In 2008 we published the first set of guidelines for standardizing research in autophagy. Since then, research on this topic has continued to accelerate, and many new scientists have entered the field. Our knowledge base and relevant new technologies have also been expanding. Accordingly, it is important to update these guidelines formonitoring autophagy in different organisms. Various reviews have described the range of assays that have been used for this purpose. Nevertheless, there continues to be confusion regarding acceptable methods to measure autophagy, especially in multicellular eukaryotes. A key point that needs to be emphasized is that there is a Do not distribute. difference between measurements that monitor the numbers or volume of autophagic elements (e.g., autophagosomes or autolysosomes) at any stage of the autophagic process vs. those that measure flux through the autophagy pathway (i.e., the complete process); thus, a block in macroautophagy that results in autophagosome accumulation needs to be differentiated fromstimuli that result in increased autophagic activity, defined as increased autophagy induction coupled with increased delivery to, and degradation within, lysosomes (in most higher eukaryotes and some protists such as Dictyostelium) or the vacuole (in plants and fungi). In other words, it is especially important that investigators new to the field understand that the appearance of more autophagosomes does not necessarily equate withmore autophagy. In fact, in many cases, autophagosomes accumulate because of a block in trafficking to lysosomes without a concomitant change in autophagosome biogenesis,whereas an increase in autolysosomes may reflect a reduction in degradative activity. Here, we present a set of guidelines for the selection and interpretation of methods for use by investigators who aim to examine macroautophagy and related processes, as well as for reviewers who need to provide realistic and reasonable critiques of papers that are focused on these processes. These guidelines are not meant to be a formulaic set of rules, because the appropriate assays depend in part on the question being asked and the system being used. In addition, we emphasize that no individual assay is guaranteed to be themost appropriate one in every situation, and we strongly recommend the use of multiple assays to monitor autophagy. In these guidelines, we consider these various methods of assessing autophagy and what information can, or cannot, be obtained from them. Finally, by discussing the merits and limits of particular autophagy assays, we hope to encourage technical innovation in the field.","author_count":2922,"contributors":["Klionsky, Daniel J","Abdel-Aziz, Amal Kamal","Abdelfatah, Sara","Abdellatif, Mahmoud","Abdoli, Asghar","Abel, Steffen","Abeliovich, Hagai","Abildgaard, Marie H","Abudu, Yakubu Princely","Acevedo-Arozena, Abraham","Adamopoulos, Iannis E","Adeli, Khosrow","Adolph, Timon E","Adornetto, Annagrazia","Aflaki, Elma","Agam, Galila","Agarwal, Anupam","Aggarwal, Bharat B","Agnello, Maria","Agostinis, Patrizia","Agrewala, Javed N","Agrotis, Alexander","Aguilar, Patricia V","Ahmad, S Tariq","Ahmed, Zubair M","Ahumada-Castro, Ulises","Aits, Sonja","Aizawa, Shu","Akkoc, Yunus","Akoumianaki, Tonia","Akpinar, Hafize Aysin","Al-Abd, Ahmed M","Al-Akra, Lina","Al-Gharaibeh, Abeer","Alaoui-Jamali, Moulay A","Alberti, Simon","Alcocer-Gómez, Elísabet","Alessandri, Cristiano","Ali, Muhammad","Alim Al-Bari, M Abdul","Aliwaini, Saeb","Alizadeh, Javad","Almacellas, Eugènia","Almasan, Alexandru","Alonso, Alicia","Alonso, Guillermo D","Altan-Bonnet, Nihal","Altieri, Dario C","Álvarez, Élida M C","Alves, Sara","Alves da Costa, Cristine","Alzaharna, Mazen M","Amadio, Marialaura","Amantini, Consuelo","Amaral, Cristina","Ambrosio, Susanna","Amer, Amal O","Ammanathan, Veena","An, Zhenyi","Andersen, Stig U","Andrabi, Shaida A","Andrade-Silva, Magaiver","Andres, Allen M","Angelini, Sabrina","Ann, David",