{"abstract":"Background: Breast reduction by the superomedial technique can relieve symptoms related to breast hypertrophy; however, as the lateral and inferior portion of the breast parenchyma is removed and displaced, reduction mammoplasty may lead to an impaired ability to breastfeed. Objectives: The aim of this study was to assess patients' ability to breastfeed after superomedial reduction mammoplasty. Methods: This was a cross-sectional study including patients treated with superomedial reduction mammoplasty between January 2009 and December 2018 at 2 tertiary hospitals in Denmark. Patients were stratified into 2 cohorts, depending on whether they had experienced childbirth before or after their reduction mammoplasty. Patients were sent specific questionnaires regarding maternity, breastfeeding before and after reduction mammoplasty, nipple sensitivity, and current demographic information. Operative details were retrieved from electronic medical records. Results: In total, 303 patients were identified as eligible for this study (37 patients giving birth after and 266 before reduction mammoplasty). Fewer patients were able to breastfeed exclusively for the recommended 6 months after reduction mammoplasty (2/37, 5.41%) compared with before (92/266, 34.59%; P < 0.05). In addition, fewer patients were able to breastfeed at all after reduction mammoplasty (18/37, 48.64%) compared with before mammoplasty (241/266, 90.60%; P < 0.001). Patients unable to breastfeed after reduction mammoplasty had lower nipple sensitivity and more breast tissue excised (P < 0.05). Conclusions: Superomedial reduction mammoplasty seems to impair the patient's ability to breastfeed exclusively for the recommended 6 months. Patients of childbearing age considering reduction mammoplasty should be made aware that reduction mammoplasty reduces their breastfeeding capacity. Level of Evidence: 4:","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","Albertsdottir, Elin","Dalaei, Farima","Hesselfeldt-Nielsen, Jørgen","Schmidt, Volker J","Sørensen, Jens Ahm","Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045231"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf"],"keyword":["Breast Feeding","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Mammaplasty adverse effects","Nipples surgery","Pregnancy","Retrospective Studies","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"superomedial reduction mammoplasty affects patients ability to breastfeed in a distinct manner a multicenter study of 000000000303 patients","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85118194445","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-045231","identifier":[{"id":"34173823","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85118194445","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ab8200ee-4b11-43e2-a14b-db9064e39da6","sdu-ff849eee-62d9-4660-86af-e34e55dac4f7"],"keyword":["Breast Feeding","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Mammaplasty/adverse effects","Nipples/surgery","Pregnancy","Retrospective Studies","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-584F7270BC83736C27713A235200A5BE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Plastic Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Plastic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Gustaf","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"aebe7465-c8a9-452a-9b45-6259e674c2ee","name":"Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","orcid":"0000-0002-8755-3446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Elin","key":"albertsdottirpau","last":"Albertsdottir","name":"Albertsdottir, Elin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Farima","key":"dalaeipau","last":"Dalaei","locid":"d9a286a0-27ec-489d-93eb-f72516d28fe0","name":"Dalaei, Farima","orcid":"0000-0003-2305-7758","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jørgen","key":"hesselfeldtnielsenpau","last":"Hesselfeldt-Nielsen","name":"Hesselfeldt-Nielsen, Jørgen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 3","first":"Volker Jürgen","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"42a7c6c8-5c08-4c7a-99b2-20df4cde63f5","name":"Schmidt, Volker J","name_org":"Schmidt, Volker Jürgen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Navid Mohamadpour","key":"toyserkanipau","last":"Toyserkani","name":"Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34173823"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/asj/sjab263","issn":["1090820X","1527330X"],"issn_org":["1090820X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Aesthetic Surgery Journal","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Aesthetic Surgery Journal","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118194445"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab8200ee-4b11-43e2-a14b-db9064e39da6","sdu-ff849eee-62d9-4660-86af-e34e55dac4f7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Superomedial Reduction Mammoplasty Affects Patients' Ability to Breastfeed in a Distinct Manner : A Multicenter Study of 303 Patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-045231","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The incidence of hospital-treated concussion is 100–300/100,000 person years. Reporting of long-lasting post-concussion symptoms (PCS) is estimated at 5–15%. Attachment insecurity is a potential vulnerability factor for physical illness and poorer disease outcomes in general. This study aimed to explore associations between attachment insecurity and PCS in young people sustaining a concussion. Methods: This cross-sectional study was embedded in a cohort of 15–30-year-old patients (n = 3080) 3 months after sustaining a concussion. Data were obtained from a database and questionnaires. PCS were measured by the Rivermead Post-Concussion Symptoms Questionnaire and attachment dimensions (anxiety and avoidance) by the Experiences in Close Relationships-Relationship Structures Questionnaire. Multiple linear regression models were performed to investigate the association between the attachment dimensions and PCS with adjustment for demographic, injury-related and psychological factors and with additional testing for interaction between the attachment dimensions. Results: In the final study sample, comprising 973 patients (31.6%), we found an interaction between the attachment dimensions. Hence, the effect of attachment anxiety on PCS was statistically insignificant at low avoidance (25th percentile) but significant at high avoidance (75th percentile, β = 0.64 (95%CI: 0.02; 1.26)), whereas the effect of attachment avoidance was significant regardless of level of attachment anxiety (25th percentile, β = 1.09 (95%CI: 0.18; 2.01); 75th percentile, β = 2.71 (95%CI: 1.80; 3.61)). Conclusion: Attachment insecurity, especially characterised by high avoidance in combination with high anxiety, also called fearful attachment, is associated with PCS. Considering the attachment perspective can potentially improve health care for this patient group.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Tuborgh, Astrid","Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","Elklit, A.","Hunter, J.","Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","Schröder, Andreas","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Thastum, Mille","Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-026559"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Tuborgh, A.","Tuborgh, Astrid"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","University of Toronto"],"keyword":["Attachment dimensions","Concussion","Experiences in close relationships relationship structures questionnaire","Mild traumatic brain injury","Post concussion symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attachment and symptom reporting in adolescents and young adults after a concussion","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/193197006/Attachment_and_symptom_reporting_in_adolescents_and_young.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project was supported by The Health Scientific Research Foundation in Central Denmark Region , Aarhus University , The Psychiatric Research Foundation of the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry , The Psychiatric Research Foundation in Central Denmark Region and Grocer Svend Hansen and wife Ina Hansen's Foundation . The founding agencies had no role or say in the design or execution of the study."],"id":"S03-100.00-026559","identifier":[{"id":"34509710","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85114678172","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b