e","orcid":"0000-0002-0484-8522","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Nikolaj","key":"krarupnikolajthurepau","last":"Krarup","locid":"4b1dd97a-666e-4745-8a23-e3ab29629b9d","name":"Krarup, Nikolaj Thure","name_org":"Krarup, Nikolaj","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Mathilde","key":"svendstrupmathildepau","last":"Svendstrup","locid":"6eaa5020-d8b9-4655-8270-e274bd60db53","name":"Svendstrup, Mathilde","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34880489"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-021-04177-9","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"journal":"Nature","pages":"500-517","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"600"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120973811"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4a61aee9-40bf-4977-860f-5627fd72cd5a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combinatorial, additive and dose-dependent drug–microbiome associations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-437857","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In Denmark, many rural schools have been closed since 2000. These school closures have often resulted in heated debates between local politicians and the local population. Locals have feared that closing their school would have adverse effects and lead to local population decline. Meanwhile, previous research has found mixed evidence on the population effect of rural school closures. The aim of this paper is to contribute to the existing literature by looking at the case of Denmark. The paper analyses the local population effects of the simultaneous closure of eight village schools in 2011 in the same peripheral municipality in Denmark. The case study offers a quasi-experimental setting, and the population effects are estimated through an ordinary and a flexible difference-in-differences (DiD) analysis. Overall, the results show clear evidence of a negative population effect of rural school closures. The ordinary DiD analysis shows a population decline of 7.6 percentage points during the 10-year post-closure period. The flexible DiD analysis points to long-term effects, as the population decline first becomes statistically significant from the sixth year following the closures and onwards. To qualify the results of the econometric tests, we report findings from interviews with local people carried out in 2015 in four of the eight rural communities. Among other things, findings from interviews point to lock-in effects in terms of social capital and housing markets, which helps to understand the dominance of long-term population effects from school closures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Jens Fyhn Lykke","Svendsen, Gunnar Lind Haase","Jensen, Peter Sandholt","Schmidt, Torben Dall"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627378"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Jens Fyhn Lykke"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helmut Schmidt University","Linnaeus University"],"keyword":["Denmark","Housing markets","Interviews","Mixed methods","Population development","School closure","Social capital","Village"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"do rural school closures lead to local population decline","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jrurstud.2021.09.016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627378","identifier":[{"id":"85115438777","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bcefd980-4d4e-40e8-9eb1-16ec79741f3b"],"keyword":["Denmark","Difference-in-differences (DiD)","Housing markets","Interviews","Mixed methods","Population development","School closure","Social capital","Village"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4CD6019DEA99AD979F489A797A1484C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jrurstud.2021.09.016","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191894091/1_s2.0_S0743016721002801_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Environmental and Business Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"linnaeus university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linnaeus University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"helmut schmidt university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmut Schmidt University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Fyhn Lykke","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"86a1d89b-e801-4de5-9599-811c496d9de2","name":"Sørensen, Jens Fyhn Lykke","orcid":"0000-0003-1227-1783","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gunnar Lind Haase","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"f78945d9-87ac-45c0-a96f-1fe38464ef58","name":"Svendsen, Gunnar Lind Haase","orcid":"0000-0003-2989-2842","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Sandholt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Peter Sandholt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben Dall","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Torben Dall","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jrurstud.2021.09.016","issn":["07430167","18731392"],"issn_org":["07430167"],"journal":"Journal of Rural Studies","pages":"226-235","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Rural Studies","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115438777"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bcefd980-4d4e-40e8-9eb1-16ec79741f3b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Do rural school closures lead to local population decline?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627378","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Major bleeding (MB) events are independent predictors of mortality after cardiac interventional procedures. The clinical relevance of MB following left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO) remains unclear. Aims: This study aimed to investigate the incidence and clinical impact of MB after LAAO in a real-world population at high risk for bleeding and contraindicated to anticoagulation. Methods: The two-year results of the Amplatzer Amulet Observational Post-Market Study were analysed. An independent committee adjudicated MBs according to the Bleeding Academic Research Consortium scale. Cox proportional hazards regression identified variables associated with MB events and mortality. Results: The MB rate was 7.2%/year, with a rate of 10.1%/year during year one, decreasing to 4.0%/year over year two. The most common bleeding location was gastrointestinal, accounting for 48% of MBs. Pre- LAAO MB was associated with an increased risk for post-LAAO MB (HR 2.34, 95% CI: 1.37-3.99). The occurrence of post-LAAO MB was associated with increased mortality (37.3% vs 12.7%; p<0.0001), driven mainly by events occurring beyond the periprocedural period. The annualised rate of ischaemic stroke or TIA was similar in patients with and without MB (2.3% vs 3.3%; p=0.446). MB post LAAO was a strong independent predictor of mortality (HR 3.07, 95% CI: 2.15-4.40). Conclusions: In real-world patients at high bleeding risk, MB following LAAO was not uncommon and associated with a significant increase in mortality, without increasing the risk of stroke.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Aminian, Adel","De Backer, Ole","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Mazzone, Patrizio","Berti, Sergio","Fischer, Sven","Lund, Juha","Montorfano, Matteo","Lam, Simon C C","Freixa, Xavier","Gage, Ryan","Diener, Hans-Christoph","Schmidt, Boris"],"cuid":["S02-090.23-012954"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Finland","Germany","Hong Kong","Italy","Spain","United States"],"glorg":["Abbott Structural Heart","All Global Affiliations","CHU de Charleroi","Gabriele Monasterio Foundation","Harzklinikum Dorothea Christiane Erxleben GmbH","Hospital Clinic de Barcelona","Markus-Krankenhaus Frankfurt","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Hong Kong","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Atrial Appendage diagnostic imaging","Atrial Fibrillation epidemiology","Bleeding","Brain Ischemia","Cardiac Catheterization adverse effects","Death","Hemorrhage epidemiology","Humans","Incidence","LAA closure","Septal Occluder Device adverse effects","Stroke","Stroke epidemiology","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence and clinical impact of major bleeding following left atrial appendage occlusion insights from the amplatzer amulet observational post market study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85108557093","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.23-012954","identifier":[{"id":"33495144","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85108557093","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-04c6492d-1841-465d-8743-be877a80c1aa","ku-665023eb-60ff-44f6-9741-5ed895c22af5"],"keyword":["Atrial Appendage/diagnostic imaging","Atrial Fibrillation/epidemiology","Bleeding","Brain Ischemia","Cardiac Catheterization/adverse effects","Death","Hemorrhage/epidemiology","Humans","Incidence","LAA closure","Septal Occluder Device/adverse effects","Stroke","Stroke/epidemiology","Treatment Outcome"],"lang