{"abstract":"Objective: To investigate the prevalence of burnout among Danish and American urologists. Methods: An email invitation was sent with 2 reminders spaced by 14 days intervals to members of the Danish Urological Association and urologists at the University of Michigan to participate in a survey consisting of the 2 item Maslach Burnout Inventory. Burnout was defined as reporting “once a week,” “a few times a week,” or “everyday” on either the emotional exhaustion or depersonalization domains of the Maslach Burnout Inventory. Two open-ended questions were added to the survey for the Danish urologists, these were then qualitatively analyzed using thematic analysis. Categorial variables were compared using Chi square analysis. Results: The response rate was 193 of 387 (49.9%) for the Danish urologists and 43 of 64 (67.1%) among American urologists. The prevalence of burnout for the American and Danish cohorts was identified in 4 (44.4%) of the American residents and 10 (32.3%) of the American attendings compared to 2 (3%) of Danish residents and 16 (12.7%) of Danish attendings. The difference in rate of burnout between Danish residents and attendings was statistically significant (P=.03). Burnout was statistically significantly different between American and Danish residents (P<.01) and attendings (P <.01). There was a statistically significant difference in rates of burnout between American and the Danish female urologists (P =.02) and similarly among male urologists (P <.01). Conclusion: This study demonstrated low rates of burnout among Danish urologists and a significant difference in burnout between residents and attendings from Michigan compared to Danish residents and attendings.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jacobsen, Frederik M.","Jensen, Christian Fuglesang S.","Schmidt, Mette L.K.","Qin, Yongmei","Akselberg, Nicholas John","Sønksen, Jens","Ohl, Dana A.","Stork, Brian R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-505054"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"burnout among urologists from denmark and michigan","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-505054","identifier":[{"id":"32916191","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85091712636","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-bafe8cba-7635-43be-a50c-1a3b28b01b92"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F3A2DD3E54EBA59E171F87C2F4613721"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Urology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik M.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Frederik M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian Fuglesang S.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Christian Fuglesang S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette L.K.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Mette L.K.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yongmei","key":"qinpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Yongmei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicholas John","key":"akselbergpau","last":"Akselberg","name":"Akselberg, Nicholas John","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens","key":"sønksenpau","last":"Sønksen","locid":"feaefc17-e926-4892-9f0a-983e08461edf","name":"Sønksen, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dana A.","key":"ohlpau","last":"Ohl","name":"Ohl, Dana A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Brian R.","key":"storkpau","last":"Stork","name":"Stork, Brian R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32916191"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.urology.2020.07.066","issn":["00904295","15279995"],"issn_org":["00904295"],"journal":"Urology","pages":"68-73","status":"p","title":"Urology","volume":"147"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091712636"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bafe8cba-7635-43be-a50c-1a3b28b01b92"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Burnout Among Urologists from Denmark and Michigan","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-505054","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
