{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The prevalence of obstructive coronary artery disease (CAD) in symptomatic patients referred for diagnostic testing has declined, warranting optimization of individualized diagnostic strategies. OBJECTIVES: This study sought to present a simple, clinically applicable tool enabling estimation of the likelihood of obstructive CAD by combining a pre-test probability (PTP) model (Diamond-Forrester approach using sex, age, and symptoms) with clinical risk factors and coronary artery calcium score (CACS). METHODS: The new tool was developed in a cohort of symptomatic patients (n = 41,177) referred for diagnostic testing. The risk factor-weighted clinical likelihood (RF-CL) was calculated through PTP and risk factors, while the CACS-weighted clinical likelihood (CACS-CL) added CACS. The 2 calculation models were validated in European and North American cohorts (n = 15,411) and compared with a recently updated PTP table. RESULTS: The RF-CL and CACS-CL models predicted the prevalence of obstructive CAD more accurately in the validation cohorts than the PTP model, and markedly increased the area under the receiver-operating characteristic curves of obstructive CAD: for the PTP model, 72 (95% confidence intervals [CI]: 71 to 74); for the RF-CL model, 75 (95% CI: 74 to 76); and for the CACS-CL model, 85 (95% CI: 84 to 86). In total, 38% of the patients in the RF-CL group and 54% in the CACS-CL group were categorized as having a low clinical likelihood of CAD, as compared with 11% with the PTP model. CONCLUSIONS: A simple risk factor and CACS-CL tool enables improved prediction and discrimination of patients with suspected obstructive CAD. The tool empowers reclassification of patients to low likelihood of CAD, who need no further testing.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Winther, Simon","Schmidt, Samuel","Mayrhofer, Thomas","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Hoffmann, Udo","Douglas, Pamela S","Wijns, William","Bax, Jeroen","Nissen, Louise","Lynggaard, Vibeke","Christiansen, Jens Juel","Saraste, Antti","Bøttcher, Morten","Knuuti, Juhani"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007291"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Winther, Simon"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Ireland","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Harvard University","Leiden University","Leiden University Medical Center","National University of Ireland, Galway","Stralsund University of Applied Sciences","Turku University Central Hospital","University of Galway","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Coronary Stenosis","Coronary artery calcium score","Coronary artery disease","Pre test probability","Risk factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incorporating coronary calcification into pre test assessment of the likelihood of coronary artery disease","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85095748589","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007291","identifier":[{"id":"33213720","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85095748589","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-96939c6d-545e-4092-8633-9eb9d5bbb10b","au-4347b648-a853-4579-ba13-c9e199c3018e"],"keyword":["coronary artery calcium score","coronary artery disease","coronary stenosis","pre-test probability","risk factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CFB724A0F884A6FCAED9799CCF409C1C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Cardiac research clinic, West"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, CardioTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"stralsund university of applied sciences","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Stralsund University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"ie","key":"university of galway","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Galway","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"ie","key":"national university of ireland galway","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National University of Ireland, Galway","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"nl"