e","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-007291","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The present paper analyzes the role of different imaging modalities for left atrial appendage (LAA) assessment and the recommended specific measurements to improve device selection with regard to the Amulet device. BACKGROUND: Morphological LAA assessment is one of the pivotal factors to achieve proper LAA sealing and potentially reduce the risk of complications by minimizing manipulation inside the appendage. METHODS: Eight experienced physicians in LAAO were asked to contribute in the preparation of a device sizing consensus manuscript after comprehensive assessment of previous published data on LAA imaging/measurement. RESULTS: LAA morphology is often complex and requires more detailed spatial resolution and 3-dimensional assessments to reduce the risk of mis-sizing. Traditionally, upsizing of devices based upon the largest measured LAA diameters have been used. However, this may lead to oversizing in markedly elliptical appendages. Thus, when 3D imaging modalities are available, utilizing the LAA mean diameters might be a better alternative. Operators should also note the systematic biases in differences in measurements obtained with different imaging modalities, with CT giving the largest measurements, followed by 3D-TEE, and then 2D-TEE and angiography. In fact, for 2D imaging techniques (2D-TEE and angiography), LAA diameters tend to be underestimated, and therefore, LAA largest diameters seem to be still the best option for device sizing. Some specific anatomies such as proximal chicken-wing or conic LAAs may require different measurements and implantations to achieve implant success. CONCLUSIONS: In conclusion, LAA mean diameters might be a better alternative to largest diameters when 3D imaging modalities are available.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Freixa, Xavier","Aminian, Adel","Tzikas, Apostolos","Saw, Jacqueline","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Ghanem, Alexander","Schmidt, Boris","Hildick-Smith, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-172205"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Freixa, Xavier"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Germany","Greece","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Asklepios Klinik St. Georg","CHU de Charleroi","Cardioangiologisches Centrum Bethanien","Hospital Clinic de Barcelona","University General Hospital of Thessaloniki \"AHEPA\"","Vancouver General Hospital"],"keyword":["Amulet","Atrial fibrillation","Left atrial appendage","Sizing","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"left atrial appendage occlusion with the amplatzer amulet update on device sizing","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85081732603","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-172205","identifier":[{"id":"32166532","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85081732603","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000563809000001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-4b41f1f1-c71f-4aff-8b8a-7560a6b706c0"],"keyword":["Amulet","Atrial fibrillation","Left atrial appendage","Sizing","Stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28D9EFB9338E5B441ADA16479A59B2CB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"es","key":"hospital clinic de barcelona","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Clinic de Barcelona","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"chu de charleroi","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CHU de Charleroi","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gr","key":"university general hospital of thessaloniki ahepa","loc":["Greece","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University General Hospital of Thessaloniki \"AHEPA\"","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"vancouver general hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Vancouver General Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"asklepios klinik st georg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Asklepios Klinik St. Georg","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"cardioangiologisches centrum bethanien","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Cardioangiologisches Centrum Bethanien","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xavier","key":"freixapau","last":"Freixa","name":"Freixa, Xavier","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Adel","key":"aminianpau","last":"Aminian","name":"Aminian, Adel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Apostolos","key":"tzikaspau","last":"Tzikas","name":"Tzikas, Apostolos","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacqueline","key":"sawpau","last":"Saw","name":"Saw, Jacqueline","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens-Erick","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","name_org":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens-Erick","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"ghanempau","last":"Ghanem","name":"Ghanem, Alexander","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Boris","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Boris","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"hildicksmithpau","last":"Hildick-Smith","name":"Hildick-Smith, David","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32166532"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10840-019-00699-5","issn":["1383875X","15728595"],"issn_org":["1383875X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","pages":"71-78","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Interventional Cardiac Electrophysiology","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081732603"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4b41f1f1-c71f-4aff-8b8a-7560a6b706c0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Left atrial appendage occlusion with the Amplatzer Amulet : update on device sizing","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-172205","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: This study sought to report early experience with the new-generation Watchman FLX device (Boston Scientific, Marlborough, Massachusetts). BACKGROUND: The new-generation Watchman FLX features a reduced height, improved anchoring and fabric coverage, and a closed distal end. These design modifications aim to simplify implantation, allow full recapture and repositioning, and reduce peridevice leak and device-related thrombosis. METHODS: A total of 165 patients undergoing left atrial appendage (LAA) occlusion (LAAO) with Watchman FLX were enrolled in a prospective, multicenter registry at 12 centers participating in the European limited market release program. RESULTS: Mean age was 75.4 ± 8.9 years, and CHA2DS2-VASc score 4.4 ± 1.4. A total of 128 patients (77.6%) had a history of major bleeding, including previous intracranial hemorrhage in 55 cases (33.3%). LAA landing zone minimal and maximal mean diameters were 19.1 ± 3.6 mm and 22.3 ± 3.7 mm, and 24.2% of LAA were considered complex by dimensions. Technical success was achieved in all patients. Successful implantation at first attempt was achieved in 129 cases (78.2%), and a second device was required in 6 cases (3.6%). Procedure-related complications occurred in 3 patients (1.8%): 2 access-related (1.2%) and 1 pericardial effusion (0.6%). No peri-procedural strokes, deaths, or device embolizations occurred. Forty-nine patients (29.7%) were discharged with single antiplatelet therapy, 105 (63.6%) on dual antiplatelet, and 11 (6.7%) on anticoagulation. Imaging follow-up displayed just 1 peridevice leak ≥5 mm and 7 cases of device-related thrombosis (4.7%). During a median follow-up of 55 days (interquartile range: 45 to 148 days), there were 6 hemorrhagic complications (4.8%), 1 patient (0.8%) had an ischemic stroke, and 1 (0.8%) died. No late device embolizations occurred. CONCLUSIONS: LAAO with the Watchman FLX is safe and effective in a wide range of LAA morphologies, with a low procedural complication rate, high degree of LAA sealing, and favorable short-term efficacy.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Cruz-Gonzalez, Ignacio","Korsholm, Kasper","Trejo-Velasco, Blanca","Thambo, Jean Benoit","Mazzone, Patrizio","Rioufol, Gilles","Grygier, Marek","Möbius-Winkler, Sven","Betts, Timothy","Meincke, Felix","Sandri, Marcus","Schmidt, Boris","Schmitz, Thomas","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-257911"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Trejo-Velasco, Blanca"],"country":["France","Germany","Poland","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Asklepios Klinik St. Georg","CHU de Bordeaux","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red en Enfermedades Cardiovasculares (CIBERCV)","Elisabeth Hospital, Essen","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","Leipzig University","NIHR Oxford Biomedical Research Centre","Universite Claude Bernard Lyon 1","University of Medical Sciences Poznan"],"keyword":["Bleeding","Left atrial appendage occlusion","Periprocedural complications","Thromboembolic events"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"procedural and short term results with the new watchman flx left atrial appendage occlusion device","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85096868966","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-257911","identifier":[{"id":"33189641","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85096868966","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e1313a82-b874-4d83-b749-7dccf060a3cc"],"keyword":["bleeding","left atrial appendage occlusion","novel devices","periprocedural complications","thromboembolic events"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B78028FF96056BFF6EA0AFCE2856E7F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"centro de investigación biomédica en red en enfermedades cardiovasculares","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red en Enfermedades Cardiovasculares (CIBERCV)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"chu de bordeaux","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"CHU de Bordeaux","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"universite claude bernard lyon 1","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite Claude Bernard Lyon 1","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"pl","key":"university of medical sciences poznan","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Medical Sciences Poznan","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"friedrich schiller university jena","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich Schiller University Jena","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"nihr oxford biomedical research centre","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"NIHR Oxford Biomedical Research Centre","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"de","key":"asklepios klinik st georg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Asklepios Klinik St. Georg","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"de","key":"leipzig university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leipzig University","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"de","key":"elisabeth hospital essen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Elisabeth Hospital, Essen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ignacio","key":"cruzgonzalezpau","last":"Cruz-Gonzalez","name":"Cruz-Gonzalez, Ignacio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"korsholmpau","last":"Korsholm","locid":"47d8c195-2a81-4cbe-8d5a-1486606be651","name":"Korsholm, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-4724-0880","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Blanca","key":"trejovelascopau","last":"Trejo-Velasco","name":"Trejo-Velasco, Blanca","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean Benoit","key":"thambopau","last":"Thambo","name":"Thambo, Jean Benoit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrizio","key":"mazzonepau","last":"Mazzone","name":"Mazzone, Patrizio","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Gilles","key":"rioufolpau","last":"Rioufol","name":"Rioufol, Gilles","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Marek","key":"grygierpau","last":"Grygier","name":"Grygier, Marek","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Sven","key":"möbiuswinklerpau","last":"Möbius-Winkler","name":"Möbius-Winkler, Sven","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Timothy","key":"bettspau","last":"Betts","name":"Betts, Timothy","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"meinckepau","last":"Meincke","name":"Meincke, Felix","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"sandripau","last":"Sandri","name":"Sandri, Marcus","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Boris","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Boris","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"schmitzpau","last":"Schmitz","name":"Schmitz, Thomas","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33189641"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcin.2020.06.056","issn":["18767605","19368798"],"issn_org":["19368798"],"issue":"23","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","pages":"2732-2741","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","title_org":"JACC. Cardiovascular interventions","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096868966"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e1313a82-b874-4d83-b749-7dccf060a3cc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Procedural and Short-Term Results With the New Watchman FLX Left Atrial Appendage Occlusion Device","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-257911","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Predators not only have direct impact on biomass but also indirect, non-consumptive effects on the behavior their prey organisms. A characteristic response of zooplankton in aquatic ecosystems is predator avoidance by diel vertical migration (DVM), a behavior which is well studied on the population level. A wide range of behavioral diversity and plasticity has been observed both between- as well as within-species and, hence, investigating predator–prey interactions at the individual level seems therefore essential for a better understanding of zooplankton dynamics. Here we applied an underwater imaging instrument, the video plankton recorder (VPR), which allows the non-invasive investigation of individual, diel adaptive behavior of zooplankton in response to predators in the natural oceanic environment, providing a finely resolved and continuous documentation of the organisms’ vertical distribution. Combing observations of copepod individuals observed with the VPR and hydroacoustic estimates of predatory fish biomass, we here show (i) a small-scale DVM of ovigerous Pseudocalanus acuspes females in response to its main predators, (ii) in-situ observations of a direct short-term reaction of the prey to the arrival of the predator and (iii) in-situ evidence of pronounced individual variation in this adaptive behavior with potentially strong effects on individual performance and ecosystem functioning.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Möller, Klas Ove","St. John, Michael","Temming, Axel","Diekmann, Rabea","Peters, Janna","Floeter, Jens","Sell, Anne F.","Herrmann, Jens-Peter","Gloe, Dominik","Schmidt, Jörn O.","Hinrichsen, Hans H.","Möllmann, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351283"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Möller, Klas Ove"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bremerhaven University of Applied Sciences","German Center for Marine Biodiversity Research","Helmholtz Centre for Ocean Research Kiel","Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon","Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","University of Hamburg"],"keyword":["Diel vertical migration","Individual behavior","Predator avoidance","Video Plankton Recorder","Zooplankton"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["International Council for the Exploration of the Sea"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predation risk triggers copepod small scale behavior in the baltic sea","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/plankt/fbaa044","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351283","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7677935","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33239965","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85097510781","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9ca83f48-9747-4b40-86e7-f504e1f8ff11"],"keyword":["Diel vertical migration","Individual behavior","Predator avoidance","Video plankton recorder","Zooplankton"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-075D138872B8678AEB4A7D5F2B650BFE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235014451/fbaa044.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/plankt/fbaa044","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"helmholtz zentrum hereon","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l