rk"],"title":"Predation risk triggers copepod small-scale behavior in the Baltic Sea","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-351283","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background & aims: Fish-oil, rich in Omega-3 long chain polyunsaturated fatty acids (n-3 LC PUFAs), may in high doses inhibit the development or progression of cancer cachexia. However, poor compliance to oral nutritional supplements is a well-known problem. We aimed to investigate acceptability and compliance to a nutritional drink with fish-oil compared to an equivalent dose of fish-oil administered as capsules in patients receiving chemotherapy for GI tract cancers. Moreover, we aimed to investigate, if there was a difference between a nutritional drink or capsules with respect to nutritional status and side effects. Finally, we aimed to examine, if n-3 LC PUFAs affect leukocyte and platelet counts, and markers of dose-limiting toxicities of chemotherapy. Methods: We consecutively included 41 patients with advanced cancer in the controlled study. Patients were allocated (not randomized) to ingest either 10 capsules/day for four weeks or 400 mL/day of a nutritional drink with same dose of n-3 LC PUFA dose. Compliance was assessed by daily self-registration and n-3 LC PUFAs in whole blood. Side effects were assessed by 10 cm visual analog scales. Results: Compliance and daily consumption of n-3 LC PUFAs were 96.4% (94.1e99.3) and 4.8 (4.7e4.9) g/day in the capsule group and 80.8 (55.4e93.6) % and 4.0 (2.8e4.7) g/day in the group, respectively (p 0.02). We found no differences between the groups with respect to changes in whole blood n-3 LC PUFAs, weight, nutritional status, acceptability or side effects. However, in the capsule group the whole blood n-3 LC PUFAs correlated negatively with the increase in nausea (rs ¼ 0.39, p ¼ 0.05), but not in the nutritional drink group. Nausea, reduced appetite and loose stools were of greatest importance for the deviations from recommended doses. The number of capsules had a negative impact on acceptability and compliance, whereas this was mainly related to taste and texture in the nutritional drink group. No changes in median thrombocyte or leukocyte blood counts were observed. Conclusions: Fish oil in capsules appeared to result in better compliance compared to a nutritional drink with an equivalent dose of n-3 LC PUFAs. However, capsules and the drink did not differ with respect to the effect on nutritional status or side effects. Trial registration ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT03751384.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schmidt, Nina","Møller, Grith","Bæksgaard, Lene","Østerlind, Kell","Stark, Ken D","Lauritzen, Lotte","Andersen, Jens Rikardt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-424866"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Cancer cachexia","Chemotherapy","EPA","Faculty of Science","n 3 LC PUFA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fish oil supplementation in cancer patients capsules or nutritional drink supplements a controlled study of compliance","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-424866","identifier":[{"id":"85077334950","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31987122","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-34ed8a62-aac0-438c-90cc-490338eb6877"],"keyword":["Cancer cachexia","Chemotherapy","EPA","Faculty of Science","Product acceptability","n-3 LC PUFA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5EA6390C6175AE8075FCB132218AA363"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"ccbfa901-2c93-4f1a-a797-6194279cc43f","name":"Schmidt, Nina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Grith","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"97088e1a-ed46-4c15-9b8f-ff0d843f69d7","name":"Møller, Grith","orcid":"0000-0002-6512-8537","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"bæksgaardpau","last":"Bæksgaard","name":"Bæksgaard, Lene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kell","key":"østerlindpau","last":"Østerlind","name":"Østerlind, Kell","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ken D","key":"starkpau","last":"Stark","name":"Stark, Ken D","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","locid":"4263561d-003a-4d4c-9f05-06a8f88155e8","name":"Lauritzen, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0001-7184-5949","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Rikardt","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a94b3044-927f-46fa-ba5e-d829d4259fe4","name":"Andersen, Jens Rikardt","orcid":"0000-0003-3503-8474","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31987122"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clnesp.2019.12.004","issn":["24054577"],"journal":"Clinical Nutrition ESPEN","pages":"63-68","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition ESPEN","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077334950"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-34ed8a62-aac0-438c-90cc-490338eb6877"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fish oil supplementation in cancer patients. Capsules or nutritional drink supplements? A controlled study of compliance","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-424866","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Uveal melanoma (UM) is the most common intraocular tumour in adults and despite surgical or radiation treatment of primary tumours, ~50% of patients progress to metastatic disease. Therapeutic options for metastatic UM are limited, with clinical trials having little impact. Here we perform whole-genome sequencing (WGS) of 103 UM from all sites of the uveal tract (choroid, ciliary body, iris). While most UM have low tumour mutation burden (TMB), two subsets with high TMB are seen; one driven by germline MBD4 mutation, and another by ultraviolet radiation (UVR) exposure, which is restricted to iris UM. All but one tumour have a known UM driver gene mutation (GNAQ, GNA11, BAP1, PLCB4, CYSLTR2, SF3B1, EIF1AX). We identify three other significantly mutated genes (TP53, RPL5 and CENPE).","author_count":35,"contributors":["Johansson, Peter A","Brooks, Kelly","Newell, Felicity","Palmer, Jane M","Wilmott, James S","Pritchard, Antonia L","Broit, Natasa","Wood, Scott","Carlino, Matteo S","Leonard, Conrad","Koufariotis, Lambros T","Nathan, Vaishnavi","Beasley, Aaron B","Howlie, Madeleine","Dawson, Rebecca","Rizos, Helen","Schmidt, Chris W","Long, Georgina V","Hamilton, Hayley","Kiilgaard, Jens Folke","Isaacs, Timothy","Gray, Elin S","Rolfe, Olivia J","Park, John J","Stark, Andrew","Mann, Graham J","Scolyer, Richard A","Pearson, John V","van Baren, Nicolas","Waddell, Nicola","Wadt, Karin","McGrath, Lindsay A","Warrier, Sunil K","Glasson, William","Hayward, Nicholas K"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494659"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cell Line Tumor","Chromosome Aberrations","Computational Biology","DNA Mutational Analysis","Disease Free Survival","Disease Progression","Gene Dosage","Genome Human","Genomics","Humans","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Markov Chains","Melanoma genetics","Mutation","Phenotype","Prognosis","Tumor Suppressor Protein p53 genetics","Ultraviolet Rays"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"whole genome landscapes of uveal melanoma show an ultraviolet radiation signature in iris tumours","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-16276-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-494659","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7229209","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85084787143","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32415113","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a976b2a1-ab95-4e82-888f-7bda7cff97e2"],"keyword":["Cell Line, Tumor","Chromosome Aberrations","Computational Biology","DNA Mutational Analysis","Disease Progression","Disease-Free Survival","Gene Dosage","Genome, Human","Genomics","Humans","Iris Neoplasms/genetics","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Markov Chains","Melanocytes/metabolism","Melanoma/genetics","Mutation","Phenotype","Prognosis","Tumor Suppressor Protein p53/genetics","Ultraviolet Rays","Uveal Neoplasms/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54C8190FDC31C3B5FEE3397359D07C05"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-16276-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/255737231/s41467_020_16276_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, 