4f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33150746"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/oby.22973","issn":["19307381","1930739X"],"issn_org":["19307381"],"issue":"11","journal":"Obesity","pages":"2163-2174","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Obesity","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85095131611"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Gubra","Hospitals","Private Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-68cac41c-1db6-4111-a485-b1e2ef003252","ku-c8f49270-c9c1-4b4f-907a-2fdccb9bb5f4","sdu-e54d48c5-5876-483f-89f9-8f5bf62f5a50"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Gut Mucosal Gene Expression and Metabolic Changes After Roux-en-Y Gastric Bypass Surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-020299","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"\"Move the City - With Children, Adolescence and Seniors\" focuses on how, by changing or improving the city's space, we can promote physical activity, social gathering or healthier lifestyles of people based on the local community. The knowledge presented in the anthology is based on an interdisciplinary research collaboration conducted from 2016 to 2020 by three higher education institutions in Denmark. To this end, a new, multidisciplinary network was established under the name Activity- and health-enhancing Physical Environments Network (APEN). The anthology presents parts of the results of the collaboration. It is hoped that it can inspire others in Denmark to include all age groups in planning and possibly. design and construction of residential and institutional outdoor areas. The goal is to help bridge the gap between the various professionals, researchers and practitioners who are each interested in how urban communities and neighborhoods can be more developed into meaningful \"places\" that reduce social, mental and spatial inequality. The target groups for the publication are thus architects, planners, Danish municipalities, professionals, social housing associations, researchers, architecture and university students, primary school classes and last but not least, the interested, curious and eager citizen.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kural, René","Johansen Nørtoft, Kamilla","Carroll, Sidse","Lamm, Bettina","Wagner, Anne Margrethe","Winge, Laura","Troelsen, Jens","Pawlowski, Charlotte Skau","Schmidt, Tanja Bettina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-128754"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bevægelse","Børn og unge","Interventionsforskning","Seniorer"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level