{"abstract":"In this review, we focus on the literature that described the various unit operations in a process design flowsheet of biorefineries. We begin by establishing the accepted definitions of a biorefinery, go on to describe how to categorize biorefineries, and finally review the literature on biorefinery process designs by listing the unit operation in each process design. Distinguishing biorefineries based on feedstock, the types of processing units, and the products emanating from the biorefinery are discussed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Chaturvedi, Tanmay","Torres, Ana I.","Stephanopoulos, George","Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-000430"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","America, South","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chaturvedi, Tanmay"],"country":["United States","Uruguay"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Universidad de la República","University of the Republic"],"keyword":["Bio products","Biomass","Biorefinery","Lignocellulose","Microalgae","Process design","Proteins","Waste"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developing process designs for biorefineries definitions categories and unit operations","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en13061493","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research work was funded by the Cooperative Agreement between the Masdar Institute of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi, UAE and the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT), Cambridge, MA, USA-Reference project BIOREFINERY-02/MI/MI/CP/11/07633/GEN/G/00 for work under the Second Five Year Agreement."],"id":"S02-100.00-000430","identifier":[{"id":"85083626441","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-08444a60-8918-4800-80b6-ff1551d27e72","sdu-91e8fb19-b1d7-4a42-bd81-4205f9e7cca1"],"keyword":["Bio-products","Biomass","Biorefinery","Lignocellulose","Microalgae","Process design","Proteins","Waste"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A4200D555FE54E2F79253D281FA1C2B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/169468129/energies_13_01493_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/en13061493","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/348929619/energies_13_01493_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"uy","key":"universidad de la república","loc":["Uruguay","America, South"],"name":"Universidad de la República","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"uy","key":"university of the republic","loc":["Uruguay","America, South"],"name":"University of the Republic","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tanmay","key":"chaturvedipau","last":"Chaturvedi","locid":"b3f5d7f0-b816-4c27-9382-1169eb40768c","name":"Chaturvedi, Tanmay","orcid":"0000-0003-1966-8898","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana I.","key":"torrespau","last":"Torres","name":"Torres, Ana I.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"George","key":"stephanopoulospau","last":"Stephanopoulos","name":"Stephanopoulos, George","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Hedegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"29912cd6-8a9e-4022-b66a-6fb13430130a","name":"Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6805-7247","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en13061493","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"6","journal":"Energies","paperid":"1493","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083626441"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-08444a60-8918-4800-80b6-ff1551d27e72","sdu-91e8fb19-b1d7-4a42-bd81-4205f9e7cca1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Developing process designs for biorefineries-definitions, categories, and unit operations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-000430","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Bariatric surgery leads to a substantial weight loss (WL), however, a subset of patients undergoing surgery fails to achieve adequate WL. The reason for the individual variation in WL remains unexplained. Using an exploratory cross-disciplinary approach, we aimed to identify preoperative and early postoperative factors explaining the variation in WL after bariatric surgery. Methods: Sixty-one subjects were recruited. Eighteen subjects did not receive surgery and three subjects dropped out, leaving a total sample of 40 subjects. Physiological, social, and psychological data were collected before and 6 months after surgery. All variables were analyzed in combination using a least absolute shrinkage and selection operator (LASSO) regression to explain the variation in WL 18 months after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (n = 30) and sleeve gastrectomy (n = 10). Results: Mean WL was 31% (range: 10-52%). The following preoperative factors predicted 59% of the variation in WL: type of surgery (14%), diabetes status (12%), economic resources (9%), sex (7%), binge eating disorder (7%), degree of depression (5%), household type (3%), and physical activity (1%). Including information on early responses after surgery increased the ability to predict WL to 78% and was explained by early WL (47%), changes in energy density of food consumed from a buffet meal (9%), changes in glicentin (5%), degree of depression (5%), sex (5%), type of surgery (2%), economic resources (2%), and changes in drive for thinness (1%). Conclusions: Using a cross-disciplinary approach, a substantial part of the individual variation in WL was explained by a combination of basic patient characteristics, psychological profile, and social conditions as well as physiological, psychological and behavioral responses to surgery. These results suggest that patient characteristics collected in a cross-disciplinary approach may help determine predictors for less successful WL after bariatric surgery. If verified in larger cohorts this may form the basis for individualized postoperative support to optimize WL outcome.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mette Søndergaard","Christensen, Bodil Just","Schmidt, Julie Berg","Tækker, Louise","Holm, Lotte","Lunn, Susanne","Ritz, Christian","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Holst, Jens Juul","Schnurr, Theresia Maria","Hansen, Torben","le Roux, Carel W","Lund, Thomas Bøker","Floyd, Andrea Karen","Sjödin, Anders Mikael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-046710"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sjödin, Anders"],"country":["Ireland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UCD Institute of Food and Health","University College Dublin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predictors of weight loss after bariatric surgery a cross disciplinary approach combining physiological social and psychological measures","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85084129598","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding This study was carried out as part of the research program “Governing Obesity” funded by the University of Copenhagen Excellence Programme for Interdisciplinary Research (www.go.ku. dk). Additional funding was obtained from the Danish Diabetes Academy supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, the Lundbeck Foundation, and the Aase and Ejnar Danielsens Foundation. Conflict of interest CWlR is supported by grants from Science Foundation Ireland (ref. 12/YI/B2480), Health Research Board (USIRL-2016–2), and the Irish Research Council during the conduct of the study. Furthermore, CWlR reported being on the advisory boards for Novo Nordisk and GI Dynamics, receiving a research grant from AnaBio, receiving honoraria for lectures and advisory work from Eli Lily, Johnson and Johnson, Sanofi Aventis, Astra Zeneca, Janssen, Bristol-Myers Squibb, and Boehringer-Ingelheim, and reported shares in Keyron. The other authors have declared that no conflict of interest exists."],"id":"S02-100.00-046710","identifier":[{"id":"32327722","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084129598","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-dd037b27-da6e-460d-9007-14c810d15b44","sdu-6a1156f4-3796-4670-a541-1164de459be1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D78F573BBD7441DF2F0872CB239247ED"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ie","key":"university college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University College Dublin","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ie","key":"ucd institute of food and health","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UCD Institute of Food and Health","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Endocrinology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mette Søndergaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"080ae329-1cd1-45c3-8531-7bfe74879f0b","name":"Nielsen, Mette Søndergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7354-4648","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bodil Just","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"610aa898-48ea-4ebe-86ff-4664cf197551","name":"Christensen, Bodil Just","orcid":"0000-0003-4529-8253","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julie Berg","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"bfd32cb7-28ed-49e9-bc8e-4f9746043c12","name":"Schmidt, Julie Berg","orcid":"0000-0002-0299-7874","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"tækkerpau","last":"Tækker","locid":"13dae618-4d80-4bab-86d9-5cc2bcf83b78","name":"Tækker, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-0363-6090","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"fbaa1305-c82c-40fa-a115-031c135c8a40","name":"Holm, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0667-7779","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne","key":"lunnpau","last":"Lunn","locid":"ad3aec0c-c6c2-41a6-b5dc-bd39fa24254d","name":"Lunn, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-6812-1867","rank":6,"rolecode":"p