"Ignacio","key":"cruzgonzalezpau","last":"Cruz-Gonzalez","name":"Cruz-Gonzalez, Ignacio","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Heyder","key":"omranpau","last":"Omran","name":"Omran, Heyder","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppe","key":"tarantinipau","last":"Tarantini","name":"Tarantini, Giuseppe","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31103540"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcin.2019.02.003","issn":["18767605","19368798"],"issn_org":["19368798"],"issue":"11","journal":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","pages":"1003-1014","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Cardiovascular Interventions","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066140526"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d5b7ebb0-8d8c-4d16-b1e9-34000d5a9a97"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Incidence, Characterization, and Clinical Impact of Device-Related Thrombus Following Left Atrial Appendage Occlusion in the Prospective Global AMPLATZER Amulet Observational Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-251370","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In a biorefinery context, pyrolysis and gasification are especially interesting as both platforms offer high feed and product flexibility, providing the possibility to convert many different biogenic feedstocks into a wide variety of products such as heat, electricity, chemicals, transport fuels, and high-value ash and char products. However, in order to increase the utilization of biomass pyrolysis and gasification and make it commercially interesting in future energy systems, new integrated biorefinery designs with optimized thermal concepts and combinations of different technologies are required to maximize product yield and value, increase the overall process efficiency, and improve the economic viability. The present chapter provides an insight on the versatility and potential of biomass pyrolysis and gasification processes and their products. It also describes some new concepts and solutions like process integration schemes, polygeneration strategies, biochar uses, and tar abatement strategies that can help to overcome the operational challenges that the technology is facing.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Puig Arnavat, Maria","Thomsen, Tobias Pape","Ravenni, Giulia","Clausen, Lasse Røngaard","Sárossy, Zsuzsa","Ahrenfeldt, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-332144"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pyrolysis and gasification of lignocellulosic biomass","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134909242","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-332144","identifier":[{"id":"85134909242","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5cb817d8-e1fe-47cd-a2e2-4d52f5df2d47"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0CB56D365C688B0A3C3723A08619DE2B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria","key":"puigarnavatpau","last":"Puig-Arnavat","locid":"cb4b1d29-7136-45d7-a059-8fdf76b474fb","name":"Puig Arnavat, Maria","name_org":"Puig-Arnavat, Maria","orcid":"0000-0002-3542-9582","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Pape","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"f75a7756-932a-4066-8a74-8955f3f30f55","name":"Thomsen, Tobias Pape","orcid":"0000-0003-3597-7199","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giulia","key":"ravennipau","last":"Ravenni","locid":"c9296947-c635-4809-93df-75a66f0f0f49","name":"Ravenni, Giulia","orcid":"0000-0002-7147-8832","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Røngaard","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"8d19087a-a7cc-4570-a917-8eb3c133b4c4","name":"Clausen, Lasse Røngaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5092-889X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zsuzsa","key":"sárossypau","last":"Sárossy","locid":"39d0a52a-2fb9-42d3-abde-a9452b7fd211","name":"Sárossy, Zsuzsa","orcid":"0000-0001-5377-258X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"ahrenfeldtpau","last":"Ahrenfeldt","locid":"9fef4394-4b16-4061-8cc6-0da0fe3996b3","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3999-5864","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_4","isbn":["9783030109615"],"pages":"79-110","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Biorefinery: Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134909242"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-5cb817d8-e1fe-47cd-a2e2-4d52f5df2d47"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Pyrolysis and Gasification of Lignocellulosic Biomass","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-332144","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Bentsen, Niclas Scott"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479045"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biomass for biorefineries availability and costs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-479045","ids":["ku-8f33722e-54e4-4919-bc43-77962ac34dcc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FC5911DB082B101F7335B416F010A8B"],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"KU University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Niclas Scott","key":"bentsenpau","last":"Bentsen","locid":"6761011f-ab0b-43f0-bf26-26588f84da9c","name":"Bentsen, Niclas Scott","orcid":"0000-0002-5130-0818","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_2","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"37-48","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114978575"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","KU University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8f33722e-54e4-4919-bc43-77962ac34dcc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Biomass for Biorefineries : Availability and Costs","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479045","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Knowledge on how to improve public open spaces in deprived neighbourhoods to increase active living among children is scarce and comprehensively evaluated public open space interventions are needed. Firstly, the aim was to explore if involving 39 local fifth-grade children (10–11 years old) from a deprived neighbourhood in creating playable installations in a public open space influenced their use of this space. Secondly, we wanted to explore if the Reach, Effectiveness, Adoption, Implementation and Maintenance framework (RE-AIM) was useful for evaluating different stages in the intervention project. RE-AIM was applied through a convergent mixed-methods triangulation design using survey, accelerometer, GPS, and interviews as data sources. Effectiveness outcomes revealed that on average the space was used less by the 39 children after the intervention. The implementation and maintenance dimensions revealed aspects of why most children involved in the project did not use the space after intervention. The evaluation cast light on children's perceptions of their role, and importance of maintenance when the intervention was completed. In future, all dimensions of built environmental projects would benefit from being planned and evaluated in a collaboration with all project partners using an evaluation framework integrated and applied from the beginning of the project.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pawlowski, Charlotte Skau","Schmidt, Tanja Bettina","Nielsen, Jonas Vestergaard","Troelsen, Jens","Schipperijn, Jasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-604843"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active living","Children","Deprived neighbourhood","Implementation","Maintenance","Participatory Design","Public open space","RE AIM"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"will the children use it a re aim evaluation of a local public open space intervention involving children from a deprived neighbourhood","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85071293620","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-604843","identifier":[{"id":"31472381","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85071293620","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6e93f33a-ea24-43e1-9d93-7450de9b0724"],"keyword":["Active living","Children","Deprived neighbourhood","Implementation","Maintenance","Participatory design","Public open space","RE-AIM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BA0A0EA2997C9A0944353766386F3EF8"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Active Living"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Skau","key":"pawlowskipau","last":"Pawlowski","locid":"889b5a08-7360-484e-84ad-5baea5e669df","name":"Pawlowski, Charlotte Skau","orcid":"0000-0003-1407-613X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tanja","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b1fba9ea-1959-49a9-be0a-9a4b9cd6ba1a","name":"Schmidt, Tanja Bettina","name_org":"Schmidt, Tanja","orcid":"0000-0003-2476-8711","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Vestergaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1e9161ad-ac9e-4797-827a-cd8bedb14a8d","name":"Nielsen, Jonas Vestergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8800-5073","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"b35581eb-1482-4559-a4dd-49ec75e4c8a9","name":"Troelsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8105-0349","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jasper","key":"schipperijnpau","last":"Schipperijn","locid":"164cb44f-53ef-4f1a-9605-8112d837fcca","name":"Schipperijn, Jasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6558-7610","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31472381"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.evalprogplan.2019.101706","issn":["01497189","18737870"],"issn_org":["01497189"],"journal":"Evaluation and Program Planning","paperid":"101706","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Evaluation and Program Planning","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071293620"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6e93f33a-ea24-43e1-9d93-7450de9b0724"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Will the children use it? - A RE-AIM evaluation of a local public open space intervention involving children from a deprived neighbourhood","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-604843","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This chapter focuses on the bioprospecting of macro algae species in the Arabian Gulf, Abu Dhabi coast. Three species of macro algae were collected and subjected for detailed analysis and determination of biogas potentials, Padina boergesenii, Colpomenia sinuosa, and Ulva sp. Composition analysis and elemental analysis were used to determine bioenergy potentials. Anaerobic digestion of the three macro algae samples was carried out at two different volatile solid loadings (0.2 and 0.5%). The results showed significant methane yield for all three species, with Ulva sp. yielding higher methane production compared to Padina boergesenii and Colpomenia sinuosa. Biogas production for Ulva sp. was furthermore carried out at 1%, 3%, and 5% VS loading. The highest specific methane production for Ulva sp. was observed with 1% VS reaching 223 ml_CH4/gVS in 27 days.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Farzanah, Rashed H.","Brudecki, Grzegorz Przemyslaw","Cybulska, Iwona","Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard"],"cuid":["S02-096.78-008655"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University","Khalifa University of Science and Technology","UCLouvain","Université catholique de Louvain"],"keyword":["Biogas","Macro algae","Seawater","Ulva sp"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"screening and production of biogas from macro algae biomass of padina boergesenii colpomenia sinuosa and ulva sp","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_33","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.78-008655","identifier":[{"id":"85134943212","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b3a03f8a-2bed-4f3c-b087-2f771169a4c6","sdu-591aca71-2fc3-4b39-89c8-69c815fb9054"],"keyword":["Biogas","Colpomenia sinuosa","Macro algae","Padina boergesenii","Seawater","Ulva sp."],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9078C5BC504D8650842343CFA7465F36"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_33","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university of science and technology","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"université catholique de louvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université catholique de Louvain","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"uclouvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"UCLouvain","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rashed H.","key":"farzanahpau","last":"Farzanah","name":"Farzanah, Rashed H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Grzegorz Przemyslaw","key":"brudeckipau","last":"Brudecki","name":"Brudecki, Grzegorz Przemyslaw","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Iwona","key":"cybulskapau","last":"Cybulska","name":"Cybulska, Iwona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Hedegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"29912cd6-8a9e-4022-b66a-6fb13430130a","name":"Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6805-7247","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"ejbyeschmidtpedh","last":"Ejbye Schmidt","name":"Ejbye Schmidt, Jens","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_33","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"727-740","place":"Cham","publisher":"Springer Publishing Company","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134943212"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b3a03f8a-2bed-4f3c-b087-2f771169a4c6","sdu-591aca71-2fc3-4b39-89c8-69c815fb9054"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Screening and Production of Biogas from Macro Algae Biomass of Padina boergesenii, Colpomenia sinuosa, and Ulva sp.","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.78-008655","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Nickel allergy and dermatitis have been associated with filaggrin gene mutations in epidemiological studies, but the mechanisms mediating these associations are unknown. Objectives: To investigate whether filaggrin-deficient flaky tail (ft/ft) mice show increased immune reactivity to nickel and elucidate the mechanisms mediating this. Methods: The immune responses to nickel, 2,4-dinitrofluorobenzene (DNFB), cinnamal and p-phenylenediamine were assessed in ft/ft and wild-type (WT) mice. The amounts of nickel in the skin of ft/ft and WT mice were determined 20 hours after nickel exposure. The effect of blocking either the interleukin (IL)-17A pathway or the IL-1 pathway on the response to nickel in ft/ft mice was evaluated. Results: Increased responsiveness to nickel, DNFB and cinnamal was observed in ft/ft mice as compared with controls. A reduced amount of nickel was found in the skin of ft/ft mice as compared with WT mice, suggesting increased nickel absorption by the skin of ft/ft mice. Blocking either the IL-17A pathway or the IL-1 pathway reduced nickel responsiveness in ft/ft mice. Conclusions: These findings suggest that the increased nickel responsiveness associated with epidermal filaggrin deficiency is mediated by a combination of increased nickel penetration and the steady-state inflammation found in the skin of filaggrin-deficient mice.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Petersen, Trine H","Jee, Mia H","Gadsbøll, Anne-Sofie Ø","Schmidt, Jonas D","Sloth, Jens Jørgen","Sonnenberg, Gregory F","Geisler, Carsten","Thyssen, Jacob P","Bonefeld, Charlotte M"],"cuid":["S02-099.72-036157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bonefeld, Charlotte M"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Weill Cornell Medical College"],"keyword":["Allergic contact dermatitis","Filaggrin","IL 17A","IL 1β","Nickel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mice with epidermal filaggrin deficiency show increased immune reactivity to nickel","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85056420201","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Sundhed og Sygdom, Det Frie Forskningsråd; The A.P. Møller Foundation for the Advancement of Medical Sciences; The Aage Bangs Foundation; The Lundbeck Foundation; Danish Council for Independent Research, Medical Sciences"],"id":"S02-099.72-036157","identifier":[{"id":"30426511","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85056420201","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9cf48d3d-2353-4c13-9163-ff84b8468210","ku-016a1a69-a91c-416d-97e4-2b7290c212a7"],"keyword":["IL-17A","IL-1β","allergic contact dermatitis","filaggrin","nickel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-45D72445B5DF8C17CDD4889767713FF7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research group for Nano-Bio Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"weill cornell medical college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Weill Cornell Medical College","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Trine H.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"fa02279a-29da-406e-9303-db2ae4787bf6","name":"Petersen, Trine Hilkjær","name_org":"Petersen, Trine H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6587-7546","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mia H.","key":"jeepau","last":"Jee","name":"Jee, Mia H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Sofie Ø.","key":"gadsbøllpau","last":"Gadsbøll","locid":"b997715c-719a-4d7a-8ab7-ea981f69b7c5","name":"Gadsbøll, Anne Sofie Ø.","orcid":"0000-0001-5757-9365","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas D.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"ed2d02bb-ee93-4334-ac75-6c2769aabaaa","name":"Schmidt, Jonas Damgård","name_org":"Schmidt, Jonas D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Jørgen","key":"slothpau","last":"Sloth","locid":"d7fb8bd1-2626-48fa-b49e-35d57b2fae5d","name":"Sloth, Jens Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-3636-8769","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregory F","key":"sonnenbergpau","last":"Sonnenberg","name":"Sonnenberg, Gregory F","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"geislerpau","last":"Geisler","locid":"bf718810-8d55-4a0d-b416-e1a555472d41","name":"Geisler, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0002-8472-0771","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob P.","key":"thyssenpau","last":"Thyssen","locid":"c02c08ab-10c1-4ce8-bec3-447154952fc2","name":"Thyssen, Jacob P.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte M.","key":"bonefeldpau","last":"Bonefeld","locid":"984200fd-eadd-4a8b-a9f0-92d4158657a8","name":"Bonefeld, Charlotte Menné","name_org":"Bonefeld, Charlotte M.","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-6229","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30426511"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cod.13153","issn":["01051873","13966669"],"issn_org":["01051873"],"issue":"3","journal":"Contact Dermatitis","pages":"139-148","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Contact Dermatitis","volume":"80"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056420201"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9cf48d3d-2353-4c13-9163-ff84b8468210","ku-016a1a69-a91c-416d-97e4-2b7290c212a7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mice with epidermal filaggrin deficiency show increased immune reactivity to nickel","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.72-036157","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Chronic pancreatitis (CP) is thought to present the end stage of a continuous disease process evolving from acute pancreatitis (AP), over recurrent AP, to early and end-stage CP. Due to the irreversible nature of CP, early detection and prevention is key. Prospective assessment based on advanced imaging modalities as well as biochemical markers of inflammation, fibrosis and oxidative stress may provide a better understanding of the underlying pathological processes and help identify novel biomarkers of disease with the ultimate goal of early diagnosis, intervention and prevention of disease progression. This paper describes the protocol of a prospective multicentre cohort study investigating the fibroinflammatory process involved in progression from acute to CP using state-of-the-art diagnostic imaging modalities and circulating biomarkers of inflammation, fibrosis and oxidative stress. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: Adult control subjects and patients at different stages of CP according to the M-ANNHEIM system will be recruited from outpatient clinics at the participating sites and form three cohorts: controls (n=40), suspected CP (n=60) and definitive CP (n=60). Included patients will be followed prospectively for 15 years with advanced MRI and contrast-enhanced endoscopic ultrasound with elastography, assessment of endocrine and exocrine pancreatic function, biochemical and nutritional assessment, and evaluation of pain processing using quantitative sensory testing. Blood samples for a biobank will be obtained. The purpose of the biobank is to allow analyses of potential circulating biomarkers of disease progression, including markers of inflammation, fibrosis and oxidative stress. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: Permissions from the Regional Science Ethics committee and the Regional Data Protection Agency have been obtained. We will submit the results of the study for publication in peer-reviewed journals regardless of whether the results are positive, negative or inconclusive.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Novovic, Srdan","Borch, Anders","Werge, Mikkel","Karran, David","Gluud, Lise","Schmidt, Palle Nordblad","Hansen, Erik Feldager","Nøjgaard, Camilla","Jensen, Annette Bøjer","Jensen, Frank Krieger","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Hansen, Mark Berner","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Drewes, Asbjørn Mohr","Olesen, Søren Schou"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-008543"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Chronic pancreatitis","Fibrosis","Inflammation","Oxidative stress","Pain processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterisation of the fibroinflammatory process involved in progression from acute to chronic pancreatitis study protocol for a multicentre prospective cohort study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-028999","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.94-008543","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6707691","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85071247075","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31439604","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-b13e249c-043a-4185-80a5-660a2272403e","ku-7485f0a1-934e-4e40-b15d-f036540d767d"],"keyword":["chronic pancreatitis","fibrosis","inflammation","oxidative stress","pain processing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8B01BD62D575ABCDCCC112BF322D3307"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2019-028999","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"