{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Treatment-requiring acute non-variceal upper gastrointestinal bleeding (NVUGIB) is a common, potentially life-threatening emergency. This study investigated whether hospital admittance volume of patients with NVUGIB was associated with reduced mortality, reduced lasting failure of haemostatic procedures defined as rate of re-endoscopy with repeated haemostasis intervention (ReWHI), transfusion requirements and conversion to surgery. METHODS: Data on Danish nationwide admissions of patients with acute NVUGIB from 2011-2013 were analysed to estimate 30-day mortality, re-bleeding (ReWHI), transfusion rates and rates of conversion to surgery. Data were analysed by regression modelling while controlling for confounders including age, admission haemoglobin, the American College of Anesthesiologists score, comorbidities and the Forrest classification. RESULTS: A total of 3,537 patients with acute non-variceal upper gastrointestinal bleeding were included in the study. The hospital admission volume of patients with NVUGIB was positively associated with a significant increase in ReWHI with an odds ratio of 1.27; p = 1.91 × 10-6. There was no significant association between admission volume and conversion to surgery, 30-day mortality or transfusion rates. CONCLUSIONS: A positive association between admission volumes of patients with NVUGIB and ReWHI was identified. No association between admission volumes and 30-day mortality or other failure of haemostasis events could be identified. FUNDING: none. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not applicable.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schmidt, Magnus Strøh","Preisler, Louise","Fabricius, Rasmus","Svenningsen, Peter","Hillingsø, Jens","Svendsen, Lars Bo","Sillesen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-433839"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Blood Transfusion statistics numerical data","Conversion to Open Surgery statistics numerical data","Denmark","Female","Gastrointestinal Hemorrhage mortality","Hospital Mortality","Hospitals statistics numerical data","Humans","Male","Odds Ratio","Patient Admission statistics numerical data","Recurrence","Registries","Regression Analysis","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of hospital admission volume on outcomes following acute non variceal upper gastrointestinal bleeding","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/241121957/a5531_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-433839","identifier":[{"id":"85061112493","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30722826","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-43ae1db5-042d-43f7-b17f-ac5a2698aa1a"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Blood Transfusion/statistics & numerical data","Conversion to Open Surgery/statistics & numerical data","Denmark","Female","Gastrointestinal Hemorrhage/mortality","Hemostatic Techniques/mortality","Hospital Mortality","Hospitals/statistics & numerical data","Humans","Male","Odds Ratio","Patient Admission/statistics & numerical data","Recurrence","Registries","Regression Analysis","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4699EC499CC578BF92C16B981C398D65"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/241121957/a5531_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/files/scientific_article_files/2019-01/a5531_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Magnus Strøh","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Magnus Strøh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"preislerpau","last":"Preisler","locid":"3fba84f9-a9e3-4655-9fb1-6ca70d136459","name":"Preisler, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"fabriciuspau","last":"Fabricius","name":"Fabricius, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"svenningsenpau","last":"Svenningsen","name":"Svenningsen, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"hillingsøpau","last":"Hillingsø","locid":"6e3f56a3-3e04-4728-872b-b833e9b702df","name":"Hillingsø, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"247c86c0-0475-4af7-a7be-f67a38812a1e","name":"Svendsen, Lars Bo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"sillesenpau","last":"Sillesen","locid":"896857bd-2dfb-4559-8033-b2f9220ab606","name":"Sillesen, Martin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30722826"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["16039629"],"issue":"2","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A5531","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-43ae1db5-042d-43f7-b17f-ac5a2698aa1a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of hospital-admission volume on outcomes following acute non-variceal upper gastrointestinal bleeding","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433839","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The wide use of non-biodegradable, petroleum-based plastics raises important environmental concerns, which urges finding alternatives. In this study, an alternative way to produce polymers from a renewable source-milk proteins-was investigated with the aim of replacing polyethylene. Whey protein can be obtained from whey residual, which is a by-product in the cheese-making process. Two different sources of whey protein were tested: Whey protein isolate (WPI) containing 91% protein concentration and whey protein concentrate (WPC) containing 77% protein concentration. These were methacrylated, followed by free radical polymerization with co-polymer poly(ethylene glycol) methyl ether methacrylate (PEGMA) to obtain polymer sheets. Different protein concentrations in water (11-14 w/v%), at two protein/PEGMA mass-ratios, 20:80 and 30:70, were tested. The polymers made from WPI and WPC at a higher protein/PEGMA ratio of 30:70 had significantly better tensile strength than the one with lower protein content, by about 1-2 MPa (the best 30:70 sample exhibited 3.8 ± 0.2 MPa and the best 20:80 sample exhibited 1.9 ± 0.4 MPa). This indicates that the ratio between the hard (protein) and soft (copolymer PEGMA) domains induce significant changes to the tensile strengths of the polymer sheets. Thermally, the WPI-based polymer samples are stable up to 277.8 ± 6.2 °C and the WPC-based samples are stable up to 273.0 ± 3.4 °C.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Chalermthai, Bushra","Chan, Wui Yarn","Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Taher, Hanifa","Olsen, Bradley","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-602490"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"country":["United Arab Emirates","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Copolymerization","Mechanical properties","Whey protein"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preparation and characterization of whey protein based polymers produced from residual dairy streams","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/polym11040722","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-602490","identifier":[{"id":"85065907501","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6523544","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31010256","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-6646e8b0-d05f-4da8-b3fe-dcfb30990cd5"],"keyword":["Copolymerization","Mechanical properties","PEGMA","Protein-based polymer","Whey protein"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA0BA2E72BA64E2A7C1BDDBCFE835979"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/polym11040722","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/155563759/Preparation_and_Characterization_of_Whey_Protein_Based_Polymers_Produced_from_Residual_Dairy_Streams.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bushra","key":"chalermthaipau","last":"Chalermthai","name":"Chalermthai, Bushra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wui Yarn","key":"chanpau","last":"Chan","name":"Chan, Wui Yarn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanifa","key":"taherpau","last":"Taher","name":"Taher, Hanifa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bradley","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Bradley","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31010256"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/polym11040722","issn":["20734360"],"issue":"4","journal":"Polymers","paperid":"722","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Polymers","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065907501"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6646e8b0-d05f-4da8-b3fe-dcfb30990cd5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Preparation and Characterization of Whey Protein-Based Polymers Produced from Residual Dairy Streams","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-602490","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Considering the harsh climate of the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and desert lands with little rain, growing biomass such as soybean or sunflower is not encouraging to provide valuable resources. In such regions, high-value products as proteins, pigments, and fatty acids can be extracted from microalgae, which can be cultivated on nonproductive lands (deserts included). In this study, we examine the potential use of microalgae as a source of biomass in the UAE. Three strains, Chlorella, Euglena, and Scenedesmus, found in the Gulf of the Arabian Sea are analyzed to identify the proper type of microalgae in creating valuable products. Chlorella shows strong resistance against high salinity and temperature, which make it a good potential source of proteins, pigments, and fatty acids for the UAE. Based on the Chlorella results, a full biorefinery is designed with the aim of producing 10 tons of proteins per day along with pigments (sodium copper chlorophylls) and saponified fatty acids (lipids). Then, an economical evaluation is conducted for the three products (proteins, pigments, and lipids) using the software SuperPro Designer. From the economical evaluation, it was identified that the three products generate revenues of 173,906,000$/year with a payback time of 2.62 years. This result suggests that the potential use of microalgae biorefinery to create revenues based on the suggested products is greatly promising in the UAE and other coastal arid/semiarid regions","author_count":7,"contributors":["AlMahri, Mariam Ali","Jung, Kichul","Alshehhi, Mashael","Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-624774"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jung, Kichul"],"country":["South Korea","United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University","Konkuk University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"techno economic assessment of microalgae biorefinery as a source of proteins pigments and fatty acids a case study for the united arab emirates","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85079074671","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-624774","identifier":[{"id":"85079074671","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b40dbf31-ad72-4b66-9387-a9fe7de8338f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E77C639745A535C6EABF934435AEE97"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"kr","key":"konkuk university","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Konkuk University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariam Ali","key":"almahripau","last":"AlMahri","name":"AlMahri, Mariam Ali","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kichul","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Kichul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mashael","key":"alshehhipau","last":"Alshehhi","name":"Alshehhi, Mashael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_30","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"679-693","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079074671"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b40dbf31-ad72-4b66-9387-a9fe7de8338f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Techno-economic Assessment of Microalgae Biorefinery as a Source of Proteins, Pigments, and Fatty acids : A Case Study for the United Arab Emirates","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-624774","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This book discusses the biorefinery of biomass feedstocks. In-depth chapters highlight the scientific and technical aspects and present a techno-economic analysis of such systems. By using a TEA approach, the authors present feasible pathways for conversion of biomass (both residual biomass, energy crops and algae biomass), showing the different possibilities for the production of biochemical materials, biofuels, and fertilizers. The concepts presented in this book will link companies, investors, and governments by providing a framework that will help reduce pollutants and create a biomass related economy that incorporates the newest developments and technologies in the area.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-629991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University"],"keyword":["Algae","Biogas","Biomass conversion","Bioprocesses","Catalytic conversion","Enzymatic synthesis","Feedstocks","Lignin","Lignocellulosic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biorefinery integrated sustainable processes for biomass conversion to biomaterials biofuels and fertilizers","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85086802421","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-629991","identifier":[{"id":"85086802421","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c64107df-b3e4-4a1b-acce-0147dfe63b8b"],"keyword":["Algae","Biogas","Biomass conversion","Bioprocesses","Catalytic conversion","Enzymatic synthesis","Feedstocks","Lignin","Lignocellulosic","Pyrolysis of biomass"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8CFDB724C1843CA1D8BB5A1736AE6425"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelped","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtped","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"publisher":"Springer","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086802421"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c64107df-b3e4-4a1b-acce-0147dfe63b8b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Biorefinery : Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-629991","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Carboxylic acid production from food waste by mixed culture fermentation is an important future waste management option. Obstacles for its implementation are the need of pH control and a broad fermentation product spectrum leading to increased product separation costs. To overcome these obstacles, the selective production of lactic acid (LA) from model food waste by uncontrolled pH fermentation was tested using different reactor configurations. Batch experiments, semi-continuously fed reactors and a percolation system reached LA concentrations of 32, 16, and 15 gCODLA/L, respectively, with selectivities of 93%, 84%, and 75% on COD base, respectively. The semi-continuous reactor was dominated by Lactobacillales. Our techno-economic analysis suggests that LA production from food waste can be economically feasible, with LA recovery and low yields remaining as major obstacles. To solve both problems, we successfully applied in situ product extraction using activated carbon.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bonk, Fabian","Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Yousef, Ahmed","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-644506"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research – UFZ","Khalifa University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the selective lactic acid production from food waste in uncontrolled ph mixed culture fermentations using different reactor configurations","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134948266","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-644506","identifier":[{"id":"85134948266","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f90ba02e-c85e-4015-be39-d5a89152571a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D01B7B14FFAD37D0A8A3243C27A4D64C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"helmholtz centre for environmental research ufz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research – UFZ","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabian","key":"bonkpau","last":"Bonk","name":"Bonk, Fabian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmed","key":"yousefpau","last":"Yousef","name":"Yousef, Ahmed","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"ejbyeschmidtpedh","last":"Ejbye Schmidt","name":"Ejbye Schmidt, Jens","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_18","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"461-477","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134948266"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f90ba02e-c85e-4015-be39-d5a89152571a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exploring the Selective Lactic Acid Production from Food Waste in Uncontrolled pH Mixed Culture Fermentations Using Different Reactor Configurations","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-644506","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Process design artifacts (e.g., process models, textual process descriptions and simulations) are increasingly used to provide input for requirements elicitation and to facilitate the design of business processes. To support the understandability of process models and make them accessible for end-users with different backgrounds, several hybrid representations combining different design artifacts have been proposed in the literature. This paper investigates the understandability of DCR-HR, a new hybrid process design artifact based on DCR graphs. Using eye-tracking and think-aloud techniques, this paper explores the benefits and challenges associated with the use of different design artifacts and investigates the way end-users engage with them. The results motivate the use of DCR-HR and provide insights about the support it provides to end-users with different backgrounds.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","Burattin, Andrea","Slaats, Tijs","Petersen, Anette Chelina Møller","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Weber, Barbara"],"cuid":["S02-080.47-033542"],"event":{"end":"2019-06-04","place":"Rome, it","start":"2019-06-03","title":"20th International Conference on Business Process Modeling, Development and Support, BPMDS 2019 and 24th International Conference on Evaluation and Modeling Methods for Systems Analysis and Development, EMMSAD 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Abbad Andaloussi, Amine"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of St. Gallen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the understandability of a hybrid process design artifact based on dcr graphs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250866149/Exploring_the_Understandability_of_a_Hybrid_Process_Design_Artifact_Based_on_DCR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-080.47-033542","identifier":[{"id":"85069160403","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2b5babab-2ca0-4ba0-8229-bb0005c1f69e","ku-aa551baf-6d1b-45a4-9fd0-f2336b5de21c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4D31F4FFA2A448E8A921D95F38954047"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250866149/Exploring_the_Understandability_of_a_Hybrid_Process_Design_Artifact_Based_on_DCR.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/183365630/camera_ready_version_of_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Software and Process Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amine","key":"abbadandaloussipau","last":"Abbad Andaloussi","locid":"ec567f0e-aa1c-42e2-a523-fccf2f03efbe","name":"Abbad Andaloussi, Amine","orcid":"0000-0002-3404-7849","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andrea","key":"burattinpau","last":"Burattin","locid":"75b43f3c-f477-4ac8-8717-c6d2b93bed02","name":"Burattin, Andrea","orcid":"0000-0002-0837-0183","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tijs","key":"slaatspau","last":"Slaats","locid":"85f00008-e9c6-439c-aae5-e5bd725f2099","name":"Slaats, Tijs","orcid":"0000-0001-6244-6970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette Chelina Møller","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Anette Chelina Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas T.","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"c1d69914-5f7a-4f0b-8ffb-766693004328","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas T.","orcid":"0000-0002-7435-5563","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"weberpau","last":"Weber","locid":"4bbfa31e-3aa1-4565-88b1-8c19946807e6","name":"Weber, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-6004-4860","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"guldenpedh","last":"Gulden","name":"Gulden, Jens","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Iris","key":"reinhartzbergerpedh","last":"Reinhartz-Berger","name":"Reinhartz-Berger, Iris","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jelena","key":"zdravkovicpedh","last":"Zdravkovic","name":"Zdravkovic, Jelena","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rainer","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Rainer","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-20618-5_5","isbn":["9783030206178"],"issn":["18651348"],"pages":"69-84","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Business Information Processing","status":"p","title":"Enterprise, Business-Process and Information Systems Modeling - 20th International Conference, BPMDS 2019, 24th International Conference, EMMSAD 2019, Held at CAiSE 2019, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069160403"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2b5babab-2ca0-4ba0-8229-bb0005c1f69e","ku-aa551baf-6d1b-45a4-9fd0-f2336b5de21c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring the Understandability of a Hybrid Process Design Artifact Based on DCR Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.47-033542","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Uveal melanoma (UM) is the most common intraocular malignancy in adults and shows a high rate of metastatic spread. As randomized clinical trials with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) have not been performed in patients with metastatic UM, we analyzed the real-world outcomes in a nationwide population-based study. Clinical data of patients with UM were extracted from the Danish Metastatic Melanoma database, a nationwide database containing unselected records of patients diagnosed with metastatic melanoma in Denmark. Survival before (pre-ICI, n = 32) and after (post-ICI, n = 94) the approval of first-line treatment with ICI was analyzed. A partial response to first-line treatment was observed in 7% of patients treated with anti-programmed cell death protein (PD)-1 monotherapy and in 21% with combined anti-cytotoxic T lymphocyte antigen (CTLA)-4 plus anti-PD-1 therapy. Median progression-free survival was 2.5 months for patients treated in the pre-ICI era compared to 3.5 months in the post-ICI era (hazard ratio (HR) 0.43; 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.28-0.67; p < 0.001). The estimated one-year overall survival rate increased from 25.0% to 41.9% and the median overall survival improved from 7.8 months to 10.0 months, respectively (HR 0.52; 95% CI 0.34-0.79; p = 0.003). Thus, the introduction of ICI as first-line treatment appears to have significantly improved the real-world survival of patients with metastatic UM, despite relatively low response rates compared to cutaneous melanoma. With the lack of therapies proven effective in randomized trials, these data support the current treatment with ICI in patients with metastatic UM.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Bol, Kalijn Fredrike","Ellebaek, Eva","Hoejberg, Lise","Bagger, Mette Marie","Larsen, Mathilde Skaarup","Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","Køhler, Ulrich Heide","Schmidt, Henrik","Bastholt, Lars","Kiilgaard, Jens Folke","Donia, Marco","Svane, Inge Marie"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-024616"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Svane, Inge Marie"],"keyword":["Immune checkpoint inhibitors","Immunotherapy","Real world data","Uveal melanoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real world impact of immune checkpoint inhibitors in metastatic uveal melanoma","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers11101489","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement no 792367 to K.F.B. The Danish Metastatic Melanoma database received financial support from BMS, Roche, Merck MSD and Novartis. The Copenhagen Epidemiological Uveal Melanoma Study database received funding from the Danish Cancer Society, Fight for Sight Denmark and the Synoptik Foundation. The funders had no role in the design of the study; in the collection, analyses or interpretation of data; in the writing of the manuscript or in the decision to publish the results."],"id":"S03-100.00-024616","identifier":[{"id":"85074733588","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6826482","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31623302","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a32906ce-fc75-41e0-8c34-7bc6d9ceb84b","ku-f30934af-787b-4a82-b8bf-89b232f33588","sdu-620e356b-cd8c-40ce-8267-628ce3ce907f"],"keyword":["Immune checkpoint inhibitors","Immunotherapy","Real-world data","Uveal melanoma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Scienc