{"abstract":"Hvad er litteraturkritikkens opgave og genstand i det 21. århundrede? Hvilke aspekter af den litterære tekst skal en kvalificeret læsning fokusere på? Hvordan kan litteraturen engagere sig kritisk i den almene samfundsdebat? Og hvad er overhovedet formålet med at læse litteratur? Alle disse spørgsmål forsøger 12 litterater fra Danmark, Norge og Sverige at besvare i denne bog. Med afsæt i den angelsaksiske nykritiks indtog i forskning og undervisning i litteratur i Skandinavien i midten af det 20. århundrede diskuteres aktuelle perspektiver på og problemstillinger ved akademikeres, studerendes og forfatteres arbejde med litteratur. Undervejs behandles fundamentale aspekter af litteraturundervisningen, bevæggrundene for at sætte medicinstuderende til at læse skønlitteratur, forholdet mellem sanglyrik og bogtrykte digte, litteraturens bidrag til debatten om samfundsaktuelle kriser og meget andet. Bogen henvender sig til alle, der interesserer sig for den fortløbende dialog om litteraturen og litteraturkritikkens fortsatte betydning for vores kultur og samfund. English: 11 articles concerning Scandinavian literary criticism from the heyday of New Criticism to the present and contemporary Scandinavian critical literature. Topics such as the introduction of New Criticism in Scandinavia, literary pedadogy, the academic study of song lyrics, narrative medicine, and the response of contemporary literature to societal problems are covered. The contributors are prominent literary scholars from Denmark, Norway, and Sweden.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Jens Lohfert","Mønster, Louise","Schmidt, Michael Kallesøe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-067710"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Literary criticism","Literary theory","Litteraturkritik","Litteraturpædagogik","New Criticism","Nordisk litteratur","Nykritik","Postcritique","Postkritik","Scandinavian Literature"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"en ny kritik","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.forlagetspring.dk/products/en-ny-kritik","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-067710","ids":["aau-3cec4e5e-6082-4ae4-abb7-edc305b92c80"],"keyword":["Nordisk litteratur","Scandinavian literature","literary criticism","literary pedagogy","literary theory","litteraturkritik","litteraturpædagogik","new criticism","nykritik","postcritique","postkritik"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5A169B6A43781DDF67E45FD2CE4185E3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Global Studies (CL)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Global Studies (CL), IRGIL - Interdisciplinære litteraturstudier (CGS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Global Studies (CL), IRGiC - The Interdisciplinary Research Group in Culture (CGS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Lohfert","key":"jørgensenped","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"5998e517-744d-4f84-a067-684c61abd4c2","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Lohfert","orcid":"0000-0003-3542-9352","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"mønsterped","last":"Mønster","locid":"6104678d-6a83-4e3b-aa45-595f743b48dd","name":"Mønster, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-3181-144X","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Kallesøe","key":"schmidtped","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9b20465e-70d2-4c54-92a9-9145cb2154bc","name":"Schmidt, Michael Kallesøe","orcid":"0000-0002-8971-4784","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793358706"],"pages":"212","place":"Hellerup","publisher":"Forlaget Spring","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3cec4e5e-6082-4ae4-abb7-edc305b92c80"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"En ny kritik","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-067710","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Disney’s animated villains have recently changed to show less conventionally villainous traits: They look and express themselves more like sympathetic characters, and they are usually only outed as villains late in the plot. This shift has prompted much academic commentary on the psychological and cultural significance of Disney’s new villains. We add to the existing literature on Disney’s new villains in two ways. First, we analyze shifts in the vocalizations of villains between the 1990s and 2010s. Second, we integrate this analysis in a biocultural account of Disney’s shifting overall representations of villains. We argue that while Disney has long employed evolutionarily explicable cues to villainy, such as a foreign accent and an unappealing exterior, the company is now reacting to challenges to norms of social representation that proscribe the linking of such overt traits with immorality. Consequently, recent Disney films do not employ socially stigmatizing cues. However, Disney continues to employ nonstigmatizing cues, such as evil laughter and abiding anger, because these cues foster antipathy in audiences at no sociomoral risk.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kjeldgaard-Christiansen, Jens","Schmidt Rasmussen, Sarah Helene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-136812"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Accent","Antipathy","Disney","Laughter","Morality","Pitch"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disney s shifting visions of villainy from the 000000001990s to the 000000002010s a biocultural analysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85087776703","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-136812","identifier":[{"id":"85087776703","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0d0f66b6-5193-4c0a-a150-1d2538318b08"],"keyword":["Accent","Antipathy","Disney","Laughter","Morality","Pitch","Villains"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5262EB31D17A0D1204BC66CBAB867BEE"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of English"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"kjeldgaardchristiansenpau","last":"Kjeldgaard-Christiansen","locid":"9a7108d7-32a1-4d46-ab10-8a2e471cb336","name":"Kjeldgaard-Christiansen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-5270-4531","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Helene","key":"schmidtrasmussenpau","last":"Schmidt Rasmussen","locid":"fdc6493a-541c-422a-bd98-92fab78d6053","name":"Schmidt Rasmussen, Sarah Helene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.26613/esic.3.2.140","issn":["24729876","24729884"],"issn_org":["24729884"],"issue":"2","journal":"Evolutionary Studies in Imaginative Culture","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Academic Studies Press","status":"p","title":"Evolutionary Studies in Imaginative Culture","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0d0f66b6-5193-4c0a-a150-1d2538318b08"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Disney’s Shifting Visions of Villainy from the 1990s to the 2010s : A Biocultural Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-136812","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background. Remote ischemic conditioning (RIC) protects against acute ischemia-reperfusion injury and may have beneficial effects in patients with stable cardiovascular disease. We investigated the effect of long-term RIC treatment in patients with chronic ischemic heart failure (CIHF). Methods. Prespecified post-hoc analysis of a prospective, exploratory and outcome-assessor blinded study. Twenty-one patients with compensated CIHF and 21 matched controls without heart failure or ischemic heart disease were treated with RIC once daily for 28 ± 4 days. RIC was conducted as 4 cycles of 5 minutes upper arm ischemia followed by 5 minutes of reperfusion. We evaluated circulating markers of inflammation and cardiac remodeling at baseline and following long-term RIC. Results. RIC reduced C-reactive protein from 1.5 (0.6–2.5) to 1.3 (0.6–2.1) mg/l following long-term RIC treatment (p =.02) and calprotectin from 477 (95% CI 380 to 600) to 434 (95% CI 354 to 533) ng/ml (p =.03) in patients with CIHF, but not in matched controls. Overall, RIC did not affect circulating markers related to adaptive or innate immunology or cardiac remodeling in patients with CIHF. Among patients with CIHF and N-terminal pro-brain natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP) plasma levels above the geometric mean of 372 ng/l, long-term RIC treatment reduced soluble ST2 (n = 9) from 22.0 ± 3.7 to 20.3 ± 3.9 ng/ml following long-term RIC treatment (p =.01). Conclusion. Our findings suggest that long-term RIC treatment has mild anti-inflammatory effects in patients with compensated CIHF and anti-remodeling effects in those with increased NT-proBNP levels. This should be further investigated in a randomized sham-controlled trial.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pryds, Kasper","Schmidt, Michael Rahbek","Bjerre, Mette","Thiel, Steffen","Refsgaard, Jens","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Østgård, René Drage","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-144477"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute myocardial infarction","Calprotectin","Cardiac remodeling","Complement","Heart failure","Inflammation","Ischemic Preconditioning","Ischemic heart disease","Mannan binding lectin","Microcirculation","Neutrophils","Pathway","Pattern recognition molecules","Remote ischemic conditioning"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of long term remote ischemic conditioning on inflammation and cardiac remodeling","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85066972446","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-144477","identifier":[{"id":"85066972446","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000471398800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"31117835","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-1a67bb8e-0fdc-4d1a-b854-cfc307d4d307"],"keyword":["ACUTE MYOCARDIAL-INFARCTION","CALPROTECTIN","COMPLEMENT","CRISP STENT","Ischemic heart disease","MANNAN-BINDING LECTIN","MICROCIRCULATION","NEUTROPHILS","PATHWAY","PATTERN-RECOGNITION MOLECULES","cardiac remodeling","heart failure","inflammation","ischemic preconditioning","remote ischemic conditioning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC82B95EAD8ADFA447708B9ACA60244E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Regional Hospital of Randers","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"prydspau","last":"Pryds","locid":"e8f8ad41-ec4a-4b07-851f-b898f7ead8c5","name":"Pryds, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0182-8718","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Rahbek","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b426fa5b-d8ea-4975-821c-43c67d717749","name":"Schmidt, Michael Rahbek","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"1337eaca-a3a1-4837-a772-261478be9f37","name":"Bjerre, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steffen","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"beb49137-797f-4a6a-841c-340818b6f472","name":"Thiel, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0002-4817-155X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"refsgaardpau","last":"Refsgaard","locid":"bef61e81-bb73-450c-a731-ec33a8e2a7e4","name":"Refsgaard, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Drage","key":"østgårdpau","last":"Østgård","locid":"55d0f083-27c9-4d6b-95d4-92ec4d785e87","name":"Østgård, René Drage","orcid":"0000-0001-6124-8972","ra