{"abstract":"This paper describes children's perceptions and visions for a healthier social and physical environment in the setting of a primary school on the Danish island of Bornholm. Guided by an everyday-life perspective and applying participatory action research methods including social imagination and visual techniques within the framework of future creating workshops, the study engaged 50 children aged 6-9 years in creative processes of identifying health-related problem areas and solutions in their school setting. The study observed that the children were very capable of articulating their thoughts, ideas and visions for a better and healthier school environment. Identified problem areas and solutions differed widely and represented a broad perspective of health including social, physical, environmental and emotional aspects. The paper discusses advantages and challenges of involving children in decision-making processes and concludes that children are visionary and creative agents of change in health promotion projects provided that applied participatory methods are appealing to the children.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Clausen, Laura Tolnov","Schmidt, Carina","Aagaard-Hansen, Jens","Reinbach, Helene Christine","Toft, Ulla","Bloch, Paul"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-001495"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bloch, Paul"],"country":["South Africa","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford","University of the Witwatersrand"],"keyword":["Child","Children","Denmark","Education methods","Female","Health promoting schools","Humans","Male","Participation","Psychology Child","School Health Services","Schools","Social imagination","Students psychology","Visual methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Ubberup Folk High School"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"children as visionary change agents in danish school health promotion","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85075436776","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-001495","identifier":[{"id":"85075436776","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30124857","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-1dae7a00-589b-4822-a476-6e35cd0d3669","dtu-e258ac86-9d94-4daf-9209-3a055d818217"],"keyword":["Child","Children","Denmark","Education/methods","Female","Health promoting schools","Humans","Male","Participation","Psychology, Child","School Health Services","Schools","Social imagination","Students/psychology","Visual methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AE5B56FEBA4212EAA25021E5195C7A6C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Ubberup Folk High School"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"za","key":"university of the witwatersrand","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"University of the Witwatersrand","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Tolnov","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"824bcf1e-2eef-40ad-a44e-18cc9ca34ea5","name":"Clausen, Laura Tolnov","orcid":"0000-0002-9952-4693","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Carina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"aagaardhansenpau","last":"Aagaard-Hansen","name":"Aagaard-Hansen, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helene Christine","key":"reinbachpau","last":"Reinbach","locid":"ae372771-6fee-474b-9a9c-9c73b5cc0123","name":"Reinbach, Helene Christine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"toftpau","last":"Toft","name":"Toft, Ulla","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"blochpau","last":"Bloch","name":"Bloch, Paul","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30124857"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/heapro/day049","issn":["09574824","14602245"],"issn_org":["09574824"],"issue":"5","journal":"Health Promotion International","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Health Promotion International","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075436776"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1dae7a00-589b-4822-a476-6e35cd0d3669","dtu-e258ac86-9d94-4daf-9209-3a055d818217"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Children as visionary change agents in Danish school health promotion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-001495","year":"2019","yearsub":2020}
{"abstract":"Between 2010 and 2015, pivotal trials with strict enrolment criteria led to the approval of several new treatments for metastatic melanoma (MM). We sought to determine the impact of these treatments in the 'real world'. We took advantage of the Danish MM database (DAMMED), which contains data on the entire, unselected population diagnosed with MM within Denmark. All MM cases (excluding ocular MM, n = 837) diagnosed in three non-consecutive years marked by major changes in the first-line treatments (2012: interleukin-2 and BRAF inhibitors; 2014: anti-CTLA-4: Cytotoxic T-Lymphocyte Antigen 4 and 2016: anti-PD-1: programmed cell death protein 1 and MEK inhibitors) were retrieved. Patients were grouped into 'trial-like' and 'trial-excluded' based on the common trial eligibility criteria. In the 'trial-like' population (39% of all MM), the median overall survival (OS) was not reached in 2016 versus 18.8 months in 2014 (hazard ratio [HR] 0.52, 95% confidence interval [CI] 0.35-0.75; p = 0.0005) and 16.5 months in 2012 (HR 0.41, 95% CI 0.27-0.63; p < 0.0001). In the 'trial-excluded' population (61% of all MM), 75% had brain metastases and/or (performance status) PS ≥ 2. Here, the median OS improved to 6.9 months in 2016 versus 5.2 months in 2014 (HR 0.66, 95% CI 0.52-0.84; p = 0.0008) and 4.2 months in 2012 (HR 0.66, 95% CI 0.52-0.84; p = 0.0007). Subgroup analysis of the BRAF wild-type population showed an improved 1-year survival rate in 2016 versus 2014 (35.9% vs 18.8%, p = 0.0153). In conclusion, the introduction of modern treatments has led to an improved survival of real-world patients with MM, regardless of their eligibility to clinical trials and the BRAF status. These data support the application of modern treatments to patient populations which are not represented in pivotal trials.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Donia, Marco","Ellebaek, Eva","Jensen, Trine Øllegaard","Duval, Lone","Aaby, Jens Bull","Hoejberg, Lise","Køhler, Ulrich Heide","Schmidt, Henrik","Bastholt, Lars","Svane, Inge Marie"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-024059"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Svane, Inge Marie"],"keyword":["COMBINED NIVOLUMAB","Immunotherapy","Improved survival","Ipilimumab","Metastatic melanoma","Modern treatment era","Pembrolizumab","Real world evidence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the real world impact of modern treatments on the survival of patients with metastatic melanoma","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85059227875","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was in part supported by Bristol-Myers Squibb, Roche, Novartis and MSD through economic support to the databaseDAMMED and by Herlev and Gentofte Research Council through a stipend to MD. The funding bodies did not have any other role in the study."],"id":"S03-100.00-024059","identifier":[{"id":"000457738500003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85059227875","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30605822","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9c2ac962-497b-4fd6-b7ad-ca763c2f163c","ku-fa8961bd-1f38-4fea-a5b6-9876b14b9004","sdu-190e869f-69b4-458c-a6fc-30760635d73b"],"keyword":["COMBINED NIVOLUMAB","IPILIMUMAB","Immunotherapy","Improved survival","Metastatic melanoma","Modern treatment era","PEMBROLIZUMAB","Real-world evidence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-8CE4BF42E7159DAC695528B1DA95BAFC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Herlev and Gentofte Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Oncology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Marco","key":"doniapau","last":"Donia","locid":"592383df-9101-495c-8282-62ddcf6b1d9f","name":"Donia, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"ellebaekpau","last":"Ellebaek","name":"Ellebaek, Eva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Heide","key":"øllegaardpau","last":"Øllegaard","locid":"48d3027b-a7ab-44b0-a6da-2cd4fa3763db","name":"Jensen, Trine Øllegaard","name_org":"Øllegaard, Trine Heide","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone","key":"duvalpau","last":"Duval","locid":"119d0202-6a61-48b1-ab64-7c58ba736597","name":"Duval, Lone","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Bull","key":"aabypau","last":"Aaby","locid":"24b24789-abea-41ca-af4c-c95ea8b962ad","name":"Aaby, Jens Bull","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise","key":"hoejbergpau","last":"Hoejberg","locid":"5284ad9f-d75f-4aac-bcb6-00437fa4ecbe","name":"Hoejberg, Lise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrich Heide","key":"køhlerpau","last":"Køhler","name":"Køhler, Ulrich Heide","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"834188a5-a600-41a5-a8a1-9e34c3837141","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"bastholtpau","last":"Bastholt","locid":"8228749a-ec51-42aa-91a1-c0ec476093bb","name":"Bastholt, Lars","orcid":"0000-0001-5478-9826","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Inge Marie","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"12c124a9-b64d-4b36-9bbd-c1665658101d","name":"Svane, Inge Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-9451-6037","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30605822"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejca.2018.12.002","issn":["09598049","18790852"],"issn_org":["09598049"],"journal":"European Journal of Cancer","pages":"25-32","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cancer","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059227875"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9c2ac962-497b-4fd6-b7ad-ca763c2f163c","ku-fa8961bd-1f38-4fea-a5b6-9876b14b9004","sdu-190e869f-69b4-458c-a6fc-30760635d73b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The real-world impact of modern treatments on the survival of patients with metastatic melanoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-024059","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: High plasma levels of YKL-40 might be associated with mortality in patients with melanoma, and it is unknown if YKL-40 is causally related to mortality. Experimental design: We studied two cohorts: 2618 patients with melanoma from hospital clinics and 1413 general population patients with melanoma, totalling 4031 patients followed up for mortality end-points for up to 20 years. All were genotyped for CHI3L1 rs4950928, highly predictive of lifelong plasma YKL-40, and plasma YKL-40 levels were measured in 2165 patients. We tested the hypotheses that measured and genetically predicted high plasma YKL-40 are associated with increased mortality in patients with melanoma. Results: For the hospital melanoma cohort, age- and sex-adjusted hazard ratios for death in individuals with measured plasma YKL-40 in the 96–100th percentile versus 1–95th percentile and per 10-percentile increase were 1.52 (95% confidence interval, 1.07–2.16) and 1.07 (1.02–1.11), respectively, most pronounced for patients with localised melanomas. Each C-allele of the CHI3L1 rs4950928 genotype was associated with plasma YKL-40 level increases of 32% in the hospital melanoma cohort (p = 6 × 10−48) and 43% in the general population melanoma cohort (p = 7 × 10−13). Multifactorially adjusted ratios for these increases in the combined cohorts were 1.04 (1.00–1.09) observationally for measured plasma YKL-40 and 0.98 (0.86–1.12) for the genetically predicted plasma YKL-40. Conclusion: Measured, but not genetically predicted, increasing plasma YKL-40 was associated with increased mortality in patients with melanoma. Plasma YKL-40 is a marker but less likely to be a cause of increased mortality in patients with melanoma.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Ismail, Hafsa","Helby, Jens","Hölmich, Lisbet R.","Chakera, Annette H.","Bastholt, Lars","Klyver, Helle","Sjoegren, Pia","Schmidt, Henrik","Schöllhammer, Liv","Johansen, Julia S.","Nordestgaard, Børge G.","Bojesen, Stig E."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-026222"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Bojesen, Stig E."],"keyword":["CHI3L1 rs4950928","Melanoma","Survival","YKL 40"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measured and genetically predicted plasma ykl 000000000040 levels and melanoma mortality","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85072604972","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank the Research Foundation for Health Research in the Capital Region of Denmark, the Research Council at Herlev and Gentofte Hospital , Chief Physician Johan Boserup and Lise Boserup's Foundation and Sawmill owner Jeppe Juhl and wife Ovita Juhl's Memorial Fund for financial support. The authors also thank Quidel for providing the YKL-40 ELISA kits at reduced price. The funders had no influence on any parts of the work and in the preparation of this manuscript."],"id":"S03-100.00-026222","identifier":[{"id":"85072604972","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31563729","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ba4b381c-df9c-47fc-8f8b-fb10e4f6ce8a","ku-8c94686a-a847-448a-ad3c-076eb471874a","sdu-07b54043-48b2-4882-ad52-3aec27bad5fb"],"keyword":["CHI3L1 rs4950928","Melanoma","Survival","YKL-40"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-1F25E1C42E023870290935F7E290C898"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Plastic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oncology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Plastic and Breast surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first"