":"1","first":"Stig E.","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"25f871c8-a69d-45d1-85b6-c438d7293b74","name":"Bojesen, Stig E","name_org":"Bojesen, Stig E.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31563729"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejca.2019.08.025","issn":["09598049","18790852"],"issn_org":["09598049"],"journal":"European Journal of Cancer","pages":"74-84","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cancer","volume":"121"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072604972"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ba4b381c-df9c-47fc-8f8b-fb10e4f6ce8a","ku-8c94686a-a847-448a-ad3c-076eb471874a","sdu-07b54043-48b2-4882-ad52-3aec27bad5fb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Measured and genetically predicted plasma YKL-40 levels and melanoma mortality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-026222","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Evidence for effective interventions to prevent long-term sequelae after concussion is sparse. This study aimed to test the efficacy of Get going After concussIoN (GAIN), an interdisciplinary, individually-tailored intervention of 8 weeks duration based on gradual return to activities and principles from cognitive behavioural therapy. Methods: We conducted an open-label, parallel-group randomised trial in a hospital setting in Central Denmark Region. Participants were 15–30-year-old patients with high levels of post-concussion symptoms (PCS) 2–6 months post-concussion (i.e., a score ≥20 on the Rivermead Post-concussion Symptoms Questionnaire (RPQ)). They were randomly assigned (1:1) to either enhanced usual care (EUC) or GAIN+EUC. Masking of participants and therapists was not possible. The primary outcome was change in RPQ-score from baseline to 3-month FU. All analyses were done on an intention-to-treat basis using linear mixed-effects models. This trial is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, number NCT02337101. Findings: Between March 1, 2015, and September 1, 2017, we included 112 patients. Patients allocated to GAIN+EUC (n=57) reported a significantly larger reduction of PCS than patients allocated to EUC (n=55) with a mean adjusted difference in improvement of 7·6 points (95% confidence interval (CI) 2·0–13·1, p=0·008), Cohen's d=0·5 (95% CI 0·1–0·9). Number needed to treat for prevention of one additional patient with RPQ ≥20 at 3-month FU was 3·6 (95% CI 2·2–11·3). No adverse events were observed. Interpretation: Compared with EUC, GAIN+EUC was associated with a larger reduction of post-concussion symptoms at 3-month FU. Funding: Central Denmark Region and the foundation “Public Health in Central Denmark Region - a collaboration between municipalities and the region”.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Thastum, Mille","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","Tuborgh, Astrid","Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Schröder, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-233284"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Thastum, Mille"],"keyword":["Brain concussion","Cognitive behavioural therapy","Illness perceptions","Intervention","Mild traumatic brain injury","Post concussion syndrome","Rivermead post concussion symptoms questionnaire"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel interdisciplinary intervention gain vs enhanced usual care to reduce high levels of post concussion symptoms in adolescents and young adults 000000000002 000000000006 months post injury a randomised trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eclinm.2019.11.007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-233284","identifier":[{"id":"85076604617","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31891145","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6933237","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-b6321e96-d594-446c-8573-43b0c9e1b48e"],"keyword":["Brain concussion","Cognitive behavioural therapy","Graded exercise therapy","Illness perceptions","Intervention","Mild traumatic brain injury","Post-concussion syndrome","Rivermead Post-Concussion Symptoms Questionnaire"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D96E3A8D94333394A7EA60D51053F6D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eclinm.2019.11.007","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mille Moeller","key":"thastumpau","last":"Thastum","locid":"c3813500-c313-4961-a854-ad2dba72d7d9","name":"Thastum, Mille","name_org":"Thastum, Mille Moeller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Ulrikka","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","locid":"1e308742-df61-47da-83ce-53d8a7c774c3","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","orcid":"0000-0002-7426-0353","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erhard Trillingsgaard","key":"næssschmidtpau","last":"Næss-Schmidt","locid":"c1a1a6b6-deb0-4e07-8cc0-f7d3beeaca85","name":"Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2539-0362","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"tuborghpau","last":"Tuborgh","locid":"f019f6a6-ef3a-403d-b9f8-60d62215cafc","name":"Tuborgh, Astrid","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Sondergaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f77754dc-4ec3-47ff-8227-808446a30644","name":"Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","name_org":"Jensen, Jens Sondergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne Wulff","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"1de9ffe9-dbf8-4bbd-8708-35bce0da950f","name":"Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"schröderpau","last":"Schröder","locid":"200c6dd9-43cd-41da-8c27-ce8adb073e24","name":"Schröder, Andreas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31891145"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.eclinm.2019.11.007","issn":["25895370"],"journal":"EClinicalMedicine","paperid":"100214","publisher":"The Lancet Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"EClinicalMedicine","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076604617"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b6321e96-d594-446c-8573-43b0c9e1b48e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Novel interdisciplinary intervention, GAIN, vs. enhanced usual care to reduce high levels of post-concussion symptoms in adolescents and young adults 2–6 months post-injury : A randomised trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-233284","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Stidsen, Marianne Søgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-418089"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Det Humanistiske Fakultet","Fænomenologi","Hermeneutik","Litteraturteori","Metode"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"privatdetektiven som rollemodel den fænomenologiske og hermeneutiske metodes langtidsholdbarhed","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-418089","ids":["ku-29487182-5292-4781-a125-438af5d1af1e"],"keyword":["Det Humanistiske Fakultet","Hermeneutik","Litteraturteori","Metode","fænomenologi"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9D84848CCC0B046963F239B1A5EB5080"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"stidsenpau","last":"Stidsen","locid":"35a779ad-6efd-4226-a3d8-e888207215fa","name":"Stidsen, Marianne Søgaard","name_org":"Stidsen, Marianne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"mønsterpedh","last":"Mønster","name":"Mønster, Louise","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Lohfert","key":"jørgensenpedh","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Jens Lohfert","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael Kallesøe","key":"schmidtpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Michael Kallesøe","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793358706"],"pages":"43-64","place":"Hellerup","publisher":"Forlaget Spring","status":"p","title":"En ny kritik"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-29487182-5292-4781-a125-438af5d1af1e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Privatdetektiven som rollemodel : Den fænomenologiske og hermeneutiske metodes langtidsholdbarhed","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-418089","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: Human papilloma virus (HPV) and tobacco smoking are important risk factors for development of oropharyngeal squamous cell carcinoma (OPSCC). Aims/objectives: To evaluate the impact of tobacco smoking on survival for cases with OPSCC with known HPV- and p16INK4A(p16)-status. Materials and Methods: OPSCC cases at the University Hospital of Copenhagen, Rigshospitalet, Denmark (2000-2014) and at University Hospital of Giessen, Germany (2000-2009) were included. Survival was illustrated with Kaplan-Meier plots. The effect of smoking exposure on survival was evaluated by Cox-regression models. HPV-positivity was defined as positivity for both HPV-DNA and p16. Results: We included 1316 OPSCC cases from 2000-2014 (48% HPV-positive). Smokers had a poorer outcome compared to non-smokers. Considering continuous smoking exposure, adding 10 pack-years of smoking increased hazard ratios irrespective of HPV-status.We observed a tendency to a greater impact on survival for cases with HPV-neg. tumours compared to cases with HPV-pos. tumours at low numbers of pack-years, yet the survival was similar at high numbers of pack-years. There was no significant difference in the impact of HPV-status on survival for non-smokers, however a highly significant difference for smokers. Conclusions and Significance: Smoking-status and number of pack-years at time of diagnosis impact survival for cases with OPSCC independent of HPV-status.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Grønhøj, Christian","Jensen, Jakob Schmidt","Wagner, Steffen","Dehlendorff, Christian","Friborg, Jeppe","Andersen, Elo","Wittekindt, Claus","Würdemann, Nora","Sharma, Shachi Jenny","Gattenlöhner, Stefan","Klussmann, Jens Peter","von Buchwald, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-545048"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact on survival of tobacco smoking for cases with oropharyngeal squamous cell carcinoma and known human papillomavirus and p000000000016 status a multicenter retrospective study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.27079","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-545048","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6659794","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85070806103","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31384393","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fe152168-41ab-48cc-a577-600f31210297"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D3EF38178B348F01159FCED0E5ADE7C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/237517155/27079_1033705_1_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.27079","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"grønhøjpau","last":"Grønhøj","name":"Grønhøj, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob Schmidt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jakob Schmidt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":