apillomavirus and p16-status : a multicenter retrospective study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-545048","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Food waste landfilling causes environmental degradation, and this work assesses a sustainable food valorization technique. In this study, food waste is converted into lactic acid in a batch assembly by dark fermentation without pH control and without the addition of external inoculum at 37°C. The effect of total solid (TS), enzymatic, and aeration pretreatment was investigated on liquid product concentration and product yield. The maximum possible TS content was 34% of enzymatic pretreated waste and showed the highest lactic acid concentration of 52 g/L, with a lactic acid selectivity of 0.6 glactic/gtotalacids. The results indicated that aeration pretreatment does not significantly improve product concentration or yield. Non-pretreated waste in a 29% TS system showed a lactic acid concentration of 31 g/L. The results showed that enzymatic pretreated waste at TS of 34% results in the highest production of lactic acid.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Yousuf, Ahasa","Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-574660"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Carboxylic acid","Food waste","Lactic Acid","Mixed culture fermentation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of total solid content and pretreatment on the production of lactic acid from mixed culture dark fermentation of food waste","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134960055","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-574660","identifier":[{"id":"85134960055","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-051c347c-357b-4e40-813a-bf19870de978"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Carboxylic acid","Enzymatic pretreatment","Food waste","Lactic acid","Mixed culture fermentation","Total solid content"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A23FBA9AD7B2103ED0AB23DF7856C5EC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahasa","key":"yousufpau","last":"Yousuf","name":"Yousuf, Ahasa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"ejbyeschmidtpedh","last":"Ejbye Schmidt","name":"Ejbye Schmidt, Jens","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_19","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"479-490","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134960055"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-051c347c-357b-4e40-813a-bf19870de978"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effect of Total Solid Content and Pretreatment on the Production of Lactic Acid from Mixed Culture Dark Fermentation of Food Waste","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-574660","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Designing a biorefinery involves the selection of the set of products and the technologies that will be used for processing a given set of biomass feedstocks. Biorefinery design methodologies have relied either in conventional conceptual process design, where the set of products and technologies under consideration is fixed, or on the optimization of processing networks where multiple products and technologies are considered and the best biomass-technology(ies)-product(s) set is found by solving a mathematical programming problem. Both approaches implicitly assume a single actor biorefinery; this is that conversion of biomass is carried out by the same facility. In this chapter, a novel framework for the analysis of biorefinery processes is discussed. The framework considers that, akin to the current petrochemical industry, the biomass-based industry should be designed as distributed multi-actor processes. The chapter starts by commenting on the current structure of the petrochemical industry and motivating the need for a distributed biomass-based industry. After reviewing the approaches commonly used for the design of biorefineries, the distributed framework developed by the authors is presented. The chapter ends by discussing a modified version of the framework useful for screening processes at early design stages.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ashraf, Muhammad Tahir","Torres, Ana Inés","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Stephanopoulos, George"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579412"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"country":["United Arab Emirates","United States","Uruguay"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","University of the Republic"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Biorefinery design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis and optimization of multi actor biorefineries","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134982244","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-579412","identifier":[{"id":"85134982244","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-15ad812d-f475-40db-8285-44fda92af9bd"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Biorefinery design","Biorefinery network","Biorefinery optimization","Multi-actor biorefineries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9BA829916E499285777F3A8AF3707E19"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"uy","key":"university of the republic","loc":["Uruguay","America, South"],"name":"University of the Republic","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Muhammad Tahir","key":"ashrafpau","last":"Ashraf","name":"Ashraf, Muhammad Tahir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana Inés","key":"torrespau","last":"Torres","name":"Torres, Ana Inés","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"George","key":"stephanopoulospau","last":"Stephanopoulos","name":"Stephanopoulos, George","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"ejbyeschmidtpedh","last":"Ejbye Schmidt","name":"Ejbye Schmidt, Jens","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_3","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"49-75","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134982244"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-15ad812d-f475-40db-8285-44fda92af9bd"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Analysis and Optimization of Multi-actor Biorefineries","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-579412","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Avicennia marina is the only naturally occurring mangrove specie in the arid Arabian Gulf coast of the United Arab Emirates (UAE). Due to water scarcity, A. marina is a precious biomass resource for the UAE that does not require freshwater for growing and is able to grow in the Arabian Gulf high salinity conditions of over 40 g/kg. Importantly, this lignocellulosic bioresource may be used for the production of high valuable chemicals. In this manuscript, we present the first lignocellulosic composition characterization of Arabian Gulf A. marina. To do this, A. marina stem, leaves, and pneumatophore samples were collected from two locations in the United Arab Emirates and chemically characterized for sugar composition, ash content, and by-products using standard protocols. Analysis revealed that A. marina arabinan, xylan, glucan, and lignin composition ranges between 1–22, 5–18, 10–31, and 21–48 g/100g_TS (TS: total solids), respectively. The highest composition of xylan and glucan was obtained for stems and pneumatophores (45 and 38 g/100 g TS, respectively). Xylan and glucan are the polymeric precursors for the production of high-value chemicals such as furfural and hydroxymethylfurfural (HMF). Under the characterization conditions, it was obtained furfural and HMF (g/100 g_TS) in the ranges of 0.05–0.42 and 0.45–2.1, respectively.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Almardeai, Saleha","Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Haris, Sabeera","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-581144"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of avicennia marina an arid coastal biomass toward biorefinery products","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134963972","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-581144","identifier":[{"id":"85134963972","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1bb6ad04-6ecf-44ed-a321-ce3736be3cf4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49C7B47478AF68C81B21FB5D2BEE5E10"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Saleha","key":"almardeaipau","last":"Almardeai","name":"Almardeai, Saleha","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabeera","key":"harispau","last":"Haris","name":"Haris, Sabeera","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpedh","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"ejbyeschmidtpedh","last":"Ejbye Schmidt","name":"Ejbye Schmidt, Jens","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-10961-5_29","eisbn":["9783030109615"],"isbn":["9783030109608"],"pages":"669-677","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Integrated Sustainable Processes for Biomass Conversion to Biomaterials, Biofuels, and Fertilizers","title":"Biorefinery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134963972"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1bb6ad04-6ecf-44ed-a321-ce3736be3cf4"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Characterization of Avicennia marina : An Arid-Coastal Biomass—Toward Biorefinery Products","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-581144","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Truslerne mod bestøvende insekter bør imødegås af en samlet strategi for både holdte og vilde bestøvere, skriver 22 forskere i denne opfordring til at få gjort noget ved sagen.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Dupont, Yoko Luise","Bang Madsen, Henning","Rasmussen, Claus","Hansted, Lise","Kryger, Per","Ravn, Hans Peter","Schmidt, Inger Kappel","Olesen, Jens M.","Holm, Eigil","Langer, Vibeke","Sigsgaard, Lene","Eilenberg, Jørgen","Skov, Charlotte","Lassen, Kristin Marie","Ahrenfeldt, Erica Juel","Calabuig, Isabel","Holst, Niels","Boelt, Birte","Jensen, Annette Bruun","Lecocq, Antoine","Howe, Andy G.","Termansen, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-089.13-027217"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California at San Diego"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"en fælles front for alle bier","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/228149683/En_f_lles_front_for_alle_bier.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.13-027217","ids":["au-c8b9032b-c987-4617-9d59-bc1e51d99ba8","ku-0dbd7bdd-e904-4c5e-8569-897f9446c64e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-E9E80B515A45B9EB7E191BE64752FBD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/228149683/En_f_lles_front_for_alle_bier.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n"