{"abstract":"2018: Arctic researchers have just witnessed another extreme summer - but in a new sense of the word. Although public interest has long been focused on general warming trends and trends towards a lower sea ice cover in the Arctic Ocean, this summer saw the realization of another predicted trend: that of increasing precipitation during the winter months and of increased year-to-year variability. In a well-studied ecosystem in Northeast Greenland, this resulted in the most complete reproductive failure encountered in the terrestrial ecosystem during more than two decades of monitoring: only a few animals and plants were able to reproduce because of abundant and late melting snow. These observations, we suggest, should open our eyes to potentially drastic consequences of predicted changes in both the mean and the variability of arctic climate.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schmidt, Niels Martin","Reneerkens, Jeroen","Christensen, Jens Hesselbjerg","Olesen, Martin","Roslin, Tomas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-020192"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Netherlands","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","University of Groningen","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["PLANT","PREDICTING TIPPING POINTS","Predator","Responses","TRENDS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-DMI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-DMI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an ecosystem wide reproductive failure with more snow in the arctic","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000392","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-020192","identifier":[{"id":"31613872","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000505712400011","type":"wos"},{"id":"85073443414","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6793841","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-67549b6e-4e93-4e8b-aef2-e0d4a266090d","ku-d4190943-c614-48e0-9973-4b9f895019ef"],"keyword":["PLANT","PREDATOR","PREDICTING TIPPING POINTS","RESPONSES","TRENDS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8CE56E3E19D791E2914839B70BDFC253"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000392","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/234144965/journal.pbio.3000392.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Centre, Roskilde","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Ecosystem Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands institute for sea research nioz","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Climate and Geophysics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"dmi danish meteorological institute","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-DMI","l3nn":"DMI Danish Meteorological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DMI Danish Meteorological Institute","namevar":["The National Danish Meteorological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-DMI","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"se","key":"swedish university of agricultural sciences","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b91704ca-e126-4c35-af20-95b2269d230a","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-6218","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeroen","key":"reneerkenspau","last":"Reneerkens","name":"Reneerkens, Jeroen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jens Hesselbjerg","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"35b65d2a-e280-41d6-8a35-26f5064f05f3","name":"Christensen, Jens Hesselbjerg","orcid":"0000-0002-9908-8203","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomas","key":"roslinpau","last":"Roslin","name":"Roslin, Tomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31613872"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pbio.3000392","issn":["15449173","15457885"],"issn_org":["15449173"],"issue":"10","journal":"PLOS Biology","paperid":"e3000392","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS Biology","title_org":"PLoS Biology","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073443414"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-67549b6e-4e93-4e8b-aef2-e0d4a266090d","ku-d4190943-c614-48e0-9973-4b9f895019ef"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An ecosystem-wide reproductive failure with more snow in the Arctic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-020192","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: About 5-15 % of patients with concussion experience persistent post-concussion symptoms (PCS) longer than 3 months post-injury. OBJECTIVE: To explore the feasibility of a new intervention for young patients with persistent PCS and long-term changes after intervention. METHODS: Thirty-two consecutive patients (15-30 years) with persistent PCS 2-4 months post-injury were recruited from a cohort study or referred to a non-randomized feasibility study of an individually tailored, 8-week, multidisciplinary intervention. Assessment was performed at baseline, end of intervention (EOI), and at 3-and 12-month follow-up (FU). Main measures were The Experience of Service Questionnaire (ESQ), Rivermead Post-Concussion Symptoms Questionnaire (RPQ) and The Quality of Life after Brain Injury-Overall Scale (QOLIBRI-OS). RESULTS: Twenty-three (72%) patients completed the intervention. The ESQ demonstrated high patient satisfaction. There was a decrease of PCS and an increase in quality of life from baseline to EOI: RPQ score-8.9 points, 95% CI 4.5 to 13.3, p < 0.001; QOLIBRI-OS score +10.5 points, 95% CI 2.5 to 18.5, p = 0.010. Improvement was maintained at 3-and 12-month FU. CONCLUSION: The new early intervention is feasible and may prevent chronification of PCS. An RCT is currently performed to evaluate the effect of the intervention.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Thastum, Mille","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","Frederiksen, Oana-Veronica","Tuborgh, Astrid","Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Schröder, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-129878"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Behavior Therapy","Brain concussion","Early intervention","Feasibility study","Mild traumatic brain injury","Post concussion syndrome","Rivermead post concussion symptoms questionnaire"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design of an early intervention for persistent post concussion symptoms in adolescents and young adults a feasibility study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85053312300","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-129878","identifier":[{"id":"30040756","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85053312300","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-010a66a4-4557-445c-a148-3559708b9c63"],"keyword":["Brain concussion","behavior therapy","early intervention","feasibility study","mild traumatic brain injury","post-concussion syndrome","rivermead post-concussion symptoms questionnaire"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-27A760454D208D13D14BC46B9B56359A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mille Moeller","key":"thastumpau","last":"Thastum","locid":"c3813500-c313-4961-a854-ad2dba72d7d9","name":"Thastum, Mille","name_org":"Thastum, Mille Moeller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Ulrikka","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","locid":"1e308742-df61-47da-83ce-53d8a7c774c3","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","orcid":"0000-0002-7426-0353","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erhard Trillingsgaard","key":"naessschmidtpau","last":"Naess-Schmidt","locid":"c1a1a6b6-deb0-4e07-8cc0-f7d3beeaca85","name":"Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","name_org":"Naess-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2539-0362","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Soendergaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f77754dc-4ec3-47ff-8227-808446a30644","name":"Jensen, Jens Søndergaard","name_org":"Jensen, Jens Soendergaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oana-Veronica","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"471708b8-684c-4ba7-9ed7-64ad884864a9","name":"Frederiksen, Oana-Veronica","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"tuborghpau","last":"Tuborgh","locid":"f019f6a6-ef3a-403d-b9f8-60d62215cafc","name":"Tuborgh, Astrid","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne Wulff","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"1de9ffe9-dbf8-4bbd-8708-35bce0da950f","name":"Svendsen, Susanne Wulff","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joergen Feldbaek","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","name_org":"Nielsen, Joergen Feldbaek","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"schröderpau","last":"Schröder","locid":"200c6dd9-43cd-41da-8c27-ce8adb073e24","name":"Schröder, Andreas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30040756"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/nre-172391","issn":["10538135","18786448"],"issn_org":["10538135"],"issue":"2","journal":"NeuroRehabilitation","pages":"155-167","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"NeuroRehabilitation","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053312300"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-010a66a4-4557-445c-a148-3559708b9c63"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Design of an early intervention for persistent post-concussion symptoms in adolescents and young adults : A feasibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-129878","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO) is a stroke prevention therapy for patients with non-valvular atrial fibrillation (AF). This study reports one-year outcomes from patients enrolled in the prospective global Amulet registry. METHODS AND RESULTS: A total of 1,088 patients were recruited, aged 75±9 years; 65% of patients were male. The CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED scores were 4.2±1.6 and 3.3±1.1, respectively. Eighty-three percent (83%) of patients had contraindications to anticoagulation (OAC); 72% had a history of major bleeding. An AMPLATZER Amulet LAA occluder was successfully implanted in 99% of cases. Transoesophageal echocardiography one to three months after implant showed no residual flow or flow <3 mm in 98.4%. The observed ischaemic stroke rate was 2.9%/year. Device-related thrombus was noted in 1.7% of patients. There were ten cases between 0 and 90 days and eight cases between 91 and 365 days. Patients discharged without OAC (>80%), in particular those on single aspirin therapy, did not appear to have a higher risk of device-related thrombus. In the first year, major bleeding occurred at an annualised rate of 10.3%. All-cause mortality was 8.4% at one year. CONCLUSIONS: In the global prospective Amulet registry of patients at high risk of stroke and bleeding, the annualised ischaemic stroke rate was 2.9%. The LAA was sealed in 98.4% after one to three months and device-related thrombus was observed in 1.7% of cases with only a minority of all patients on anticoagulation treatment.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Landmesser, Ulf","Tondo, Claudio","Camm, John","Diener, Hans-Christoph","Paul, Vince","Schmidt, Boris","Settergren, Magnus","Teiger, Emmanuel","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Hildick-Smith, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-191817"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"left atrial appendage occlusion with the amplatzer amulet device one year follow up from the prospective global amulet observational registry","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85051212767","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-191817","identifier":[{"id":"29806820","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85051212767","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6d8c18ad-8c30-44f3-8e6e-d994c347c77e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-BFB6E6B612C667F7B39286ABA21B2603"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"german cancer research center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulf","key":"landmesserpau","last":"Landmesser","name":"Landmesser, Ulf","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudio","key":"tondopau","last":"Tondo","name":"Tondo, Claudio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"cammpau","last":"Camm","name":"Camm, John","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans-Christoph","key":"dienerpau","last":"Diener","name":"Diener, Hans-Christoph","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Vince","key":"paulpau","last":"Paul","name":"Paul, Vince","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Boris","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Boris","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"settergrenpau","last":"Settergren","name":"Settergren, Magnus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmanuel","key":"teigerpau","last":"Teiger","name":"Teiger, Emmanuel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"hildicksmithpau","last":"Hildick-Smith","name":"Hildick-Smith, David","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29806820"],"pub":{"doi":"10.4244/eij-d-18-00344","issn":["1774024X","19696213"],"issn_org":["1774024X"],"issue":"5","journal":"EuroIntervention","publisher":"Europa Group","status":"p","title":"EuroIntervention","title_org":"EuroIntervention : journal of EuroPCR in collaboration with the Working Group on Interventional Cardiology of the European Society of Cardiology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051212767"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6d8c18ad-8c30-44f3-8e6e-d994c347c77e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Left atrial appendage occlusion with the AMPLATZER Amulet device : one-year follow-up from the prospective global Amulet observational registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-191817","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Plant functional traits directly affect ecosystem functions. At the species level, trait combinations depend on trade-offs representing different ecological strategies, but at the community level trait combinations are expected to be decoupled from these trade-offs because different strategies can facilitate co-existence within communities. A key question is to what extent community-level trait composition is globally filtered and how well it is related to global versus local environmental drivers. Here, we perform a global, plot-level analysis of trait–environment relationships, using a database with more than 1.1 million vegetation plots and 26,632 plant species with trait information. Although we found a strong filtering of 17 functional traits, similar climate and soil conditions support communities differing greatly in mean trait values. The two main community trait axes that capture half of the global trait variation (plant stature and resource acquisitiveness) reflect the trade-offs at the species level but are weakly associated with climate and soil conditions at the global scale. Similarly, within-plot trait variation does not vary systematically with macro-environment. Our results indicate that, at fine spatial grain, macro-environmental drivers are much less important for functional trait composition than has been assumed from floristic analyses restricted to co-occurrence in large grid cells. Instead, trait combinations seem to be predominantly filtered by local-scale factors such as disturbance, fine-scale soil conditions, niche partitioning and biotic interactions.","author_count":105,"contributors":["Bruelheide, Helge","Dengler, Jürgen","Purschke, Oliver","Lenoir, Jonathan","Jiménez-Alfaro, Borja","Hennekens, Stephan M.","Botta-Dukát, Zoltán","Chytrý, Milan","Field, Richard","Jansen, Florian","Kattge, Jens","Pillar, Valério D.","Schrodt, Franziska","Mahecha, Miguel D.","Peet, Robert K.","Sandel, Brody","van Bodegom, Peter","Altman, Jan","