:25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid E","key":"lundbergpau","last":"Lundberg","name":"Lundberg, Ingrid E","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17","corresponding":null,"first":"Hector","key":"chinoypau","last":"Chinoy","name":"Chinoy, Hector","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29259048"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/annrheumdis-2017-212382","issn":["00034967","14682060"],"issn_org":["00034967"],"issue":"8","journal":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","paperid":"e51","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049024561"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","zitelab aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6e61863b-e560-489c-a5a7-0251bf0052b4"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Response to: 'Antisynthetase syndrome or what else? Different perspectives indicate the need for new classification criteria' by Cavagna et al","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-604781","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To establish whether the round window approach (RWA) leads to less vestibular dysfunction and dizziness than the standard cochleostomy approach (SCA) during cochlear implant (CI) surgery, as assessed using the video head impulse test (vHIT). Additionally, objective findings were compared with the subjective dizziness perceived by the patient. Study Design: Double blinded, clinical randomized trial. Setting: University Hospital. Patients: Fifty-two ears from 46 patients were included. Inclusion criterion was a gain value more than 0.50. Intervention: Patients were randomized to the RWA or the SCA. Evaluation with the vHIT was performed before surgery, 1 day after surgery, and 1 month after surgery. Subjective dizziness was measured using a visual analogue scale (VAS) and the dizziness handicap inventory (DHI). Main Outcome Measures: Gain values and the incidence of catch-up saccades. Results: Three out of 23 patients in the SCA group experienced catch-up saccades compared with no patients in the RWA group, indicating the occurrence of objective vestibular dysfunction after CI surgery; the difference was not statistically significant. The VAS increased in both groups the day after surgery. The difference between the groups was not statistically significant. No statistically significant changes in the gain value or the DHI score could were observed between the two groups. Conclusion: No statistically significant difference between the cochleostomy approach and the round window approach using the vHIT and subjective dizziness perceived by the patient was found.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hviid Korsager, Leise Elisabeth","Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","Faber, Christian Emil","Wanscher, Jens Højberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-613626"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cochlear implant","Vestibular function","Video head impulse test"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vestibular outcome after cochlear implantation is not related to surgical technique a double blinded randomized clinical trial of round window approach versus cochleostomy","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MAO.0000000000001695","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-613626","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5821484","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85042497100","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29283913","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-8d133ddd-0072-4d2c-a748-6e62ebfbe941"],"keyword":["Cochlear implant","Cochleostomy","Round window approach","Vestibular function","Video head impulse test"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-847A776C366172DEE65733E31F926732"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/140661683/Vestibular_Outcome_After_Cochlear_Implantation_Is_Not_Related_to_Surgical_Technique.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MAO.0000000000001695","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oto Rhino Laryngology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leise Elisabeth Hviid","key":"korsagerpau","last":"Korsager","locid":"04fd1226-1580-4e42-997d-319eec9c8286","name":"Hviid Korsager, Leise Elisabeth","name_org":"Korsager, Leise Elisabeth Hviid","orcid":"0000-0001-6906-4756","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Hvass","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"db84fc4e-28da-45af-a608-13ce8f4ec719","name":"Schmidt, Jesper Hvass","orcid":"0000-0001-7683-1407","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"41aa4a5b-b537-43a3-942c-8beeae29c5c6","name":"Faber, Christian Emil","name_org":"Faber, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5078-6481","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Højberg","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","locid":"33130a0a-a7b5-4e60-b090-5a6e43f3396a","name":"Wanscher, Jens Højberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29283913"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mao.0000000000001695","issn":["15317129","15374505"],"issn_org":["15317129"],"issue":"3","journal":"Otology & Neurotology","pages":"306-312","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Otology & Neurotology","title_org":"Otology & neurotology : official publication of the American Otological Society, American Neurotology Society [and] European Academy of Otology and Neurotology","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042497100"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8d133ddd-0072-4d2c-a748-6e62ebfbe941"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Vestibular Outcome After Cochlear Implantation Is Not Related to Surgical Technique : A Double Blinded, Randomized Clinical Trial of Round Window Approach Versus Cochleostomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-613626","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Abstract It has been suggested that in order to infer ecological processes from observed patterns of species abundance we need to investigate the covariance in species abundance. Consequently, an expression for the expected covariance of pin-point cover measurements of two speciesisdeveloped.By comparing the observed covariance with the expected covariance we get a new type of information on the spatial arrangement of two species. Here the discrepancy between the observed and expected covariance may be thought of as a measure of the spatial conﬁguration of the two species that may indicate underling ecological processes. The method is applied in a case study of Calluna vulgaris and Deschampsia ﬂexuosa on dry heathland sites. The observed covariance of Calluna and Deschampsia at the level of the sites was positively and signiﬁcantly correlated with the expected covariance. Negative covariance was observed on sites where both Calluna and Deschampsia had a high cover, which is in gree- ment with the notion that both species form distinct patches. Oppositely, at sites where both species have a low cover, we found that both the expected and observed covari-ance were positive. The proposed measure for the expected covariance of two species does capture information on the combined spatial conﬁguration of the two species if the species are common. We show how this may be relevant for understanding the underlying ecological processes leading to the observed covariance.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Damgaard, Christian","Ehlers, Bodil","Ransijn, Johannes C. G.","Schmidt, Inger Kappel","Svenning, Jens Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024087"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NAK Services"],"keyword":["Covariance","Ecological processes","Faculty of Science","Spatial dynamics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insights on plant interaction between dominating species from patterns of plant association expected covariance of pin point cover measurements of two species","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85045067088","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024087","identifier":[{"id":"85045067088","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9c89b90b-c300-42fd-9e50-bf4d3151947f","ku-3af735da-8e79-40f7-80e3-9596d75053d2"],"keyword":["Covariance","Covariance · Distribution of plant abundance · Ecological processes ·","Distribution of plant abundance","Ecological processes","Faculty of Science","Pin-point cover","Plant associations","Spatial dynamics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-11852847057ED456A606A8ADC69EE873"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"nak services","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"NAK Services","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Frølund","key":"damgaardpau","last":"Damgaard","locid":"719d46aa-2846-41c9-9b1e-fd5278eaa711","name":"Damgaard, Christian","name_org":"Damgaard, Christian Frølund","orcid":"0000-0003-3932-4312","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil","key":"ehlerspau","last":"Ehlers","locid":"2e03906c-567b-4530-9627-83864bdf84b7","name":"Ehlers, Bodil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes C. G.","key":"ransijnpau","last":"Ransijn","name":"Ransijn, Johannes C. G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Inger Kappel","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Inger Kappel","orcid":"0000-0003-3880-2060","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens-Christian","key":"svenningpau","last":"Svenning","locid":"33c3c4e2-57ab-478c-889d-06c594e57b8b","name":"Svenning, Jens Christian","name_org":"Svenning, Jens-Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-3415-0862","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10651-018-0400-z","issn":["13528505","15733009"],"issn_org":["13528505"],"issue":"2","journal":"Environmental and Ecological Statistics","pages":"221-235","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Environmental and Ecological Statistics","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045067088"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9c89b90b-c300-42fd-9e50-bf4d3151947f","ku-3af735da-8e79-40f7-80e3-9596d75053d2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Insights on plant interaction between dominating species from patterns of plant association: expected covariance of pin-point cover measurements of two species","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024087","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Histamine H2 receptor activation promotes cardiac fibrosis and apoptosis in mice. However, the potential effectiveness of histamine H2 receptor antagonists (H2RAs) in humans with heart failure is largely unknown. We examined the association between H2RA initiation and all-cause mortality among patients with heart failure. Methods: Using Danish medical registries, we conducted a nationwide population-based active-comparator cohort study of new users of H2RAs and proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) after first-time hospitalization for heart failure during the period 1995-2014. Hazard ratios (HRs) for all-cause mortality and hospitalization due to worsening of heart failure, adjusting for age, sex, and time between heart failure diagnosis and initiation of PPI or H2RA therapy, index year, comorbidity, cardiac surgery, comedications, and socioeconomic status were computed based on Cox regression analysis. Results: Our analysis included 42,902 PPI initiators (median age 78 years, 46% female) and 3,296 H2RA initiators (median age 76 years, 48% female). Mortality risk was lower among H2RA initiators than PPI initiators after 1 year (26% vs 31%) and 5 years (60% vs 66%). In multivariable analyses, the 1-year HR was 0.80 (95% CI, 0.74-0.86) and the 5-year HR was 0.85 (95% CI, 0.80-0.89). These findings were consistent after propensity score matching and for ischemic and nonischemic heart failure, as for sex and age groups. The rate of hospitalization due to worsening of heart failure was lower among H2RA initiators than PPI initiators. Conclusion: In patients with heart failure, H2RA initiation was associated with 15%-20% lower mortality than PPI initiation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Adelborg, Kasper","Sundbøll, Jens","Schmidt, Morten","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Weiss, Noel S","Pedersen, Lars","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-222566"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Heart failure","Mortality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of histamine h receptor antagonists and outcomes in patients with heart failure a nationwide population based cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85047734848","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-222566","identifier":[{"id":"85047734848","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5944448","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29765253","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a3a88b0a-228d-49b5-b3b2-760cc69bb9c3"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Heart failure","Histamine H receptor","Mortality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-064D4D6A577B0102D5E76087063AA05D"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of washington","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Washington","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"adelborgpau","last":"Adelborg","locid":"2744cdbf-8516-46f6-ad71-f99fee1afaa0","name":"Adelborg, Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Noel S","key":"weisspau","last":"Weiss","name":"Weiss, Noel S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29765253"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s162909","issn":["11791349"],"journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"521-530","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","title_org":"Clinical epidemiology","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047734848"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a3a88b0a-228d-49b5-b3b2-760cc69bb9c3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Use of histamine H receptor antagonists and outcomes in patients with heart failure : a nationwide population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-222566","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Increased risk of dementia after myocardial infarction (MI) may be mediated by shared risk factors (eg, atherosclerosis) and post-MI stroke. We examined risk of dementia in 1-year survivors of MI. Methods: Using Danish medical registries, we conducted a nationwide population-based cohort study of all patients with first-time MI and a sex-, birth year-, and calendar year-matched general population comparison cohort without MI (1980-2012). Cox regression analysis was used to compute 1-to 35-year adjusted hazard ratios (aHRs) for dementia, controlled for matching factors and adjusted for comorbidities and socioeconomic status. Results: We identified 314 911 patients with MI and 1 573 193 matched comparison cohort members randomly sampled from the general population (median age, 70 years; 63% male). After 35 years of follow-up, the cumulative incidence of all-cause dementia in the MI cohort was 9% (2.8% for Alzheimer disease, 1.6% for vascular dementia, and 4.5% for other dementias). Compared with the general population cohort, MI was not associated with all-cause dementia (aHR, 1.01; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.98-1.03). Risk of Alzheimer disease (aHR, 0.92; 95% CI, 0.88-0.95) and other dementias (aHR, 0.98; 95% CI, 0.95-1.01) also approximated unity. However, MI was associated with higher risk of vascular dementia (aHR, 1.35; 95% CI, 1.28-1.43), which was substantially strengthened for patients experiencing stroke after MI (aHR, 4.48; 95% CI, 3.29-6.12). Conclusions: MI was associated with higher risk of vascular dementia throughout follow-up, and this association was stronger in patients with stroke. The risk of Alzheimer disease and other dementias was not higher in patients with MI.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sundbøll, Jens","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Adelborg, Kasper","Schmidt, Morten","Pedersen, Lars","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Henderson, Victor W","Sørensen, Henrik T"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-231020"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"higher risk of vascular dementia in myocardial infarction survivors","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85048409281","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-231020","identifier":[{"id":"85048409281","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29025764","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b23a28d0-9225-4a76-b67d-1e0b3d3a98e9"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-008AE0924F48214EFF2B6101E6EA9B4C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erzsébet","key":"hováthpuhópau","last":"Hováth-Puhó","locid":"20f5c6bd-6ac1-4edb-a393-f34d60db546c","name":"Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","name_org":"Hováth-Puhó, Erzsébet","orcid":"0000-0002-3594-2212","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"adelborgpau","last":"Adelborg","locid":"2744cdbf-8516-46f6-ad71-f99fee1afaa0","name":"Adelborg, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Victor W","key":"hendersonpau","last":"Henderson","name":"Henderson, Victor W","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik T","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"600941c8-6dec-4ee2-b745-3e759dcd7c35","name":"Sørensen, Henrik T","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29025764"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circulationaha.117.029127","issn":["00097322","15244539"],"issn_org":["00097322"],"issue":"4","journal":"Circulation","pages":"567-577","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Circulation","volume":"137"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048409281"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b23a28d0-9225-4a76-b67d-1e0b3d3a98e9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Higher Risk of Vascular Dementia in Myocardial Infarction Survivors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-231020","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Microbial life inhabiting subseafloor sediments plays an important role in Earth’s carbon cycle. However, the impact of geodynamic processes on the distributions and carbon-cycling activities of subseafloor life remains poorly constrained. We explore a submarine mud volcano of the Nankai accretionary complex by drilling down to 200 m below the summit. Stable isotopic compositions of water and carbon compounds, including clumped methane isotopologues, suggest that ~90% of methane is microbially produced at 16° to 30°C and 300 to 900 m below seafloor, corresponding to the basin bottom, where fluids in the accretionary prism are supplied via megasplay faults. Radiotracer experiments showed that relatively small microbial populations in deep mud volcano sediments (10 2 to 10 3 cells cm −3) include highly active hydrogenotrophic methanogens and acetogens. Our findings indicate that subduction-associated fluid migration has stimulated microbial activity in the mud reservoir and that mud volcanoes may contribute more substantially to the methane budget than previously estimated.","author_count":41,"contributors":["Ijiri, Akira","Inagaki, Fumio","Kubo, Yusuke","Adhikari, Rishi R.","Hattori, Shohei","Hoshino, Tatsuhiko","Imachi, Hiroyuki","Kawagucci, Shinsuke","Morono, Yuki","Ohtomo, Yoko","Ono, Shuhei","Sakai, Sanae","Takai, Ken","Toki, Tomohiro","Wang, David T.","Yoshinaga, Marcos Y.","Arnold, Gail Lee","Ashi, Juichiro","Case, David H.","Feseker, Tomas","Hinrichs, Kai-Uwe","Ikegawa, Yojiro","Ikehara, Minoru","Kallmeyer, Jens","Kumagai, Hidenori","Lever, Mark","Morita, Sumito","Nakamura, Ko-ichi","Nakamura, Yuki","Nishizawa, Manabu","Orphan, Victoria J.","Røy, Hans","Schmidt, Frauke","Tani, Atsushi","Tanikawa, Wataru","Terada, Takeshi","Tomaru, Hitoshi","Tsuji, Takeshi","Tsunogai, Urumu","Yamaguchi, Yasuhiko T.","Yoshida, Naohiro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-250127"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_siz