id":"8288d58c-4602-4c0c-9b76-949cc83d281b","name":"Nyengaard, Jens Randel","name_org":"Nyengaard, J R","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"landaypau","last":"Landay","name":"Landay, A","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"O S","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"1939f653-c3a3-482e-a947-b1a7501b3986","name":"Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","name_org":"Søgaard, O S","orcid":"0000-0001-9107-2023","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"S K","key":"pillaipau","last":"Pillai","name":"Pillai, S K","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M","key":"tolstruppau","last":"Tolstrup","locid":"36e9f1d5-608c-46b7-8d41-2505c02086fc","name":"Tolstrup, Martin","name_org":"Tolstrup, M","orcid":"0000-0001-7020-5173","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P W","key":"dentonpau","last":"Denton","locid":"3d7dbf0b-7b11-4d73-b45c-c166c830714c","name":"Denton, Paul W","name_org":"Denton, P W","orcid":"0000-0003-2458-8147","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28766555"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/mi.2017.59","issn":["19330219","19353456"],"issn_org":["19330219"],"issue":"2","journal":"Mucosal Immunology","pages":"449-461","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Mucosal Immunology","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046098289"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-913564ab-6f1f-42d1-a78e-d0dcddbd7179","ku-f9478202-b414-4435-b1b3-d52c58cad2d2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The TLR9 agonist MGN1703 triggers a potent type I interferon response in the sigmoid colon","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-023268","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In Denmark and other countries, there has been a shift in the management of patients with an implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD) with remote device monitoring largely replacing in-hospital visits. Less patient-nurse and patient-physician interaction may lead to gaps in patients' quality of care and impede patients' adaptation to living successfully with the ICD. A comprehensive eHealth intervention that include goal-setting, monitoring of symptoms of depression, anxiety, and quality of life, psychological treatment, information provision, supportive tools, online dialogues with nursing staff and access to an online community network, may help fill these gaps and be particularly beneficial to patients who suffer from anxiety and depression. This study will evaluate the effectiveness of the ACQUIRE-ICD care innovation, a comprehensive and interactive eHealth intervention, on patient-reported and clinical outcomes. METHODS: The ACQUIRE-ICD study is a multicenter, prospective, two-arm, unblinded randomised controlled superiority trial that will enroll 478 patients implanted with a first-time ICD or ICD with cardiac synchronisation therapy (CRT-D) from the six implanting centers in Denmark. The trial will evaluate the clinical effectiveness and cost-effectiveness of the ACQUIRE-ICD care innovation, as add-on to usual care compared with usual care alone. The primary endpoint, device acceptance, assessed with the Florida Patient Acceptance Survey, is evaluated at 12 months' post implant. Secondary endpoints, evaluated at 12 and 24 months' post implant, include patient-reported outcomes, return to work, time to first ICD therapy and first hospitalisation, mortality and cost-effectiveness. DISCUSSION: The effectiveness of a comprehensive and interactive eHealth intervention that relies on patient-centred and personalised tools offered via a web-based platform targeted to patients with an ICD has not been assessed so far. The ACQUIRE-ICD care innovation promotes and facilitates that patients become active participants in the management of their disease, and as such addresses the need for a more patient-centered disease-management approach. If the care innovation proves to be beneficial to patients, it may not only increase patient empowerment and quality of life but also free up time for clinicians to care for more patients. TRIAL REGISTRATION: The trial has been registered on https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT02976961 on November 30, 2016 with registration number [ NCT02976961 ].","author_count":15,"contributors":["Pedersen, Susanne S","Skovbakke, Søren J","Wiil, Uffe K","Schmidt, Thomas","dePont Christensen, Rene","Brandt, Carl J","Sørensen, Jan","Vinther, Michael","Larroudé, Charlotte E","Melchior, Thomas M","Riahi, Sam","Smolderen, Kim G E","Spertus, John A","Johansen, Jens B","Nielsen, Jens C"],"cuid":["S03-099.06-011439"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Missouri at Kansas City","University of Missouri-Kansas City"],"keyword":["Anxiety","Depression","Device acceptance","EHealth intervention","Heart disease","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Patient centered tools","Quality of Life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Research Unit of General Practice, Odense, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness of a comprehensive interactive ehealth intervention on patient reported and clinical outcomes in patients with an implantable cardioverter defibrillator acquire icd trial study protocol of a national danish randomised controlled trial","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12872-018-0872-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.06-011439","identifier":[{"id":"85049430753","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6029360","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29969990","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-ef74533f-1511-4c00-983d-aac9521733f1","au-a54d112b-5534-47a3-9cc9-7b172de32be0","sdu-0cfe88c2-2550-4ed4-b86f-f3453f6bfce9"],"keyword":["Anxiety","Depression","Device acceptance","EHealth intervention","Heart disease","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Patient-centered tools","Quality of life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-268D7C1982B298E0371E9293B474BCAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12872-018-0872-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/283278123/Effectiveness_of_a_comprehensive_interactive_eHealth_intervention_on_patient_reported_and_clinical_outcomes_in_patients_with_an_implantable_cardioverter_defibrillator.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/143266491/Effectiveness_of_a_comprehensive.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department 