 in Sports","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine and Science in Sports","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051703291"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f0804547-9d84-49d7-9e91-d1175fb2666d","ku-2de3a492-1dae-4dc2-9a90-449c1ebf54a8","nfa-364ee736-12b8-4ff3-a155-3812f8bd31b2","sdu-6f9a90e7-0f42-4ee9-a9f9-223733c48565"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The “Football is Medicine” platform—scientific evidence, large-scale implementation of evidence-based concepts and future perspectives","type":"Editorial","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-097.29-785240","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Ebola (EBOV) and Zika viruses (ZIKV) are responsible for recent global health threats. As no preventive vaccines or antiviral drugs against these two re-emerging pathogens are available, we evaluated whether the molecular tweezer CLR01 may inhibit EBOV and ZIKV infection. This small molecule has previously been shown to inactivate HIV-1 and herpes viruses through a selective interaction with lipid-raft-rich regions in the viral envelope, which results in membrane disruption and loss of infectivity. We found that CLR01 indeed blocked infection of EBOV and ZIKV in a dose-dependent manner. The tweezer inhibited infection of epidemic ZIKV strains in cells derived from the anogenital tract and the central nervous system, and remained antivirally active in the presence of semen, saliva, urine and cerebrospinal fluid. Our findings show that CLR01 is a broad-spectrum inhibitor of enveloped viruses with prospects as a preventative microbicide or antiviral agent.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Röcker, Annika E.","Müller, Janis A.","Dietzel, Erik","Harms, Mirja","Krüger, Franziska","Heid, Christian","Sowislok, Andrea","Riber, Camilla Frich","Kupke, Alexandra","Lippold, Sina","von Einem, Jens","Beer, Judith","Knöll, Bernd","Becker, Stephan","Schmidt-Charnasit, Jonas","Otto, Markus","Vapalahti, Olli","Zelikin, Alexander N.","Bitan, Gal","Schrader, Thomas","Münch, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-231848"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine","Ulm University","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Helsinki","University of Marburg"],"keyword":["Ebola virus","Lipid rafts","Virus inactivation","Zika virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the molecular tweezer clr000000000001 inhibits ebola and zika virus infection","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85042057717","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-231848","identifier":[{"id":"85042057717","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29428508","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b3a7cd84-89b8-4080-9b65-52143dca9b72"],"keyword":["Broadly active antiviral agents","Ebola virus","Lipid rafts","Virus inactivation","Zika virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A62A440725C7B3D0EE53578AEA610B1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ulm university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ulm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of marburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Marburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of duisburg essen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Duisburg-Essen","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"bernhard nocht institute for tropical medicine","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","use