orgaard","name":"Norgaard, K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15209156","15578593"],"issn_org":["15209156"],"journal":"Diabetes Technology & Therapeutics","paperid":"072","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Technology & Therapeutics","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-58021d63-3413-4f23-8ebb-22b5216233e9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MODERATE EXERCISE DOES NOT IMPAIR THE EFFECT OF GLUCAGON IN INSULIN PUMP TREATED INDIVIDUALS WITH TYPE 1 DIABETES: A RANDOMIZED CROSSOVER STUDY : [Meeting Abstract}","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446059","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"From a labor market perspective concerning a balanced development in Denmark, this chapter proposes an answer to the question: Does migration and commuting to rural areas strengthen employment in Danish rural municipalities? Based on register data from 2006 to 2011, the chapter offers insights into whether migration and commuting to a rural municipality is one instrument to strengthen rural municipalities that would otherwise see weaknesses in development of employment. This is based on upstream and downstream links in local production processes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schmidt, Torben Dall"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-575030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kan beskæftigelsen i de danske landdistrikter styrkes ved tilflyttere og pendlere til kommuner på landet","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.universitypress.dk/shop/vaekst-og-vilkaar-3691p.html","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-575030","ids":["sdu-0669b985-4b93-4899-be4c-9293edea1409"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E0D19A9A3FCFC077280052E28DF7030D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Economics","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Economics, Econometrics and Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Dall","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"ec808865-a087-40bc-95b4-443ffae4b2e1","name":"Schmidt, Torben Dall","orcid":"0000-0002-7662-1669","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunnar L.H.","key":"svendsenpedh","last":"Svendsen","name":"Svendsen, Gunnar L.H.","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens F.L.","key":"sørensenpedh","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Jens F.L.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Egon B.","key":"noepedh","last":"Noe","name":"Noe, Egon B.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788740831559"],"issn":["16025962"],"pages":"131-140","place":"Odense","publisher":"Syddansk Universitetsforlag","series":"University of Southern Denmark Studies in History and Social Sciences","status":"p","subtitle":"Viden, visioner og virkemidler","title":"Vækst og vilkår på landet"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0669b985-4b93-4899-be4c-9293edea1409"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Kan beskæftigelsen i de danske landdistrikter styrkes ved tilflyttere og pendlere til kommuner på landet?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-575030","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aims T he EuroMyositis Registry facilitates collaboration across the idiopathic inflammatory myopathy (IIM) research community. This inaugural report examines pooled Registry data. Methods Cross-sectional analysis of IIM cases from 11 countries was performed. Associations between clinical subtypes, extramuscular involvement, environmental exposures and medications were investigated. Results O f 3067 IIM cases, 69% were female. The most common IIM subtype was dermatomyositis (DM) (31%). Smoking was more frequent in connective tissue disease overlap cases (45%, OR 1.44, 95% CI 1.09 to 1.90, p=0.012). Smoking was associated with interstitial lung disease (ILD) (OR 1.32, 95% CI 1.06 to 1.65, p=0.013), dysphagia (OR 1.43, 95% CI 1.16 to 1.77, p=0.001), malignancy ever (OR 1.78, 95% CI 1.36 to 2.33, p<0.001) and cardiac involvement (OR 2.40, 95% CI 1.60 to 3.60, p<0.001). D ysphagia occurred in 39% and cardiac involvement in 9%; either occurrence was associated with higher Health Assessment Questionnaire (HAQ) scores (adjusted OR 1.79, 95% CI 1.43 to 2.23, p<0.001). HAQ scores were also higher in inclusion body myositis cases (adjusted OR 3.85, 95% CI 2.52 to 5.90, p<0.001). Malignancy (ever) occurred in 13%, most commonly in DM (20%, OR 2.06, 95% CI 1.65 to 2.57, p<0.001). ILD occurred in 30%, most frequently in antisynthetase syndrome (71%, OR 10.7, 95% CI 8.6 to 13.4, p<0.001). Rash characteristics differed between adult-onset and juvenile-onset DM cases ('V' sign: 56% D M vs 16% juvenile-DM, OR 0.16, 95% CI 0.07 to 0.36, p<0.001). Glucocorticoids were used in 98% of cases, methotrexate in 71% and azathioprine in 51%. Conclusion T his large multicentre cohort demonstrates the importance of extramuscular involvement in patients with IIM, its association with smoking and its influence on disease severity. Our findings emphasise that IIM is a multisystem inflammatory disease and will help inform prognosis and clinical management of patients.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Lilleker, James B","Vencovsky, Jiri","Wang, Guochun","Wedderburn, Lucy R","Diederichsen, Louise C. Pyndt Raun","Schmidt, Jens","Oakley, Paula","Benveniste, Olivier","Danieli, Maria Giovanna","Danko, Katalin","Thuy, Nguyen Thi Phuong","Vazquez-Del Mercado, Monica","Andersson, Helena","De Paepe, Boel","deBleecker, Jan L","Maurer, Britta","McCann, Liza J","Pipitone, Nicolo","McHugh, Neil","Betteridge, Zoe E","New, Paul","Cooper, Robert G","Ollier, William E","Lamb, Janine A","Krogh, Niels Steen","Lundberg, Ingrid E","Chinoy, Hector"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586748"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["all EuroMyositis contributors"],"country":["Belgium","China","Czechia","France","Germany","Hungary","Italy","Mexico","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Alder Hey Children's Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Arcispedale Santa Maria Nuova","Charles University","China-Japan Friendship Hospital","Department of Genetic Medicine, Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, Manchester, United Kingdom.","Ghent University Hospital","Karolinska Institute","Manchester Academic Health Science Centre","Oslo University Hospital","Pitié-Salpêtrière University Hospital","Royal National Hospital for Rheumatic Diseases","Salford Royal NHS Foundation Trust","University College London","University Hospital Zurich","University Medical Center Göttingen","University of Bath","University of Debrecen","University of Guadalajara","University of Liverpool","University of Manchester"],"keyword":["Biomedical Research methods","Cohort Studies","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Health Status","Humans","International Cooperation","Male","Prognosis","Registries statistics numerical data","Severity of Illness Index","Smoking adverse effects","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra"