{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Gender, possibly due to the influence of gonadal hormones, is presumed to play a role in the pathogenesis of multiple sclerosis (MS), but no studies have evaluated whether male infertility is associated with MS. OBJECTIVE: To study the association between male factor infertility and prevalent as well as incident MS. METHOD: Our cohort was established by linkage of the Danish National in vitro fertilization (IVF) registry to The Danish Multiple Sclerosis Registry and consisted of 51,063 men whose partners had undergone fertility treatment in all public and private fertility clinics in Denmark between 1994 and 2015. RESULTS: With a median age of 34 years at baseline, 24,011 men were diagnosed with male factor infertility and 27,052 did not have male factor infertility and made up the reference group. Men diagnosed with male factor infertility had a higher risk of prevalent (odds ratio (OR) = 1.61, 95% confidence interval (95% CI) 1.04-2.51) and incident MS (hazard ratio (HR) = 1.28, 95% CI 0.76-2.17) when compared to the reference group. CONCLUSION: This nationwide cohort study has shown, for the first time, an association between male infertility and MS which may be due to underlying common etiologies such as hypogonadism, shared genetics, or a joint autoimmune component.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Glazer, Clara Helene","Tøttenborg, Sandra Søgaard","Giwercman, Aleksander","Bräuner, Elvira Vaclavik","Eisenberg, Michael L","Vassard, Ditte","Magyari, Melinda","Pinborg, Anja","Schmidt, Lone","Bonde, Jens Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411173"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Fertility","Gender","Journal Article","Male infertility","Multiple sclerosis","Semen quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Mental Health Center Ballerup, Capital Region of Denmark, Center for Eating Disorders, Research Unit, Ballerup, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"male factor infertility and risk of multiple sclerosis a register based cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-411173","identifier":[{"id":"85043306664","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29027840","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1dcf5e23-aa82-4260-9f9f-bb962696d6f4"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Male infertility","epidemiology","fertility","gender","multiple sclerosis","semen quality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0713FAA6F90B67ACC65DF0AABEF161A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Mental Health Center Ballerup, Capital Region of Denmark, Center for Eating Disorders, Research Unit, Ballerup, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Clara Helene","key":"glazerpau","last":"Glazer","name":"Glazer, Clara Helene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sandra Søgaard","key":"tøttenborgpau","last":"Tøttenborg","name":"Tøttenborg, Sandra Søgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Aleksander","key":"giwercmanpau","last":"Giwercman","name":"Giwercman, Aleksander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Elvira Vaclavik","key":"bräunerpau","last":"Bräuner","name":"Bräuner, Elvira Vaclavik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Michael L","key":"eisenbergpau","last":"Eisenberg","name":"Eisenberg, Michael L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Ditte","key":"vassardpau","last":"Vassard","locid":"82a74f62-e1bb-44e5-a099-94605ee1f584","name":"Vassard, Ditte","orcid":"0000-0001-6298-4146","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 1","first":"Melinda","key":"magyaripau","last":"Magyari","locid":"1efd2abb-1b20-49bb-a6c6-f3dc13b48021","name":"Magyari, Melinda","orcid":"0000-0002-0972-5222","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Anja","key":"pinborgpau","last":"Pinborg","locid":"28eb0e05-b8d4-4063-9350-54ae5d522ed4","name":"Pinborg, Anja","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Lone","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"5f2dcc97-1887-47eb-8a0a-662e840273df","name":"Schmidt, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-9518-1734","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Jens Peter","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","locid":"51baf59f-51c4-4a3a-ad40-ada6edcac800","name":"Bonde, Jens Peter","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29027840"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1352458517734069","issn":["13524585","14770970"],"issn_org":["13524585"],"issue":"14","journal":"Multiple Sclerosis Journal","pages":"1835-1842","status":"p","title":"Multiple Sclerosis Journal","title_org":"Multiple Sclerosis","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043306664"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1dcf5e23-aa82-4260-9f9f-bb962696d6f4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Male factor infertility and risk of multiple sclerosis : A register-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-411173","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In order to introduce bone tissue engineering to the field of oncological reconstruction, we are investigating for the first time the effect of various doses of ionizing irradiation on axially vascularized bone constructs. Synthetic bone constructs were created and implanted in 32 Lewis rats. Each construct was axially vascularized through an arteriovenous loop made by direct anastomosis of the saphenous vessels. After 2 weeks, the animals received ionizing irradiation of 9 Gy, 12 Gy and 15 Gy, and were accordingly classified to groups I, II and III, respectively. Group IV was not irradiated and acted as a control. Tissue generation, vascularity, cellular proliferation and apoptosis were investigated either 2 or 5 weeks after irradiation through micro-computed tomography, histomorphometry and real-time polymerase chain reaction (PCR). At 2 weeks after irradiation, tissue generation and central vascularity were significantly lower and apoptosis was significantly higher in groups II and III than group IV, but without signs of necrosis. Cellular proliferation was significantly lower in groups I and II. After 5 weeks, the irradiated groups showed improvement in all parameters in relation to the control group, indicating a retained capacity for angiogenesis after irradiation. PCR results confirmed the expression of osteogenesis-related genes in all irradiated groups. Dense collagen was detected 5 weeks after irradiation, and one construct showed discrete islands of bone indicating a retained osteogenic capacity after irradiation. This demonstrates for the first time that axial vascularization was capable of supporting a synthetic bone construct after a high dose of irradiation that is comparable to adjuvant radiotherapy. Copyright © 2016 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Eweida, Ahmad","Frisch, Oliver","Giordano, Frank A","Fleckenstein, Jens","Wenz, Frederik","Brockmann, Marc A","Schulte, Matthias","Schmidt, Volker J","Kneser, Ulrich","Harhaus, Leila"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470446"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Clinical Neurobiology/A230, Heidelberg University Hospital at DKFZ, Im Neuenheimer Feld 280, 69120 Heidelberg, Germany. k.khodosevich@dkfz-heidelberg.de","Heidelberg University "],"keyword":["Animals","Bone Marrow diagnostic imaging","Bone and Bones blood supply","Cell Proliferation radiation effects","Dose Response Relationship Radiation","Gene Expression Regulation radiation effects","Implants Experimental","Male","Neovascularization Physiologic","Rats Inbred Lew","Tissue Engineering methods","Tissue Scaffolds chemistry","X Ray Microtomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"axially vascularized tissue engineered bone constructs retain their in vivo angiogenic and osteogenic capacity after high dose irradiation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-470446","identifier":[{"id":"85016436577","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27696709","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-80a38fc0-b7d5-464b-83e4-632c8472dbe3"],"keyword":["Animals","Apoptosis/radiation effects","Bone Marrow/diagnostic imaging","Bone and Bones/blood supply","Cell Proliferation/radiation effects","Dose-Response Relationship, Radiation","Gene Expression Regulation/radiation effects","Implants, Experimental","Male","Neovascularization, Physiologic","Osteogenesis/radiation effects","Rats, Inbred Lew","Tissue Engineering/methods","Tissue Scaffolds/chemistry","X-Ray Microtomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8B77B264B055A3F1D746814A20BBE571"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"department of clinical neurobiology a230 heidelberg university hospital at dkfz im neuenheimer feld 280 69120 heidelberg germany k khodosevich dkfz heidelberg de","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Department of Clinical Neurobiology/A230, Heidelberg University Hospital at DKFZ, Im Neuenheimer Feld 280, 69120 Heidelberg, Germany. k.khodosevich@dkfz-heidelberg.de","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Plastic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"heidelberg university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Heidelberg University ","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmad","key":"eweidapau","last":"Eweida","name":"Eweida, Ahmad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Oliver","key":"frischpau","last":"Frisch","name":"Frisch, Oliver","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frank A","key":"giordanopau","last":"Giordano","name":"Giordano, Frank A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"fleckensteinpau","last":"Fleckenstein","name":"Fleckenstein, Jens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik","key":"wenzpau","last":"Wenz","name":"Wenz, Frederik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marc A","key":"brockmannpau","last":"Brockmann","name":"Brockmann, Marc A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, Matthias","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Volker J","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","l