{"abstract":"The students’ activities during their final thesis work have been organised in project families, i.e. a group of individual student project organized in a shared learning environment. The aim is more efficient supervision and support, simultaneously to improved learning. DTU Byg have now tested this concept for 100+ students with experimental activities and found a major improvement in their learning, grades, interaction and behaviour in the laboratories, just as they now provides a strong support for the supervisors’ research. The use of resources for the supervision and the support in the laboratories has also been significantly reduced.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Goltermann, Per","Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Nielsen, Jens Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-306972"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-23","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2017-08-20","title":"XXIII Symposium on Nordic Concrete Research &amp; Development","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Knowledge and Teaching","Testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"project families a new concept for student thesis activities","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131105620/Project_families_Per_Goltermann_et_al_020417_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-306972","ids":["dtu-07fd1c83-2a72-4c8a-a81c-ffc102727325"],"keyword":["Knowledge and Teaching","Testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9DE252846AF0C733A9F217C2C3DCF284"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131105620/Project_families_Per_Goltermann_et_al_020417_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Section for Structural Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"goltermannpau","last":"Goltermann","locid":"c5c0abe9-e221-4cac-96aa-2d7cd40039d9","name":"Goltermann, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-6821-3115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lisbeth M.","key":"ottosenpau","last":"Ottosen","locid":"653cfe69-d98d-42ec-b241-5409bbfc951c","name":"Ottosen, Lisbeth M.","orcid":"0000-0001-7756-382X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"2a187e49-ed7b-44eb-a0d4-f9d00cc245ce","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1153cf58-bb0e-42da-a4d0-1ea0dd13b752","name":"Nielsen, Jens Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0705-9382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"4","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the XXIII Nordic Concrete Research Symposium"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-07fd1c83-2a72-4c8a-a81c-ffc102727325"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Project families: A new concept for student thesis activities","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-306972","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: This study compared the ability of glucagon to restore plasma glucose (PG) after mild hypoglycemia in patients with type 1 diabetes on an isocaloric high-carbohydrate diet (HCD) versus a low-carbohydrate diet (LCD). RESEARCH DESIGN AND METHODS: Ten patients with insulin pump-treated type 1 diabetes randomly completed 1 week of the HCD (≥250 g/day) and 1 week of the LCD (≤50 g/day). After each week, mild hypoglycemia was induced by a subcutaneous insulin bolus in the fasting state. When PG reached 3.9 mmol/L, 100 µg glucagon was given subcutaneously, followed by 500 µg glucagon 2 h later. RESULTS: Compared with the HCD, the LCD resulted in lower incremental rises in PG after the first (mean ± SEM: 1.3 ± 0.3 vs. 2.7 ± 0.4 mmol/L, P = 0.002) and second glucagon bolus (4.1 ± 0.2 vs. 5.6 ± 0.5 mmol/L, P = 0.002). No differences were observed between the diets regarding concentrations of insulin, glucagon, and triglycerides. CONCLUSIONS: The LCD reduces the treatment effect of glucagon on mild hypoglycemia. Carbohydrate intake should be considered when low-dose glucagon is used to correct hypoglycemia.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ranjan, Ajenthen","Schmidt, Signe","Damm-Frydenberg, Camilla","Steineck, Isabelle","Clausen, Trine Ryberg","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Nørgaard, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416286"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low carbohydrate diet impairs the effect of glucagon in the treatment of insulin induced mild hypoglycemia a randomized crossover study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-416286","identifier":[{"id":"27797928","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85008219837","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-263af720-1c98-4b92-808f-a73200b84a65"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3721F2A09986D327A4D912A8437602C9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ajenthen","key":"ranjanpau","last":"Ranjan","name":"Ranjan, Ajenthen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Signe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla","key":"dammfrydenbergpau","last":"Damm-Frydenberg","name":"Damm-Frydenberg, Camilla","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Isabelle","key":"steineckpau","last":"Steineck","name":"Steineck, Isabelle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Trine Ryberg","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Trine Ryberg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27797928"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2337/dc16-1472","issn":["01495992"],"issn_org":["19355548"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diabetes Care","pages":"132-135","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Care","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85008219837"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-263af720-1c98-4b92-808f-a73200b84a65"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Low-Carbohydrate Diet Impairs the Effect of Glucagon in the Treatment of Insulin-Induced Mild Hypoglycemia : A Randomized Crossover Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-416286","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"STUDY QUESTION: Is male factor infertility associated with an increased risk of developing diabetes? SUMMARY ANSWER: The study provides evidence that male factor infertility may predict later occurrence of diabetes mellitus with the risk being related to the severity of the underlying fertility problem. WHAT IS KNOWN ALREADY: Previous cross-sectional studies have shown an increased prevalence of comorbidities among infertile men when compared to controls. STUDY DESIGN, SIZE, DURATION: In this prospective cohort study, 39 516 men who had since 1994 undergone fertility treatment with their female partner were identified from the Danish national IVF register, which includes data on assumed cause of couple infertility (male/female factor, mixed and unexplained infertility) and type of fertility treatment. With a median follow-up time of 5.6 years, each man was followed for diabetes occurrence from enrollment until 31 December 2012 using the National Diabetes Register (NDR). Men with a history of diabetes prior to their fertility diagnosis were excluded. Hazard ratios (HR) were estimated by Cox proportional hazard models with age as the underlying time scale. In addition to analyzing the data for the entire IVF registration period (1994-2012), separate analyses were performed for men identified from the first (1994-2005) and second (2006-2012) IVF registration period owing to heterogeneity in the reporting of male factor infertility in these two time periods, because the reason for male factor infertility was not available from the first register. PARTICIPANTS/MATERIALS, SETTING, METHODS: Male factor infertility was identified from the variable 'yes' or 'no' from the first IVF register and through a diagnosis code (e.g. oligospermia, azoospermia) from the second IVF register. The reference group was men with male factor infertility (='no') and those with normal semen quality or sterilized men. Of the included men, 18 499 (46.8%) had male factor infertility and 21 017 (53.2%) made up the reference group. MAIN RESULTS AND THE ROLE OF CHANCE: A total of 651 (1.6%) diabetes cases were identified during the follow-up period. The adjusted HR's for diabetes risk among men with male factor infertility when compared to the reference group were HR = 1.08 (95% CI: 0.89, 1.31) and HR = 1.45 (95% CI: 1.06, 1.97) for the first and second IVF registration period, respectively. When assessing the effects of individual causes of male factor infertility, the adjusted HR's for men with oligospermia, azoospermia and aspermia were HR = 1.44 (95% CI: 1.01, 2.06), HR = 2.10 (95% 1.25, 3.56) and HR = 3.20 (95% CI 1.00, 10.31), respectively. LIMITATIONS, REASONS FOR CAUTION: We found no increased risk among men identified from the first IVF register, which may be related to exposure misclassification as the reason for male factor infertility was not available from this time period. The NDR does not distinguish between type 1 and type 2 diabetes. WIDER IMPLICATIONS OF THE FINDINGS: These findings support previous studies that a man's reproductive and somatic health are closely intertwined and highlight the importance for further monitoring of these men. Further, implementation of diabetes screening may be especially relevant among aspermic and azoospermic men. STUDY FUNDING/COMPETING INTERESTS: This article is part of the ReproUnion collaborative study, co-financed by the European Union, Intereg V Öresund-Kattegat-Skagerrak. None of the authors declare any conflict of interest. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: None.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Glazer, Clara Helene","Bonde, Jens Peter","Giwercman, Aleksander","Vassard, Ditte","Pinborg, Anja","Schmidt, Lone","Bräuner, Elvira Vaclavik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-464010"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of diabetes according to male factor infertility a register based cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/humrep/dex097","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-464010","identifier":[{"id":"85021795036","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5850522","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28486688","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-75ff129a-e68e-42e8-a7b8-088176ab9f2a"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5AA1B8772ABE75BB77A66A3BB6406CFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/humrep/dex097","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/188787107/dex097.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Clara Helene","key":"glazerpau","last":"Glazer","name":"Glazer, Clara Helene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","locid":"51baf59f-51c4-4a3a-ad40-ada6edcac800","name":"Bonde, Jens Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Aleksander","key":"giwercmanpau","last":"Giwercman","name":"Giwercman, Aleksander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ditte","key":"vassardpau","last":"Vassard","locid":"82a74f62-e1bb-44e5-a099-94605ee1f584","name":"Vassard, Ditte","orcid":"0000-0001-6298-4146","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja","key":"pinborgpau","last":"Pinborg","locid":"28eb0e05-b8d4-4063-9350-54ae5d522ed4","name":"Pinborg, Anja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lone","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"5f2dcc97-1887-47eb-8a0a-662e840273df","name":"Schmidt, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-9518-1734","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elvira Vaclavik","key":"bräunerpau","last":"Bräuner","name":"Bräuner, Elvira Vaclavik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28486688"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/humrep/dex097","issn":["02681161","14602350"],"issn_org":["02681161"],"issue":"7","journal":"Human Reproduction","pages":"1474-1481","status":"p","title":"Human Reproduction","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021795036"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-75ff129a-e68e-42e8-a7b8-088176ab9f2a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of diabetes according to male factor infertility : a register-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-464010","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The intake of animal products in food has been associated with both the development of insulin resistance and gastrointestinal cancers (GIC). Through the digestion of animal protein and other constituents of animal products, the commensal bacteria in the gut (the gut microbiota) forms metabolites that can contribute to the development of both insulin resistance and cancer. Trimethylamine-N-Oxide (TMAO) is such a molecule and has recently drawn a lot of attention as it may be a risk factor for - and a link between - the gut microbiota and cardiovascular and renal disease. Further, TMAO is anticipated to have significance as a biomarker of - or even an independent risk factor for - other undesirable conditions, including insulin resistance and GIC. TMAO originates from a precursor, trimethylamine (TMA) that is a metabolite of various precursors; mainly choline and carnitine from ingested foods. METHODS: We review the literature on TMAO as a shared risk factor and/or pathway between insulin resistance and GIC risk and take the reader through the literature of interventions that could reduce formation of TMAO and thereby the risk of insulin resistance and GIC. The purpose of the work is to generate a hypothesis to be tested in preclinical and clinical studies. RESULTS: TMAO seems to be associated with both insulin resistance and GIC risk and also with atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease. One shared pathway is the formation of N-Nitroso compounds, a group of metabolites that can cause DNA-damage and epigenetic changes. Levels of TMAO can be reduced by limiting the dietary intake of certain foods, most importantly animal products. Further, certain drugs, namely Meldonium and 3,3-dimethyl- 1-butanol, may inhibit the formation of TMAO by inhibiting bacterial enzymes. CONCLUSIONS: The TMAO pathway and its metabolites are possibly involved in the development of two major health problems: insulin resistance and cancer. Within these pathways novel therapeutic targets may be identified. Further research is needed in order to verify existing or develop new pharmacological agents that modify these pathways and reduce the risk of insulin resistance and GIC.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Oellgaard, Jens","Winther, Signe Abitz","Hansen, Tobias Schmidt","Rossing, Peter","von Scholten, Bernt Johan"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-042729"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trimethylamine n oxide tmao as a new potential therapeutic target for insulin resistance and cancer","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85033407759","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-042729","identifier":[{"id":"85033407759","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28641532","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5c7c3775-0872-42cf-8c5c-6e83ef3aa458","sdu-4709794c-dc2d-4603-8127-8936e65097ee"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E5E35B0FA78840EB6150681A8BCF7660"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"oellgaardpau","last":"Oellgaard","locid":"1c16cc34-6848-4823-b93d-357f202928aa","name":"Oellgaard, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Abitz","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","name":"Winther, Signe Abitz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Schmidt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Tobias Schmidt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 2","first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","locid":"ca397e2f-e1b3-430b-a537-a047438b44b6","name":"Rossing, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-1531-4294","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernt Johan","key":"vonscholtenpau","last":"von Scholten","name":"von Scholten, Bernt Johan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28641532"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/1381612823666170622095324","issn":["13816128","18734286"],"issn_org":["13816128"],"issue":"25","journal":"Current Pharmaceutical Design","pages":"3699-3712","publisher":"Bentham Science Publishers","status":"p","title":"Current Pharmaceutical Design","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85033407759"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5c7c3775-0872-42cf-8c5c-6e83ef3aa458","sdu-4709794c-dc2d-4603-8127-8936e65097ee"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Trimethylamine N-oxide (TMAO) as a New Potential Therapeutic Target for Insulin Resistance and Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-042729","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The global, prospective AMPLATZER Amulet observational study documents real-world periprocedural, transoesophageal echocardiographic (TEE) and clinical outcomes from left atrial appendage occlusion (LAAO) using the AMPLATZER Amulet device. The aim of this report is to describe the periprocedural and early clinical/TEE results from this study. METHODS AND RESULTS: This multicentre prospective real-world registry included 1,088 patients (75±8.5 years, 64.5% male, CHA2DS2-VASc: 4.2±1.6, HAS-BLED: 3.3±1.1) with non-valvular atrial fibrillation; 82.8% of patients were considered to have an absolute or relative contraindication to long-term anticoagulation and 72.4% had had a previous major bleeding. Periprocedural results, clinical outcomes up to the first three months and the available TEE results from the first scheduled follow-up (one to three months post implant) are reported. Successful device implantation was achieved in 99.0% of patients. During the procedure and index hospitalisation, major adverse events occurred in 3.2% of patients. Patients were discharged on a single antiplatelet agent (23.0%), dual antiplatelets (54.3%) or an oral anticoagulant (18.9%). TEE follow-up 67±23 days post procedure in 673 patients showed adequate (<3 mm jet) occlusion of the appendage in 98.2% of patients and device thrombus in 10 patients (1.5%), as evaluated by core laboratory analysis. CONCLUSIONS: This large real-world prospective registry of catheter-based LAAO using the AMPLATZER Amulet device reports a high implant success rate and a low periprocedural complication rate in a population with a high risk of stroke and bleeding. Transoesophageal echo data confirm good closure rates during follow-up and low rates of device-associated thrombus.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Landmesser, Ulf","Schmidt, Boris","Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","Lam, Cheung Chi Simon","Park, Jai-Wun","Tarantini, Giuseppe","Cruz-Gonzalez, Ignacio","Geist, Volker","della Bella, Paolo","Colombo, Antonio","Zeus, Tobias","Omran, Heyder","Piorkowski, Christopher","Lund, Juha","Tondo, Claudio","Hildick-Smith, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-249374"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"left atrial appendage occlusion with the amplatzer amulet device periprocedural and early clinical echocardiographic data from a global prospective observational study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84997078152","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-249374","identifier":[{"id":"28649053","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84997078152","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d219ad59-02b0-4d64-9308-10cab7213843"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CCB15A76299BB5EB4EAD0765693ABA79"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité-Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulf","key":"landmesserpau","last":"Landmesser","name":"Landmesser, Ulf","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Boris","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Boris","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Erik","key":"nielsenkudskpau","last":"Nielsen-Kudsk","locid":"8629b763-e23e-41d9-ac4f-61579d19565e","name":"Nielsen-Kudsk, Jens Erik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cheung Chi Simon","key":"lampau","last":"Lam","name":"Lam, Cheung Chi Simon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jai-Wun","key":"parkpau","last":"Park","name":"Park, Jai-Wun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Giuseppe","key":"tarantinipau","last":"Tarantini","name":"Tarantini, Giuseppe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ignacio","key":"cruzgonzalezpau","last":"Cruz-Gonzalez","name":"Cruz-Gonzalez, Ignacio","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Volker","key":"geistpau","last":"Geist","name":"Geist, Volker","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"dellabellapau","last":"della Bella","name":"della Bella, Paolo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonio","key":"colombopau","last":"Colombo","name":"Colombo, Antonio","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"zeuspau","last":"Zeus","name":"Zeus, Tobias","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Heyder","key":"omranpau","last":"Omran","name":"Omran, Heyder","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"piorkowskipau","last":"Piorkowski","name":"Piorkowski, Christopher","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Juha","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Juha","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudio","key":"tondopau","last":"Tondo","name":"Tondo, Claudio","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"hildicksmithpau","last":"Hildick-Smith","name":"Hildick-Smith, David","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28649053"],"pub":{"doi":"10.4244/eij-d-17-00493","issn":["1774024X","19696213"],"issn_org":["1774024X"],"issue":"7","journal":"EuroIntervention","pages":"867-876","publisher":"Europa Group","status":"p","title":"EuroIntervention","title_org":"EuroIntervention : journal of EuroPCR in collaboration with the Working Group on Interventional Cardiology of the European Society of Cardiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030639297"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d219ad59-02b0-4d64-9308-10cab7213843"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Left atrial appendage occlusion with the AMPLATZER Amulet device : periprocedural and early clinical/echocardiographic data from a global prospective observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-249374","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We describe a new technique for the efficient generation of high-energy ions with electromagnetic ion cyclotron waves in multi-ion plasmas. The discussed three-ion scenarios are especially suited for strong wave absorption by a very low number of resonant ions. To observe this effect, the plasma composition has to be properly adjusted, as prescribed by theory. We demonstrate the potential of the method on the world-largest plasma magnetic confinement device, JET (Joint European Torus, Culham, UK), and the high-magnetic-field tokamak Alcator C-Mod (Cambridge, USA). The obtained results demonstrate efficient acceleration of 3He ions to high energies in dedicated hydrogendeuterium mixtures. Simultaneously, effective plasma heating is observed, as a result of the slowing-down of the fast He-3 ions. The developed technique is not only limited to laboratory plasmas, but can also be applied to explain observations of energetic ions in space-plasma environments, in particular, 3He-rich solar flares.","author_count":1275,"contributors":["Kazakov, Ye O.","Kiptily, V. G.","Lin, Y.","Nocente, M.","Baranov, Y.","Bilato, R.","Faustin, J. M.","Felton, R.","Jacquet, Ph","Van Schoor, M.","Marmar, E. S.","Baek, S. G.","Barnard, H.","Bonoli, P.","Brunner, D.","Dekow, G.","Ennever, P.","Faust, I.","Fiore, C.","Gao, Chi","Golfinopoulos, T.","Greenwald, M.","Hartwig, Z. S.","Hubbard, A. E.","Hughes, J. W.","Hutchinson, I. H.","Irby, J.","LaBombard, B.","Lin, Yijun","Mumgaard, R.","Parker, R. R.","Porkolab, M.","Rice, J. E.","Shiraiwa, S.","Sorbom, B.","Terry, D.","Terry, J. L.","Vieira, R.","Walk, J. R.","Wallace, G. M.","White, A.","Whyte, D.","Wolfe, S. M.","Wright, G. M.","Wukitch, S. J.","Xu, P.","Candy, J.","Snyder, P.","Canik, J.","Churchill, R. M.","Delgado-Aparicio, L.","Diallo, A.","Edlund, E.","Scott, S. D.","Cziegler, I.","Holland, C.","Lipschultz, B.","Reinke, M. L.","Loarte, A.","Theiler, C.","Asunta, O.","Groth, M.","Jarvinen, A.","Karhunen, J.","Koskela, T.","