{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Graversen, Ebbe Krogh","Lyngs, Allan Rye","Kalpazidou Schmidt, Evanthia","Ludvigsen, Jens Viuff","Nielsen, Maria Lehmann","Lauridsen, Per Stig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-199688"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uddannelsesledelse ved danske videregående uddannelsesinstitutioner studielederes rolle i uddannelsernes kvalitetsarbejde","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.qnhe.no/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Uddannelsesledelse-ved-danske-videreg%C3%A5ende-uddannelsesinstitutioner-2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-199688","ids":["au-7af5fe66-9c91-448c-b5aa-2634b87bf30f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D751686F6187ADC3D95B1EB40C7E31BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.qnhe.no/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/Uddannelsesledelse-ved-danske-videreg%C3%A5ende-uddannelsesinstitutioner-2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Political Science, Department of Political Science - Danish Centre for Studies in Research and Research Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ebbe Krogh","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","locid":"7ad5f98b-e0b1-48c6-a8f3-a9c413ea584f","name":"Graversen, Ebbe Krogh","orcid":"0000-0003-4009-2678","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan Rye","key":"lyngspau","last":"Lyngs","locid":"dc8e6304-b5c3-4dd5-b091-1057edc3c9f2","name":"Lyngs, Allan Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-8806-8875","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Evanthia","key":"kalpazidouschmidtpau","last":"Kalpazidou Schmidt","locid":"30cd8ce5-47fe-495b-a57f-03e9c5e5eae6","name":"Kalpazidou Schmidt, Evanthia","orcid":"0000-0002-3204-0803","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Viuff","key":"ludvigsenpau","last":"Ludvigsen","locid":"e42706ad-1abd-4f33-9ed0-c6a0a3a74820","name":"Ludvigsen, Jens Viuff","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Lehmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ab7a4733-2d2d-4371-98c2-5b463d00f5ee","name":"Nielsen, Maria Lehmann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per S.","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"f22f9bd0-3da2-4ce0-beb1-382554c4fa68","name":"Lauridsen, Per Stig","name_org":"Lauridsen, Per S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"51","publisher":"Dansk Center for Forskningsanalyse, Aarhus Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7af5fe66-9c91-448c-b5aa-2634b87bf30f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Uddannelsesledelse ved danske videregående uddannelsesinstitutioner : Studielederes rolle i uddannelsernes kvalitetsarbejde","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-199688","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with atrial fibrillation or flutter (AFF) are at increased risk of ischemic stroke, but their risk of other thromboembolic events remains less clear. METHODS: During 2004-2013, we conducted a nationwide population-based cohort study using Danish medical registries. We identified all patients with first-time AFF and sampled a sex-, age-, and calendar year-matched general population comparison cohort without AFF. For myocardial infarction, peripheral embolism, ischemic stroke, hemorrhagic stroke, deep venous thrombosis, and pulmonary embolism, we computed cumulative risks and adjusted incidence rate ratios (aIRRs) adjusted for comorbidity and medication. RESULTS: The study population consisted of 103,989 patients with AFF and 519,935 individuals without AFF from the general population. Ten-year cumulative risks in the AFF cohort were 3.5% for myocardial infarction, 0.5% for peripheral embolism, 6.7% for ischemic stroke, 1.3% for hemorrhagic stroke, 1.0% for deep venous thrombosis, and 1.3% for pulmonary embolism. During the first 30days following AFF, aIRRs were markedly (4 to 16-fold) increased for all outcomes and similarly elevated for myocardial infarction (aIRR=8.0, 95% confidence interval (CI): 6.8-9.5) and ischemic stroke (aIRR=9.9, 95% CI: 8.5-11.5). Thereafter, aIRRs decreased gradually, reaching unity after 5years for myocardial infarction, deep venous thrombosis, and pulmonary embolism, but remained 1.6 to 3.5-fold increased for peripheral embolism, ischemic stroke, and hemorrhagic stroke. CONCLUSIONS: AFF was a risk factor for all arterial and venous outcomes during the first year of follow-up, but only for peripheral embolism, ischemic stroke, and hemorrhagic stroke thereafter.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sundbøll, Jens","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Adelborg, Kasper","Ording, Anne Gulbech","Schmidt, Morten","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244488"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of arterial and venous thromboembolism in patients with atrial fibrillation or flutter a nationwide population based cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85018400755","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244488","identifier":[{"id":"28473169","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85018400755","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c998f581-8725-43e9-b2e0-dad50ffad429"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-819ACC5C84F8D5C1B8FF60A77BC308BF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erzsébet","key":"horváthpuhópau","last":"Horváth-Puhó","locid":"20f5c6bd-6ac1-4edb-a393-f34d60db546c","name":"Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","orcid":"0000-0002-3594-2212","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"adelborgpau","last":"Adelborg","locid":"2744cdbf-8516-46f6-ad71-f99fee1afaa0","name":"Adelborg, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Gulbech","key":"ordingpau","last":"Ording","locid":"f7919566-69b3-425f-8ea8-a1dedd34b685","name":"Ording, Anne Gulbech","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28473169"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2017.04.081","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"182-187","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"241"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018400755"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c998f581-8725-43e9-b2e0-dad50ffad429"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Risk of arterial and venous thromboembolism in patients with atrial fibrillation or flutter : A nationwide population-based cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244488","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The 2014–2016 JET results are reviewed in the light of their significance for optimising the ITER research plan for the active and non-active operation. More than 60 h of plasma operation with ITER first wall materials successfully took place since its installation in 2011. New multi-machine scaling of the type I-ELM divertor energy flux density to ITER is supported by first principle modelling. ITER relevant disruption experiments and first principle modelling are reported with a set of three disruption mitigation valves mimicking the ITER setup. Insights of the L–H power threshold in Deuterium and Hydrogen are given, stressing the importance of the magnetic configurations and the recent measurements of fine-scale structures in the edge radial electric. Dimensionless scans of the core and pedestal confinement provide new information to elucidate the importance of the first wall material on the fusion performance. H-mode plasmas at ITER triangularity (H = 1 at βN ~ 1.8 and n/nGW ~ 0.6) have been sustained at 2 MA during 5 s. The ITER neutronics codes have been validated on high performance experiments. Prospects for the coming D–T campaign and 14 MeV neutron calibration strategy are reviewed.","author_count":1223,"contributors":["Litaudon, X.","Abduallev, S.","Abhangi, M.","Abreu, P.","Afzal, M.","Aggarwal, K.M.","Ahlgren, T.","Ahn, Jong Hyun","Aho-Mantila, L.","Aiba, N.","Airila, M.","Albanese, R.","Aldred, V.","Alegre, D.","Alessi, E.","Aleynikov, P.","Alfier, A.","Alkseev, A.","Allinson, M.","Alper, B.","Alves, E.","Ambrosino, G.","Ambrosino, R.","Amicucci, L.","Amosov, V.","Andersson Sundén, E.","Angelone, M.","Anghel, M.","Angioni, C.","Appel, L.","Appelbee, C.","Arena, P.","Ariola, M.","Arnichand, H.","Arshad, S.A.","Ash, A.","Ashikawa, N.","Aslanyan, V.","Asunta, O.","Auriemma, F.","Austin, Y.","Avotina, L.","Axton, M.D.","Ayres, C.","Bacharis, M.","Baciero, A.","Baião, D.","Bailey, Stephen","Baker, A.","Balboa, I.","Balden, M.","Balshaw, N.","Ba