{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Fang, Chuanji","Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","Frankær, Christian G.","Brudecki, Grzegorz P.","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","AlNashef, Inas Muen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415713"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reviving pretreatment effectiveness of deep eutectic solvents on lignocellulosic date palm residues by prior recalcitrance reduction","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-415713","identifier":[{"id":"000398248000004","type":"wos"},{"id":"85019839980","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-254d9618-acaa-44cd-949d-420d5ea2eed5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16CDC6D70DD1CFE44FEBDD53851DEE49"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Chuanji","key":"fangpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Chuanji","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette Hedegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Grundahl","key":"frankærpau","last":"Frankær","locid":"45b770a9-25fb-4925-91e9-21ce9871b0f4","name":"Frankær, Christian G.","name_org":"Frankær, Christian Grundahl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Grzegorz P.","key":"brudeckipau","last":"Brudecki","name":"Brudecki, Grzegorz P.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Inas Muen","key":"alnashefpau","last":"AlNashef","name":"AlNashef, Inas Muen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.iecr.6b04733","issn":["08885885","15205045"],"issn_org":["08885885"],"issue":"12","journal":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","pages":"3167-3174","status":"p","title":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019839980"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-254d9618-acaa-44cd-949d-420d5ea2eed5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reviving Pretreatment Effectiveness of Deep Eutectic Solvents on Lignocellulosic Date Palm Residues by Prior Recalcitrance Reduction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415713","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Exercise training leads to favourable adaptations within skeletal muscle; however, this effect of exercise training may be blunted in postmenopausal women due to the loss of oestrogens. Furthermore, postmenopausal women may have an impaired vascular response to acute exercise. We examined the haemodynamic response to acute exercise in matched pre- and postmenopausal women before and after 12 weeks of aerobic high intensity exercise training. Twenty premenopausal and 16 early postmenopausal (3.1 ± 0.5 [mean ± SEM] years after final menstrual period) women only separated by 4 (50 ± 0 versus 54 ± 1) years of age were included. Before training, leg blood flow, O2 delivery, O2 uptake, and lactate release during knee-extensor exercise were similar in pre- and postmenopausal women. Exercise training reduced (P < 0.05) leg blood flow, O2 delivery, O2 uptake, lactate release, blood pressure and heart rate during the same absolute workloads in the postmenopausal women. These effects were not detected in the premenopausal women. Quadriceps muscle protein contents of mitochondrial complex II, III, and IV, endothelial nitric oxide synthase (eNOS), cyclooxygenase-1 (COX.1), COX-2, and oestrogen related receptor α (ERRα) were increased (P < 0.05) with training in the postmenopausal women whereas only the levels of mitochondrial complex V, eNOS, and COX-2 were increased (P < 0.05) in the premenopausal women. These findings demonstrate that vascular and skeletal muscle mitochondrial adaptations to aerobic high intensity exercise training are more pronounced in recent post- compared to premenopausal women, possibly as an effect of enhanced ERRα signalling. Also, the hyperaemic response to acute exercise appears to be preserved in the early postmenopausal phase. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Nyberg, Michael Permin","Egelund, Jon","Mandrup, Camilla Maria","Roland, Caroline Borup","Hansen, Karen Margrethe Brøgger E","Hergel, Ida-Marie F","Valbak-Andersen, Nicholai","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Stallknecht, Bente","Bangsbo, Jens","Hellsten, Ylva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518591"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"leg vascular and skeletal muscle mitochondrial adaptations to aerobic high intensity exercise training are enhanced in the early postmenopausal phase","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-518591","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5407965","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28231611","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85016575246","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d16bb9d0-fb09-4329-8501-f6703095e14c"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-71A8A037C9B675A5BF654C50A39EE33F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Permin","key":"nybergpau","last":"Nyberg","locid":"3a44876c-6484-4899-ade6-7e80d0483f3d","name":"Nyberg, Michael Permin","orcid":"0000-0002-3937-4697","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon","key":"egelundpau","last":"Egelund","locid":"b1d76378-3e05-496b-bc2f-6f8d44f10bc1","name":"Egelund, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-4353-0362","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Maria","key":"mandrupjensenpau","last":"Mandrup Jensen","locid":"7dc1cc65-c77a-4a36-9a2b-9eafda518d47","name":"Mandrup, Camilla Maria","name_org":"Mandrup Jensen, Camilla Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline Borup","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"ec0d3a17-a0e6-4894-b5d5-b8e7534b1702","name":"Roland, Caroline Borup","name_org":"Andersen, Caroline Borup","orcid":"0000-0003-1268-9215","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen Margrethe Brøgger E","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"9cb4ac56-c778-46d5-87e7-724053825bc8","name":"Hansen, Karen Margrethe Brøgger E","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida-Marie F","key":"hergelpau","last":"Hergel","locid":"1e5aab02-ac8d-4b3c-94cf-7b7931c2c2e5","name":"Hergel, Ida-Marie F","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicholai","key":"valbakandersenpau","last":"Valbak-Andersen","locid":"05f2217c-a853-4e6e-a4e3-89c8b8154aa9","name":"Valbak-Andersen, Nicholai","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ruth","key":"frikkeschmidtpau","last":"Frikke-Schmidt","locid":"bce2c3b4-6e08-46c7-96c6-7e385b0ec8b3","name":"Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente Merete","key":"stallknechtpau","last":"Stallknecht","locid":"eddf86eb-44d6-44ca-985b-79a29dd3cec7","name":"Stallknecht, Bente","name_org":"Stallknecht, Bente Merete","orcid":"0000-0003-3117-0451","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ylva","key":"hellstenpau","last":"Hellsten","locid":"902a8d03-73c1-41fa-a0a3-7f250470e2f0","name":"Hellsten, Ylva","orcid":"0000-0002-2435-9558","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28231611"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1113/jp273871","issn":["00223751","14697793"],"issn_org":["00223751"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Physiology","pages":"2969-2983","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physiology","volume":"595"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016575246"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d16bb9d0-fb09-4329-8501-f6703095e14c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Leg vascular and skeletal muscle mitochondrial adaptations to aerobic high-intensity exercise training are enhanced in the early postmenopausal phase","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518591","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A limited amount of research has examined the effect of changing public open spaces on active living. This abstract presents the study protocol of an intervention study designed in an interdisciplinary collaboration built on principles of Community-Based Participatory Research (CBPR) to develop urban installations highly tailored to promote active living among children (10-13-years-old) and seniors (>60-years-old) in a deprived neighbourhood in Copenhagen. METHODS: The study builds on a quasi-experimental study design including two sub-studies: 1) a children study and 2) a senior study. During spring 2017 the interventions will be developed, designed and implemented in collaboration with local children and seniors, respectively, using different co-design tools and methods. We will evaluate the effect of the interventions on children’s and senior’s use of the new-built urban installations using accelerometers in combination wit GPS and the System for Observing Play and Recreation in Communities (SOPARC). A process evaluation based on elements from the re-aim model will be conducted with focus groups consisting of the various stakeholders in the two sub-studies. The process evaluation will be used to gain knowledge of the intervention processes. DISCUSSION: The study presents new methods and approaches in the field of public open space interventions through interdisciplinary collaboration, participatory co-design approach and combination of measurements. Using both effect and process evaluations the study will provide unique insights in the role and importance of the interdisciplinary collaboration, participatory processes, tailoring changes in public open space to local needs and wishes. These results can be used to guide urban renewal projects in deprived neighbourhoods in the future.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Pawlowski, Charlotte Skau","Winge, Laura","Carroll, Sidse","Schmidt, Tanja Bettina","Wagner, Anne Margrethe","Nørtoft, Kamilla Pernille Johansen","Lamm, Bettina","Kural, René","Schipperijn, Jasper","Troelsen, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-603754"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-10","place":"Victoria, ca","start":"2017-06-07","title":"16th Annual Meeting of the International Society of Behavioral Nutrition and Physical Activity","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"move the neighbourhood a novel study design of a participatory public open space intervention in a danish deprived neighbourhood to promote active living","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-603754","ids":["sdu-6ae939a8-7f36-436d-b6fb-c39718c944e7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-972A602A20907BCB2288C427E50CE2CF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Active Living"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Skau","key":"pawlowskipau","last":"Pawlowski","locid":"889b5a08-7360-484e-84ad-5baea5e669df","name":"Pawlowski, Charlotte Skau","orcid":"0000-0003-1407-613X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"wingepau","last":"Winge","name":"Winge, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidse","key":"carrollpau","last":"Carroll","name":"Carroll, Sidse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tanja Bettina","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b1fba9ea-1959-49a9-be0a-9a4b9cd6ba1a","name":"Schmidt, Tanja Bettina","orcid":"0000-0003-2476-8711","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Margrethe","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","name":"Wagner, Anne Margrethe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kamilla Pernille Johansen","key":"nørtoftpau","last":"Nørtoft","name":"Nørtoft, Kamilla Pernille Johansen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bettina","key":"lammpau","last":"Lamm","name":"Lamm, Bettina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"René","key":"kuralpau","last":"Kural","name":"Kural, René","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jasper","key":"schipperijnpau","last":"Schipperijn","locid":"164cb44f-53ef-4f1a-9605-8112d837fcca","name":"Schipperijn, Jasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6558-7610","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","locid":"b35581eb-1482-4559-a4dd-49ec75e4c8a9","name":"Troelsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-8105-0349","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6ae939a8-7f36-436d-b6fb-c39718c944e7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Move the Neighbourhood: a novel study design of a participatory public open space intervention in a Danish deprived neighbourhood to promote active living","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-603754","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Black silicon (bSi) is promising for integration into silicon solar cell fabrication flow due to its excellent light trapping and low reflectance, and a continuously improving passivation. However, intensive ion bombardment during the reactive ion etching used to fabricate bSi induces surface damage that causes significant recombination. Here, we present a process optimization strategy for bSi, where surface damage is reduced and surface passivation is improved while excellent light trapping and low reflectance are maintained. We demonstrate that reduction of the capacitively coupled plasma power, during reactive ion etching at non-cryogenic temperature (-20°C), preserves the reflectivity below 1% and improves the effective minority carrier lifetime due to reduced ion energy. We investigate the effect of the etching process on the surface morphology, light trapping, reflectance, transmittance, and effective lifetime of bSi. Additional surface passivation using atomic layer deposition of Al2O3 significantly improves the effective lifetime. For n-type wafers, the lifetime reaches 12 ms for polished and 7.5 ms for bSi surfaces. For p-type wafers, the lifetime reaches 800 ls for both polished and bSi surfaces.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Plakhotnyuk, Maksym","Gaudig, Maria","Davidsen, Rasmus Schmidt","Michael-Lindhard, Jonas","Hirsch, Jens","Lausch, Dominik","Schmidt, Michael Stenbæk","Stamate, Eugen","Hansen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738483"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anhalt University of Applied Sciences","Fraunhofer Center for Silicon Photovoltaics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low surface damage dry etched black silicon","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/138328246/Untitled.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-738483","identifier":[{"id":"85031506568","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-df862176-2448-41db-8e6a-6cab304fb0f0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFE9A18E34F67929CEF1BB6DA322D729"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/138328246/Untitled.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"anhalt university of applied sciences","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Anhalt University of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer center for silicon photovoltaics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Center for Silicon Photovoltaics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maksym M.","key":"plakhotnyukpau","last":"Plakhotnyuk","locid":"13fcae31-a621-49d2-a262-d90c8495d8a1","name":"Plakhotnyuk, Maksym","name_org":"Plakhotnyuk, Maksym M.","orcid":"0000-0003-4493-4713","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gaudigpau","last":"Gaudig","name":"Gaudig, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Schmidt","key":"davidsenpau","last":"Davidsen","locid":"9bf815fc-994c-4d99-b89c-28ce33e7f2a8","name":"Davidsen, Rasmus Schmidt","orcid":"0000-0002-5782-9018","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"michaellindhardpau","last":"Michael-Lindhard","locid":"2233cbd1-74bd-405d-afd7-5eabc202067a","name":"Michael-Lindhard, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0003-0478-6015","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"hirschpau","last":"Hirsch","name":"Hirsch, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominik","key":"lauschpau","last":"Lausch","name":"Lausch, Dominik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Stenbæk","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"c47946d3-04a1-42d3-98f6-62ef38222262","name":"Schmidt, Michael Stenbæk","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eugen","key":"stamatepau","last":"Stamate","locid":"cdccdf75-364a-4cf1-929b-d85b45d73a7e","name":"Stamate, Eugen","orcid":"0000-0002-9649-2438","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8d678857-a721-4f7f-9a33-1dadb7401ce4","name":"Hansen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-6090-8323","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1063/1.4993425","issn":["00218979","10897550"],"issn_org":["00218979"],"issue":"14","journal":"Journal of Applied Physics","paperid":"143101","publisher":"American Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Physics","volume":"122"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031506568"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-df862176-2448-41db-8e6a-6cab304fb0f0"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Low surface damage dry etched black silicon","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738483","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundThe prognostic impact of previous depression on myocardial infarction survival remains poorly understood.AimsTo examine the association between depression and all-cause mortality following myocardial infarction.MethodUsing Danish medical registries, we conducted a nationwide population-based cohort study. We included all patients with first-time myocardial infarction (1995-2014) and identified previous depression as either a depression diagnosis or use of antidepressants. We used Cox regression to compute adjusted mortality rate ratios (aMRRs) with 95% confidence intervals.ResultsWe identified 170 771 patients with first-time myocardial infarction. Patients with myocardial infarction and a previous depression diagnosis had higher 19-year mortality risks (87% v. 78%). The overall aMRR was 1.11 (95% CI 1.07-1.15) increasing to 1.22 (95% CI 1.17-1.27) when including use of antidepressants in the depression definition.ConclusionsA history of depression was associated with a moderately increased all-cause mortality following myocardial infarction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sundbøll, Jens","Schmidt, Morten","Adelborg, Kasper","Pedersen, Lars","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Videbech, Poul Bror Hemming","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S02-094.96-021001"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Denmark epidemiology","Depressive Disorder complications","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction mortality","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of pre admission depression on mortality following myocardial infarction","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85019947889","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-094.96-021001","identifier":[{"id":"28254961","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85019947889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-71e2a337-5171-4f84-8e68-11fcafb026bd","ku-be77d66c-8b02-4e90-bdb0-abc4134e4e3e"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Denmark/epidemiology","Depressive Disorder/complications","Female","Humans","Journal Article","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction/mortality","Prognosis","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FA7542495233C6D0B8167ECE2602721A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"adelborgpau","last":"Adelborg","locid":"2744cdbf-8516-46f6-ad71-f99fee1afaa0","name":"Adelborg, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Poul","key":"videbechpau","last":"Videbech","locid":"30ef0c08-97c7-48b1-b034-d9fb316f6bd8","name":"Videbech, Poul","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28254961"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1192/bjp.bp.116.194605","issn":["00071250","09605371"],"issn_org":["00071250"],"issue":"5","journal":"British Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"356-361","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Psychiatry","title_org":"The British journal of psychiatry : the journal of mental science","volume":"210"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019947889"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-71e2a337-5171-4f84-8e68-11fcafb026bd","ku-be77d66c-8b02-4e90-bdb0-abc4134e4e3e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of pre-admission depression on mortality following myocardial infarction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.96-021001","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Seawater-based pretreatment of lignocellulosic biomass is an innovative process at research stage. With respect to process optimization, factors affecting seawater-based pretreatment of lignocellulosic date palm residues were studied for the first time in this paper. Pretreatment temperature (180 °C–210 °C), salinity of seawater (0 ppt–50 ppt), and catalysts (H2SO4, Na2CO3, and NaOH) were investigated. The results showed that pretreatment temperature exerted the largest influence on seawater-based pretreatment in terms of the enzymatic digestibility and fermentability of pretreated solids, and the inhibition of pretreatment liquids to Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Salinity showed the least impact to seawater-based pretreatment, which widens the application spectrum of saline water sources such as brines discharged in desalination plant. Sulfuric acid was the most effective catalyst for seawater-based pretreatment compared with Na2CO3 and NaOH.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fang, Chuanji","Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","Frankær, Christian Grundahl","Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo","Brudecki, Grzegorz P.","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S02-096.15-004164"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Khalifa University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Biomass","Biorefinery","Date palm residues","Lignocellulosic","Lignocellulosic biomass","Pretreatment","Seawater"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"factors affecting seawater based pretreatment of lignocellulosic date palm residues","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85029160901&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.15-004164","identifier":[{"id":"000412443500068","type":"wos"},{"id":"28898854","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85029160901","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-553a6f6c-fdf8-4af7-8237-a1db7932dace","ku-ff13920f-6bc1-43f7-8591-09108806486b"],"keyword":["Biorefinery","Date palm residues","Lignocellulosic","Lignocellulosic biomass","Pretreatment","Seawater","biomass"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-140615C273FC64B3B1CA471B2A1D5E84"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university of science and technology","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Esbjerg Energy Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuanji","key":"fangpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Chuanji","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Hedegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"29912cd6-8a9e-4022-b66a-6fb13430130a","name":"Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6805-7247","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian Grundahl","key":"frankaerpau","last":"Frankaer","locid":"45b770a9-25fb-4925-91e9-21ce9871b0f4","name":"Frankær, Christian G.","name_org":"Frankaer, Christian Grundahl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan Rodrigo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Grzegorz P.","key":"brudeckipau","last":"Brudecki","name":"Brudecki, Grzegorz P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28898854"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biortech.2017.08.184","issn":["09608524","18732976"],"issn_org":["09608524"],"issue":"PART A","journal":"Bioresource Technology","pages":"540-548","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Bioresource Technology","volume":"245"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029160901"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-553a6f6c-fdf8-4af7-8237-a1db7932dace","ku-ff13920f-6bc1-43f7-8591-09108806486b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Factors affecting seawater-based pretreatment of lignocellulosic date palm residues","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.15-004164","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Utilization of multi-specie feedstocks is imperative for application of lignocellulosic biorefineries in arid regions. Different lignocellulosic residues vary in composition and anatomical features. Pretreatment and enzymatic hydrolysis are two processes at the front end of any lignocellulosics biorefinery applying biochemical pathway, and have to efficiently deal with the variance in the feedstock composition and properties. However, there is limited knowledge about effect of mixing different lignocellulosics on pretreatment and enzymatic hydrolysis yields. In this study effect of mixing on the yields from hydrothermal pretreatment and enzymatic hydrolysis was analyzed by mixing three different lignocellulosic residues — Bermuda grass, Jasmine hedges, and date palm fronds. Results showed that the individual and the mixed lignocellulosics gave same yields when treated under similar conditions of hydrothermal pretreatment and enzymatic hydrolysis. It indicates that this mixture can be a suitable feedstock for lignocellulosic biorefinery.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ashraf, Muhammad Tahir","Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089213"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Masdar Institute of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Enzymatic hydrolysis","Hydrothermal pretreatment","Mixing","Residues"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrothermal pretreatment and enzymatic hydrolysis of mixed green and woody lignocellulosics from arid regions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85018753897&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-089213","identifier":[{"id":"000402485500045","type":"wos"},{"id":"85018753897","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8686dc45-9a68-43ad-996d-d72ae0732e55"],"keyword":["Enzymatic hydrolysis","Hydrothermal pretreatment","Mixed lignocellulosic residues","Mixing","Residues"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F7A8071672F4A07E6B8457A0770DE0BB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"masdar institute of science and technology","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Masdar Institute of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Muhammad Tahir","key":"ashrafpau","last":"Ashraf","name":"Ashraf, Muhammad Tahir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Hedegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"29912cd6-8a9e-4022-b66a-6fb13430130a","name":"Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6805-7247","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biortech.2017.04.065","issn":["09608524","18732976"],"issn_org":["09608524"],"journal":"Bioresource Technology","pages":"369-378","publisher":"Elsevier","stat