{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: The prognostic impact of glucocorticoids on stroke mortality remains uncertain. We, therefore, examined whether preadmission use of glucocorticoids is associated with short-term mortality after ischemic stroke, intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH), or subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH). METHODS: We conducted a nationwide population-based cohort study using medical registries in Denmark. We identified all patients with a first-time inpatient diagnosis of stroke between 2004 and 2012. We categorized glucocorticoid use as current use (last prescription redemption ≤90 days before admission), former use, and nonuse. Current use was further classified as new or long-term use. We used Cox regression to compute 30-day mortality rate ratios with 95% confidence intervals (CIs), controlling for confounders. RESULTS: We identified 100 042 patients with a first-time stroke. Of these, 83 735 patients had ischemic stroke, 11 779 had ICH, and 4528 had SAH. Absolute mortality risk was higher for current users compared with nonusers for ischemic stroke (19.5% versus 10.2%), ICH (46.5% versus 34.4%), and SAH (35.0% versus 23.2%). For ischemic stroke, the adjusted 30-day mortality rate ratio was increased among current users compared with nonusers (1.58, 95% CI: 1.46-1.71), driven by the effect of glucocorticoids among new users (1.80, 95% CI: 1.62-1.99). Current users had a more modest increase in the adjusted 30-day mortality rate ratio for hemorrhagic stroke (1.26, 95% CI: 1.09-1.45 for ICH and 1.40, 95% CI: 1.01-1.93 for SAH) compared with nonusers. Former use was not substantially associated with mortality. CONCLUSIONS: Preadmission use of glucocorticoids was associated with increased 30-day mortality among patients with ischemic stroke, ICH, and SAH.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sundbøll, Jens","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Schmidt, Morten","Dekkers, Olaf M.","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","Pedersen, Lars","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-271070"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preadmission use of glucocorticoids and 000000000030 day mortality after stroke","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84959514392","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-271070","identifier":[{"id":"84959514392","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26903585","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f87c20ae-4afa-4e9e-8643-f4e8d0a53041"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E76C73484445D12D36F4792611A52A0D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erzsébet","key":"horváthpuhópau","last":"Horváth-Puhó","locid":"20f5c6bd-6ac1-4edb-a393-f34d60db546c","name":"Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","orcid":"0000-0002-3594-2212","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olaf M","key":"dekkerspau","last":"Dekkers","locid":"33484775-3cb8-444e-b567-bf2184aa9911","name":"Dekkers, Olaf M.","name_org":"Dekkers, Olaf M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian F","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"b1104ec4-1322-428f-af8f-7771361930bb","name":"Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","name_org":"Christiansen, Christian F","orcid":"0000-0002-0727-953X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik T","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","name_org":"Sørensen, Henrik T","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26903585"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/strokeaha.115.012231","issn":["00392499","15244628"],"issn_org":["00392499"],"issue":"3","journal":"Stroke","pages":"829-35","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"Stroke","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959514392"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f87c20ae-4afa-4e9e-8643-f4e8d0a53041"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Preadmission Use of Glucocorticoids and 30-Day Mortality After Stroke","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-271070","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Glucose is an important inducer of insulin secretion, but it also stimulates long-term adaptive changes in gene expression that can either promote or antagonize the proliferative potential and function of β cells. Here, we have generated time-resolved profiles of enhancer and transcriptional activity in response to glucose in the INS-1E pancreatic β cell line. Our data outline a biphasic response with a first transcriptional wave during which metabolic genes are activated, and a second wave where cell-cycle genes are activated and β cell identity genes are repressed. The glucose-sensing transcription factor ChREBP directly activates first wave enhancers, whereas repression and activation of second wave enhancers are indirect. By integrating motif enrichment within late-regulated enhancers with expression profiles of the associated transcription factors, we have identified multiple putative regulators of the second wave. These include RORγ, the activity of which is important for glucose-induced proliferation of both INS-1E and primary rat β cells.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Schmidt, Søren Fisker","Madsen, Jesper Grud Skat","Frafjord, Kari Østerli","Poulsen, Lars la Cour","Salö, Sofia","Boergesen, Michael","Loft, Anne","Larsen, Bjørk Ditlev","Madsen, Maria Stahl","Holst, Jens Juul","Maechler, Pierre","Dalgaard, Louise Torp","Mandrup, Susanne"],"cuid":["S03-097.28-043190"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Geneva"],"keyword":["CELLS","ChIP seq","ChREBP","Glucose","Journal Article","Metabolism","Proliferation","RNA seq","RoR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrative genomics outlines a biphasic glucose response and a chrebp rorγ axis regulating proliferation in β cells","src":["ku","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2016.07.063","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-097.28-043190","identifier":[{"id":"27545881","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84990212640","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6af2a742-d454-4240-b465-e5a750113604","ruc-acda460a-c0ea-48ce-b206-4928d60ebef0","sdu-bd0d626c-c06a-45f3-9dd8-485d8db53c67"],"keyword":["ChIP-seq","ChREBP","Journal Article","RNA-seq","RORγ","glucose","metabolism","pancreatic β cells","proliferation","β cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F353CD4E5C959E5657D42CC970720C61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128916307/Integrative_Genomics_Outlines_a_Biphasic_Glucose_Response_and_a_ChREBP_ROR_Axis_Regulating_Proliferation_in_Cells.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/111466004/Schmidt_2016_Cell_Reports_incl_suppl.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2016.07.063","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"