{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Long-term nationwide trends in atrial fibrillation (AF) incidence and 5-year outcomes are rare. METHODS: We conducted a population-based cohort study using the Danish National Patient Registry covering all Danish hospitals. We computed standardized incidence rates during 1983-2012. We used Cox regression to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) of heart failure, stroke, and death within 5years, comparing 5-year calendar periods with the earliest period (1983-1987) as reference. RESULTS: We identified 312,420 patients with first-time hospital-diagnosed AF. The incidence rate per 100,000person-years increased from 98 in 1983 to 307 in 2012. The mean annual increase during the 30-year study period was 4%, with a 6% increase annually until 2000 and a 1.4% increase annually thereafter. The incidence trends were most pronounced among men and persons above 70years. Among high-risk subgroups, AF incidence was consistently highest in patients with valvular heart disease or heart failure. The rate of heart failure following AF declined by 50% over the entire study period (HR: 0.49, 95% confidence interval (CI): 0.48-0.51) and the mortality rate declined by 40% (HR: 0.62, 95% CI: 0.61-0.63). Within the last two decades, the rate for ischemic stroke declined by 20% (HR 0.81, 95% CI: 0.78-0.84), but increased almost as much for haemorrhagic stroke (HR: 1.14, 95% CI: 1.01-1.29). CONCLUSIONS: The long-term risk of heart failure, ischemic stroke, and death following onset of AF has decreased remarkably over the last three decades. Still, the threefold increased incidence of hospital-diagnosed AF during the same period is a major public health concern.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Schmidt, Morten","Ulrichsen, Sinna Pilgaard","Pedersen, Lars","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-196322"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000030 year nationwide trends in incidence of atrial fibrillation in denmark and associated 000000000005 year risk of heart failure stroke and death","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84989321419","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-196322","identifier":[{"id":"27705839","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84989321419","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7544a9e5-8c9a-4a28-98df-87cf8cb0cf64"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBBCB5D8035698756BDE244F1E118AA2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medicinsk afdeling, Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sinna Pilgaard","key":"ulrichsenpau","last":"Ulrichsen","locid":"28d145ca-92b9-49f2-8be2-e6d9f59c01ce","name":"Ulrichsen, Sinna Pilgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-8679-5163","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27705839"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2016.09.071","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"30-36","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"225"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84989321419"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7544a9e5-8c9a-4a28-98df-87cf8cb0cf64"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"30-year nationwide trends in incidence of atrial fibrillation in Denmark and associated 5-year risk of heart failure, stroke, and death","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-196322","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Next generation sequencing of uveal melanoma (UM) samples has identified a number of recurrent oncogenic or loss-of-function mutations in key driver genes including: GNAQ, GNA11, EIF1AX, SF3B1 and BAP1. To search for additional driver mutations in this tumor type we carried out whole-genome or whole-exome sequencing of 28 tumors or primary cell lines. These samples have a low mutation burden, with a mean of 10.6 protein changing mutations per sample (range 0 to 53). As expected for these sun-shielded melanomas the mutation spectrum was not consistent with an ultraviolet radiation signature, instead, a BRCA mutation signature predominated. In addition to mutations in the known UM driver genes, we found a recurrent mutation in PLCB4 (c.G1888T, p.D630Y, NM_000933), which was validated using Sanger sequencing. The identical mutation was also found in published UM sequence data (1 of 56 tumors), supporting its role as a novel driver mutation in UM. PLCB4 p.D630Y mutations are mutually exclusive with mutations in GNA11 and GNAQ, consistent with PLCB4 being the canonical downstream target of the former gene products. Taken together these data suggest that the PLCB4 hotspot mutation is similarly a gain-of-function mutation leading to activation of the same signaling pathway, promoting UM tumorigenesis.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Johansson, Peter","Aoude, Lauren G","Wadt, Karin","Glasson, William J","Warrier, Sunil K","Hewitt, Alex W","Kiilgaard, Jens Folke","Heegaard, Steffen","Isaacs, Tim","Franchina, Maria","Ingvar, Christian","Vermeulen, Tersia","Whitehead, Kevin J","Schmidt, Christopher W","Palmer, Jane M","Symmons, Judith","Gerdes, Anne-Marie","Jönsson, Göran","Hayward, Nicholas K"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support Non U S Gov t"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep sequencing of uveal melanoma identifies a recurrent mutation in i plcb000000000004 i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.6614","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-429159","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4826231","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26683228","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84957990067","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3bd32cc6-5a1b-4b94-b705-8169553a38e9"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0F49842F04E8BD1014DC1C23834EE6BC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.6614","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lauren G","key":"aoudepau","last":"Aoude","name":"Aoude, Lauren G","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karin","key":"wadtpau","last":"Wadt","name":"Wadt, Karin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"William J","key":"glassonpau","last":"Glasson","name":"Glasson, William J","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sunil K","key":"warri