{"abstract":"The effects of 52 weeks of soccer or resistance training were investigated in untrained elderly men. The subjects aged 68.1±2.1 yrs were randomised into a soccer (SG; n = 9), a resistance (RG; n = 9) and a control group (CG; n = 8). The subjects in SG and RG, respectively, trained 1.7±0.3 and 1.8±0.3 times weekly on average during the intervention period. Muscle function and body composition were determined before and after 16 and 52 weeks of the intervention period. In SG, BMI was reduced by 1.5% and 3.0% (p<0.05) after 16 and 52 weeks, respectively, unchanged in RG and 2% higher (p<0.05) in CG after 52 weeks of the intervention period. In SG, the response to a glucose tolerance test was 16% lower (p<0.05) after 16 wks, but not after 52 wks, compared to before the intervention period, and unchanged in RG and CG. In SG, superoxide dismutase-2 expression was 59% higher (p<0.05) after 52 wks compared to before the intervention period, and unchanged in RG and CG. In RG, upper body lean mass was 3 and 2% higher (p<0.05) after 16 and 52 wks, respectively, compared to before the intervention period, and unchanged in SG and CG. In RG, Akt-2 expression increased by 28% (p<0.01) and follistatin expression decreased by 38% (p<0.05) during the 52-wk intervention period, and was unchanged in SG and CG. Thus, long-term soccer training reduces BMI and improves anti-oxidative capacity, while long-term resistance training impacts muscle protein enzyme expression and increases lean body mass in elderly men. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT01530035.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rostgaard Andersen, Thomas","Schmidt, Jakob Friis","Pedersen, Mogens Theisen","Krustrup, Peter","Bangsbo, Jens"],"cuid":["S02-086.61-666916"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Aged","Anthropometry","Blood Glucose","Body composition","Diet","Fasting","Fluorescent Antibody Technique","Glucose Tolerance Test","Hemoglobin A Glycosylated","Humans","Insulin","Journal Article","Lipids","Male","Muscle Proteins","Muscles","Randomized Controlled Trial","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Resistance Training","Soccer","Tissue Extracts"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of 000000000052 weeks of soccer or resistance training on body composition and muscle function in 000000000065 year old healthy males a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0148236","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.61-666916","identifier":[{"id":"26886262","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84960369690","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4757560","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-96920815-17b1-4c6a-8c81-519dbc821727","sdu-0cd92aef-a890-4577-9358-e619f43747b8"],"keyword":["Aged","Anthropometry","Blood Glucose","Body Composition","Diet","Fasting","Fluorescent Antibody Technique","Glucose Tolerance Test","Hemoglobin A, Glycosylated","Humans","Insulin","Journal Article","Lipids","Male","Muscle Proteins","Muscles","Randomized Controlled Trial","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Resistance Training","Soccer","Tissue Extracts"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E4514AABCA34EA1AAD291817282E3959"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/156027200/Andersen_et_al_P_L_o_S_ONE_2016_Vol_11_2_e0148236.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/123116046/journal.pone.0148236.PDF","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0148236","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, The August Krogh Section for Human Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"rostgaardandersenpau","last":"Rostgaard Andersen","locid":"8f0fc396-7917-4d99-ba5d-33ddf19e9566","name":"Rostgaard Andersen, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jakob Friis","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"74b58d72-77a1-4d66-aaaa-c36189cbf0b6","name":"Schmidt, Jakob Friis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mogens Theisen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5390946b-e1a6-47e1-817a-72dfb5283a42","name":"Pedersen, Mogens Theisen","orcid":"0000-0002-3178-6320","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Peter","key":"krustruppau","last":"Krustrup","locid":"9b334221-94f3-4a68-a2de-ee9f419704d8","name":"Krustrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9843-7320","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26886262"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0148236","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"2","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0148236","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960369690"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-96920815-17b1-4c6a-8c81-519dbc821727","sdu-0cd92aef-a890-4577-9358-e619f43747b8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Effects of 52 Weeks of Soccer or Resistance Training on Body Composition and Muscle Function in +65-Year-Old Healthy Males : A Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.61-666916","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"AIM OF DATABASE: To monitor the development of diabetic eye disease in Denmark and to evaluate the accessibility and effectiveness of diabetic eye screening programs with focus on interregional variations. TARGET POPULATION: The target population includes all patients diagnosed with diabetes. Denmark (5.5 million inhabitants) has ~320,000 diabetes patients with an annual increase of 27,000 newly diagnosed patients. The Danish Registry of Diabetic Retinopathy (DiaBase) collects data on all diabetes patients aged ≥18 years who attend screening for diabetic eye disease in hospital eye departments and in private ophthalmological practice. In 2014-2015, DiaBase included data collected from 77,968 diabetes patients. MAIN VARIABLES: The main variables provide data for calculation of performance indicators to monitor the quality of diabetic eye screening and development of diabetic retinopathy. Data with respect to age, sex, best corrected visual acuity, screening frequency, grading of diabetic retinopathy and maculopathy at each visit, progression/regression of diabetic eye disease, and prevalence of blindness were obtained. Data analysis from DiaBase's latest annual report (2014-2015) indicates that the prevalence of no diabetic retinopathy, nonproliferative diabetic retinopathy, and proliferative diabetic retinopathy is 78%, 18%, and 4%, respectively. The percentage of patients without diabetic maculopathy is 97%. The proportion of patients with regression of diabetic retinopathy (20%) is greater than the proportion of patients with progression of diabetic retinopathy (10%). CONCLUSION: The collection of data from diabetic eye screening is still expanding in Denmark. Analysis of the data collected during the period 2014-2015 reveals an overall decrease of diabetic retinopathy compared to the previous year, although the number of patients newly diagnosed with diabetes has been increasing in Denmark. DiaBase is a useful tool to observe the quality of screening, prevalence, and progression/regression of diabetic eye disease.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, Nis","Hjortdal, Jesper Østergaard","Schielke, Katja Christina","Bek, Toke","Grauslund, Jakob","Laugesen, Caroline Schmidt","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Cerqueira, Charlotte","Andresen, Jens"],"cuid":["S04-098.52-009103"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Danish diabetes database","Database","DiaBase","Diabetes","National annual report","Quality indicator","Quality of care","Registry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Danish Ophthalmological Society, Copenhagen; Organization of Danish Ophthalmologists in Private Practice, Copenhagen."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish registry of diabetic retinopathy","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S99507","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-098.52-009103","identifier":[{"id":"84995655293","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000390397800003","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5094648","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27822108","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-bcbb0053-36fd-44c4-a286-5873591e945c","au-5982dbba-e4af-4707-9c40-7feab328b148","ku-49f86403-3177-42a8-8562-a7ae8635ed81","sdu-6f408808-ca64-45cf-9f0d-44bda340cd98"],"keyword":["Danish diabetes database","Database","DiaBase","Diabetes","National annual report","Quality indicator","Quality of care","Registry"],"lang":"English