{"abstract":"Phosphoric acid and phosphoric acid doped polymer membranes are widely used as electrolytes in hydrogen based fuel cells operating at elevated temperatures. Such electrolytes have been explored for direct oxidation of methanol to further increase the versatility of the systems, however, with demonstrated lifetimes of only a few days to weeks. In this work the methyl phosphate formation from the acid and methanol is identified and proposed to be a major mechanism for the cell degradation. Proton conductivity and fuel cell durability tests validate the mechanism at high methanol contents.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Aili, David","Vassiliev, Anton","Jensen, Jens Oluf","Schmidt, Thomas J.","Li, Qingfeng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352866"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paul Scherrer Institute"],"keyword":["Degradation","Direct methanol fuel cells DMFC","Durability","Durability test","Electrolytes","Elevated temperature","Fuel cell","Fuel cells","Methanol","Methanol fuels","Phosphoric acid","Proton conductivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"methyl phosphate formation as a major degradation mode of direct methanol fuel cells with phosphoric acid based electrolytes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpowsour.2015.01.010","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352866","identifier":[{"id":"84920735969","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a1d860e5-e29a-4a92-a2c3-89a920789bca"],"keyword":["Acid doped","Cell degradations","Degradation","Direct methanol fuel cells (DMFC)","Direct oxidation","Durability","Durability test","Electrolytes","Elevated temperature","Fuel cell","Fuel cells","Methanol","Methanol content","Methanol fuels","Methyl phosphates","Phosphoric acid","Phosphoric acid fuel cells (PAFC)","Proton conductivity","Proton conductivity and fuel cells"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86C1B1396093216C3C16AA89D3C184BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpowsour.2015.01.010","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Energy Conversion and Storage, Proton conductors"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"paul scherrer institute","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Paul Scherrer Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"David","key":"ailipau","last":"Aili","locid":"6e8c9f86-3b5b-4046-bcb6-33f77ecbd09b","name":"Aili, David","orcid":"0000-0002-3510-135X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"vassilievpau","last":"Vassiliev","locid":"c145dccb-20a9-4ec7-a98e-83f72c9c71d9","name":"Vassiliev, Anton","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Oluf","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"14e30120-4ae0-4d04-b379-d9caaf3fe087","name":"Jensen, Jens Oluf","orcid":"0000-0002-2427-7763","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas J.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Thomas J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qingfeng","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"905a9410-e476-40fa-b8b5-2c0430d86608","name":"Li, Qingfeng","orcid":"0000-0002-5460-055X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2015.01.010","issn":["03787753","18732755"],"issn_org":["03787753"],"journal":"Journal of Power Sources","pages":"517-521","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Power Sources","volume":"279"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920735969"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a1d860e5-e29a-4a92-a2c3-89a920789bca"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Methyl phosphate formation as a major degradation mode of direct methanol fuel cells with phosphoric acid based electrolytes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352866","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Intensive insulin treatment in type 1 diabetes reduces the incidence and slows the progression of microvascular and macrovascular complications; however, it is associated with an increased risk of hypoglycaemia and weight gain. In this review, we propose dual-hormone treatment with insulin and glucagon as a method for achieving near normalization of blood glucose levels without increasing hypoglycaemia frequency and weight gain. We briefly summarize glucagon pathophysiology in type 1 diabetes as well as the current applications of glucagon for the treatment of hypoglycaemia. Until now, the use of glucagon has been limited by the need for reconstitution immediately before use, because of instability of the available compounds; however, stabile compounds are soon to be launched and will render long-term intensive dual-hormone treatment in type 1 diabetes possible.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Reiband, H K","Schmidt, S","Ranjan, Ajenthen","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Nørgaard, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-478519"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dual hormone treatment with insulin and glucagon in patients with type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-478519","identifier":[{"id":"25533565","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84943666159","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8e48c089-2e9e-4dbb-9845-9fb40a9ee90c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7B8D465A085A13540BD1C463D0C68F1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"H K","key":"reibandpau","last":"Reiband","name":"Reiband, H K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"S","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, S","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ajenthen","key":"ranjanpau","last":"Ranjan","name":"Ranjan, Ajenthen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"S","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","name_org":"Madsbad, S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"K","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","name_org":"Nørgaard, K","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25533565"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/dmrr.2632","issn":["15207552","15207560"],"issn_org":["15207552"],"issue":"7","journal":"Diabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews","pages":"672-9","status":"p","title":"Diabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews","title_org":"Diabetes - Metabolism: Research and Reviews (Print Edition)","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84943666159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8e48c089-2e9e-4dbb-9845-9fb40a9ee90c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dual-hormone treatment with insulin and glucagon in patients with type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-478519","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: Potent, less toxic, directly acting antivirals (DAAs) for treatment of hepatitis C virus (HCV) infection promise to improve HCV cure rates among HIV/ HCV-co-infected individuals. However, the costs of treatment will necessitate prioritization of those at greatest risk of liver-related death (LRD) for therapy. This study aims to provide guidance on who should be prioritized for DAA treatment. Methods: Three thousand, nine hundred and forty-one HCV antibody-positive PSHREG and FIB-4 are names not acronyms (EuroSIDA) patients with follow-up after 1 January 2000 were included, with causes of death classified using Coding causes of Death in HIV (CoDe) methodology. Crude death rates, competing-risks Cox proportional- hazards models and cumulative incidence functions were used to describe factors associated with LRD. Results: LRD accounted for 145 of 670 (21.6%) deaths in the study population. LRD rates peaked in those aged 35'45 years, and occurred almost exclusively in those with at least F2 fibrosis at baseline. In adjustedCoxmodels, risk factors for LRDincluded F4 or F2/F3 fibrosis [sub-distribution hazard ratio (sHR) 6.3, 95%confidence interval (CI)4.1'9.6; andsHR2.5, 95%CI 1.5'4.2 vs. F0/F1, respectively), CD4 cell count (sHR 0.83, 95%CI 0.73'0.95 per doubling) and hepatitis B surface antigen-positive (sHR 2.2, 95% CI 1.3'3.5 vs. hepatitis B surface antigen-negative). The 5-year probability of LRD was low in those with F0/F1 fibrosis (sHR2.2%, 95%CI 1.7''2.9), but substantial in those withF2/F3 and F4 fibrosis (sHR 10.3%, 95% CI 7.6'13.5; and sHR 14.0%, 95% CI 10.3'18.3, respectively). Conclusion: Treatment with DAAs should be prioritized for those with at least F2 fibrosis. Early initiation of cART with the aim of avoiding low CD4 cell counts should be considered essential to decrease the risk of LRD and the need for HCV treatment.","author_count":185,"contributors":["Grint, Daniel","Peters, Lars","Rockstroh, Juergen K.","Rakmanova, Aza","Trofimova, Tatiana","Lacombe, Karine","Karpov, Igor","Galli, Massimo","Domingo, Pere","Kirk, Ole","Lundgren, Jens D.","Mocrofta, Amanda","Losso, M.","Kundro, M.","Vetter, N.","Zangerle, R.","Karpov, I.","Vassilenko, A.","Mitsura, V. M.","Paduto, D.","Clumeck, N.","De Wit, S.","Delforge, M.","Florence, E.","Vandekerckhove, L.","Hadziosmanovic, V.","Kostov, K.","Begovac, J.","Machala, L.","Jilich, D.","Sedlacek, D.","Nielsen, J.","Kronborg, G.","Benfield, T.","Larsen, M.","Gerstoft, J.","Katzenstein, T.","Hansen, A. B.E.","Skinhøj, P.","Pedersen, Carsten","Møller, Niels","Ostergaard, L.","Dragsted, U. B.","Nielsen, L. N.","Zilmer, K.","Smidt, Jelena","Ristola, M.","Katlama, C.","Viard, J. P.","Girard, P. M.","Vanhems, P.","Pradier, C.","Dabis, F.","Neau, D.","Duvivier, C.","Rockstroh, J.","Schmidt, R.","Van Lunzen, J.","Degen, O.","Stellbrink, H. J.","Stefan, C.","Bogner, J.","Fätkenheuer, G.","Chkhartishvili, N.","Kosmidis, J.","Gargalianos, P.","Xylomenos, G.","Perdios, J.","Sambatakou, H.","Banhegyi, D.","Gottfredsson, M.","Mulcahy, F.","Yust, I.","Turner, D.","Burke, M.","Shahar, E.","Hassoun, G.","Elinav, H.","Haouzi, M.","Sthoeger, Z. M.","Monforte, A. D.arminio","Esposito, R.","Mazeu, I.","Mussini, C.","Pristera, R.","Mazzotta, F.","Gabbuti, A.","Vullo, V.","Lichtner, M.","Zaccarelli, M.","Antinori, A.","Acinapura, R.","D'Offizi, G.","Lazzarin, A.","Castagna, A.","Gianotti, N.","Galli, M.","Ridolfo, A.","Rozentale, B.","Uzdaviniene, V.","Staub, T.","Hemmer, R.","Reiss, P.","Ormaasen, V.","Maeland, A.","Bruun, J.","Knysz, B.","Gasiorowski, J.","Inglot, M.","Horban, A.","Bakowska, E.","Grzeszczuk, A.","Flisiak, R.","Parczewski, M.","Pynka, M.","Maciejewska, K.","Beniowski, M.","Mularska, E.","Smiatacz, T.","Jablonowska, E.","Malolepsza, E.","Wojcik, K.","Mozer-Lisewska, I.","Doroana, M.","Caldeira, L.","Mansinho, K.","Maltez, F.","Radoi, R.","Oprea, C.","Babes, Victor","Rakhmanova, A.","Rakhmanova, A.","Trofimora, T.","Khromova, I.","Kuzovatova, E.","Jevtovic, D.","Shunnar, A.","Staneková, D.","Tomazic, J.","Moreno, S.","Rodriguez, J. M.","Clotet, B.","Jou, A.","Paredes, R.","Tural, C.","Puig, J.","Bravo, I.","Gatell, J. M.","Miró, J. M.","Domingo, P.","Gutierrez, M.","Mateo, G.","Sambeat, M. A.","Laporte, J. M.","Blaxhult, A.","Flamholc, L.","Thalme, A.","Sonnerborg, A.","Ledergerber, B.","Weber, R.","Cavassini, M.","Calmy, A.","Furrer, H.","Battegay, M.","Elzi, L.","Schmid, P.","Kravchenko, E.","Chentsova, N.","Frolov, V.","Kutsyna, G.","Baskakov, I.","Servitskiy, S.","Kuznetsova, A.","Kyselyova, G.","Gazzard, B.","Johnson, A. M.","Simons, E.","Edwards, S.","Phillips, A.","Johnson, M. A.","Mocroft, A.","Orkin, C.","Weber, J.","Scullard, G.","Fisher, M.","Leen, C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-668068"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grint, Daniel"],"country":["Argentina","Austria","Belarus","Belgium","Croatia","Czechia","Estonia","Finland","France","Germany","Greece","Iceland","Ireland","Israel","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Poland","Portugal","Slovenia","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","Ukraine","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Athens General Hospital","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Barts Health NHS Trust","Belarusian State Medical University","Brighton and Sussex University Hospitals NHS Trust","CHU de Nice","Charles University","Ghent University","Goethe University Frankfurt","Gomel State Medical University","Hadassah University Medical Centre","Hannover Medical School","Hopital Hotel-Dieu AP-HP","Hospital Curry Cabral","Hospital General de Agudos José María Ramos Mejía","Hospital Ramon y Cajal","Hospital of Santa Creu i Sant Pau","INSERM","IRCCS Istituto per le Malattie Infettive Lazzaro Spallanzani - Roma","IRCCS San Raffaele Scientific Institute","Imperial College London","Innsbruck Medical University","