:"Leen, C.","rank":186,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25870984"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/qad.0000000000000674","issn":["02699370"],"issue":"10","journal":"AIDS","pages":"1205-1215","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"AIDS","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938990344"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4291904c-d23c-4643-a125-ecb13a93fc35"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Liver-related death among HIV/hepatitis C virus-co-infected individuals : Implications for the era of directly acting antivirals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-668068","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The large water consumption (1.9-5.9 m3 water per m3 of biofuel) required by biomass processing plants has become an emerging concern, which is particularly critical in arid/semiarid regions. Seawater, as a widely available water source, could be an interesting option. This work was to study the technical feasibility of using seawater to replace freshwater in the pretreatment of date palm leaflets, a lignocellulosic biomass from arid regions, for bioethanol production. It was shown that leaflets pretreated with seawater exhibited lower cellulose crystallinity than those pretreated with freshwater. Pretreatment with seawater produced comparably digestible and fermentable solids to those obtained with freshwater. Moreover, no significant difference of inhibition to Saccharomyces cerevisiae was observed between liquids from pretreatment with seawater and freshwater. The results showed that seawater could be a promising alternative to freshwater for lignocellulose biorefineries in coastal and/or arid/semiarid areas.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fang, Chuanji","Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","Brudecki, Grzegorz P","Cybulska, Iwona","Frankær, Christian Grundahl","Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808495"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Masdar Institute of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"seawater as alternative to freshwater in pretreatment of date palm residues for bioethanol production in coastal and or arid areas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84948698133","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808495","identifier":[{"id":"84948698133","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26487350","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-6b8d3748-c192-4815-82ea-275cc639095d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D40A816063E0315388CF3A2DA2833CE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ae","key":"masdar institute of science and technology","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Masdar Institute of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Organic Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, X-ray Crystallography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuanji","key":"fangpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Chuanji","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Hedegaard","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Mette Hedegaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Grzegorz P","key":"brudeckipau","last":"Brudecki","name":"Brudecki, Grzegorz P","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iwona","key":"cybulskapau","last":"Cybulska","name":"Cybulska, Iwona","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Grundahl","key":"frankærpau","last":"Frankær","locid":"e42b149c-4f0f-4ac2-a10c-3c500a9e59d4","name":"Frankær, Christian Grundahl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan-Rodrigo","key":"bastidasoyanedelpau","last":"Bastidas-Oyanedel","name":"Bastidas-Oyanedel, Juan-Rodrigo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26487350"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cssc.201501116","issn":["18645631","1864564X"],"issn_org":["18645631"],"issue":"22","journal":"ChemSusChem","pages":"3823-3831","publisher":"Chemistry Europe - European Chemical Societies Publishing","status":"p","title":"ChemSusChem","title_org":"ChemSusChem (Print)","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84948698133"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6b8d3748-c192-4815-82ea-275cc639095d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Seawater as Alternative to Freshwater in Pretreatment of Date Palm Residues for Bioethanol Production in Coastal and/or Arid Areas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808495","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Long-term trends in use of implantable cardioverter-defibrillators (ICDs) and outcomes are rare. OBJECTIVE: We examined 13-year nationwide trends in ICD implantation and survival rates in Denmark. METHODS: Using medical databases, we identified all first-time ICD implantations in Denmark during 2000-2012 (n=8,460) and ascertained all-cause mortality. We computed standardized annual implantation rates and mortality rate ratios according to age, sex, comorbidity, indication, and device type. RESULTS: The standardized annual implantation rate increased from 42 per million persons in 2000 to 213 in 2012 (from 34 to 174 for men and from 8 to 39 for women). The increase was driven by secondary prophylactic ICDs until 2006 and primary prophylactic ICDs thereafter. The increase occurred particularly among older patients and those with a high level of comorbidity. Independent of indication, 76% of all ICD patients were alive after five years. Men had a higher mortality rate compared with women (mortality rate ratio=1.28, 95% CI: 1.10-1.49). Compared with low comorbidity level, moderate, severe, and very severe comorbidity levels were associated with 1.6-fold, 2.5-fold, and 4.9-fold increased mortality rates, respectively. The most influential individual comorbidities were heart failure, diabetes, liver disease, and renal disease. CONCLUSION: The annual implantation rate of ICDs increased fivefold in Denmark between 2000 and 2012. The rate increase occurred for both men and women, but particularly among the elderly and patients with severe comorbidity. Five-year survival probability was high, but severe comorbidity and male gender were associated with shorter survival.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schmidt, Morten","Pedersen, Susanne Bendesgaard","Farkas, Dóra Kormendine","Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjær","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S02-096.51-011244"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000013 year nationwide trends in use of implantable cardioverter defibrillators and subsequent long term survival","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hrthm.2015.04.040","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.51-011244","identifier":[{"id":"25937527","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84939775678","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000360359000030","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-eb4a946a-673f-4fb6-aaf9-945cf8f5c856","au-f2fe2863-26d5-4edb-a71c-b78f708d12b8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E2E7D642F2F16A2CD84D15D565257312"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hrthm.2015.04.040","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susanne Bendesgaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"858eb103-7bd2-4736-b8ea-bb02d96d0169","name":"Pedersen, Susanne Bendesgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dóra Kormendine","key":"farkaspau","last":"Farkas","locid":"573f7202-6799-4977-bf11-f1e017ac21a2","name":"Farkas, Dóra Körmendiné","name_org":"Farkas, Dóra Kormendine","orcid":"0000-0002-8577-048X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Pihlkjær","key":"hjortshøjpau","last":"Hjortshøj","locid":"d24227f4-62ce-4a90-86ec-482cf4e88a34","name":"Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-4231-9963","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25937527"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.hrthm.2015.04.040","issn":["15475271","15563871"],"issn_org":["15475271"],"issue":"9","journal":"Heart Rhythm","pages":"2018-2027","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Heart Rhythm","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939775678"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-eb4a946a-673f-4fb6-aaf9-945cf8f5c856","au-f2fe2863-26d5-4edb-a71c-b78f708d12b8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Thirteen-year nationwide trends in use of implantable cardioverter-defibrillators and subsequent long-term survival","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.51-011244","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Pretreating lignocellulosic biomass for cellulosic ethanol production in a West African setting requires smaller scale and less capital expenditure compared to current state of the art. In the present study, three low-tech methods applicable for West African conditions, namely Boiling Pretreatment (BP), Soaking in Aqueous Ammonia (SAA) and White Rot Fungi pretreatment (WRF), were compared to the high-tech solution of hydrothermal pretreatment (HTT). The pretreatment methods were tested on 11 West African biomasses, i.e. cassava stalks, plantain peelings, plantain trunks, plantain leaves, cocoa husks, cocoa pods, maize cobs, maize stalks, rice straw, groundnut straw and oil palm empty fruit bunches. It was found that four biomass’ (plantain peelings, plantain trunks, maize cobs and maize stalks) were most promising for production of cellulosic ethanol with profitable enzymatic conversion of glucan (>30 g glucan per 100 g total solids (TS)). HTT did show better results in both enzymatic convertibility and fermentation, but evaluated on the overall ethanol yield the low-tech pretreatment methods are viable alternatives with similar levels to the HTT (13.4–15.2 g ethanol per 100 g TS raw material).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","Londoño, Jorge Enrique González","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Kádár, Zsófia"],"cuid":["S03-092.71-000852"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"corresponding_author":["Kádár, Zsófia"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute Center for Energy–iEnergy","Khalifa University of Science and Technology","Masdar Institute of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Biomass","Cellulosic ethanol","Lignocellulose","Pretreatment","West Africa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of different pretreatment strategies for ethanol production of west african biomass","src":["aau","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12010-014-1444-7","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-092.71-000852","identifier":[{"id":"84924085611","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25542239","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-1064b722-57e7-42a1-a76c-a085c95b5bcb","dtu-bfe8be38-7ad6-49e4-a1fd-f68747cec362","ku-78b2d51f-3e51-4b79-9989-88df4d759c0d"],"keyword":["Biomass","Cellulosic ethanol","Lignocellulose","Pretreatment","West Africa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-692D451BB53F351D879994A22932DA2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12010-014-1444-7","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Center for BioProcess Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Civil Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ae","key":"institute center for energy ienergy","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Institute Center for Energy–iEnergy","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ae","key":"khalifa university of science and technology","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Khalifa University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sune Tjalfe","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"48069d0c-8a66-43de-99ab-484cfa5ff52d","name":"Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","orcid":"0000-0002-6744-2642","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jorge Enrique","key":"gonzalezlondonopau","last":"Gonzalez Londono","locid":"75542888-9d8b-49be-ba55-55eb58b6e7fc","name":"Gonzalez Londono, Jorge Enrique","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"f3b10fc3-ff7d-440d-9ee8-921079f6e769","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zsófia","key":"kádárpau","last":"Kádár","locid":"8b49b135-09d1-4d2d-879c-5d8cb263be04","name":"Kádár, Zsófia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25542239"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12010-014-1444-7","issn":["02732289","15590291"],"issn_org":["02732289"],"issue":"5","journal":"Applied Biochemistry and Biotechnology","pages":"2589-2601","publisher":"Humana Press","status":"p","title":"Applied Biochemistry and Biotechnology","volume":"175"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924085611"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1064b722-57e7-42a1-a76c-a085c95b5bcb","dtu-bfe8be38-7ad6-49e4-a1fd-f68747cec362","ku-78b2d51f-3e51-4b79-9989-88df4d759c0d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparison of Different Pretreatment Strategies for Ethanol Production of West African Biomass","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.71-000852","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Fejø, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-287575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what is an undertaking in eu competition law","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-287575","ids":["cbs-7ffed7a5-f3f8-4123-8d72-ec7b95eb6a10"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FD22C8C894E9E27F62AA7D1B39681FBA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Business Humanities and Law, CBS LAW"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"fejøpau","last":"Fejø","locid":"71ce3eb1-5e68-43c0-8454-a5f3dbb47abf","name":"Fejø, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"arntnielsenpedh","last":"Arnt Nielsen","name":"Arnt Nielsen, Peter","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"koerverschmidtpedh","last":"Koerver Schmidt","name":"Koerver Schmidt, Peter","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Katja","key":"dyppelweberpedh","last":"Dyppel Weber","name":"Dyppel Weber, Katja","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788757435245"],"pages":"33-49","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Juridisk Institut CBS","title":"Erhvervsretlige emner"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-7ffed7a5-f3f8-4123-8d72-ec7b95eb6a10"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"What is an Undertaking in EU Competition Law?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-287575","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Agriculture is expected to contribute in substituting of fossil fuels in the future. This constitutes a paradox as agriculture depends heavily on fossil energy for providing fuel, fodder, nutrients, and machinery. The aim of this paper is to investigate whether organic agriculture is capable of providing both food and surplus energy to the society as evalu - ated from a model study. We evaluated bioenergy technologies in a Danish dairy-farming context in four different scenarios: (1) vegetable oil based on oilseed rape, (2) biogas based on cattle manure and grass-clover lays, (3) bioethanol from rye grain and whey, and (4) a combination of (1) and (2). When assessing the energetic net-contribution to society from bioenergy systems, two types of problems arise: how to aggregate non-equivalent types of energy services and how to account for non-equivalent types of inputs and coproducts from the farming? To avoid the first type, the net output of liquid fuels, electricity, useful heat, and food were calculated separately. Furthermore, to avoid the second type, all scenarios were designed to provide self-sufficiency with fodder and fertilizer and to utilize coproducts within the system. This approach resulted in a transparent assessment of the net-contribution to society, which is easy to interpret. We conclude that if 20% of land is used for energy crops, farm-gate energy self-sufficiency can be achieved at the cost of 17% reduction in amount of food produced. These results demonstrate the strong limitations for (organic) agriculture in providing both food and surplus energy.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Markussen, Mads Ville","Pugesgaard, Siri","Oleskowicz-Popiel, Piotr","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Østergård, Hanne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316104"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bioethanol","Biogas","Dairy farms","Net energy","Organic farming","Self sufficiency","Vegetable oil"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"net energy analysis of integrated food and bioenergy systems exemplified by a model of a self sufficinet system of dairy farms","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fenrg.2015.00049","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316104","identifier":[{"id":"85058053932","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-26d68b2d-58dc-4654-b5ca-e207f09b01b7"],"keyword":["Bioethanol","Biogas","Dairy farms","Net-energy","Organic farming","Self-sufficiency","Vegetable oil"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C0D3A2609809DAE8ACE1EE60DDAD826"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fenrg.2015.00049","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/118549331/Markussen_et_al_Bioenergy_Frontiers_2015.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Ville","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","locid":"813275b5-9ee4-4285-9a50-543a4a1a7853","name":"Markussen, Mads Ville","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siri","key":"pugesgaardpau","last":"Pugesgaard","name":"Pugesgaard, Siri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Piotr","key":"oleskowiczpopielpau","last":"Oleskowicz-Popiel","locid":"f20fe170-864a-46ab-ab59-6472bc7e9a54","name":"Oleskowicz-Popiel, Piotr","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"4f0d57ca-a0c5-43cf-ada5-378c053ab8c7","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne","key":"østergårdpau","last":"Østergård","locid":"4bb69d26-b003-44ef-94c9-01e57fbf15a6","name":"Østergård, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0001-6131-5717","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fenrg.2015.00049","issn":["2296598X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Energy Research","paperid":"49","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","publisher_org":"Frontiers Media S.A.","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Energy Research","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058053932"],"sdg":["2. Zero Hunger","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-26d68b2d-58dc-4654-b5ca-e207f09b01b7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Net-energy analysis of integrated food and bioenergy systems exemplified by a model of a self-sufficinet system of dairy farms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316104","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Chronic heart failure (HF) is characterized by reduced serum T3 levels and increased activity of the T3 degrading enzyme deiodinase D3. This may result in an intracellular composition of the cardiomyocyte mimicking that of hypothyroidism. Short-term T3-administration to systolic HF patients might be beneficial. QUESTION: Does long-term treatment with T3 have a beneficial effect on cardiac function and neurohormonal activation in chronic systolic HF patients with serum T3 levels below 1·6 nmol/l? DESIGN: A randomized, double-blind, cross-over, placebo-controlled intervention study with oral T3 treatment twice daily for 3 months. The T3 dose was uptitrated to a final dose avoiding reduced TSH levels. PRIMARY END-POINT: Left-ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF). METHODS: Cardiac imaging was performed using multiple gated tomographic radionuclide ventriculography (MUGA-SPECT). Neurohormonal stimulation was evaluated by plasma measurements of natriuretic peptides, aldosterone, renin, noradrenalin and copeptin levels. The patients were monitored for potential cardiac arrhythmias at the start of each treatment period. RESULTS: Thirteen patients completed the protocol. Mean LVEF was 43%, range: 37-52 and serum T3 levels 1·4 nmol/l (0·9-1·6). The T3 dose was 20 μg per day (10-40). TSH levels did not change between groups, whereas serum T3 levels increased in the active arm. Cardiac function as measured by LVEF, end-diastolic and end-systolic volumes and cardiac output did not change during T3-treatment and neither did the neurohormonal profile. There were no side-effects in terms of cardiac arrhythmias and no change in resting heart rate. CONCLUSIONS: This study does not support the hypothesis that oral T3 treatment might be beneficial to patients with chronic, stable systolic HF with a modest degree of reduced LVEF and low-normal serum T3 concentrations. The study included both functional studies of heart contractility as well as measures of the neurohormonal activation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Holmager, Pernille","Schmidt, Ulla","Mark, Peter","Andersen, Ulrik","Dominguez, Helena","Raymond, Ilan","Zerahn, Bo","Nygaard, Birte","Kistorp, Caroline","Faber, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-404163"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term l triiodothyronine t000000000003 treatment in stable systolic heart failure patients a randomised double blind cross over placebo controlled intervention study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-404163","identifier":[{"id":"84919775434","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25359424","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1217b5a0-53a3-49ed-afc7-f536eaef5ac8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B69C4A431869742AE232F8D7EDF3D095"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Pernille","key":"holmagerpau","last":"Holmager","name":"Holmager, Pernille","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulla","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Ulla","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"markpau","last":"Mark","name":"Mark, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulrik","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Ulrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helena","key":"dominguezpau","last":"Dominguez","name":"Dominguez, Helena","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ilan","key":"raymondpau","last":"Raymond","name":"Raymond, Ilan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo","key":"zerahnpau","last":"Zerahn","name":"Zerahn, Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birte","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","name":"Nygaard, Birte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Caroline","key":"kistorppau","last":"Kistorp","locid":"42328645-d772-4f53-9f70-438ff40291b9","name":"Kistorp, Caroline","orcid":"0000-0002-3019-6775","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"42925e6e-5e0c-475f-aca8-13159f10abc7","name":"Faber, Jens","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25359424"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cen.12648","issn":["03000664","13652265"],"issn_org":["03000664"],"issue":"6","journal":"Clinical Endocrinology","pages":"931-937","status":"p","title":"Clinical Endocrinology","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84919775434"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1217b5a0-53a3-49ed-afc7-f536eaef5ac8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term L-Triiodothyronine (T3) treatment in stable systolic heart failure patients : a randomised, double-blind, cross-over, placebo-controlled intervention study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-404163","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Schmidt, Sidsel Birkelund","Persson, Daniel Olof","Powikrowska, Marta","Frydenvang, Jens","Schjørring, Jan Kofod","Jensen, Poul Erik","Husted, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-406446"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metal binding in photosystem ii super and subcomplexes from barley thylakoids","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-406446","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4528757","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26084923","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84939207920","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-15c9f1b1-ed24-4bb4-a7ed-69c2057998b0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A75F03201E537DFA3A36F71640EA42C6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant and Soil Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sidsel Birkelund","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"897894ee-b8f2-4718-b15a-404476b6e5f1","name":"Schmidt, Sidsel Birkelund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel Olof","key":"perssonpau","last":"Persson","locid":"6897c9d6-c31c-4b1f-9390-f81a3e727187","name":"Persson, Daniel Olof","orcid":"0000-0003-3976-190X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marta","key":"powikrowskapau","last":"Powikrowska","locid":"487f877f-fb04-45bb-9057-661880a8280b","name":"Powikrowska, Marta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"frydenvangpau","last":"Frydenvang","locid":"133c00bf-5214-4309-9c86-e211d48b5097","name":"Frydenvang, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-9294-1227","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Kofod","key":"schjørringpau","last":"Schjørring","locid":"27ae87a2-1631-4248-93bc-ed9a98e8785d","name":"Schjørring, Jan Kofod","orcid":"0000-0002-2852-3298","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Poul Erik","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"cb8fdf4a-6052-43b4-b731-384346885e4d","name":"Jensen, Poul Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6524-7723","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"hustedpau","last":"Husted","locid":"8d9d5df0-e48a-4f38-a4a8-46baf7fd6621","name":"Husted, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-2020-1902","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26084923"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1104/pp.15.00559","issn":["00320889","15322548"],"issn_org":["00320889"],"issue":"4","journal":"Plant Physiology","pages":"1490-1502","status":"p","title":"Plant Physiology","volume":"168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939207920"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-15c9f1b1-ed24-4bb4-a7ed-69c2057998b0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Metal binding in photosystem II super- and subcomplexes from barley thylakoids","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-406446","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Context: GLP-1 analogues have recently been promoted as anti-hyperglycemic agents in critically ill patients with systemic inflammation, but the effects of TNF-α on glucose metabolism during GLP-1 administration are unknown. Objective: To determine whether infusion of TNF-α at high physiological levels impairs GLP-1's effects on glucose metabolism. Design: Randomized, controlled, cross-over trial. Setting: Hospital clinical research laboratory. Participants: Twelve healthy males (age 24±3 y; BMI 22.9±1.3 kg/m(2)). Interventions: Following an overnight fast, either saline (0.9%) or recombinant human TNF-α (1000 ng/m(2)/h) was infused from t = 0-6 hours. At t = 2 hours, GLP-1 infusion (0.5 pmol/kg/min) began. From t = 4-6 hours, the GLP-1 infusion rate was increased to 1.2 pmol/kg/min. Plasma glucose was clamped at 5 mmol/L throughout via a variable-rate 20% dextrose infusion. Trials were 7-14 days apart. Main outcome measures: Endogenous glucose production (EGP) was measured by [6,6-(2)H2]glucose isotope tracer dilution method. Results: GLP-1 infusion suppressed plasma glucagon (P<0.01), elevated plasma insulin and C-peptide (P<0.01), and suppressed EGP (P<0.001) during saline infusion. In contrast, infusion of TNF-α increased plasma TNF-α and IL-6, elevated body temperature, and blunted the GLP-1-induced suppression of EGP during high dose GLP-1 infusion (all P<0.05, TNF-α vs. saline). However, TNF-α infusion lowered plasma GLP-1 during high dose GLP-1 infusion (P<0.001). Conclusions: TNF-α induces systemic inflammation and reduces plasma GLP-1, thereby reducing the suppression of EGP during GLP-1 infusion. This may have clinical relevance if GLP-1 analogue drugs are used for the treatment of hyperglycemia in critically ill patients.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lehrskov-Schmidt, Louise","Lehrskov-Schmidt, Lars","Nielsen, Signe T","Holst, Jens Juul","Møller, Kirsten","Solomon, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503901"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of tnf α on glp 000000000001 stimulated plasma glucose kinetics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-503901","identifier":[{"id":"84927615412","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25675385","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b90b2ecb-0569-4e9e-9405-bc7a752dda0f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA94327F6AC69196053159957F15B328"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"lehrskovschmidtlouisepau","last":"Lehrskov-Schmidt","name":"Lehrskov-Schmidt, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"lehrskovschmidtlarspau","last":"Lehrskov-Schmidt","name":"Lehrskov-Schmidt, Lars","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe T","key":"nielsensignetpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Signe T","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstjensjuulpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten","key":"møllerkirstenpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Kirsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas P J","key":"solomonthomaspau","last":"Solomon","locid":"c869ee86-bba2-4b49-bd24-17f5654c9cff","name":"Solomon, Thomas","name_org":"Solomon, Thomas P J","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25675385"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2014-4244","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of clinical endocrinology and metabolism","volume":"100"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84927615412"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b90b2ecb-0569-4e9e-9405-bc7a752dda0f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of TNF-α on GLP-1-stimulated plasma glucose kinetics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503901","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Wheeler, Helen","Høye, Toke Thomas","Schmidt, Niels Martin","Svenning, Jens Christian","Forchhammer, Mads C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-181682"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phenological mismatch with abiotic conditions implications for flowering in arctic plants","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1890/14-0338.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-181682","identifier":[{"id":"26236873","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84929657390","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5bca1cb1-9610-458c-bc99-57b67236f3fe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7EEE628BC4DF8FEF4B5836D9D32A36BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1890/14-0338.1","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Ecoinformatics and Biodiversity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H.C.","key":"wheelerpau","last":"Wheeler","locid":"1376a799-376f-4d76-a4f6-0cd291191eb2","name":"Wheeler, Helen","name_org":"Wheeler, H.C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke Thomas","key":"høyepau","last":"Høye","locid":"3dd7f6f7-5f2a-481f-ac0f-e2315af69467","name":"Høye, Toke Thomas","orcid":"0000-0001-5387-3284","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b91704ca-e126-4c35-af20-95b2269d230a","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-6218","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.-C.","key":"svenningpau","last":"Svenning","locid":"33c3c4e2-57ab-478c-889d-06c594e57b8b","name":"Svenning, Jens Christian","name_org":"Svenning, J.-C.","orcid":"0000-0002-3415-0862","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads C.","key":"forchhammerpau","last":"Forchhammer","locid":"7045087f-4763-4cbf-8264-0f4af36bc6d9","name":"Forchhammer, Mads C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26236873"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1890/14-0338.1","issn":["00129658","19399170"],"issn_org":["00129658"],"issue":"3","journal":"Ecology","pages":"775-787","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Ecology","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84929657390"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5bca1cb1-9610-458c-bc99-57b67236f3fe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Phenological mismatch with abiotic conditions - implications for flowering in Arctic plants","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-181682","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Stenting of the iliac veins has been an established treatment for improving venous runoff from the legs after thrombolysis of iliofemoral deep venous thrombosis for more than a decade, yet little is known about the long-term fate of stents in the central veins. We describe a case of heavily calcified in-stent restenosis in a 10-year-old venous stent as well as a way of treating this rare condition. With growing numbers of venous stents reaching a significant age, a need for treatment of long-term complications like the one presented here most probably will arise.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schmidt, Jens-Ove","Christensen, Johnny","Houlind, Kim Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-588986"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"calcified in stent restenosis in a venous stent","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jvsc.2015.07.008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-588986","identifier":[{"id":"84946401127","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-373de619-7907-4135-a319-b92e561e818a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E3A81A3812272C1BD43665ADAE305B1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jvsc.2015.07.008","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121233402/1_s2.0_S2352667X15001009_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Vascular Surgery (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens-Ove","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"8939f183-b866-46c8-aff8-748037bd1fe9","name":"Schmidt, Jens-Ove","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johnny","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"1662a091-edbf-4237-888e-09a4191279ab","name":"Christensen, Johnny","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kim Christian","key":"houlindpau","last":"Houlind","locid":"405b9fac-bba4-46ff-8d96-f40eeee21d12","name":"Houlind, Kim Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1600-4415","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jvsc.2015.07.008","issn":["2352667X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Vascular Surgery Cases","pages":"261-263","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Vascular Surgery Cases","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84946401127"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-373de619-7907-4135-a319-b92e561e818a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Calcified in-stent restenosis in a venous stent","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-588986","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundIn the past decade, early treatment of cardiac arrest (CA) victims has been improved in several ways, leading to more optimistic over all prognoses. However, the global survival rate after out-of-hospital CA (OHCA) is still not more than 5-10%. With a better knowledge of the predictors for outcome among CA patients, we can improve the management of CA, in order to strengthen the leads in the chain of survival.MethodsA retrospective cohort study including 172 CA patients admitted to the intensive care unit (ICU) in Odense University Hospital (OUH) in a three-year period was conducted. We determined the 90-day mortality and neurological outcome at discharge for CA patients treated with therapeutic hypothermia (TH), in regard to determine the importance of the predictors for mortality and neurological outcome, with emphasize on combining initial rhythm and time to return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC).ResultsThe overall mortality was 44% and a favorable neurological outcome was seen among 52%. Strong predictors for survival and favorable neurological outcome were ventricular tachycardia/ventricular fibrillation (VT/VF) as initial rhythm, cardiac etiology and time to ROSC¿<¿20 minutes. Age¿<¿60 years was a predictor for survival only. Patients with the combination of VT/VF and ROSC¿<¿20 minutes had undeniably the best chance of both survival and a favorable neurological outcome.ConclusionsWe found significant predictors for both survival and neurological outcome, in which an initial rhythm of VT/VF and a cardiac etiology were the strongest.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wibrandt-Johansen, Ida Maria","Norsted, Kristine","Schmidt, Henrik","Schierbeck, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-600442"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Female","Heart Arrest mortality","Humans","Hypothermia Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest mortality","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Survival Rate","Time Factors","Ventricular Fibrillation etiology","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predictors for outcome among cardiac arrest patients the importance of initial cardiac arrest rhythm versus time to return of spontaneous circulation a retrospective cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129580950/Predictors_for_outcome_among_cardiac_arrest_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-600442","identifier":[{"id":"84924035264","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25648841","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4320834","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-5f4368a4-4805-4906-b1dc-009f5202b5b7"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Female","Heart Arrest/mortality","Humans","Hypothermia, Induced","Male","Middle Aged","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest/mortality","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Survival Rate","Tachycardia, Ventricular/etiology","Time Factors","Ventricular Fibrillation/etiology","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8A05113F02293ADAC220DE9263FB14B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129580950/Predictors_for_outcome_among_cardiac_arrest_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12873-015-0028-3","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Maria","key":"wibrandtjohansenpau","last":"Wibrandt-Johansen","locid":"6bc20c92-f7e5-4210-8bfa-0755e6f4e247","name":"Wibrandt-Johansen, Ida Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine","key":"norstedpau","last":"Norsted","name":"Norsted, Kristine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"9789920f-4b31-4f28-8211-97afced9d61e","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"schierbeckpau","last":"Schierbeck","locid":"166d4f2f-d76e-4dee-bf5f-7cefc440807e","name":"Schierbeck, Jens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25648841"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12873-015-0028-3","issn":["1471227X"],"issue":"February","journal":"BMC Emergency Medicine","paperid":"3","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Emergency Medicine","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924035264"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5f4368a4-4805-4906-b1dc-009f5202b5b7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Predictors for outcome among cardiac arrest patients : the importance of initial cardiac arrest rhythm versus time to return of spontaneous circulation, a retrospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-600442","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The prognostic impact of preadmission use of calcium channel blockers (CCBs) and beta blockers (BBs) on stroke mortality remains unclear. We aimed to examine whether preadmission use of CCBs or BBs was associated with improved short-term mortality following ischemic stroke, intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH), or subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH). METHODS: We conducted a nationwide population-based cohort study using Danish medical registries. We identified all patients with a first-time inpatient diagnosis of stroke between 2004 and 2012 and their comorbidities. We defined CCB/BB use as current use, former use, or non-use. Current use was further classified as new or long-term use. We used Cox regression modeling to compute 30-day mortality rate ratios (MRRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs), controlling for potential confounders. RESULTS: We identified 100,043 patients with a first-time stroke. Of these, 83,736 (83.7%) patients had ischemic stroke, 11,779 (11.8%) had ICH, and 4,528 (4.5%) had SAH. Comparing current users of CCBs or BBs with non-users, we found no association with mortality for ischemic stroke [adjusted 30-day MRR = 0.99 (95% CI: 0.94-1.05) for CCBs and 1.01 (95% CI: 0.96-1.07) for BBs], ICH [adjusted 30-day MRR = 1.05 (95% CI: 0.95-1.16) for CCBs and 0.95 (95% CI: 0.87-1.04) for BBs], or SAH [adjusted 30-day MRR = 1.05 (95% CI: 0.85-1.29) for CCBs and 0.89 (95% CI: 0.72-1.11) for BBs]. Former use of CCBs or BBs was not associated with mortality. CONCLUSIONS: Preadmission use of CCBs or BBs was not associated with 30-day mortality following ischemic stroke, ICH, or SAH.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sundbøll, Jens","Schmidt, Morten","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","Pedersen, Lars","Bøtker, Hans Erik","Sørensen, Henrik Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-198024"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of preadmission treatment with calcium channel blockers or beta blockers on short term mortality after stroke a nationwide cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12883-015-0279-3","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-198024","identifier":[{"id":"84928231319","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25783545","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-781015cc-cdea-4205-b5f0-8255c926ebcc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59BD5B91E671C0A10E0F444A252D6726"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12883-015-0279-3","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"21e3a3e6-e25e-48cf-b243-b8f43dca3bb8","name":"Schmidt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4935-4059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erzsébet","key":"horváthpuhópau","last":"Horváth-Puhó","locid":"20f5c6bd-6ac1-4edb-a393-f34d60db546c","name":"Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","orcid":"0000-0002-3594-2212","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian F","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"b1104ec4-1322-428f-af8f-7771361930bb","name":"Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","name_org":"Christiansen, Christian F","orcid":"0000-0002-0727-953X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"45a14ac2-d69c-426f-9790-99740888db24","name":"Pedersen, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Erik","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"09b03c00-11a8-4f72-800f-181f26155750","name":"Bøtker, Hans Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-6358-8962","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25783545"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12883-015-0279-3","issn":["14712377"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Neurology","pages":"279","paperid":"24","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Neurology","title_org":"B M C Neurology","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84928231319"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-781015cc-cdea-4205-b5f0-8255c926ebcc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Impact of preadmission treatment with calcium channel blockers or beta blockers on short-term mortality after stroke : a nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-198024","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Biodegradation is one of the most favored and sustainable means of removing organic pollutants from contaminated aquifers but the major steering factors are still surprisingly poorly understood. Growing evidence questions some of the established concepts for control of biodegradation. Here, we critically discuss classical concepts such as the thermodynamic redox zonation, or the use of steady state transport scenarios for assessing biodegradation rates. Furthermore, we discuss if the absence of specific degrader populations can explain poor biodegradation. We propose updated perspectives on the controls of biodegradation in contaminant plumes. These include the plume fringe concept, transport limitations, and transient conditions as currently underestimated processes affecting biodegradation.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Meckenstock, Rainer U.","Elsner, Martin","Griebler, Christian","Lueders, Tillmann","Stumpp, Christine","Aamand, Jens","Agathos, Spiros N.","Albrechtsen, Hans-Jørgen","Bastiaens, Leen","Bjerg, Poul Løgstrup","Boon, Nico","Dejonghe, Winnie","Huang, Wei E.","Schmidt, Susanne I.","Smolders, Erik","Sørensen, Sebastian R.","Springael, Dirk","van Breukelen, Boris M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-345305"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Flemish Institute for Technological Research","Ghent University","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","KU Leuven","University of Birmingham","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Oxford","Université catholique de Louvain","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biodegradation updating the concepts of control for microbial cleanup in contaminated aquifers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/144911080/Meckenstock_RU_2015_Biodegradation_Updating_the_concepts_of_control_for_microbial.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-345305","identifier":[{"id":"84934986610","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26000605","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-88a29cdb-996e-4fd6-899c-d2f887f10eb8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DBA0656741DE56DF941DF1CD1E6AA2D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/144911080/Meckenstock_RU_2015_Biodegradation_Updating_the_concepts_of_control_for_microbial.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of duisburg essen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Duisburg-Essen","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"helmholtz zentrum münchen german research center for environmental health","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"université catholique de louvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université catholique