{"abstract":"In recent years the focus on sustainable biofuel production from agricultural residues has increased considerably. However, the scientific work within this field has predominantly been concentrated upon bioresources from industrialised and newly industrialised countries, while analyses of the residues from most developing countries remain sparse. In this study the theoretical bioenergy potentials (bioethanol and biogas) of a spectrum of West African agricultural residues were estimated based on their compositions. We analysed 13 of the most common residues: yam peelings, cassava peelings, cassava stalks, plantain peelings, plantain trunks, plantain leaves, cocoa husks, cocoa pods, maize cobs, maize stalks, rice straw, groundnut straw and oil palm empty fruit bunches. The yam peelings showed the highest methane and bioethanol potentials, with 439 L methane (kg Total Solids)−1 and 0.61 L bioethanol (kg TS)−1 based on starch and cellulose alone due to their high starch content and low content of un-biodegradable lignin and ash. A complete biomass balance was done for each of the 13 residues, providing a basis for further research into the production of biofuels or biorefining from West African agricultural residues.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","Kádár, Zsófia","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S02-095.50-036163"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bioethanol","Biogas","Biomass","Composition","Residue","West Africa"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"compositional analysis and projected biofuel potentials from common west african agricultural residues","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2014.01.045","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.50-036163","identifier":[{"id":"84897466411","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9d3b6bb5-6148-4102-b89a-0cf78c38bb27","ku-3d65e8e6-a3a0-4b8b-ba35-6beefeb66f1a"],"keyword":["Bioethanol","Biogas","Biomass","Composition","Residue","West Africa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-64779302D4EBBDAB8A0F3C0F52AD50BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2014.01.045","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Center for BioProcess Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sune Tjalfe","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"48069d0c-8a66-43de-99ab-484cfa5ff52d","name":"Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","orcid":"0000-0002-6744-2642","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zsófia","key":"kádárpau","last":"Kádár","locid":"77632fb2-eb08-43a2-b320-3d9133ba2a88","name":"Kádár, Zsófia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"4f0d57ca-a0c5-43cf-ada5-378c053ab8c7","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2014.01.045","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","pages":"210-217","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","title_org":"Biomass and Bioenergy","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897466411"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9d3b6bb5-6148-4102-b89a-0cf78c38bb27","ku-3d65e8e6-a3a0-4b8b-ba35-6beefeb66f1a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Compositional analysis and projected biofuel potentials from common West African agricultural residues","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.50-036163","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIM: The prognostic impact of ACE inhibitors (ACE-Is) or angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs) on stroke mortality remains unclear. We aimed to examine whether prestroke use of ACE-Is or ARBs was associated with improved short-term mortality following ischaemic stroke, intracerebral haemorrhage (ICH) and subarachnoid haemorrhage (SAH). METHODS: We conducted a nationwide population-based cohort study using medical registries in Denmark. We identified all first-time stroke patients during 2004-2012 and their comorbidities. We defined ACE-I/ARB use as current use (last prescription redemption <90 days before admission for stroke), former use and non-use. Current use was further classified as new or long-term use. We used Cox regression modelling to compute 30-day mortality rate ratios (MRRs) with 95% CIs, controlling for potential confounders. RESULTS: We identified 100 043 patients with a first-time stroke. Of these, 83 736 patients had ischaemic stroke, 11 779 had ICH, and 4528 had SAH. For ischaemic stroke, the adjusted 30-day MRR was reduced in current users compared with non-users (0.85, 95% CI 0.81 to 0.89). There was no reduction in the adjusted 30-day MRR for ICH (0.95, 95% CI 0.87 to 1.03) or SAH (1.01, 95% CI 0.84 to 1.21), comparing current users with non-users. No association with mortality was found among former users compared with non-users. No notable modification of the association was observed within sex or age strata. CONCLUSIONS: Current use of ACE-Is/ARBs was associated with reduced 30-day mortality among patients with ischaemic stroke. We found no association among patients with ICH or SAH.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sundbøll, Jens","Schmidt, Morten","Horváth-Puhó, Erzsébet","Christiansen, Christian Fynbo","Pedersen, L","Bøtker, He","Sørensen, Ht"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-143194"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preadmission use of ace inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and short term mortality after stroke","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/jnnp-2014-308948","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-143194","identifier":[{"id":"25209418","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84939225923","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-18222d24-6011-4ae2-bb8c-d7c878bc3392"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B7DAF0351CE2EDFBAF56FD9D4EE018ED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/jnnp-2014-308948","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"sundbøllpau","last":"Sundbøll","locid":"47396c7b-4f59-4aef-9cb1-0c63a6a8bbe2","name":"Sundbøll, Jens","name_org":"Sundbøll, J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pa