{"abstract":"Aim: The polyphenol resveratrol has in animal studies been shown to influence several pathways of importance for angiogenesis in skeletal muscle. The aim was to examine the angiogenic effect of resveratrol supplementation with parallel exercise training in aged men. Methods: Forty-three healthy physically inactive aged men (65±1 years) were divided into A) a training group that conducted 8 weeks of intense exercise training where half of the subjects received a daily intake of either 250 mg trans resveratrol (n=14) and the other half received placebo (n=13); and B) a non-training group that received either 250 mg trans resveratrol (n=9) or placebo (n=7). Results: The group that trained with placebo showed a ~20% increase in capillary to fiber (C:F) ratio, an increase in the muscle protein expression of vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF), VEGF receptor-2, and tissue inhibitor of matrix metalloproteinase (TIMP-1) but unaltered thrombospodin-1 (TSP-1) levels. Muscle interstitial VEGF and TSP-1 protein levels were unchanged after the training period. The group training with resveratrol supplementation did not show an increase in C:F ratio or an increase in muscle VEGF protein. Muscle TIMP-1 protein levels were lower in the training and resveratrol group than in the training and placebo group. Both training groups showed an increase in Forkhead box O1 protein. In the non-training groups, TIMP-1 protein was lower in the resveratrol group than the placebo group after 8 weeks. Conclusion: These data show that exercise training has a strong angiogenic effect whereas resveratrol supplementation may limit basal and training-induced angiogenesis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gliemann, Lasse","Olesen, Jesper","Biensø, Rasmus Sjørup","Schmidt, Jakob Friis","Åkerström, Thorbjörn","Nyberg, Michael Permin","Lindqvist, Anna Maria Charlotte K","Bangsbo, Jens","Hellsten, Ylva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489770"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resveratrol modulates the angiogenic response to exercise training in skeletal muscle of aged men","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpheart.00168.2014","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-489770","identifier":[{"id":"84908093903","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25128170","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a11772ea-a53c-445f-af77-c208dbebf37b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A040AF6561C90F205BEBD2DC2BD8B021"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpheart.00168.2014","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, PhD"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lasse","key":"gliemannhybholtpau","last":"Gliemann Hybholt","locid":"20155bf6-30de-4f27-b1d4-e5eb07d3ad7a","name":"Gliemann, Lasse","name_org":"Gliemann Hybholt, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-0382-2523","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"eaf9b770-cd72-45dd-9ca8-e0e4ecc19c11","name":"Olesen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus S","key":"biensøpau","last":"Biensø","locid":"c6f3c9d2-fa70-4da8-bafc-c37d0334c653","name":"Biensø, Rasmus Sjørup","name_org":"Biensø, Rasmus S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Friis","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"74b58d72-77a1-4d66-aaaa-c36189cbf0b6","name":"Schmidt, Jakob Friis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thorbjörn","key":"åkerströmpau","last":"Åkerström","locid":"44559d6f-7705-41e4-8c22-5fb0fe1c9b6d","name":"Åkerström, Thorbjörn","orcid":"0000-0002-7330-1723","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Permin","key":"nybergpau","last":"Nyberg","locid":"3a44876c-6484-4899-ade6-7e80d0483f3d","name":"Nyberg, Michael Permin","orcid":"0000-0002-3937-4697","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna","key":"lindqvistpau","last":"Lindqvist","locid":"70e5199d-5c8a-4c4e-8ccd-5e4fac31e0ed","name":"Lindqvist, Anna Maria Charlotte K","name_org":"Lindqvist, Anna","orcid":"0000-0003-4058-9932","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ylva","key":"hellstenpau","last":"Hellsten","locid":"902a8d03-73c1-41fa-a0a3-7f250470e2f0","name":"Hellsten, Ylva","orcid":"0000-0002-2435-9558","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25128170"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpheart.00168.2014","issn":["03636135","15221539"],"issn_org":["03636135"],"issue":"8","journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Heart and Circulatory Physiology","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Heart and Circulatory Physiology","volume":"307"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84908093903"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a11772ea-a53c-445f-af77-c208dbebf37b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resveratrol modulates the angiogenic response to exercise training in skeletal muscle of aged men","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489770","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This study examined the effect of recreational football and resistance training on bone mineral density (BMD) and bone turnover markers (BTMs) in elderly men. Twenty-six healthy sedentary men (age 68.2 ± 3.2 years) were randomized into three groups: football (F; n = 9) and resistance training (R; n = 9), completing 45-60 min training two to three times weekly, and inactive controls (C; n = 8). Before, after 4 months, and after 12 months, BMD in proximal femur (PF) and whole body (WB) were determined together with plasma osteocalcin (OC), procollagen type-1 amino-terminal propeptide (P1NP), and carboxy-terminal type-1 collagen crosslinks (CTX-1). In F, BMD in PF increased up to 1.8% (P < 0.05) from 0 to 4 months and up to 5.4% (P < 0.001) from 0 to 12 months; WB-BMD remained unchanged. After 4 and 12 months of football, OC was 45% and 46% higher (P < 0.001), and P1NP was 41% and 40% higher (P < 0.001) than at baseline, respectively. After 12 months, CTX-1 showed a main effect of 43% (P < 0.05). In R and C, BMD and BTM remained unchanged. In conclusion, 4 months of recreational football for elderly men had an osteogenic effect, which was further developed after 12 months, whereas resistance training had no effect. The anabolic response may be due to increased bone turnover, especially improved bone formation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Helge, Eva Wulff","Rostgaard Andersen, Thomas","Schmidt, Jakob Friis","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Hornstrup, Therese","Krustrup, Peter","Bangsbo, Jens"],"cuid":["S02-098.37-040717"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry Photon","Aged","Biomarkers","Bone Density","Collagen Type I","Comparative Study","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Osteocalcin","Peptide Fragments","Procollagen","Randomized Controlled Trial","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Resistance Training","Soccer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recreational football improves bone mineral density and bone turnover marker profile in elderly men","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.12239","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.37-040717","identifier":[{"id":"84902662313","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24903207","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1f403d4f-147d-4c91-99b4-75e7134ba037","sdu-50440cd9-ed03-4ea7-98e0-6f6294ed2bc6"],"keyword":["Absorptiometry, Photon","Aged","Biomarkers","Bone Density","Collagen Type I","Comparative Study","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Osteocalcin","Peptide Fragments","Procollagen","Randomized Controlled Trial","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Resistance Training","Soccer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0F419ECF3FE38AF78A3D9F147763EB46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.12239","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Movement and Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Glostrup Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Eva Wulff","key":"helgepau","last":"Helge","locid":"9bcf2b77-54e8-41d5-b356-d93a8350899b","name":"Helge, Eva Wulff","orcid":"0000-0002-4351-0137","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"rostgaardandersenpau","last":"Rostgaard Andersen","locid":"8f0fc396-7917-4d99-ba5d-33ddf19e9566","name":"Rostgaard Andersen, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Friis","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"74b58d72-77a1-4d66-aaaa-c36189cbf0b6","name":"Schmidt, Jakob Friis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Therese","key":"hornstruppau","last":"Hornstrup","locid":"a44d0bc0-e622-481b-ba67-4527d7ad6519","name":"Hornstrup, Therese","orcid":"0000-0001-6937-958X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"krustruppau","last":"Krustrup","locid":"9b334221-94f3-4a68-a2de-ee9f419704d8","name":"Krustrup, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9843-7320","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"bangsbopau","last":"Bangsbo","locid":"24839560-f889-42a6-9b73-97b69f101548","name":"Bangsbo, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1305-9274","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24903207"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sms.12239","issn":["09057188","16000838"],"issn_org":["09057188"],"issue":"Suppl 1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","pages":"98-104","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Medicine & Science in Sports","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902662313"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1f403d4f-147d-4c91-99b4-75e7134ba037","sdu-50440cd9-ed03-4ea7-98e0-6f6294ed2bc6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Recreational football improves bone mineral density and bone turnover marker profile in elderly men","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.37-040717","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We investigated the effects of 3 and 6 months of regular football training on cardiac structure and function in hypertensive men. Thirty-one untrained males with mild-to-moderate hypertension were randomized 2:1 to a football training group (n = 20) and a control group receiving traditional recommendations on healthy lifestyle (n = 11). Cardiac measures were evaluated by echocardiography. The football group exhibited significant (P < 0.05) changes in cardiac dimensions and function after just 3 months: Left ventricular (LV) end-diastolic volume increased from 104 ± 25 to 117 ± 29 mL. LV diastolic function improved measured as E/A ratio (1.15 ± 0.32 to 1.54 ± 0.38), early diastolic velocity, E' (11.0 ± 2.5 to 11.9 ± 2.6 cm/s), and isovolumetric relaxation time (74 ± 13 to 62 ± 13 ms). LV systolic function improved measured as longitudinal displacement (10.7 ± 2.1 to 12.1 ± 2.3 mm). Right ventricular function improved with respect to tricuspid annular plane systolic excursion (21.8 ± 3.2 to 24.5 ± 3.7 mm). Arterial blood pressure decreased in both groups, but significantly more in the football training group. No significant changes were observed in the control group. In conclusion, short-term football training improves LV diastolic function in untrained men with mild-to-moderate arterial hypertension. Furthermore, it may improve longitudinal systolic function of both ventricles. The results suggest that football training has favorable effects on cardiac function in hypertensive men.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, L. J.","Randers, M. B.","Hansen, P. R.","Hornstrup, T.","Schmidt, J. F.","Dvorak, J.","Søgaard, Peter","Krustrup, P.","Bangsbo, J."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-006179"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","F-MARC","FIFA Medical Assessment and Research Centre (F-MARC) and Schulthess Klinik, Zurich","Schulthess Klinik, Zürich","University of Exeter"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Pressure Determination","Exercise Test","Exercise Therapy","Heart Ventricles","Humans","Hypertension","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Oxygen Consumption","Randomized Controlled Trial","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Soccer","Treatment Outcome","Ultrasonography Doppler Pulsed","Ventricular Function Left","Ventricular Function Right"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["FIFA Medical Assessment and Research Centre (F-MARC)"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structural and functional cardiac adaptations to 000000000006 months of football training in untrained hypertensive men","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sms.12237","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-006179","identifier":[{"id":"24903081","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000337640300005","type":"wos"},{"id":"84902660967","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7f8f2ebf-5dd0-4199-8cd5-8d9c9b07a2ee","ku-da3627e3-ec90-445d-ae5c-dfb5921694b9","sdu-b207b107-8ac4-4a5f-b707-bc4f359a99a7"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Pressure Determination","Exercise Test","Exercise Therapy","Heart Ventricles","Humans","Hypertension","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Oxygen Consumption","Randomized Controlled Trial","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Soccer","Treatment Outcome","Ultrasonography, Doppler, Pulsed","Ventricular Function, Left","Ventricular Function, Right"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],