{"abstract":"An experimental program was carried out to investigate the behaviour of high performance concrete (HPC) thin plates in fire for use in sandwich panels. To reveal the influence of moisture two initial moisture contents for wet and dry samples were examined. In addition, two thicknesses were used to disclose the temperature distributions during the test. A non-linear coupled model for time dependent heat and mass transfer in concrete thin plates was used for temperature and pore pressure computations. Results from modelling and tests are compared and discussed. Moisture content was found to be a critical parameter in the spalling process. The calculated pore pressure induced too low tensile stresses in the matrix to trigger failure, suggesting a major role played by thermal stresses","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hulin, Thomas","Hodicky, Kamil","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Nielsen, Jens Henrik","Stang, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-320265"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-04","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2013-09-02","title":"5th International Conference on Structural Engineering, Mechanics and Computation","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a model for spalling of hpc thin plates exposed to fire","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/b15963-302","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-320265","identifier":[{"id":"84889051019","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-34b7b493-b1b5-4d23-ae13-7fefd5118f68"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-46912508729429D6C7E2826B16BA595E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1201/b15963-302","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Section for Structural Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"hulinpau","last":"Hulin","locid":"9bdd0adf-855a-453d-902b-ac128bdc7b5f","name":"Hulin, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kamil","key":"hodickypau","last":"Hodicky","locid":"0107b990-508e-4331-9d2a-fd863888e565","name":"Hodicky, Kamil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"2a187e49-ed7b-44eb-a0d4-f9d00cc245ce","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1153cf58-bb0e-42da-a4d0-1ea0dd13b752","name":"Nielsen, Jens Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0705-9382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"stangpau","last":"Stang","locid":"57fe0e89-5130-43bb-a270-b38b7f8b885e","name":"Stang, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-5812-4028","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1201/b15963-302","isbn":["9781138000612"],"pages":"1685-1690","publisher":"CRC Press","status":"p","title":"Research and Applications in Structural Engineering, Mechanics and Computation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84889051019"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-34b7b493-b1b5-4d23-ae13-7fefd5118f68"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A model for spalling of HPC thin plates exposed to fire","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-320265","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A high-caloric intake combined with a sedentary lifestyle is an important player in the development of type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM). The present study was undertaken to examine if the level of physical activity has impact on the metabolic effects of a high-caloric (+2,000 kcal/day) intake. Therefore, healthy individuals on a high caloric intake were randomized to either 10,000 or 1,500 steps per day for 14 days. Step-number, total energy expenditure, dietary records, neuropsychological tests, maximal oxygen uptake (VO2max), whole body dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DXA)- and abdominal magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)- scans, continuous glucose monitoring (CGM), and oral glucose tolerance tests (OGTT) with stable isotopes were performed before and after the intervention. Both study groups gained the same amount of body weight. However, the inactive group accumulated significantly more visceral fat compared to the active group. Following the two-week period, the inactive group also experienced a poorer glycaemic control, increased endogenous glucose production, decreased hepatic insulin extraction, increased baseline plasma levels of total cholesterol and LDL, and a decreased cognitive function with regard to capacity of attention. In conclusion, we find evidence to support that habitual physical activity may prevent pathophysiological symptoms associated with diet-induced obesity.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Krogh-Madsen, Rikke","Pedersen, Maria","Solomon, Thomas","Knudsen, Sine Haugaard","Hansen, Louise Seier","Karstoft, Kristian","Lehrskov-Schmidt, Louise","Pedersen, Karin Kaereby","Thomsen, Carsten","Holst, Jens Juul","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-450546"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"normal physical activity obliterates the deleterious effects of high caloric intake","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/japplphysiol.00155.2013","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-450546","identifier":[{"id":"84893839748","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24201706","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5f64789a-0d0e-4011-a276-52b389603635"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7A559A0C18EB2C0C5F52B14247E45265"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1152/japplphysiol.00155.2013","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BSc + MSc programme"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"kroghmadsenrikkepau","last":"Krogh-Madsen","locid":"5baab859-52d2-4a53-b243-d718f00f5c3a","name":"Krogh-Madsen, Rikke","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"pedersenmariapau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"17050e52-f326-4fe7-ac2f-88ff809e8812","name":"Pedersen, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"solomonthomaspau","last":"Solomon","locid":"c869ee86-bba2-4b49-bd24-17f5654c9cff","name":"Solomon, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sine Haugaard","key":"knudsensinehaugaardpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Sine Haugaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise Seier","key":"hansenlouiseseierpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Louise Seier","r