{"abstract":"Tutte proved that every 3-connected graph G on more than 4 vertices contains a contractible edge. We strengthen this result by showing that every depth-first-search tree of G contains a contractible edge. Moreover, we show that every spanning tree of G contains a contractible edge if G is 3-regular or if G does not contain two disjoint pairs of adjacent degree-3 vertices.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Elmasry, Amr Ahmed Abd Elmoneim","Mehlhorn, Kurt","Schmidt, Jens M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-487780"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","FU Berlin","MPI für informatik"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"every dfs tree of a 000000000003 connected graph contains a contractible edge","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-487780","identifier":[{"id":"84867896169","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9dd838a4-8183-461f-890a-3bfb0eacca5f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-76CE8E8B08C7B9DF66F23C35AFE2D5AE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"mpi für informatik","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"MPI für informatik","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"fu berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"FU Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Amr Ahmed Abd Elmoneim","key":"elmasrypau","last":"Elmasry","locid":"c957eece-f671-46d7-8bec-184d44665143","name":"Elmasry, Amr Ahmed Abd Elmoneim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kurt","key":"mehlhornpau","last":"Mehlhorn","name":"Mehlhorn, Kurt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jens M.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Jens M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jgt.21635","issn":["03649024","10970118"],"issn_org":["03649024"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Graph Theory","pages":"112-121","status":"p","title":"Journal of Graph Theory","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867896169"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9dd838a4-8183-461f-890a-3bfb0eacca5f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Every DFS tree of a 3-connected graph contains a contractible edge","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-487780","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to evaluate interpretations and the reproducibility of interpretations when looking at colposcopic photographs in a forensic setting, as well as discussing some of the dilemmas and pitfalls of forensic colposcopic photography. A total of 316 colposcopic photographs from 51 women taken on three occasions following consensual sexual intercourse, and 78 colposcopic photographs from 39 rape victims, were evaluated by four different observers. Photographs were taken in the same setting, by the same group of investigators, before and after application of toluidine blue dye. The overall Kappa-value for the four observers' judgment of lesion vs. no lesion was 0.41 which can be interpreted as moderate agreement. Intra-observer agreement was calculated for two of the observers looking at photographs with a 10 months' time-gap, and the Kappa-values were 0.41 and 0.52. Positive and negative predictive values of the photographs were 82 and 81 % respectively. This study demonstrates relatively poor reliability of colposcopic photography. Some would argue that this makes colposcopic photography a low-quality method of evaluation and that forensic science should aim for higher standards because of its use in court. Others would argue that as long as the limitations of a scientific method are acknowledged then it is still eligible for use. The moderate agreement and accuracy stresses the need for quality control in the gynecological part of a rape examination. Colposcopic photography also provides a good option for supervision and teaching in an ethically difficult setting. It strengthens the legal rights for both victim and perpetrator.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Astrup, Birgitte Schmidt","Lauritsen, Jens","Thomsen, Jørgen Lange","Ravn, Pernille"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-575172"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"colposcopic photography of genital injury following sexual intercourse in adults","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12024-012-9394-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-575172","identifier":[{"id":"23247984","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84874117111","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-06ed85ff-6b43-42b1-82fb-7178ab0986c1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7C00323041B8304E6F6A9F33C632CFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12024-012-9394-2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte Schmidt","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"7f6334d2-e0ea-473e-adbb-e1246c3db81a","name":"Astrup, Birgitte Schmidt","orcid":"0000-0003-4266-9290","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"lauritsenpau","last":"Lauritsen","locid":"4c460020-fd7b-478a-ad2d-183a6808842a","name":"Lauritsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-9281-8990","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Lange","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"02c01238-a1bb-411b-97e9-54415fc12c59","name":"Thomsen, Jørgen Lange","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"b86a181f-31f7-452e-9900-74267c1011d3","name":"Ravn, Pernille","orcid":"0000-0001-8752-1121","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23247984"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12024-012-9394-2","issn":["1547769X","15562891"],"issn_org":["1547769X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Forensic Science, Medicine, and Pathology","pages":"24-30","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Forensic Science, Medicine, and Pathology","title_org":"Forensic Science, Medicine and Pathology","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874117111"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-06ed85ff-6b43-42b1-82fb-7178ab0986c1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Colposcopic photography of genital injury following sexual intercourse in adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-575172","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Asking a bioenergy researcher about the composition of wheat straw, he would know it by heart. But if enquiring about typical African biomasses – it would be another case. Until now, biomasses common to African countries have not received the same scientific attention as biomasses from Europe, North America or Brazil. For that reason, it is difficult to estimate bioenergy potentials in the African region. As a part of an on‐going research collaboration investigating production of 2g biofuels in Ghana, this study have analysed 13 common African agricultural residues: yam peelings, cassava peelings, cassava stalks, plantain peelings, plantain trunks, plantain leaves, cocoa husks, cocoa pods, maize cobs, maize stalks, rice straw, groundnut straw and oil palm empty fruit bunches (EFB). This was done to establish detailed compositional mass balances, enabling estimations of accurate bioenergy potentials for bioethanol and biogas. Furthermore, biomasses high in specific biomass constituents, such as hemicellulose or lignin, have been identified for future biorefinery applications.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","Kádár, Zsófia","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S02-098.16-033963"],"event":{"end":"2013-05-02","place":"Portland OR, us","start":"2013-04-29","title":"The 35th Symposium on Biotechnology for Fuels and Chemicals","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["United Arab Emirates"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Masdar Institute of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimating bioenergy potentials of common african agricultural residues","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/63045121/35th%20SBFC%20Poster%20SUNT%20april%202013.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.16-033963","ids":["dtu-3d80ad35-ecdc-4b75-bf8b-73c85f2b9d81","sdu-5ec4069b-42ac-4d62-ba88-d8a88ca8e27f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-45C5656C914AB1B783572FD8DBCC2996"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/63045121/35th%20SBFC%20Poster%20SUNT%20april%202013.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Center for BioProcess Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ae","key":"masdar institute of science and technology","loc":["United Arab Emirates","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Masdar Institute of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sune Tjalfe","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"48069d0c-8a66-43de-99ab-484cfa5ff52d","name":"Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","orcid":"0000-0002-6744-2642","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zsófia","key":"kádárpau","last":"Kádár","locid":"77632fb2-eb08-43a2-b320-3d9133ba2a88","name":"Kádár, Zsófia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"14ca7f5b-030e-46a8-8aef-a09f6fa018f5","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","orcid":"0000-0001-6067-5032","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3d80ad35-ecdc-4b75-bf8b-73c85f2b9d81","sdu-5ec4069b-42ac-4d62-ba88-d8a88ca8e27f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Estimating bioenergy potentials of common African agricultural residues","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.16-033963","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Grass biomass is a prospective type of lignocellulosic biomass for bioenergy and fuel production, but the low dry matter in grass at harvest calls for new pretreatment strategies for cellulosic conversion. In this study, ensiling was tested as a biological pretreatment method of the high yielding grass variety Festulolium Hykor. The biomass was harvested in four cuts over a growing season. Three important factors of ensiling: biomass composition, dry matter (DM) at ensiling, and inoculation of lactic acid bacteria, were assessed in relation to subsequent enzymatic cellulose hydrolysis. The organic acid profile after ensiling was dependant on the composition of the grass and the DM, rather than on the inocula. High levels of organic acids, notably lactic acid, produced during ensiling improved enzymatic cellulose convertibility in the grass biomass. Ensiling of less mature grass gave higher convertibility. Low DM at ensiling (<25%) resulted in the highest cellulose convertibilities, which ranged from 32 to 70% of the available cellulose in the four cuts after ensiling. The study confirms that ensiling can enhance cellulose convertibility of green biomass, and provides new insight to ensiling as a biological pretreatment method for green biomass conversion.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ambye-Jensen, Morten","Johansen, Katja S.","Didion, Thomas","Kádár, Zsófia","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Meyer, Anne S."],"cuid":["S03-097.78-003850"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Meyer, Anne S."],"keyword":["Biomass characterisation","Cellulose convertibility","Ensiling","Enzymatic hydrolysis","Grass"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ensiling as biological pretreatment of grass festulolium hykor the effect of composition dry matter and inocula on cellulose convertibility","src":["aau","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58335368/JBB_3333.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S03-097.78-003850","identifier":[{"id":"84888847264","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4ecc96bd-76e1-4281-9422-4b974502d344","dtu-4e6a5a2f-b028-4a48-94ac-5c901351b3f0","ku-f85eddfb-4824-4375-a242-0600e24ac922"],"keyword":["Biomass characterisation","Cellulose convertibility","Ensiling","Enzymatic hydrolysis","Grass"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-B3FED881C677E2048F05245D74D6CB06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2013.08.015","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58335368/JBB_3333.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Center for BioProcess Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novozymes A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["DLF TRIFOLIUM A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Sustainable Biotechnology, Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"ambyejensenpau","last":"Ambye-Jensen","locid":"28d63080-6072-492c-82cb-a513fb2e6832","name":"Jensen, Morten","name_org":"Ambye-Jensen, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Katja S.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Katja S.","orcid":"0000-0002-7587-5990","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"didionpau","last":"Didion","name":"Didion, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zsofiá","key":"kádárpau","last":"Kádár","locid":"8b49b135-09d1-4d2d-879c-5d8cb263be04","name":"Kádár, Zsófia","name_org":"Kádár, Zsofiá","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens E.","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"f3b10fc3-ff7d-440d-9ee8-921079f6e769","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","name_org":"Schmidt, Jens E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne S.","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"1e9f4759-72d8-4d52-94ec-ce192ffca184","name":"Meyer, Anne S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8910-9931","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2013.08.015","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","pages":"303-312","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","title_org":"Biomass and Bioenergy","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84888847264"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","dlf a/s","dlf trifolium a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4ecc96bd-76e1-4281-9422-4b974502d344","dtu-4e6a5a2f-b028-4a48-94ac-5c901351b3f0","ku-f85eddfb-4824-4375-a242-0600e24ac922"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ensiling as biological pretreatment of grass (Festulolium Hykor) : The effect of composition, dry matter, and inocula on cellulose convertibility","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.78-003850","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The mortality after aneurysmal subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH) is 50%, and most survivors suffer severe functional and cognitive deficits. Half of SAH patients deteriorate 5 to 14 days after the initial bleeding, so-called delayed cerebral ischemia (DCI). Although often attributed to vasospasms, DCI may develop in the absence of angiographic vasospasms, and therapeutic reversal of angiographic vasospasms fails to improve patient outcome. The etiology of chronic neurodegenerative changes after SAH remains poorly understood. Brain oxygenation depends on both cerebral blood flow (CBF) and its microscopic distribution, the so-called capillary transit time heterogeneity (CTH). In theory, increased CTH can therefore lead to tissue hypoxia in the absence of severe CBF reductions, whereas reductions in CBF, paradoxically, improve brain oxygenation if CTH is critically elevated. We review potential sources of elevated CTH after SAH. Pericyte constrictions in relation to the initial ischemic episode and subsequent oxidative stress, nitric oxide depletion during the pericapillary clearance of oxyhemoglobin, vasogenic edema, leukocytosis, and astrocytic endfeet swelling are identified as potential sources of elevated CTH, and hence of metabolic derangement, after SAH. Irreversible changes in capillary morphology and function are predicted to contribute to long-term relative tissue hypoxia, inflammation, and neurodegeneration. We discuss diagnostic and therapeutic implications of these predictions.Journal of Cerebral Blood Flow & Metabolism advance online publication, 25 September 2013; doi:10.1038/jcbfm.2013.173.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Østergaard, Leif","Aamand, Rasmus","Karabegovic, Sanja","Tietze, Anna","Blicher, Jakob","Mikkelsen, Irene Klærke","Iversen, Nina Kerting","Secher, Niels","Engedal, Thorbjørn Søndergaard","Anzabi, Maryam","Gutiérrez-Jiménez, Eugenio","Cai, Changsi","Koch, Klaus Ulrik","Næss-Schmidt, Erhard Trillingsgaard","Obel, Annette","Juul, Niels","Rasmussen, Mads","Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-187664"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of the microcirculation in delayed cerebral ischemia and chronic degenerative changes after subarachnoid hemorrhage","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/jcbfm.2013.173","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-187664","identifier":[{"id":"24064495","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84889094930","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3851911","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-66209e54-16b6-4756-8949-deb0b65aafee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25032AC93AF2A220673702DB6BE64F2D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/jcbfm.2013.173","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center of Functionally Integrative Neuroscience","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Neuroradiology, NBG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leif","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"af45ec8c-f95a-4937-9e48-ffabe2b8933d","name":"Østergaard, Leif","orcid":"0