{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Raida, Zindy","Hundahl, Christian Ansgar","Kelsen, Jesper","Nyengaard, Jens Randel","Hay-Schmidt, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-230721"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"correction reduced infarct size in neuroglobin null mice after experimental stroke in vivo","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3751158/pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-230721","identifier":[{"id":"84882659500","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23926921","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3751158","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-b1b39f94-e30e-4171-9b0f-d18b0258b12e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3A76EA04E2CA7EDFF3AA56058561FF23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/2040-7378-5-10","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3751158/pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurosurgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zindy","key":"raidapau","last":"Raida","name":"Raida, Zindy","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Ansgar","key":"hundahlpau","last":"Hundahl","locid":"03ecdba8-e37b-44fb-8702-065cf1a31e62","name":"Hundahl, Christian Ansgar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"kelsenpau","last":"Kelsen","locid":"5d9b376f-8fa3-4879-b27e-184ef5f90a43","name":"Kelsen, Jesper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Randel","key":"nyengaardpau","last":"Nyengaard","locid":"8288d58c-4602-4c0c-9b76-949cc83d281b","name":"Nyengaard, Jens Randel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"hayschmidtpau","last":"Hay-Schmidt","name":"Hay-Schmidt, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23926921"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/2040-7378-5-10","issn":["20407378"],"issue":"1","journal":"Experimental & Translational Stroke Medicine","pages":"10","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Experimental & Translational Stroke Medicine","title_org":"Experimental & translational stroke medicine","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882659500"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b1b39f94-e30e-4171-9b0f-d18b0258b12e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Correction: Reduced infarct size in neuroglobin-null mice after experimental stroke in vivo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-230721","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"An experimental program was carried out to investigate the influence of basalt FRP (BFRP) reinforcing mesh on the fire behaviour of thin high performance concrete (HPC) plates applied to sandwich elements. Samples with BFRP mesh were compared to samples with no mesh, samples with steel mesh and samples displaying a full sandwich structure. Final results confirmed the bond loss between concrete and BFRP mesh with temperature. The available void where the epoxy burnt away allowed the concrete matrix to release pressure and limit pore stresses, delaying spalling. It also reduced the mechanical resistance of the structure, since the ability of the mesh to bond on the concrete matrix was lost. A theoretical approach for numerical modelling is proposed based on the experimental observations. It describes the change of boundary condition at the vicinity of the mesh as an outer pressure dependent on a linear increase of the volume of melted epoxy and the outflow of moisture from the concrete matrix. It was concluded that the use of a BFRP mesh to reinforce HPC exposed to fire reduces the mechanical strength despite a beneficial effect related to spalling.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hulin, Thomas","Hodicky, Kamil","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Nielsen, Jens Henrik","Stang, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-338119"],"event":{"end":"2013-12-13","place":"Melbourne, au","start":"2013-12-11","title":"4th Asia-Pacific Conference on FRP in Structures","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fire performance of basalt frp mesh reinforced hpc thin plates","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/82967255/prod11389309171439.full_paper_APFIS_reviewed_version_Thomas_Hulin.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-338119","identifier":[{"id":"84926039686","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7067d808-13a9-45c4-afbf-78ef14eaafea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-EB68A9A5CF751D906247D385E8C066E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/82967255/prod11389309171439.full_paper_APFIS_reviewed_version_Thomas_Hulin.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil Engineering, Section for Structural Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"hulinpau","last":"Hulin","locid":"9bdd0adf-855a-453d-902b-ac128bdc7b5f","name":"Hulin, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kamil","key":"hodickypau","last":"Hodicky","locid":"0107b990-508e-4331-9d2a-fd863888e565","name":"Hodicky, Kamil","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Wittrup","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"2a187e49-ed7b-44eb-a0d4-f9d00cc245ce","name":"Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","orcid":"0000-0003-0603-4546","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Henrik","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1153cf58-bb0e-42da-a4d0-1ea0dd13b752","name":"Nielsen, Jens Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-0705-9382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"stangpau","last":"Stang","locid":"57fe0e89-5130-43bb-a270-b38b7f8b885e","name":"Stang, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-5812-4028","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780987593016"],"publisher":"Swinburne University of Technology","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 4th Asia-Pacific Conference on FRP in Structures (APFIS 2013)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84926039686"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7067d808-13a9-45c4-afbf-78ef14eaafea"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fire performance of basalt FRP mesh reinforced HPC thin plates","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-338119","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: A recent randomized controlled trial suggests that hypothyroid subjects may find levothyroxine (l-T4) and levotriiodothyronine combination therapy to be superior to l-T4 monotherapy in terms of quality of life, suggesting that the brain registered increased T3 availability during the combination therapy. HYPOTHESIS: Peripheral tissue might also be stimulated during T4/T3 combination therapy compared with T4 monotherapy. METHODS: Serum levels of sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG), pro-collagen-1-N-terminal peptide (PINP), and N-terminal pro-brain natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP) (representing hepatocyte, osteoblast, and cardiomyocyte stimulation respectively) were measured in 26 hypothyroid subjects in a double-blind, randomized, crossover trial, which compared the replacement therapy with T4/T3 in combination (50 μg T4 was substituted with 20 μg T3) to T4 alone (once daily regimens). This was performed to obtain unaltered serum TSH levels during the trial and between the two treatment groups. Blood sampling was performed 24 h after the last intake of thyroid hormone medication. RESULTS: TSH remained unaltered between the groups ((median) 0.83 vs 1.18 mU/l in T4/T3 combination and T4 monotherapy respectively; P=0.534). SHBG increased from (median) 75 nmol/l at baseline to 83 nmol/l in the T4/T3 group (P=0.015) but remained unaltered in the T4 group (67 nmol/l); thus, it was higher in the T4/T3 vs T4 group (P=0.041). PINP levels were higher in the T4/T3 therapy (48 vs 40 μg/l (P<0.001)). NT-proBNP did not differ between the groups. CONCLUSIONS: T4/T3 combination therapy in hypothyroidism seems to have more metabolic effects than the T4 monotherapy.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Schmidt, Ulla","Nygaard, Birte","Winther Jensen, Ebbe","Kvetny, Jan","Jarløv, Anne","Faber, Jens"],"cuid":["S02-093.35-047313"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"peripheral markers of thyroid function the effect of t 000000000004 monotherapy vs t 000000000004 t 000000000003 combination therapy in hypothyroid subjects in a randomized crossover study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-12-0064","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-093.35-047313","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3680960","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23781319","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f1497240-c27d-48a4-9fc6-807a91cf2cef","sdu-11965619-bb4b-4440-8ca6-900a121a00e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C41A13B53E0FB4D1C2BBD789EBD85043"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-12-0064","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Næstved, Slagelse, Ringsted Hospitals (NSR)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Ulla","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birte","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"0b76de04-6dd1-4c43-9181-dcfce2b9e815","name":"Nygaard, Birte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ebbe","key":"wintherjensenpau","last":"Winther Jensen","name":"Winther Jensen, Ebbe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ebbe Winther","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Ebbe Winther","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"kvetnypau","last":"Kvetny","locid":"8971793f-1215-493b-93f0-7625c4df9c3f","name":"Kvetny, Jan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"jarløvpau","last":"Jarløv","name":"Jarløv, Anne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"42925e6e-5e0c-475f-aca8-13159f10abc7","name":"Faber, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23781319"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1530/ec-12-0064","issn":["20493614"],"journal":"Endocrine Connections","pages":"55-60","publisher":"BioScientifica Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Endocrine Connections","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f1497240-c27d-48a4-9fc6-807a91cf2cef","sdu-11965619-bb4b-4440-8ca6-900a121a00e3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Peripheral markers of thyroid function : the effect of T(4) monotherapy vs T(4)/T(3) combination therapy in hypothyroid subjects in a randomized crossover study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.35-047313","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"An analytical method for separation and quantitative determination of nine dithiocarbamates (DTCs) in fruits and vegetables by using LC-MS/MS was developed, validated and applied to samples purchased in local supermarkets. The nine DTCs were ziram, ferbam, thiram, maneb, zineb, nabam, metiram, mancozeb and propineb. Validation parameters of mean recovery for two matrices at two concentration levels, relative repeatability (RSDr), relative within-laboratory reproducibility (RSDR) and LOD were obtained for the nine DTCs. The results from the analysis of fruits and vegetables served as the basis for an exposure assessment within the given commodities and a risk assessment by comparing the calculated exposure to the acceptable daily intake and acute reference dose for various exposure groups. The analysis indicated positive findings of DTCs in apples, pears, plums, table grapes, papaya and broccoli at concentrations ranging from 0.03 mg/kg to 2.69 mg/kg expressed as the equivalent amount of CS2. None of the values exceeded the Maximum residue level (MRL) set by the European Union, and furthermore, it was not possible to state whether illegal use had taken place or not, because a clear differentiation between the various DTCs in the LC-MS/MS analysis was lacking. The exposure and risk assessment showed that only for maneb in the case of apples and apple juice, the acute reference dose was exceeded for infants in the United Kingdom and for children in Germany, respectively.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schmidt, Bjørn","Christensen, Hanne Bjerre","Petersen, Annette","Sloth, Jens Jørgen","Poulsen, Mette Erecius"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-355173"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"method validation and analysis of nine dithiocarbamates in fruits and vegetables by lc ms ms","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19440049.2013.801083","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-355173","identifier":[{"id":"23799268","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84880037236","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a9761942-720c-468c-97ca-5a2928a4f286"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-634636B43F13B32E64060CB106569377"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19440049.2013.801083","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Food Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"2efd5b97-c8d6-4fc4-9612-532a1e298599","name":"Schmidt, Bjørn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne Bjerre","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"d60f5dd2-72b6-4dbe-952e-243f23973bf1","name":"Christensen, Hanne Bjerre","orcid":"0000-0003-0268-8884","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"d03592bf-e4ec-4247-9b1c-92f0abaeabde","name":"Petersen, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-3996-2701","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Jørgen","key":"slothpau","last":"Sloth","locid":"d7fb8bd1-2626-48fa-b49e-35d57b2fae5d","name":"Sloth, Jens Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-3636-8769","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Erecius","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"92af9ffe-af69-4755-88d5-d72168a62275","name":"Poulsen, Mette Erecius","orcid":"0000-0003-3578-1583","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23799268"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/19440049.2013.801083","issn":["19440049","19440057"],"issn_org":["19440049"],"issue":"7","journal":"Food Additives & Contaminants: Part A - Chemistry, Analysis, Control, Exposure & Risk Assessment","pages":"1287-1298","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Food Additives & Contaminants: Part A - Chemistry, Analysis, Control, Exposure & Risk Assessment","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880037236"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a9761942-720c-468c-97ca-5a2928a4f286"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Method validation and analysis of nine dithiocarbamates in fruits and vegetables by LC-MS/MS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-355173","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Stroke is a major cause of death and severe disability, but effective treatments are limited. Neuroglobin, a neuronal heme-globin, has been advocated as a novel pharmacological target in combating stroke and neurodegenerative disorders based on cytoprotective properties. Using thoroughly validated antibodies and oligos, we give a detailed brain anatomical characterization of transgenic mice over expressing Neuroglobin. Moreover, using permanent middle artery occlusion the effect of elevated levels of Neuroglobin on ischemic damage was studied. Lastly, the impact of mouse strain genetic background on ischemic damage was investigated. PRINCIPAL FINDINGS: A four to five fold increase in Neuroglobin mRNA and protein expression was seen in the brain of transgenic mice. A β-actin promoter was used to drive Neuroglobin over expression, but immunohistochemistry and in situ hybridization showed over expression to be confined to primarily the cortex, hippocampus, cerebellum, and only in neurons. The level and expression pattern of endogenous Neuroglobin was unaffected by insertion of the over expressing Ngb transgene. Neuroglobin over expression resulted in a significant reduction in infarct volume 24 hours after ischemia. Immunohistochemistry showed no selective sparing of Neuroglobin expressing cells in the ischemic core or penumbra. A significant difference in infarct volume was found between mice of the same strain, but from different colonies. SIGNIFICANCE: In contrast to some previous reports, Neuroglobin over expression is not global but confined to a few well-defined brain regions, and only in neurons. This study confirms previous reports showing a correlation between reduced infarct volume and elevated Neuroglobin levels, but underlines the need to study the likely contribution from compensatory mechanisms to the phenotype following a genetic perturbation. We also stress, that care should be taken when comparing results where different mouse strains and colonies have been used due to large genetic background contribution to the observed phenotype.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Raida, Zindy","Hundahl, Christian Ansgar","Nyengaard, Jens R","Hay-Schmidt, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532034"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Actins","Animals","Brain Infarction","Brain Ischemia","Cerebellum","Cerebral Cortex","Gene expression","Globins","Hippocampus","Male","Mice","Mice Transgenic","Nerve Tissue Proteins","Neurons","Neuroprotective Agents","Promoter Regions Genetic","Species Specificity","Transgenes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuroglobin over expressing mice expression pattern and effect on brain ischemic infarct size","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0076565","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532034","identifier":[{"id":"24098534","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84885029621","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3788103","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-e816cbd3-7588-4598-b8f1-0fc492cb7de6"],"keyword":["Actins","Animals","Brain Infarction","Brain Ischemia","Cerebellum","Cerebral Cortex","Gene Expression","Globins","Hippocampus","Male","Mice","Mice, Transgenic","Nerve Tissue Proteins","Neurons","Neuroprotective Agents","Promoter Regions, Genetic","Species Specificity","Transgenes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-273A4388A35C15559845C95CBF9C785B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0076565","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Zindy","key":"raidapau","last":"Raida","name":"Raida, Zindy","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian Ansgar","key":"hundahlpau","last":"Hundahl","locid":"4068fa43-1969-4dc4-ad4b-f3f9a477ce70","name":"Hundahl, Christian Ansgar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens R","key":"nyengaardpau","last":"Nyengaard","name":"Nyengaard, Jens R","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"hayschmidtpau","last":"Hay-Schmidt","locid":"f0f495a2-fe48-4cdf-8f27-ea207182bda8","name":"Hay-Schmidt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9984-7014","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24098534"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0076565","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"10","journal":"PLOS ONE","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84885029621"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e816cbd3-7588-4598-b8f1-0fc492cb7de6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neuroglobin over expressing mice : expression pattern and effect on brain ischemic infarct size","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532034","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) is associated with peripheral insulin resistance, impaired incretin effect, and increased plasma levels of tumor necrosis factor-alpha (TNF-α). Whereas TNF-α infusion at a dose that induces systemic inflammation in healthy volunteers has been demonstrated to induce peripheral insulin resistance, the influence of this cytokine on the incretin effect is unknown.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Signe Tellerup","Lehrskov-Schmidt, Louise","Krogh-Madsen, Rikke","Solomon, Thomas","Lehrskov-Schmidt, Lars","Holst, Jens Juul","Møller, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-536928"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of tumor necrosis factor alpha infusion on the incretin effect in healthy volunteers","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/dmrr.2441","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-536928","identifier":[{"id":"84887728995","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23904405","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f07884e2-1a53-4d79-b487-073475b52c75"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EF640E30453C21E6A6EEBFC572EE817D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/dmrr.2441","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Graduate School of Health and Medical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Signe Tellerup","key":"nielsensignetelleruppau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Signe Tellerup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"lehrskovschmidtlouisepau","last":"Lehrskov-Schmidt","name":"Lehrskov-Schmidt, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke","key":"kroghmadsenrikkepau","last":"Krogh-Madsen","name":"Krogh-Madsen, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"solomonthomaspau","last":"Solomon","locid":"c869ee86-bba2-4b49-bd24-17f5654c9cff","name":"Solomon, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"lehrskovschmidtlarspau","last":"Lehrskov-Schmidt","name":"Lehrskov-Schmidt, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstjensjuulpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten","key":"møllerkirstenpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Kirsten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23904405"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/dmrr.2441","issn":["15207552","15207560"],"issn_org":["15207560"],"issue":"8","journal":"Diabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews","pages":"655-663","status":"p","title":"Diabetes/Metabolism Research and Reviews","title_org":"Diabetes - Metabolism: Research and Reviews (Online)","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887728995"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f07884e2-1a53-4d79-b487-073475b52c75"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of tumor necrosis factor-alpha infusion on the incretin effect in healthy volunteers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-536928","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Despite rapid revascularisation with circulatory support using inotropes and intra-aortic balloon counterpulsation, the mortality of cardiogenic shock complicating acute myocardial infarction still exceeds 50%. An alternative treatment strategy is restoration of cardiac output by using a ventricular assist device which can be inserted in the acute setting using the Impella device, a catheter-based flow pump. DanShock is a Danish multicentre study that will assess whether circulatory support using the Impella device will improve the outcome of cardiogenic shock compared to conventional management.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Junker, Anders","Kaltoft, Anne Kjer","Hassager, Christian","Christensen, Erika Frischknecht","Lippert, Freddy","Ravn, Hanne Berg","Eiskjær, Hans","Tilsted, Hans-Henrik","Schmidt, Henrik","de Haas, Inge","Møller, Jacob Eifer","Ravkilde, Jan","Lassen, Jens Flensted","Wachtell, Kristian","Holmvang, Lene","Jensen, Lise Okkels","Greve, Matias Lindholm","Engstrøm, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-082.99-011167"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["DanShockInvestigatorerne"],"keyword":["Cardiac Output","Denmark","Fluoroscopy","Heart Assist Devices","Humans","Prosthesis Design","Shock Cardiogenic","Treatment Outcome","Ventricular Function Left"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Anæstesiologisk Afdeling, NBG"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behandling af kardiogent shock med perkutan mekanisk cirkulationsstøtte","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lfappet.laeger.dk/LF/UFL/2013/4/pdf/VP08120500.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-082.99-011167","identifier":[{"id":"84872968464","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23347740","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e99324d3-614c-4934-8408-197cd442226c","ku-8bad01f1-e90a-4e39-8e3b-430aad6affd1"],"keyword":["Cardiac Output","Denmark","Fluoroscopy","Heart-Assist Devices","Humans","Prosthesis Design","Shock, Cardiogenic","Treatment Outcome","Ventricular Function, Left"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-16DE1415387D5F3395829D411CE1A16A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://lfappet.laeger.dk/LF/UFL/2013/4/pdf/VP08120500.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Hjertemedicinsk Afdeling B, SKS"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Anæstesiologisk Afdeling, NBG"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU"},{"affno":5,"key":"danshockinvestigatorerne","name":"DanShockInvestigatorerne","role":"oau"},{"affno":6,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Surgery and Internal Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"junkerpau","last":"Junker","name":"Junker, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Kjer","key":"kaltoftpau","last":"Kaltoft","name":"Kaltoft, Anne Kjer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","name":"Hassager, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erika Frischknecht","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Erika Frischknecht","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Freddy","key":"lippertpau","last":"Lippert","locid":"48ac5d81-3437-4345-b6c3-394683a09d5d","name":"Lippert, Freddy","orcid":"0000-0002-2356-8809","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"eiskjærpau","last":"Eiskjær","name":"Eiskjær, Hans","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans-Henrik","key":"tilstedpau","last":"Tilsted","name":"Tilsted, Hans-Henrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Henrik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Inge","key":"dehaaspau","last":"de Haas","name":"de Haas, Inge","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jan","key":"ravkildepau","last":"Ravkilde","name":"Ravkilde, Jan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Flensted","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","name":"Lassen, Jens Flensted","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristian","key":"wachtellpau","last":"Wachtell","name":"Wachtell, Kristian","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lene","key":"holmvangpau","last":"Holmvang","name":"Holmvang, Lene","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lise Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lise Okkels","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matias Lindholm","key":"grevepau","last":"Greve","name":"Greve, Matias Lindholm","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"engstrømpau","last":"Engstrøm","name":"Engstrøm, Thomas","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23347740"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"4","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"205-8","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"175"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84872968464"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","hjertemedicinsk afdeling b, sks"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e99324d3-614c-4934-8408-197cd442226c","ku-8bad01f1-e90a-4e39-8e3b-430aad6affd1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Behandling af kardiogent shock med perkutan mekanisk cirkulationsstøtte","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.99-011167","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) have an increased risk of cardiovascular disease, which is worsened by physical inactivity. Subclinical myocardial dysfunction is associated with increased risk of heart failure and impaired prognosis in T2DM; however, it is not clear if exercise training can counteract the early signs of diabetic heart disease. PURPOSE: This study aimed to evaluate the effects of soccer training on cardiac function, exercise capacity, and blood pressure in middle-age men with T2DM. METHODS: Twenty-one men age 49.8 ± 1.7 yr with T2DM and no history of cardiovascular disease participated in a soccer training group (n = 12) that trained 1 h twice a week or a control group (n = 9) with no change in lifestyle. Examinations included comprehensive transthoracic echocardiography, measurements of blood pressure, maximal oxygen consumption (V̇O2max), and intermittent endurance capacity before and after 12 and 24 wk. Two-way repeated-measures ANOVA was applied. RESULTS: After 24 wk of soccer training, left ventricular (LV) end-diastolic diameter and volume were increased (P < 0.001) compared to baseline. LV longitudinal systolic displacement was augmented by 23% (P < 0.001) and global longitudinal two-dimensional strain increased by 10% (P < 0.05). LV diastolic function, determined by mitral inflow (E/A ratio) and peak diastolic velocity E′, was increased by 18% (P < 0.01) and 29% (P < 0.001), respectively, whereas LV filling pressure E/E′ was reduced by 15% (P = 0.05). Systolic, diastolic, and mean arterial pressures were all reduced by 8 mm Hg (P < 0.01, P < 0.001, and P < 0.001, respectively). V̇O2max and intermittent endurance capacity was 12% and 42% (P < 0.001) higher, respectively. No changes in any of the measured parameters were observed in control group. CONCLUSION: Regular soccer training improves cardiac function, increases exercise capacity, and lowers blood pressure in men with T2DM.","author_count":10,"con