{"abstract":"Glial cell-line-derived neurotrophic factor (GDNF) is a potent neurotrophic factor that has reached clinical trials for Parkinson's disease. GDNF binds to its coreceptor GFRα1 and signals through the transmembrane receptor tyrosine kinase RET, or RET independently through NCAM or syndecan-3. Whereas the GDNF signaling cascades are well described, cellular turnover and trafficking of GDNF and its receptors remain poorly characterized. Here, we find that SorLA acts as sorting receptor for the GDNF/GFRα1 complex, directing it from the cell surface to endosomes. Through this mechanism, GDNF is targeted to lysosomes and degraded while GFRα1 recycles, creating an efficient GDNF clearance pathway. The SorLA/GFRα1 complex further targets RET for endocytosis but not for degradation, affecting GDNF-induced neurotrophic activities. SorLA-deficient mice display elevated GDNF levels, altered dopaminergic function, marked hyperactivity, and reduced anxiety, all of which are phenotypes related to abnormal GDNF activity. Taken together, these findings establish SorLA as a critical regulator of GDNF activity in the CNS.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Glerup, Simon","Lume, Maria","Olsen, Ditte","Nyengaard, Jens Randel","Vægter, Christian Bjerggaard","Gustafsen, Camilla","Christensen, Erik Ilsø","Kjolby, Mads","Hay-Schmidt, Anders","Bender, Dirk","Madsen, Peder","Saarma, Mart","Nykjær, Anders","Petersen, Claus Munck"],"cuid":["S02-098.89-023601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animals","Anxiety","Behavior Animal","Cell Membrane","Cell Survival","Dopaminergic Neurons","Endocytosis","Glial Cell Line Derived Neurotrophic Factor","HEK293 Cells","Humans","Lysosomes","Membrane Transport Proteins","Mice","Mice Inbred C57BL","Mice Knockout","Multiprotein Complexes","Protein Binding","Protein Transport","Proto Oncogene Proteins c ret","Receptors LDL"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sorla controls neurotrophic activity by sorting of gdnf and its receptors gfrα000000000001 and ret","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2012.12.011","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.89-023601","identifier":[{"id":"84873162291","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23333276","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-961e6f80-9938-4a5d-b031-cf94e5960127","ku-d1c3c8f8-cd9c-4e91-8f03-8cf19944e865"],"keyword":["Animals","Anxiety","Behavior, Animal","Cell Membrane","Cell Survival","Dopaminergic Neurons","Endocytosis","Glial Cell Line-Derived Neurotrophic Factor","Glial Cell Line-Derived Neurotrophic Factor Receptors","HEK293 Cells","Humans","Lysosomes","Membrane Transport Proteins","Mice","Mice, Inbred C57BL","Mice, Knockout","Multiprotein Complexes","Protein Binding","Protein Transport","Proto-Oncogene Proteins c-ret","Receptors, LDL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F3C2542617C93C3A721FEF00C7D56977"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2012.12.011","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Vest"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universiti