{"abstract":"Rape straw can be used for production of second generation bioethanol. In this paper we optimized the pretreatment of rape straw for this purpose using Wet oxidation (WO). The effect of reaction temperature, reaction time, and oxygen gas pressure was investigated for maximum ethanol yield via Simultaneous Saccharification and Fermentation (SSF). To reduce the water use and increase the energy efficiency in WO pretreatment features like recycling liquid (filtrate), presoaking of rape straw in water or recycled filtrate before WO, skip washing pretreated solids (filter cake) after WO, or use of whole slurry (Filter cake + filtrate) in SSF were also tested. Except ethanol yields, pretreatment methods were evaluated based on achieved glucose yields, amount of water used, recovery of cellulose, hemicellulose, and lignin.The highest ethanol yield obtained was 67% after fermenting the whole slurry produced by WO at 205 °C for 3 min with 12 bar of oxygen gas pressure and featured with presoaking in water. At these conditions after pre-treatment, cellulose and hemicellulose was recovered quantitatively (100%) together with 86% of the lignin. WO treatments of 2–3 min at 205–210 °C with 12 bar of oxygen gas produced higher ethanol yields and cellulose, hemicelluloses, and lignin recoveries, than 15 min WO treatment at 195 °C. Also, recycling filtrate and use of higher oxygen gas pressure reduced recovery of materials. The use of filtrate could be inhibitory for the yeast, but also reduced lactic acid formation in SSF.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Arvaniti, Efthalia","Bjerre, Anne Belinda","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349846"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Enzymatic hydrolysis","Ethanol","Rape straw","Wet oxidation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wet oxidation pretreatment of rape straw for ethanol production","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2011.12.040","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-349846","identifier":[{"id":"84857800268","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-97bfc26b-7349-43e3-a870-67ef51bc734c"],"keyword":["Enzymatic hydrolysis","Ethanol","Rape straw","Wet oxidation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-825BB07E781471E604413B10F710E5E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2011.12.040","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Center for BioProcess Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Efthalia","key":"arvanitipau","last":"Arvaniti","locid":"24a3d746-56af-468b-bfa9-08e1c8dc7b47","name":"Arvaniti, Efthalia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Belinda","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","name":"Bjerre, Anne Belinda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"4f0d57ca-a0c5-43cf-ada5-378c053ab8c7","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2011.12.040","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","pages":"94-105","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857800268"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-97bfc26b-7349-43e3-a870-67ef51bc734c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Wet oxidation pretreatment of rape straw for ethanol production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-349846","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Neuroglobin (Ngb), a neuron-specific oxygen-binding globin with an unknown function, has been proposed to play a key role in neuronal survival. We have previously shown Ngb to be highly expressed in the rat suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN). The present study addresses the effect of Ngb deficiency on circadian behavior. Ngb-deficient and wild-type (wt) mice were placed in running wheels and their activity rhythms, endogenous period and response to light stimuli were investigated. The effect of Ngb deficiency on the expression of Period1 (Per1) and the immediate early gene Fos was determined after light stimulation at night and the neurochemical phenotype of Ngb expressing neurons in wt mice was characterized. Loss of Ngb function had no effect on overall circadian entrainment, but resulted in a significantly larger phase delay of circadian rhythm upon light stimulation at early night. A light-induced increase in Per1, but not Fos, gene expression was observed in Ngb-deficient mice. Ngb expressing neurons which co-stored Gastrin Releasing Peptide (GRP) and were innervated from the eye and the geniculo-hypothalamic tract expressed FOS after light stimulation. No PER1 expression was observed in Ngb-positive neurons. The present study demonstrates for the first time that the genetic elimination of Ngb does not affect core clock function but evokes an increased behavioural response to light concomitant with increased Per1 gene expression in the SCN at early night.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hundahl, Christian Ansgar","Fahrenkrug, Jan","Hay-Schmidt, Anders","Georg, Birgitte","Faltoft, Birgitte","Hannibal, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-400673"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Behavior Animal","Blotting Western","Circadian rhythm","Female","Fluorescent Antibody Technique","Globins","Immunoenzyme Techniques","Immunoprecipitation","Light","Male","Mice","Mice Inbred C57BL","Nerve Tissue Proteins","Neurons","Proto Oncogene Proteins c fos","RNA Messenger","Rats","Real Time Polymerase Chain Reaction","Reverse Transcriptase Polymerase Chain Reaction","Suprachiasmatic nucleus","Synapses"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circadian behaviour in neuroglobin deficient mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0034462","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-400673","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3320642","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84859344720","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22496809","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0c144f82-5ea1-4f5f-b536-1e8e8cd719b3"],"keyword":["Animals","Behavior, Animal","Blotting, Western","Circadian Rhythm","Female","Fluorescent Antibody Technique","Globins","Immunoenzyme Techniques","Immunoprecipitation","Light","Male","Mice","Mice, Inbred C57BL","Nerve Tissue Proteins","Neurons","Period Circadian Proteins","Proto-Oncogene Proteins c-fos","RNA, Messenger","Rats","Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction","Reverse Transcriptase Polymerase Chain Reaction","Suprachiasmatic Nucleus","Synapses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D4ABD24F0D5D0F9480B85F62CC1F6D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0034462","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Diagnostic Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christian A","key":"hundahlpau","last":"Hundahl","locid":"4068fa43-1969-4dc4-ad4b-f3f9a477ce70","name":"Hundahl, Christian Ansgar","name_org":"Hundahl, Christian A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"fahrenkrugpau","last":"Fahrenkrug","locid":"ad1d6e49-d84d-4c14-b169-6a8642a0a5b1","name":"Fahrenkrug, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"hayschmidtpau","last":"Hay-Schmidt","locid":"f0f495a2-fe48-4cdf-8f27-ea207182bda8","name":"Hay-Schmidt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9984-7014","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"georgpau","last":"Georg","locid":"02e3d874-7eaf-4090-aaa4-e768fb6cb798","name":"Georg, Birgitte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"faltoftpau","last":"Faltoft","name":"Faltoft, Birgitte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","locid":"b2810b1e-a8c8-41cb-bb4f-669ad1ff6b65","name":"Hannibal, Jens","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22496809"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0034462","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"PloS one","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84859344720"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0c144f82-5ea1-4f5f-b536-1e8e8cd719b3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Circadian behaviour in neuroglobin deficient mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-400673","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The ALICE experiment has measured low-mass dimuon production in pp collisions at \\sqrt{s} = 7 TeV in the dimuon rapidity region 2.5y\\eta^{}, \\phi) into muons and semi-leptonic decays of charmed mesons. The measured production cross sections for \\omega and \\phi are \\sigma_\\omega (1p_t5 GeV/c,2.5y4) = 5.28 +- 0.54 (stat) +- 0.50 (syst) mb and \\sigma_\\phi(1p_t5 GeV/c,2.5y4)=0.940 +- 0.084 (stat) +- 0.078 (syst) mb. The differential cross sections d^2\\sigma/dy dp_t are extracted as a function of p_t for \\omega and \\phi. The ratio between the \\rho and \\omega cross section is obtained. Results for the \\phi are compared with other measurements at the same energy and with predictions by models.","author_count":927,"contributors":["Collaboration, ALICE","Abelev, B.","Abrahantes Quintana, A.","Adamová, D.","M. Adare, A.","M. Aggarwal, M.","Aglieri Rinella, G.","G. Agocs, A.","Agostinelli, A.","Aguilar Salazar, S.","Ahammed, Z.","Ahmad, N.","Ahmad Masoodi, A.","U. Ahn, S.","Akindinov, A.","Aleksandrov, D.","Alessandro, B.","Alfaro Molina, R.","Alici, A.","Alkin, A.","Almaráz Aviña, E.","Alt, T.","Altini, V.","Altinpinar, S.","Altsybeev, I.","Andrei, C.","Andronic, A.","Anguelov, V.","Anson, C.","Antičić, T.","Antinori, F.","Antonioli, P.","Aphecetche, L.","Appelshäuser, H.","Arbor, N.","Arcelli, S.","Arend, A.","Armesto, N.","Arnaldi, R.","Aronsson, T.","C. Arsene, I.","Arslandok, M.","Asryan, A.","Averbeck, R.","C. Awes, T.","Äystö, J.","D. Azmi, M.","Badalà, A.","W. Baek, Y.","Bailhache, R.","Bala, R.","Baldini Ferroli, R.","Baldisseri, A.","Baldit, A.","Baltasar Dos Santos Pedrosa, F.","Bán, J.","C. Baral, R.","Barbera, R.","Barile, F.","G. Barnaföldi, G.","S. Barnby, L.","Barret, V.","Bartke, J.","Basile, M.","Bastid, N.","Bathen, B.","Batigne, G.","Batyunya, B.","Baumann, C.","Bearden, Ian","Beck, Halfdan","Belikov, I.","Bellini, F.","Bellwied, R.","Belmont-Moreno, E.","Beole, S.","Berceanu, I.","Bercuci, A.","Berdnikov, Y.","Berenyi, D.","Berz