{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The purpose of this study was to make a normative description of the nature and duration of genital lesions sustained during consensual sexual intercourse, using the three most commonly used techniques; visualisation using the naked eye, colposcopy and toluidine blue dye followed by colposcopy. METHODS: Ninety eight women were examined within 48h of consensual sexual intercourse. Fifty of the women were examined twice again within the following 7 days of sexual abstinence after the first examination. RESULTS: The participants had a median age of 22.4 years and 88% were nulliparous. Lesions were frequent; 34% seen with the naked eye, 49% seen with colposcopy and 52% seen with toluidine blue dye and subsequent colposcopy. The lesions lasted for several days; the median survival times for lacerations were 24, 40 and 80h, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: The legal implications of these findings are that genital lesions by themselves do not corroborate a rape complaint. Genital lesions may, however, corroborate specific details of a case and should be documented as carefully as any other lesion in rape complaints.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Astrup, Birgitte Schmidt","Ravn, Pernille","Lauritsen, Jens","Thomsen, Jørgen Lange"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-609530"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Voldtægt","frivilligt samleje"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nature frequency and duration of genital lesions after consensual sexual intercourse implications for legal proceedings","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.forsciint.2011.11.028","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-609530","identifier":[{"id":"22192579","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84861571809","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7f08e251-c1e3-446f-808d-8624ded8ac91"],"keyword":["Voldtægt","frivilligt samleje","læsioner"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-32D95A10452AD35BBA0BAB024ECA2979"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.forsciint.2011.11.028","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Gynaecology and Obstetrics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine, Forensic Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgitte Schmidt","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"7f6334d2-e0ea-473e-adbb-e1246c3db81a","name":"Astrup, Birgitte Schmidt","orcid":"0000-0003-4266-9290","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"b86a181f-31f7-452e-9900-74267c1011d3","name":"Ravn, Pernille","orcid":"0000-0001-8752-1121","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"lauritsenpau","last":"Lauritsen","locid":"4c460020-fd7b-478a-ad2d-183a6808842a","name":"Lauritsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-9281-8990","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen Lange","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"02c01238-a1bb-411b-97e9-54415fc12c59","name":"Thomsen, Jørgen Lange","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22192579"],"pub":{"