{"abstract":"Postprandial hyperglucagonemia is frequently found in patients with diabetes. Recently, a loss of the inverse relationship between pulsatile insulin and glucagon secretion has been reported in patients with type 2 diabetes. The crosstalk between pulsatile islet hormone secretion in prediabetic individuals has not yet been examined.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rohrer, Stefan","Menge, Björn A","Grüber, Lena","Deacon, Carolyn F.","Schmidt, Wolfgang E","Veldhuis, Johannes D","Holst, Jens Juul","Meier, Juris J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514531"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Blood Glucose","Female","Glucagon","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Insulin","Male","Middle Aged","Postprandial Period","Prediabetic State"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impaired crosstalk between pulsatile insulin and glucagon secretion in prediabetic individuals","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/jc.2011-3439","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514531","identifier":[{"id":"22399501","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84860764263","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cac34463-65b0-4f7c-abfe-782bfe717074"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Blood Glucose","Female","Glucagon","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Insulin","Male","Middle Aged","Postprandial Period","Prediabetic State"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-86F8F43D8B5459F2338FEA695480D9C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/jc.2011-3439","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Translational Metabolic Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Stefan","key":"rohrerpau","last":"Rohrer","name":"Rohrer, Stefan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Björn A","key":"mengepau","last":"Menge","name":"Menge, Björn A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lena","key":"grüberpau","last":"Grüber","name":"Grüber, Lena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carolyn F","key":"deaconpau","last":"Deacon","locid":"b2d3dfed-9e39-46d3-bec7-3cc850404b47","name":"Deacon, Carolyn F.","name_org":"Deacon, Carolyn F","orcid":"0000-0003-2611-5642","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wolfgang E","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Wolfgang E","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Johannes D","key":"veldhuispau","last":"Veldhuis","name":"Veldhuis, Johannes D","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juris J","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Juris J","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22399501"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2011-3439","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860764263"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cac34463-65b0-4f7c-abfe-782bfe717074"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impaired crosstalk between pulsatile insulin and glucagon secretion in prediabetic individuals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514531","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Background: In the development of glucose control algorithms, mathematical models of glucose metabolism are useful for conducting simulation studies and making real-time predictions upon which control calculations can be based. To obtain type 1 diabetes (T1D) data for the modeling of glucose metabolism, we designed and conducted a clinical study.Methods: Patients with insulin pump–treated T1D were recruited to perform everyday life events on two separate days. During the study, patients wore their insulin pumps and, in addition, a continuous glucose monitor and an activity monitor to estimate energy expenditure. The sequence of everyday life events was predetermined and included carbohydrate intake, insulin boluses, and bouts of exercise; the events were introduced, temporally separated, in different orders and in different quantities. Throughout the study day, 10-min plasma glucose measurements were taken, and samples for plasma insulin and glucagon analyses were obtained every 10 min for the first 30 min after an event and subsequently every 30 min.Results: We included 12 patients with T1D (75% female, 34.3±9.1 years old [mean±SD], hemoglobin A1c 6.7±0.4%). During the 24 study days we collected information-rich, high-quality data during fast and slow changes in plasma glucose following carbohydrate intake, exercise, and insulin boluses.Conclusions: This study has generated T1D data suitable for glucose modeling, which will be used in the development of glucose control strategies. Furthermore, the study has given new physiologic insight into the metabolic effects of carbohydrate intake, insulin boluses, and exercise in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion–treated patients with T1D.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Schmidt, Signe","Finan, Daniel Aaron","Duun-Henriksen, Anne Katrine","Jørgensen, John Bagterp","Madsen, Henrik","Bengtsson, Henrik","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Nørgaard, Kirsten"],"cuid":["S02-091.31-037471"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living","Adult","Blood Glucose","Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus Type 1","Dietary Carbohydrates","Exercise Test","Female","Glucagon","Heart Rate","Hemoglobin A Glycosylated","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents","Infusions Subcutaneous","Insulin","Insulin Infusion Systems","Male","Middle Aged","Models Theoretical"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"OT":["Mathematical Statistics"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-NOVO","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of everyday life events on glucose insulin and glucagon dynamics in continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion treated type 000000000001 diabetes collection of clinical data for glucose modeling","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1089/dia.2011.0101","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.31-037471","identifier":[{"id":"22023376","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84857809758","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d89ebb10-9c18-46eb-84e9-93079cf05a5d","ku-a0a9fc57-5c15-4edb-87d9-2d76a32abe38"],"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living","Adult","Blood Glucose","Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 1","Dietary Carbohydrates","Exercise Test","Female","Glucagon","Heart Rate","Hemoglobin A, Glycosylated","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents","Infusions, Subcutaneous","Insulin","Insulin Infusion Systems","Male","Middle Aged","Models, Theoretical"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A86B8E8FB584B1BD5872209DE565E625"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","t