blisher":"Mary AnnLiebert, Inc. Publishers","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Technology & Therapeutics","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84857809758"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Novo Nordisk","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d89ebb10-9c18-46eb-84e9-93079cf05a5d","ku-a0a9fc57-5c15-4edb-87d9-2d76a32abe38"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of Everyday Life Events on Glucose, Insulin, and Glucagon Dynamics in Continuous Subcutaneous Insulin Infusion–Treated Type 1 Diabetes: Collection of Clinical Data for Glucose Modeling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.31-037471","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Autonomous Aerial Sensors, i.e. meteorological sensors mounted on Unmanned Aerial Systems UAS, can characterise the atmospheric flow in and around wind farms. We instrumented three planes, a helicopter and a lighter-than-air LTA system to fly one week together in a well-instrumented wind farm, partly with nano-synchronised sensors (time stamped with about 100 ns global accuracy). Between bankruptcy of a partner, denied overflight rights at the main test location, denied Civil Aviation Authorities permits at the alternative location, stolen planes, and crashed UAS we managed to collect data at a wind farm in Lolland and on an atmospheric campaign in France. Planning of an offshore campaign using the developed techniques is underway.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Giebel, Gregor","Schmidt Paulsen, Uwe","Bange, Jens","la Cour-Harbo, Anders","Reuder, Joachim","Mayer, Stephanie","van der Kroonenberg, Aline","Mølgaard, John"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011316"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eberhard Karls Universität Tübingen","University of Bergen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomous aerial sensors for wind power meteorology a pre project","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/60873544/PSOAerialSensors_FinalReport.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011316","ids":["aau-ed0442dd-700a-402c-8395-2ade81454edc","dtu-b5d291b5-8a82-4571-afa5-61380d2fb0bc"],"keyword":["Risø-R-17