{"abstract":"Nerve Growth Factor (NGF) has therapeutic effects on the cholinergic neurodegeneration in Alzheimer's disease (AD). We have previously described an implantable Encapsulated Cell Biodelivery™ device, NsG0202, capable of local delivery of NGF to the human cholinergic basal forebrain. Results from a small Phase 1b clinical study showed that the NGF dose could advantageously be increased. We have therefore developed a second generation clinical device named NsG0202.1, containing an RPE cell line (NGC0211) generated with transposon expression technology for highdose NGF production. Furthermore, to promote cell attachment and long-term viability of NGC0211, a polyethylene terephthalate (PET) yarn scaffolding was used. The safety was tested in Göttingen minipigs during a six months period with NsG0202.1 implants placed in the basal forebrain. The devices were well tolerated and the NGC0211 viability and NGF secretion remained after 6 months in vivo. The NGF induced relevant biological responses in the surrounding cholinergic target neurons.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Fjord-Larsen, Lone","Kusk, Philip","Torp, Malene","Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt Ettrup","Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","Tornøe, Jens","Juliusson, Bengt","Wahlberg, Lars U."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806866"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Fjord-Larsen, Lone"],"keyword":["Alzheimer s disease","Göttingen minipigs","Nerve Growth Factor","Sleeping Beauty","Transposon"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"encapsulated cell biodelivery of transposon mediated high dose ngf to the göttingen mini pig basal forebrain","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2174/1875043501205010035","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806866","identifier":[{"id":"84861866391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8190f2d3-5f8e-4f80-a0c8-9ecb4d839df4"],"keyword":["Alzheimer's disease","Encapsulated cell biodelivery™","Göttingen minipigs","Nerve growth factor","Preclinical testing","Sleeping beauty","Transposon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FE15023E9F96839487932E1EC58F7C03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2174/1875043501205010035","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurosurgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"fjordlarsenpau","last":"Fjord-Larsen","name":"Fjord-Larsen, Lone","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip","key":"kuskpau","last":"Kusk","name":"Kusk, Philip","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"torppau","last":"Torp","name":"Torp, Malene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Christian H.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f442e934-3b4d-4fc2-91dc-93621be94d60","name":"Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","name_org":"Sørensen, Jens Christian H.","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-7405","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaare","key":"ettruppau","last":"Ettrup","locid":"8863b0b7-8c38-42cd-be8d-4544230a3d4e","name":"Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt Ettrup","name_org":"Ettrup, Kaare","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten R.","key":"bjarkampau","last":"Bjarkam","locid":"a1770adc-a79f-434a-98bc-02e64ffd13cd","name":"Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","name_org":"Bjarkam, Carsten R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"tornøepau","last":"Tornøe","name":"Tornøe, Jens","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bengt","key":"juliussonpau","last":"Juliusson","name":"Juliusson, Bengt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars U.","key":"wahlbergpau","last":"Wahlberg","name":"Wahlberg, Lars U.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/1875043501205010035","issn":["18750435"],"issue":"1","journal":"Open Tissue Engineering and Regenerative Medicine Journal","pages":"35-42","status":"p","title":"Open Tissue Engineering and Regenerative Medicine Journal","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84861866391"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8190f2d3-5f8e-4f80-a0c8-9ecb4d839df4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Encapsulated Cell Biodelivery of Transposon-Mediated High-Dose NGF to the Göttingen Mini Pig Basal Forebrain","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806866","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Alterations in the human gut microbiota caused, for example, by diet, functional foods, antibiotics, or occurring as a function of age are now known to be of relevance for host health. Therefore, there is a strong need for methods to detect such alterations in a rapid and comprehensive manner. In the present study, we developed and validated a high-throughput real-time quantitative PCR-based analysis platform, termed 'GUt Low-Density Array' (GULDA). The platform was designed for simultaneous analysis of the change in the abundance of 31 different microbial 16S rRNA gene targets in fecal samples obtained from individuals at various points in time. The target genes represent important phyla, genera, species, or other taxonomic groups within the five predominant bacterial phyla of the gut, Firmicutes, Bacteroidetes, Actinobacteria, Proteobacteria, and Verrucomicrobia and also Euryarchaeota. To demonstrate the applicability of GULDA, analysis of fecal samples obtained from six healthy infants at both 9 and 18 months of age was performed and showed a significant increase over time of the relative abundance of bacteria belonging to Clostridial cluster IV (Clostridia leptum group) and Bifidobacterium bifidum and concurrent decrease in the abundance of Clostridium butyricum and a tendency for decrease in Enterobacteriaceae over the 9-month period.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bergström, Anders","Licht, Tine Rask","Wilcks, Andrea","Andersen, Jens Bo","Schmidt, Line Rieck","Grønlund, Hugo Ahlm","Vigsnæs, Louise Kristine","Michaelsen, Kim F","Bahl, Martin Iain"],"cuid":["S02-096.76-036909"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Gut microbiology","LinRegPCR","Microbiota","qPCR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introducing gut low density array gulda a validated approach for qpcr based intestinal microbial community analysis","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1574-6968.12004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.76-036909","identifier":[{"id":"22967145","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84869081555","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-be597651-2ac7-4de5-bc7d-1ee3aa66a823","ku-5f6c4b74-ac55-4f68-9e1e-3f237e987d4a"],"keyword":["Gut microbiology","LinRegPCR","Microbiota","qPCR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E89ABD0C6AB42ECB25B3517158461F6C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/1574-6968.12004","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Food Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Human Nutrition, Paediatric Nutrition and International Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"bergströmpau","last":"Bergström","locid":"0d713b3e-4609-47dc-9997-f8a542798b05","name":"Bergström, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0961-0799","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine Rask","key":"lichtpau","last":"Licht","locid":"b5270ea1-1dc7-4db8-8644-c7ef75331664","name":"Licht, Tine Rask","orcid":"0000-0002-6399-9574","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrea","key":"wilckspau","last":"Wilcks","locid":"6aacd625-74d9-4ffb-bd02-0aa5adf84f00","name":"Wilcks, Andrea","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Bo","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"3741bce4-5dbe-49a4-a79d-61154c20e7c0","name":"Andersen, Jens Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line R","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"36aa9703-959f-43d1-8c8e-1813229c067b","name":"Schmidt, Line Rieck","name_org":"Schmidt, Line R","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hugo A","key":"grønlundpau","last":"Grønlund","locid":"fa288034-81c2-42a2-9928-956e31f484cc","name":"Grønlund, Hugo Ahlm","name_org":"Grønlund, Hugo A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise K","key":"vigsnaespau","last":"Vigsnaes","locid":"5db553a1-31e2-4364-a432-c4e13e735575","name":"Vigsnæs, Louise Kristine","name_org":"Vigsnaes, Louise K","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kim F.","key":"michaelsenpau","last":"Michaelsen","locid":"c29a2565-4c7e-4a5b-ab39-899baedae963","name":"Michaelsen, Kim F.","orcid":"0000-0003-0449-0839","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Iain","key":"bahlpau","last":"Bahl","locid":"6e2651b2-1c65-49a5-81c3-9065190c95e2","name":"Bahl, Martin Iain","orcid":"0000-0003-1579-8038","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22967145"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1574-6968.12004","issn":["03781097","15746968"],"issn_org":["03781097"],"issue":"1","journal":"FEMS Microbiology Letters","pages":"38-47","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"FEMS Microbiology Letters","title_org":"F E M S Microbiology Letters","volume":"337"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84869081555"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-be597651-2ac7-4de5-bc7d-1ee3aa66a823","ku-5f6c4b74-ac55-4f68-9e1e-3f237e987d4a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introducing GUt Low-Density Array (GULDA) - a validated approach for qPCR-based intestinal microbial community analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.76-036909","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Introduction. Shrinkage during polymerization of resin-based composite materials may lead to gap formation and hamper the marginal adaptaion of the restorations. To reduce the problem of polymerization shrinkage, a new composite material (Filtek™ Silorane, 3M-ESPE, Germany), with a reduced shrinkage, has been marketed. Objective. To investigate whether reduced polymerization shrinkage improves the marginal adaptation of composite restorations. Material and methods. A total of 156 scanning electron microscopy (SEM) pictures (78 baseline, 78 follow-up) of the occlusal part of Class II restorations in molars were included in the study. The restorations originated from a randomized clinical trial, conducted in 2007-2009 which compared the clinical performance of a low-shrinkage composite material (Filtek™ Silorane) with that of a methacrylate-based composite material (Ceram•X™mono). Epon-casts of the restorations were used for SEM pictures at x 16 magnification. Pictures from baseline and follow-up (398 days, SD 29 days) were randomized and the examiner was blinded to the material and the age of the restoration. Stereologic measurements were used to calculate the length and the width of the marginal discrepancies. Results. No statistically significant difference in gap formation and chipping was found between the two materials. Conclusion. The results of the present study do not support the hypothesis that reduced polymerization shrinkage improves the marginal adaptation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schmidt, Malene","Bindslev, Preben Hørsted","Poulsen, Sven","Nyengaard, Jens Randel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154963"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Polymerization shrinkage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"marginal adaptation of a low shrinkage silorane based composite a sem analysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/52048596/Marginal_adaptation_of_a_low_shrinktage_silorane_based_composite.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154963","ids":["au-2cce0379-c6dc-49f7-8e33-d8b158ade34d"],"keyword":["Polymerization shrinkage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9797DD2A3863FE305FF38F1619102D44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.tandlaegebladet.dk/tbarkiv/736-742.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/52048596/Marginal_adaptation_of_a_low_shrinktage_silorane_based_composite.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health, Department of Dentistry and Oral Health - Section for Pediatric Dentistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"5cd2e04c-40d9-4ae2-acfc-bdd5e3382842","name":"Schmidt, Malene","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Preben Hørsted","key":"bindslevpau","last":"Bindslev","locid":"23fd703e-36ff-4164-9e77-7af6a9ed483c","name":"Bindslev, Preben Hørsted","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sven","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8aef5b7c-d4cd-47eb-8326-03ed409802d1","name":"Poulsen, Sven","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Randel","key":"nyengaardpau","last":"Nyengaard","locid":"8288d58c-4602-4c0c-9b76-949cc83d281b","name":"Nyengaard, Jens Randel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00399353","24458112"],"issn_org":["00399353"],"issue":"10","journal":"Tandlægebladet","pages":"736-742","publisher":"Tandlægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Tandlægebladet","volume":"116"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2cce0379-c6dc-49f7-8e33-d8b158ade34d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Marginal adaptation of a low-shrinkage silorane-based composite: A SEM-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154963","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt Ettrup","Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","Rodell, Anders","Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-218699"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypothalamic deep brain stimulation influence autonomic and limbic circuitry involved in regulation of aggression and cardio cerebrovascular control in the göttingen minipig","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-218699","ids":["au-9ce6a531-4e82-44ef-bd90-ec7e679e7e5d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-072604BED2F455E57A8F8CABF00C500E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Health Administrative Centre, Health Administrative Centre - PhD Administration"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kåre Schmidt Ettrup","key":"ettruppau","last":"Ettrup","locid":"8863b0b7-8c38-42cd-be8d-4544230a3d4e","name":"Ettrup, Kåre Schmidt Ettrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian H.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"f442e934-3b4d-4fc2-91dc-93621be94d60","name":"Sørensen, Jens Christian Hedemann","name_org":"Sørensen, Jens Christian H.","orcid":"0000-0001-5139-7405","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rodellpau","last":"Rodell","locid":"8393d270-02cc-401d-9662-5e1698e8ac45","name":"Rodell, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aage Kristian Olsen","key":"alstruppau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"fa66f5b8-0468-4e85-b570-969776c5ebde","name":"Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","orcid":"0000-0002-0084-9122","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Reidies","key":"bjarkampau","last":"Bjarkam","locid":"a1770adc-a79f-434a-98bc-02e64ffd13cd","name":"Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10116125","14230372"],"issn_org":["10116125"],"journal":"Stereotactic and Functional Neurosurgery","pages":"281-291","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Stereotactic and Functional Neurosurgery","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9ce6a531-4e82-44ef-bd90-ec7e679e7e5d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Hypothalamic deep brain stimulation influence autonomic and limbic circuitry involved in regulation of aggression and cardio-cerebrovascular control in the Göttingen minipig","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-218699","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"sorLA is a sorting receptor for amyloid precursor protein (APP) genetically linked to Alzheimer's disease (AD). Retromer, an adaptor complex in the endosome-to-Golgi retrieval pathway, has been implicated in APP transport because retromer deficiency leads to aberrant APP sorting and processing and levels of retromer proteins are altered in AD. Here we report that sorLA and retromer functionally interact in neurons to control trafficking and amyloidogenic processing of APP. We have identified a sequence (FANSHY) in the cytoplasmic domain of sorLA that is recognized by the VPS26 subunit of the retromer complex. Accordingly, we characterized the interaction between the retromer complex and sorLA and determined the role of retromer on sorLA-dependent sorting and processing of APP. Mutations in the VPS26 binding site resulted in receptor redistribution to the endosomal network, similar to the situation seen in cells with VPS26 knockdown. The sorLA mutant retained APP-binding activity but, as opposed to the wild-type receptor, misdirected APP into a distinct non-Golgi compartment, resulting in increased amyloid processing. In conclusion, our data provide a molecular link between reduced retromer expression and increased amyloidogenesis as seen in patients with sporadic AD.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Fjorback, Anja W","Seaman, Matthew","Gustafsen, Camilla","Mehmedbasic, Arnela","Gokool, Suzanne","Wu, Chengbiao","Militz, Daniel","Schmidt, Vanessa","Madsen, Peder","Nyengaard, Jens Randel","E Willnow, Thomas","Christensen, Erik Ilsø","B Mobley, William","Nykjær, Anders","Andersen, Olav Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-236223"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"retromer binds the fanshy sorting motif in sorla to regulate amyloid precursor protein sorting and processing","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1523/JNEUROSCI.2272-11.2012","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-236223","identifier":[{"id":"22279231","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84863011338","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bb31233b-4214-44a8-ba1e-ddc40122b1e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D0DB32D3FB9D58AA258C5B0D93CD354"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1523/JNEUROSCI.2272-11.2012","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.jneurosci.org/content/32/4/1467","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Vest"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja W","key":"fjorbackpau","last":"Fjorback","locid":"e7301cb3-ebea-4315-9101-4e8a254615fa","name":"Fjorback, Anja W","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthew","key":"seamanpau","last":"Seaman","name":"Seaman, Matthew","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"gustafsenpau","last":"Gustafsen","locid":"a22c704a-d543-4ccf-b3d8-52a5461f8b48","name":"Gustafsen, Camilla","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arnela","key":"mehmedbasicpau","last":"Mehmedbasic","locid":"971bd310-19a4-46f5-8eb9-4cf0099f76ba","name":"Mehmedbasic, Arnela","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Suzanne","key":"gokoolpau","