{"abstract":"Coronary angiography is the current standard method to evaluate coronary atherosclerosis in patients with suspected angina pectoris, but non-invasive CT scanning of the coronaries are increasingly used for the same purpose. Low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol and other lipid and lipoprotein variables are major risk factors for coronary artery disease. Small dense LDL particles may be of particular importance, but clinical studies evaluating their predictive value for coronary atherosclerosis are few.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Toft-Petersen, Anne Pernille","Tilsted, Hans-Henrik","Aarøe, Jens","Rasmussen, Klaus","Christensen, T.","Griffin, Bruce A","Aardestrup, Inge Valbak","Andreasen, Annette","Schmidt, Erik Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-138437"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case Control Studies","Coronary Angiography","Coronary artery disease","Female","Humans","Lipoproteins LDL","Male","Middle Aged","Particle Size","Tomography X Ray Computed"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"small dense ldl particles a predictor of coronary artery disease evaluated by invasive and ct based techniques a case control study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1476-511X-10-21","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-138437","identifier":[{"id":"78951495282","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21262005","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3038964","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-0fd7ac82-2ed0-48dc-a341-04d42b9e433f"],"keyword":["Case-Control Studies","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease","Female","Humans","Lipoproteins, LDL","Male","Middle Aged","Particle Size","Tomography, X-Ray Computed"],"lang":"Englis