{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Treatment methods for improved anaerobic digestion (AD) of waste activated sludge were evaluated. Pretreatments at moderate thermal (water bath at 80 °C), high thermal (loop autoclave at 130–170 °C) and thermo-chemical (170 °C/pH 10) conditions prior to AD in batch vials (40 days/37 °C) were compared with inter-stage treatments under the same conditions carried out between two separate steps of AD (19–21 days/37 °C). Combined treatment at 80 °C with CO2/ NH3-stripping was also evaluated. RESULTS: Pretreatment at 80 °C had no effect on methane yield while inter-stage treatment gave a 20% increase, compared with controls. Combining inter-stage treatment with CO2/ NH3-stripping gave an increase in pH (7.1 to 9.3), a drop in ammonia-N concentration (910 mg-N to 510 mg-N) and a methane yield improvement of 31%. Pretreatment at 130 °C, 170 °C and 170 °C/pH 10 considerably increased the methane production within the first 4 days but the improvement following 40 days of digestion was only 13%, 9% and 2%, respectively. In comparison, inter-stage treatment led to improvements of 9% (130 °C), 29% (170 °C) and 28% (170 °C/pH 10). All treatment processes increased sludge solubilization. CONCLUSION: Thermal treatment of waste activated sludge for improved anaerobic digestion seems more effective when applied as an inter-stage treatment rather than a pretreatment. Copyright © 2010 Society of Chemical Industry","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bangsø Nielsen, Henrik","Thygesen, Anders","Thomsen, Anne Belinda","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347466"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio refinery","Bio systems","Bioraffinaderi","Biosystemer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anaerobic digestion of waste activated sludge comparison of thermal pretreatments with thermal inter stage treatments","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jctb.2509","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-347466","identifier":[{"id":"78651062313","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8fc79e73-6f84-46e8-9a9a-df2119a743f8"],"keyword":["Bio refinery","Bio systems","Bioraffinaderi","Biosystemer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2A3106D79158F78302376C7C9018FCB0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jctb.2509","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division, Bioenergy and Biomass"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"bangsønielsenpau","last":"Bangsø Nielsen","locid":"4cd7caa6-1ad7-4481-8c17-b7d8fc702426","name":"Bangsø Nielsen, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","locid":"8225946c-d334-4d1e-8325-fba8f0a965e2","name":"Thygesen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8440-1121","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Belinda","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"6d41381f-5828-44bd-8130-e36b2b35e4b6","name":"Thomsen, Anne Belinda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"4f0d57ca-a0c5-43cf-ada5-378c053ab8c7","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jctb.2509","issn":["02682575","03681084"],"issn_org":["02682575"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Chemical Technology and Biotechnology","pages":"238-245","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Chemical Technology and Biotechnology","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78651062313"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8fc79e73-6f84-46e8-9a9a-df2119a743f8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Anaerobic digestion of waste activated sludge—comparison of thermal pretreatments with thermal inter-stage treatments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347466","year":"2011","yearsub":"2010"}
{"abstract":"This poster describes a new approach for measurements in wind power meteorology using small unmanned flying platforms. During a week of flying a lighter-than-air vehicle, two small electrically powered aeroplanes and a larger helicopter at the Risø test station at Høvsøre [NEWS: due to legal reasons regarding overflight rights, we will fly at Nøjsomheds Odde], we will compare wind speed measurements with fixed mast and LIDAR measurements, investigate optimal flight patterns for each measurement task, and measure other interesting meteorological features like the air-sea boundary in the vicinity of the wind farm. In order to prepare the measurement campaign, a workshop was held, soliciting input from various communities.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Giebel, Gregor","Schmidt Paulsen, Uwe","Reuder, Joachim","la Cour-Harbo, Anders","Thomsen, Carsten","Bange, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378170"],"event":{"end":"2011-04-08","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2011-04-03","title":"European Geosciences Union General Assembly 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bergen","University of Tübingen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DELTA Microelectronics"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomous aerial sensors for wind power meteorology","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/203299146/GiebelEtAl_AutonomousAerialSensorsForWindPowerMeteorology_Poster_EGU2011.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-378170","ids":["dtu-f608