{"abstract":"Ensiling of humid biomass samples wrapped in plastic bales has been investigated as a wet-storage for bioethanol production from three lignocellulosic biomass samples i.e. maize, rye, and clover grass. During the silage process, lactic acid bacteria fermented free sugars to lactic acid, and consequently by lowing pH, inhibiting other microbes to degrade the polysaccharides. Following silage treatment, enzymatic convertibility tests showed that 51.5%, 36.5%, and 41.9% of the cellulose was converted by cellulytic enzymes in ensiled maize, rye, and clover grass, respectively. In addition, tests of SSF (simultaneous saccharification and fermentation) were carried out using combined enzymatic hydrolysis and fermentation with two different microorganisms Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Kluyveromyces marxianus. The ethanol production was 33.0%, 27.5%, 36.9% (by K. marxianus) and 29.0%, 28.1%, 34.5% (by S. cerevisiae); the yields significantly increased after hydrothermal pretreatment: 77.7%, 72.8%, 79.5% (by K. marxianus) and 72.0%, 80.7%, 75.7% (by S. cerevisiae) of the theoretical based on the C6 sugar contents in maize, rye, and clover grass, respectively.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Oleskowicz-Popiel, Piotr","Thomsen, Anne Belinda","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325318"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio refinery","Bioraffinaderi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ensiling wet storage method for lignocellulosic biomass for bioethanol production","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2011.02.003","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-325318","identifier":[{"id":"79953271438","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-45b9d701-aaa5-4b08-a881-ffd8e496b352"],"keyword":["Bio refinery","Bioraffinaderi"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD9C422B431EB26628C963E086328C9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biombioe.2011.02.003","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division, Bioenergy and Biomass"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Piotr","key":"oleskowiczpopielpau","last":"Oleskowicz-Popiel","locid":"f20fe170-864a-46ab-ab59-6472bc7e9a54","name":"Oleskowicz-Popiel, Piotr","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Belinda","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"6d41381f-5828-44bd-8130-e36b2b35e4b6","name":"Thomsen, Anne Belinda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ejbye","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"4f0d57ca-a0c5-43cf-ada5-378c053ab8c7","name":"Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biombioe.2011.02.003","issn":["09619534","18732909"],"issn_org":["09619534"],"issue":"5","journal":"Biomass & Bioenergy","pages":"2087-2092","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biomass & Bioenergy","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953271438"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Uni