he Göttingen minipig : intubation, bladder catheterization, femoral vessel catheterization, and transcardial perfusion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.87-704160","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"One way of reducing the emissions of fossil fuel‐derived CO2 is to replace fossil fuels with biofuels produced from agricultural biomasses or residuals. However, cultivation of soils results in emission of other greenhouse gasses, especially nitrous oxide (N2O). Previous studies have shown that field emissions of N2O contribute significantly to total greenhouse gas emissions during biofuel production, and in terms of global warming N2O emissions may counterbalance a considerable part of the avoided fossil CO2 emissions that are achieved by fossil fuel displacement. In the present study, we relate measured field emissions of N2O to the reduction in fossil fuel‐derived CO2, which is obtained when agricultural biomasses are used for biofuel production. The analysis includes five organically managed crops (viz. maize, rye, rye‐vetch, vetch and grass‐clover) and three scenarios for conversion of biomass to biofuel. The scenarios are 1) bioethanol, 2) biogas and 3) co‐production of bioethanol and biogas. In scenarios 3, the biomass is first used for bioethanol fermentation and subsequently the residue from this process is utilized for biogas production. The net reduction in greenhouse gas emissions is calculated as the avoided fossil fuel‐derived CO2, where the N2O emission has been subtracted. This value does not account for CO2 emissions from farm machinery and during biofuel production. We obtained the greatest net reduction in greenhouse gas emissions by co‐production of bioethanol and biogas or by biogas alone produced from either fresh grass‐clover or whole crop maize. Here the net reduction corresponded to about 8 tons CO2 ha‐1 yr‐1.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Carter, Mette Sustmann","Hauggaard-Nielsen, Henrik","Heiske, Stefan","Thomsen, Sune Tjalfe","Jensen, Morten","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye","Johansen, Anders","Ambus, Per"],"cuid":["S02-099.23-013606"],"event":{"end":"2011-11-04","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2011-11-02","title":"Sixth International Symposium on Non-CO2 Greenhouse gases (NCGG-6),","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Environment and climate","Miljø og klima"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"field emissions of n000000000002o during biomass production may affect the sustainability of agro biofuels","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6244952/Field%20emissions.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.23-013606","ids":["au-0dfaa1a0-1f19-4d04-9f0a-8efd942ff8b2","dtu-f6be01ff-2676-4e14-a013-962e420d4b2d"],"keyword":["Environment and climate","Miljø og klima"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-907C48E1321F37D3B0D1DC2E9A7479E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6244952/Field%20emissions.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Biosystems Division, Ecosystems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","