{"abstract":"Aims  The Liraglutide Effect and Action in Diabetes 6 trial was an open-label trial comparing liraglutide with exenatide as an 'add-on' to metformin and/or sulphonylurea. Methods  Patients with Type 2 diabetes were randomized to liraglutide 1.8 mg once daily or exenatide 10 μg twice daily for 26 weeks. This was followed by a 14-week extension phase, in which all patients received liraglutide 1.8 mg once daily. Results  Patient-reported outcomes were measured in 379 patients using Diabetes Treatment Satisfaction Questionnaire status (DTSQs) and DTSQ change (DTSQc). The change in overall treatment satisfaction (DTSQs score) from baseline at week 26 with liraglutide was 4.71 and with exentaide was 1.66 [difference between groups 3.04 (95% CI 1.73-4.35), P ","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schmidt, W E","Christiansen, Jens Sandahl","Hammer, Michael","Zychma, M J","Buse, J B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244697"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcomes are superior in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes treated with liraglutide as compared with exenatide when added to metformin sulphonylurea or both results from a randomized open label study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2011.03276.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244697","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3123703","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"21388442","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79955950106","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c9f1cf7a-566e-4173-9ed8-42a5d809575c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C0B4DED8108D04A476FD8CDF3266DB70"],"oa_link":[{"acc