{"abstract":"In this work protective \"sight glasses\" for infrared gas sensors showing a sub-wavelength nanostructure with random patterns have been fabricated by reactive ion etching (RIE) in an easy and comparable cheap single step mask-less process. By an organic coating, the intrinsic water repellent property of the surface could be enhanced, shown by contact angle and roll-off angle measurements. The \"self-cleaning\" surface property and chemical robustness towards aggressive environments are demonstrated. FT-IR spectroscopy concerning the optical properties of these nanostructured silicon windows revealed a stable anti-reflective \"moth-eye\" effect in certain wavelength ranges owing to the nanostructures.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bergmann, René","Davis, Zachary James","Schmidt, Michael Stenbæk","Clausen, Sønnik","Boisen, Anja","Jensen, Jens Muller","Buchner, Rainer","Stolberg-Rohr, Thomine","Jakobsen, Mogens Havsteen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-337019"],"event":{"end":"2011-04-28","place":"Orlando, us","start":"2011-04-27","title":"Window and Dome Technologies and Materials XII","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Combustion pollution control technologies","Forbrænding miljøforbedrende teknologier","Nanostructured surface","Superhydrophobic"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-DFS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-DFS","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of nanostructured protective sight glasses for ir gas sensors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.883921","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-337019","identifier":[{"id":"79959820577","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6c940af9-c63d-42cd-86de-8f7b0dc4c5bf"],"keyword":["Anti-reflective surface","Combustion pollution control technologies","Forbrænding miljøforbedrende teknologier","Infrared gas sensor","Nanostructured surface","Protective window","Superhydrophobic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7CC035EF6900D48C5177B20CFAB5CEB4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.883921","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danfoss","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-DFS","l3nl":"Danfoss","l3nn":"Danfoss","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danfoss","namevar":["Danfoss AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-DFS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René","key":"bergmannpau","last":"Bergmann","locid":"b48d0dd2-528b-456e-8274-55c5587f952c","name":"Bergmann, René","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zachary James","key":"davispau","last":"Davis","locid":"a869d6d4-d10c-4463-aa97-8e7c3c7052f0","name":"Davis, Zachary James","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Stenbæk","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"c47946d3-04a1-42d3-98f6-62ef38222262","name":"Schmidt, Michael Stenbæk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sønnik","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"270d6b1a-9f81-41c3-b267-67db70e4f3e1","name":"Clausen, Sønnik","orcid":"0000-0002-8178-5545","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","locid":"898c472f-7fe0-4454-83d8-564450caa2cb","name":"Boisen, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-9918-6567","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Muller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jens Muller","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rainer","key":"buchnerpau","last":"Buchner","name":"Buchner, Rainer","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomine","key":"stolbergrohrpau","last":"Stolberg-Rohr","name":"Stolberg-Rohr, Thomine","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens Havsteen","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"2e09303d-f3ed-46f8-9124-272437651149","name":"Jakobsen, Mogens Havsteen","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-718X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1117/12.883921","issn":["0277786X","1996756X"],"issn_org":["0277786X"],"journal":"Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering","publisher":"SPIE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of SPIE - The International Society for Optical Engineering","volume":"8016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79959820577"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Danfoss","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6c940af9-c63d-42cd-86de-8f7b0dc4c5bf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Development of nanostructured protective \"sight glasses\" for IR gas sensors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-337019","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Marine (blue) biomasses, such as macroalgaes, represent a huge unexploited amount of biomass. With their various chemical compositions, macroalgaes can be a potential substrate for food, feed, biomaterials, pharmaceuticals, health care products and also for bioenergy. Algae use seawater as a growth medium, light as energy source and they capture CO2 for the synthesis of new organic material, thus can grow on non-agricultural land, without increasing food prices, or using fresh water. Due to all these advantages in addition to very high biomass yield with high carbohydrate content, macroalgaes can be the well suited candidates as feedstock for biofuel production in the future. The aim of our studies is to examine the possibility producing liquid biofuel (ethanol and butanol) from macroalgaes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kádár, Zsófia","Jensen, Annette E.","Bangsø Nielsen, Henrik","Schmidt, Jens Ejbye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-369853"],"event":{"end":"2011-05-12","place":"Roskilde, dk","start":"2011-05-10","title":"Risø International Energy Conference 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio refinery","Bioraffinaderi","Risø R 1776","Risø R 1776 EN"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liquid biofuels from blue biomass","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5564580/ris-r-1776.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-369853","ids":["dtu-da4d5778-b581-4a5d-856e-b14086be2875"],"keyword":["Bio refinery","Bioraffinaderi","Risø-R-1776","Risø-R-1776(EN)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69AA15E8AB2AC